{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread","id":541856,"title":"Beast: Character Idea Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-05T17:14:54-07:00","id":541856,"title":"Beast: Character Idea Thread","content":"So, lets start an Idea Thread for characters that way we can spread those creative juices.<br /> <br /> 1. DMV Hag<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I'm reading through the Hungers and I get to the Hunger for Punishment and my brain suddenly clicks, &quot;That explains the DMV! No wonder people who have DUI's and Suspensions tend to file the wrong paperwork, they are given it 'on accident' by Hag-Beasts who feed their Hunger for Punishment by sending them chasing their tails through paperwork for months!&quot;<br /> <br /> Dear god, those hags could spend Satity like it was going out of style, that would be the best feeding ground ever. And any hero's who attack get overwhelmed by the coven of Hag-Beasts with the massive home advantage. </div> </div> </div><br /> 2. Dentist Tooth Collector<br /> At a young age you had many nightmares about all of your teeth falling out as you ran through a maze-like castle made of teeth. Then one day you heard a voice calling you from the center of the castle that led you to a massive hall, with a throne made from a giant bleeding tooth. From that day forth, you collected the teeth of those you met and fed your Soul from this. Your obsession with teeth eventually led you to attend medical school and become a surgical dentist. Your Soul's form is made up of a swarm of small tooth fairy-like creatures <a href=\"https://arafinas.files.wordpress.com/2010/11/rtuk_feature_hellboy_fullsize_03.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://arafinas.files.wordpress.com...ullsize_03.jpg</a><br /> You also have Mafia Contacts who do you favors and in return you patch up their boys when they end up hurt, and if you tell them that a tooth needs to come out, well your the doc right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T18:13:43-07:00","id":541919,"title":"","content":"I was watching American History X at the team of the reading so my mind when to an odd place to feed, dominating on the basketball court. &quot;I got a bet. I come in this game right now, same score. We play black guys against the white guys. No money, for these courts. And not just today, for good....&quot; Be a giant who shuts out the best on the street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T20:03:28-07:00","id":542056,"title":"","content":"I have a Dragon Tyrant who I expect casual observers would confuse for a Predator, because the manifestation of her Hunger for Power is being acknowledged as <i>The </i>Ultimate Apex Predator.<br /> <br /> Think about it. What is a Western Style Dragon, when you break it up into it's component parts?<br /> <br /> The Body of a cat. The long neck and tail of a serpent(dragonfire could also be an exaggeration of venom-especially from a spitting snake), the wings and talons of a raptor, wrapped in the hide of a crocodilian and with teeth to match.<br /> <br /> It's a combination of all four of the predators of early man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T13:01:13-07:00","id":547449,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of a few character concepts:<br /> <br /> - A professional dominant Anakim Tyrant specialized in the public humiliation of his clients. His scenes are always spectacular, and often cathartic as he teaches his submissives their true place at his feet.<br /> <br /> -A vigilante Eshmaki Nemesis working at a women's shelter. She makes sure that abusive partners are punished for their actions, again and again. She never kills them, not even when they beg her to.<br /> <br /> -An Ugallu Ravager working as an inestigative journalist. She likes destroying the image and standing of the rich and powerful by exposing to the world their failings and corruption. She doesn't care about the repercussions, she only wants to tear off the masks and show the true, ugly faces of the so-called elite.<br /> <br /> -A Makara Collector who works as a talent scout for a modeling agency. He has a very good eye for new talents and a silver tongue. Once he has his sights on someone it is only a matter of time before he sign them up. It's a harsh business though, and models leave all the time, submerged by the demands of the job, or lured away by the competition. It's all right though, it just means he has to find more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T13:32:02-07:00","id":547464,"title":"","content":"I've got afew Ideas, one of which i posted in the main Beast thread, so won't repost it here (Might do later). I've seen afew i can use as examples, but I've thought of one that I need too use sometime, possibly as antagonists for a group.<br /> <br /> - The Gang: A group of Criminals and a Brood of Begotten that is lead by a Eshmaki Collector, who arranges for the cops too be tipped off on the fact that they are operating in the City, but never where and when just that they are and will be stealing things for the next week/month/year. The rest of the Gang feeds on different things, atleast one of them feeds on the paranoia that they create in the populace and Police. Especially when they Tear the doors off of Bank vaults and safety deposit boxes, or get up after being shot in the chest 2-3 times.<br /> <br /> Will put more when i think of them.<br /> <br /> Edit: ....... I Just realised you can Use Beast too make a Predator and a Xenomorph....Now... anyone for Alien Vs Predator?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 06-09-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:30:25-07:00","id":547550,"title":"","content":"An Eshmaki Tyrant pop/rock singer that uses their Nightmares to sabotage others careers and propel themselves to the top of the charts by manipulating the Temenos.<br /> <br /> They're able to feed equally on the crushed dreams of their rivals and the adoration of their fans as both reinforce their position of dominance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 06-09-2015, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:38:35-07:00","id":547556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=547550#post547550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Eshmaki Tyrant pop/rock singer that uses their Nightmares to sabotage others careers and propel themselves to the top of the charts by manipulating the Temenos.<br /> <br /> They're able to feed equally on the crushed dreams of their rivals and the adoration of their fans as both reinforce their position of dominance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes me think of the Misfits from Jem and te Holograms. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T15:02:58-07:00","id":547576,"title":"","content":"I've been considering Atavisms for a Beast based off Silent Hill, possibly using Pyramid Head or Alessa.<br /> <br /> Eye of Heaven and Siren's Treacherous Song are a nasty combo when combined with the starting Lair traits of Fog &amp; Mirages...<br /> <br /> The two Nightmares I'd go with for chargen would be <i>You Deserve This</i> and <i>You Can't Wake Up</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3951,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","user":"wander","date":". 06-09-2015, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T15:03:31-07:00","id":547578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=547550#post547550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Eshmaki Tyrant pop/rock singer that uses their Nightmares to sabotage others careers and propel themselves to the top of the charts by manipulating the Temenos.<br /> <br /> They're able to feed equally on the crushed dreams of their rivals and the adoration of their fans as both reinforce their position of dominance.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd go with Makara for this, both because the Family has the best sort of mythic resonance(both in darker mermaid myths and in the popular misconception of the Sirens) and because doing so would allow you to start with both Siren's Treacherous Song and Alien Allure rather than picking between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T15:31:17-07:00","id":547600,"title":"","content":"The high school swim team is coached by a Makara Predator; a hydra to be exact! Normal practice goes just fine, but when its time to compete against other teams, the coach 'cheats' to win. They harness their power over Nightmares to fill their swimmers with the sense of being chased, a carnivorous predator swimming after them. He doesn't go all out and make them suffer hallucinations, but he does give them enough of a scare to pump them full of adrenaline, making them swim faster and harder than the opponents.<br /> <br /> Of course if that doesn't work, he can also fill the enemy team with a stronger version, making it difficult for them to hold their breath and concentrate on their lane!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T17:36:44-07:00","id":547782,"title":"","content":"I'm working on an Anakim Tyrant who's a surgeon, and embodies the hopelessness of sickness while feeding off the power her job gives her over the lives of her patients.<br /> <br /> I also want to make a Namtaru made of bees who actually owns several hives of bees and makes a living off selling their all organic honey. I'm thinking a Gaia's Revenge sort of Nemesis who leaves their victims at the local national park. I really just want to make a flower child who is made up of bees, okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5972-lovecraft-lite","name":"lovecraft lite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5972_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T18:01:41-07:00","id":547805,"title":"","content":"I've been gradually threading together an Ugallu Tyrant student teacher/TA for some time now; recent consideration has led to adjusting the Tutor's Soul to be decidedly spidery after a lot more faffing about with winged creatures despite lacking the MO to necessitate the appendages.<br /> <br /> There's also Tensai, the faceless Namtaru Ravager who's hanging around a ring of Saboteurs for the sake of Chamber-scrapbooking divine fallout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T18:30:14-07:00","id":547843,"title":"","content":"Anakim Predator who feeds by sleeping around. The hunt is the seduction and he feeds as his partners are exhausted in the after glow helpless. (Doesn't actually hurt them...but he <i>could</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T18:34:07-07:00","id":547848,"title":"","content":"Making a Namtaru Collector who works in as a librarian whats surprising for his brood is that he doesn't collect books but games ranging from card games to videos games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T19:08:36-07:00","id":547873,"title":"","content":"A Mr.Grey styled Ravager, very likely an Ugallu, who enjoys feeding his Hunger very much on the assorted people he takes back to his 'special place'. He is not fussy on what gender he takes in, though he does Feed from destroying the limits his partners have and he enjoys breaking them whilst he gets gratification from them. He is an Ugallu rather than an Anakim as it's more about making his partners exposed and embarrassed than actually causing them harm or taking their power from them. Holds You Deserve This and You Must Obey as his Nightmares (of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:00:18-07:00","id":547909,"title":"","content":"A Nemesis, not sure of the family, based on the Furies<br /> <br /> He would feed by denouncing crimes against family, stalking his prey and reminding them of their faults while protecting their victims (thus feasting on their powerlessness to harm more). He would not touch his victims if possible, preferring haunting them in their dreams, harrassing them by anonymous letters, with the goal to push the worst of them to suicide.<br /> <br /> And for those who would ask, crimes against family are : abuse of your own children, casting them out, mistreating your parents in their old age, and of course kinslaying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:10:30-07:00","id":547917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=547909#post547909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Nemesis, not sure of the family, based on the Furies<br /> <br /> He would feed by denouncing crimes against family, stalking his prey and reminding them of their faults while protecting their victims (thus feasting on their powerlessness to harm more). He would not touch his victims if possible, preferring haunting them in their dreams, harrassing them by anonymous letters, with the goal to push the worst of them to suicide.<br /> <br /> And for those who would ask, crimes against family are : abuse of your own children, casting them out, mistreating your parents in their old age, and of course kinslaying</div> </div> </div> </div> The stalkerish tone to it makes me think Eshmaki, personally. Might want to also go for Ugallu; either way, Eyes Of Heaven and Needs Must sound like necessities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T22:20:26-07:00","id":548000,"title":"","content":"An Eshmaki Nemesis...who used to be a Hero, and still hunts his fellow Begotten, sating his hunger for Punishment by seeking out freshly-fed Beasts and slaughtering them ritually. He doesn't have his Hero capability to lay Anathema, but he does have the full host of powers that come with Homecoming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:04:01-07:00","id":548146,"title":"","content":"I really like that concept malonkey. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T13:15:37-07:00","id":549222,"title":"","content":"A few simple ones I want to play:<br /> <br /> A Makara Ravager, who runs an illicit gambling den, feeding off of people destroying their own lives, risking everything on a roll of the (rigged) dice.<br /> <br /> An Anakim Tyrant, who trains as an MMA fighter. Guess how he feeds.<br /> <br /> An Ugallu Punisher, who used to be a Catholic Priest in Spain. Nobody expects the Spanish Inquisition!<br /> <br /> And of course, the Eshmaki Predator Slenderman clone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T17:17:20-07:00","id":549529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=548000#post548000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Eshmaki Nemesis...who used to be a Hero, and still hunts his fellow Begotten, sating his hunger for Punishment by seeking out freshly-fed Beasts and slaughtering them ritually. He doesn't have his Hero capability to lay Anathema, but he does have the full host of powers that come with Homecoming.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could also work with a former Frankeinstein Fury, having Nightmare about her previous existence and becoming a Namtaru Nemesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T18:15:57-07:00","id":549559,"title":"","content":"Former Basement-Dwelling (&amp; formerly teenaged) Eshmaki living out of a &quot;haunted&quot; house of his own design. His nightmare is a voiceless monster that only speaks when spoken too (kind of like Echo from Greek Mythology), and is a known Nemesis that feeds by telling his &quot;victims&quot; which punishment room they will be sent to if they break his household rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T18:20:11-07:00","id":549560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=549559#post549559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Former Basement-Dwelling (&amp; formerly teenaged) Eshmaki living out of a &quot;haunted&quot; house of his own design. His nightmare is a voiceless monster that only speaks when spoken too (kind of like Echo from Greek Mythology), and is a known Nemesis that feeds by telling his &quot;victims&quot; which punishment room they will be sent to if they break his household rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or in less ambiguous terms: &quot;Not the (Insert terrifying Animal here) Room! Anything but that!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T12:05:07-07:00","id":550493,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">* Eshmaki Predator</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> * Youngest child with one or two MUCH OLDER siblings -- like a fifteen and eleven year age gap, so they were leaving home just as he was getting old enough to miss their absence. Grew up mostly alone in a great big house with the occasional babysitter, latchkey, always hated being alone because SCARY AND NEVER REALLY ALONE BECAUSE *SOMETHING* WAS THERE THAT NOBODY ELSE COULD/WOULD SEE.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> * Became gregarious and outgoing as he got older so he would *have* to be alone. ENFP? Possibly. Got way into both athletic and artistic pursuits to fill pretty much every moment with some sort of activity that would keep his fears at bay.<br /> <br /> * Got waaaaaaaaaaay into backpacking/hiking/mountaineering/adventure sports in college/early adulthood and on one such expedition with a group of friends got caught in a bad situation -- I'm thinking an avalache/rockslide/unexpected blizzard -- something that forced him to literally or metaphorically &quot;cut the rope&quot; that someone else could survive and in the ensuing spiritual katabasis finally met the SCARY THING THAT WAS STALKING HIM HIS WHOLE LIFE and BECAME IT.<br /> <br /> * Back and forth about whether or not his friends/family think he's dead. &quot;Thinks he's dead&quot; means he essentially had to adopt a new identity. &quot;Came back *different*&quot; means he's still got a friends/family support network -- i.e., access to greater resources -- and people he's likely walled off a part of his new existence from, generally for their own protection.<br /> <br /> * In any case, he came back *different.* Still artistic and athletic but less outgoing, more reserved, and his art took a generally darker cast than it had thus far, his predatory nature starting to shine through in a manner that makes spirit hunting in the Primordial Realms of those souls effected by his imagery and music always a basic possibility.<br /> <br /> * Owns a home on Marrowstone Island, which is his primary residence and the location of his home studio for more traditional artistic pursuits -- multiple physical media and plays multiple instruments -- as well as having a habit of leaving spontaneously arranged artistic displays scattered all over the island. His neighbors would probably be less charmed if they realized their true purpose. He maintains a &quot;hunting camp&quot; in the Picket Range of the high North Cascades that is exactly what it sounds like -- where he goes when he needs to feed on flesh and blood. He mostly tries to confine these predations to other (nonhuman) predators, though there have been a few unlucky backpackers whose bones he was forced to put to artistic uses over the years.<br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wyrd Sister<br /> Freelance Penmonkey For Hire<br /> Moloch's PR Chick</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3896-nagaina","name":"Nagaina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:10:29-07:00","id":550592,"title":"","content":"Another Couple I've got...<ul><li>An Anakim Predator, that arranges and competes in Gaming Tournaments, preying on the fear's of Gamers by using overwhelming Force and cheap tactics in Games. Known too have a Nasty temper, but will never phsyically harm people. If he Loses he congratulates the winner with a Little Nightmare he's concocted that makes them lose their sense of balance and co-ordination, will regularly blame the Game/Console/Computer for his own failures.</li> <li>A Namtaru Ravager, Radio Presenter/Critic who harshly judges peoples work and stories from the &quot;Darkness&quot; of the Airwaves, He Takes news stories, films, songs, books and deconstructs them down to the core themes and tells people Why they shouldn't like them. And Judges anyone who does like what he destroys as a Hypocrite/Adulter/Nazi etc. Off of the radio he's a perfectly nice person who funds charity and loves half the things he &quot;Feasts&quot; on, he's Harsh but he's only doing it because he wants the creators too understand that the world isn't Nice too those who Dream. (He's &quot;Ugly&quot; with the Truth, people hate when your honest with them and critical of what they do).</li> </ul><br /> Both are likely too create their own Heroes and try their best too help them &quot;overcome&quot; the narrative they are bound by. I can See the Radio Presenter being especially vocal about things his Hero does if he realises he caused it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T13:40:52-07:00","id":550624,"title":"","content":"-She was always a troubled kid. She had night terrors, and two years ago, she acquired he certitude that her older sister had been replaced by an alien. She tried to warn her parents, but they simply send her see a doctor who prescribed her some medication that made her too confused and apathetic to act.<br /> She didn't resent her parents though, since now too tired to flee the monster that hounded her dreams, she finally stopped running and faced it.<br /> Now aware of who and hat she really was she could comfront the thing living her sister's life. Things were tense for a while, but creature wasn't that bad, all things considered, they even became friends, but still, it doesn't give it the right to replace her sister (Family is important after all). She knows she'll have to do something about it soon, but she hasn't yet decided what it will be.<br /> Ideally she'd like to get her sister back. If it isn't possible... well someone will have to pay for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T14:22:27-07:00","id":550702,"title":"","content":"This is pretty similar to one of Anteros's ideas, but I wanted to share it anyway. It's loosely inspired by a friend of mine, though he's actually mostly a nice guy. :P<br /> <br /> A serpent broods among the kelp beds and broken ships off of San Francisco's Ocean Beach. Some say that the cold of the arctic currents and chilling fog of his home has seeped into this Makara Tyrant's soul, but the truth is that the cold is simply part of his nature. Few passions stir his steady heart, and his ice-blue eyes reveal no hint of emotion beyond whatever mask he chooses to present.<br /> <br /> The serpent lurks within several of the disparate subcultures that make up the City's kink scene, and seems to have an uncanny ability to attract a certain type of prey. Those who come to him are eager to feed his hunger. They crave debasement, draw pleasure from being bound and silenced, and thrill at the sensation of true helplessness that he grants them. He feasts at the threshold where terror meets ecstasy, and always leaves his meals begging for more.<br /> <br /> The serpent never does any permanent, physical harm to those from which he feeds - at least, not on purpose. Indeed, he abhors the sight of blood, and he views those Beasts who indulge in more grisly feasts with distaste. When push comes to shove he prefers to dispose of his enemies by smothering - either drowning them or squeezing the life from their bodies like a monstrous python.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the serpent has little awareness or care for the emotional wounds he leaves in his wake. He pushes those who provide his meals to the very limits of their comfort zone, and sometimes well beyond, and once their willing submission has ceased to satisfy his hunger, he abandons them like an apple core or the wrapper of a candy bar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-11-2015, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T15:45:36-07:00","id":550831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=549560#post549560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or in less ambiguous terms: &quot;Not the (Insert terrifying Animal here) Room! Anything but that!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me.<br /> <br /> An Anakim whose Astral Soul is a massive <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=egptlC4rKOc\" target=\"_blank\">Moose in a blank white Lair.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T20:55:46-07:00","id":551040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=550831#post550831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Anakim whose Astral Soul is a massive <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=egptlC4rKOc\" target=\"_blank\">Moose in a blank white Lair.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And this is reminding me the Eshmaki's Soul of pure Darkness that Hungers for Ruin and haunts little town of <i>Bright Falls</i>. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TX6J0yy-qKM\" target=\"_blank\">The Soul finally overtakes the reporter comming to settlment...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T22:46:07-07:00","id":551138,"title":"","content":"A Mummy/Beast crossover character idea:<br /> <br /> Makara Predator, lives two lives: one as a guide and survivalist in the deserts of Africa. She knows how to get from town to town safely and quickly, and how to read the moods and weather shifts.<br /> <br /> Second life is as a high priestess/recruiter for a cult. Her Prey in this case is people who seem like they'd make good cultists, and she takes them out into the wastes and harries them towards the Tomb. If they die, clearly they weren't actually cut ou; if they make it, then they get a chance to become a cultist. Either way, she gets what she needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T05:55:19-07:00","id":551286,"title":"","content":"Not really a character concept, but I feel a really great Beast story could be made out of &quot;The Dragon of Mordiford&quot; (Also known as &quot;Maud and the Wyvern&quot;). A wyvern hatchling (In this case a proto-Beast, probably a troubled child) is befriended by a girl named Maud. In spite of her parents ordering her to keep away from it, Maud still visits the wyvern in the woods- feeding it, playing with it, cuddling, etc. That is, until the wyvern fully matures. (Homecoming. Ugallu Predator) The wyvern feasts on sheep and cattle, destroying anyone or anything in its way except for Maud. She stubbornly stayed with the wyvern, trying to get it to turn its attentions elsewhere, and while it wouldn't hurt her, no one else was safe. One day, a knight shows up (Experienced Hero) and kills the beast with contemptuous ease- even as Maud pelts him with rocks in an effort to turn him aside. After the wyvern dies, and the Hero marches off to claim his reward, bewildered as to why she's not thanking him, she throws herself over the corpse and sobs inconsolably.<br /> <br /> When I was a child, this story really struck me. I still was in a 'black and white' frame of mind, and so I wanted to side with the knight- but because the story was about Maud, and not him, I was still sad when the wyvern was killed. I knew it was a monster. I knew it was killing people, destroying their farms, but I didn't want it to die because Maud showed there was some good in it. And when it did die, I was upset instead of relieved, which is terribly confusing to a five year old who just wanted to read a story about a dragon.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the character you could get out of this is a mortal who was childhood friends with the Beast, and never abandoned them- no matter how monstrous and inhuman they became. They could enter the Beast's Lair at will, bring out the best in it, and are utterly determined in their pursuit to change them, even if it seems futile. The story of the Dragon of Mordiford isn't about the knight or the wyvern- it's about the little girl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:03:15-07:00","id":551753,"title":"","content":"A famous, high-profile actor who takes up cannibalism to feed his Hunger for Prey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o0u4M6vppCI\" data-code=\"o0u4M6vppCI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/o0u4M6vppCI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:35:29-07:00","id":552185,"title":"","content":"I made an Ugallu Nemesis who can be summed up in a single sentence as &quot;Kenshiro with a PHD.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5391-krycanelo","name":"Krycanelo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5391_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:17:45-07:00","id":556333,"title":"","content":"So, this isn't a character idea, but an example of something I've run into while playtesting both Beast and Hurt Locker Material in my PbP game.<br /> <br /> Luke is a Makara Predator with Strength 3 and Brawl 5 (Grappling Specialty). He is attacking a Hero after being dealt 5 Aggravated Damage by a Bane Weapon (a fishing gaff-hook)<br /> <br /> In this attack, Luke is using the Clinching Strike Merit, Ground and Pound Merit, Limb from Limb Atavism and Monster From the Deep Atavism. He started with 5 Satiety.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Luke Chetty rolled 5 successes using 10d10 with the World of Darkness nWoD system with a target of 8, rerolling on 9 or more with rolls of 2,9(+8),6,6,2,9(+10,3),8,3,3,3. Strength + Brawl (Asset Skill) + Specialty (Brawl) + WP (Grapple) - 2 (Wound Modifiers).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Luke Chetty rolled 4 successes using 7d10 with the World of Darkness nWoD system with a target of 8, rerolling on 9 or more with rolls of 8,9(+5),3,10(+7),8,5,1. Rote Action (Ground and Pound).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">It turns out that is enough to do 28 AGGRAVATED DAMAGE in a single attack. Cause the Arm Wrack Tilt and Knockdown Tilt.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Here is the breakdown of that damage.:</span></span><ul><li>Limb from Limb does Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack Tilt on an attack that does more damage than the victims Stamina.</li> <li>Spending Satiety on Limb from Limb causes the attack to do Aggravated Damage. (Reflexive Action)</li> <li>Spending Satiety on Monster from the Deep makes the attack ignore Defense and can attack all enemies within Lair x2 yards. It also adds Lair to Weapon damage. (Reflexive Action) 1 Lair = 1 Aggravated Damage Weapon Modifier.</li> <li>Low Satiety on Monster from the Deep makes Unarmed Attacks 2L and causes the Knocked Down Tilt on a successful attack. Now 3 Aggravated Weapon Modifier.</li> <li>The Clinch Strike Merit inflicts standard Brawl damage when initiating a grapple instead of sacrificing the opportunity to damage someone in order to grab. (Instant Action) (8 Aggravated Damage)</li> <li>Exceptional Success on the Grapple allows 1 Maneuver on a grapple [Damage Move] (8 Aggravated Damage)</li> <li>Makara Birthright allows 1 Maneuver on a Grapple [Damage Move] (8 Aggravated Damage)</li> <li>Ground and Pound Merit: When using Brawl to strike or inflict the Damage grappling maneuver on a prone opponent, you may declare your character uses this maneuver. You gains the Rote benefit (re-roll failed dice) to your attack, but automatically fall prone, and if grappled, your opponent automatically breaks free. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">(4 additional Aggravated Damage)</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">I'm guessing the Devs aren't expecting a base character (0XP) to be able to do 28 Aggravated Damage on a 5 Success Grapple Attack?<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:50:18-07:00","id":560914,"title":"","content":"I don't know if they expected anybody to stack all that stuff together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:07:40-07:00","id":560945,"title":"","content":"Well if both go to print as is, then there is nothing stopping a player from using them as written.<br /> <br /> That's why I am bringing it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:35:37-07:00","id":560974,"title":"","content":"You are using two playtest documents together. That's <i>bound</i> to cause problems.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think your math is right.<ul><li>Limb from Limb inflcits the Arm or Leg Wrack Tilts</li> <li>Limb from Limb Low Satiety Expenditure makes it Aggravaged.</li> <li>Limb from Limb <i>sets</i> the damage to 1L.</li> <li>Terror from the deep's Low Satiety option <i>sets </i>the damage to 2L. This does not stack with the above, but the player would get to choose which applies.</li> <li>Clinch Strike should not stack with the Damage Move in a grapple. If it does, that's a problem. But okay, we're at 7A for the first attack.</li> <li>Exceptional Success allows you to pick a move. Damage move is acceptable. +7A, for 14A total.</li> <li>You can't select the Damage move twice. It allows you to select an additional move, not the same move multiple times. Still at 14A.</li> <li>The target isn't prone until after your action's conclusion, so this wouldn't apply.</li> </ul>An aside, since you spend Satiety consecutively and not simultaniously, you'd have to start at 4 Satiety or less, not 5 or less, to pull this off.<br /> <br /> So we have 14A damage, which is still obscene. The culprit is Clinch Strike which shouldn't be allowed to stack with the Damage grapple maneuver. There is a basic design principle that says no multiple attacks against the same target, so anything that allows you to get multiple attacks is obviously an error. That said, spending 2 Satiety is a pretty big deal. There is a Nightmare that lets you inflict +2L damage per Satiety expended, which can get deep into one-shot territory.<br /> <br /> As for whether 7A damage can be a problem... Joe Standard Mortal with STR 2, Brawl 5 (Grapple), Professional Training [Brawl] 5, Street Fighting 3, Cheap Shot 2, and 2L weapon can get pretty close to matching that damage output. It'll deal Lethal instead of Aggravated damage and won't inflict the Arm Wrack (though it will inflict Knockdown). So a combat-focused Beast is slightly better than a combat focused mortal. Functioning as intended, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 06-19-2015, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:07:11-07:00","id":561015,"title":"","content":"I agree with the principle that says Clinch Strike, Damage Move and Damage Move shouldn't stack, but there is nowhere in any of the texts that says that. Since it's technically 1 Attack with 3 Damage outputs, it's not 'multiple attacks' in the normal sense of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't select the Damage move twice. It allows you to select an additional move, not the same move multiple times. </div> </div> </div>Where does it say you can't choose the same move twice? Not that I don't agree with you, but where is it stated that you 'must' choose 2 separate moves in a grapple with an Exceptional Success?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An aside, since you spend Satiety consecutively and not simultaniously, you'd have to start at 4 Satiety or less, not 5 or less, to pull this off. </div> </div> </div>Limb from Limb Satiety Expenditure is the first one used, bringing Satiety from 5 to 4. Monster from the Deep is the second one used, bringing Satiety from 4 to 3 (Low Satiety Threshold) which allows all 3 versions of Monster from the Deep.<br /> <br /> Another thing to consider is that the Character has the Systema (Style) at 3 dots, which allows the Knockdown Move, so he could use Ground and Pound on the second Damage Move (which would add 4 more Damage)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2545,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","user":"Ninjar","date":". 06-19-2015, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:14:03-07:00","id":561034,"title":"","content":"Clinch Strike is under playtest. 1 Attack with 3 Damage Outputs is functionally the same as multiple attacks, for balance purposes.<br /> <br /> The wording of the ability precludes selecting the same move multiple times. It's even clarified in parenthesis. &quot;When using grappling attacks, a Makara chooses one additional move, including during the turn when she initiates it (so one move when initiating a grapple, two for an exceptional success). Grappling is described on p. XX.&quot;<br /> <br /> You have Set (A, B, C, D, E). I tell you to select one thing from that Set. Lets say you pick A. If I had told you to select two things from that set or to select one additional thing, most people would not interpret that as you being able to select A twice. That isn't &quot;additional&quot; or &quot;selecting two things.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, I think we are getting pretty off topic. You should make a new thread if you want to discuss balance concerns, I think. This thread is for interesting Beast Character Concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T08:09:28-07:00","id":563032,"title":"","content":"<b>That Homeless Guy</b> - Ugallu who wonders the streets of the upper class homes going through their trash for food. Late at night he awakens those who have domestics troubles, abusive spouses and cheating love ones, staring into their souls bringing what they thought they could hide to the surface. motionless he waits for them to react to his stair feeding on their panic &quot;who is this guy, What does he know&quot;. Sometimes he even breaks into homes and leaves messages for the guilty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T11:37:22-07:00","id":563184,"title":"","content":"Tyler Durden, an Eshmaki Nemesis with lots of Social and Fighting Style Merits, that hungers for bring low the socially powerful. Definitely rocking high Mystery Cult and multiple Professional Training and Alternate Identities, and Nightmares revolving in making the prey feel powerless. Also, definitely starting with Limb from Limb and Undersea Creature(?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T11:51:11-07:00","id":563213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=563184#post563184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tyler Durden, an Eshmaki Nemesis with lots of Social and Fighting Style Merits, that hungers for bring low the socially powerful. Definitely rocking high Mystery Cult and multiple Professional Training and Alternate Identities, and Nightmares revolving in making the prey feel powerless. Also, definitely starting with Limb from Limb and Undersea Creature(?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Cameron Frye, whose Horror is a Tyrant that feeds on the the power that comes with basically owning the souls of everybody he knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T01:12:27-08:00","id":795466,"title":"","content":"Caution, a Raptor Nemesis whose Kinship with the spirit courts of the city intersections has led to an upswing in predatory behavior by the local Car Descants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T09:32:38-08:00","id":796867,"title":"","content":"The great leech of Tlanusi'yi (a giant leech from Cherokee legend), would be a great horror for a Namtaru or Makara (the leech is said to live in the caves beneath the Hiwassee river) Predator that terrorizes tourists in and around Murphy North Carolina (where the leech is said to live).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T12:48:19-08:00","id":796967,"title":"","content":"Three-headed draconic Anakim Tyrant that uses Smaug-esque persuasion to tie people in a Gordian knot of paranoia and suspicion before sweeping in and sorting everything out, making everyone dependant on him in the process, without them ever noticing. Inspired by The Dragon, a play by Evgeny Schwartz","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T19:21:48-08:00","id":797597,"title":"","content":"I don't have access to the book, but I plan to play a Collector with a spider theme, specifically Atavisms and Liar traits consistent with a trapdoor spider. Swarm Form, Infested, that kind of thing. Not sure what family, probably Namtaru?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3T