to eventually lead to his downfall after many &quot;Heroic&quot; Encounters and the like? I can Dig that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:51:19-08:00","id":818053,"title":"","content":"I have three characters floating around my head<br /> <br /> The first one's Horror is a colossal snake, an Ouroboros Anakim that crawls in a desert littered with ruins and abandoned temples. It embodies the notion that nothing ever lasts, that even the greatest empires are doomed to become dust and that all the works of man will eventually be forgotten. The character itself works as an history teacher in a small school, which helps to get the lesson across but is rarely enough to sate his Hunger for destabilizing Ruin. He is torn between the fundamental truth at the core of his nature and the desire to keep the place safe and peaceful<br /> <br /> The second is a Tyrant Eshmaki, his Horror a majestic deer with the skin made of darkness and antlers covered in fire, like some sort burning bush. He's a sheriff who sees his town as a glade he has the duty to protect. As the guardian and king of the place, he keeps an eye over all the inhabitants, supernatural or not, somehow managing to exert his control from the shadow. Nobody is exactly afraid of him, it's not like he gave them reason to, but they all know he's the one who has the final word over all the issues in town.<br /> <br /> Still a bit unsure about the last one. I'm thinking about a Namtaru Nemesis with a terrifying scarecrow as Horror. She punishes those who dare to cross bounduaries, but I'm still working on how to translate this to a character","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-27-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:06:40-08:00","id":818069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Still a bit unsure about the last one. I'm thinking about a Namtaru Nemesis with a terrifying scarecrow as Horror. She punishes those who dare to cross bounduaries, but I'm still working on how to translate this to a character</div> </div> </div> </div> Such a character might create Kinship with Forsaken and Scarecrow Ministers at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T02:49:54-08:00","id":821517,"title":"","content":"A Beast who was a former astronaut and who underwent the Devouring while onboard the ISS. His Horror is an alien thing, golden eyes in an amorphous oily body which can seep around barriers and which can shape itself into tendrils and spikes on which to impale its prey. Its Lair is the same space station on which he underwent the Devouring, save that it is abandoned, save for the thing. When Heroes come to try and kill it, it need only open an airlock to fling them into the endless blackness of space.<br /> Now retired, the Beast feeds its Hunger for Prey by isolation, making its prey so alone and helpless that it might as well be in the void before swooping in and delivering the final blow, a mark upon his prey to forever remind them of how empty life is without others. He targets those who think themselves an island, able to stand on their own. He tries to teach that an empty life is no life at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> For imagery, have a look at the form of Hermaeus Mora from the Elder Scrolls series. At least for the whole 'oil and eyes' thing. For Atavisms I'd take Infestation and Limb from Limb. I'm not sure about Nightmares. Perhaps Behold! My True Form, except that instead of showing the victim a visage that's so horrifying to look at it physically hurts the, instead it shows them the truth of their utter insignificance in comparison to the vastness of the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-02-2016, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T13:42:17-08:00","id":823666,"title":"","content":"I was reading about the Hannibal TV series by Bryan Fuller, and that really sold me on the idea that the eponymous serial killer could be a Beast just as much as a Slasher. And I kept thinking about Beasts with vibes of medical horror. Soon a concept came to me.<br /> <br /> A Namtaru who chooses to be a street surgeon despite graduating with great honor from an admired institution, much to the disgust and shame of his family and colleagues. He simply doesn't care, because he believes true knowledge and breakthroughs are only possible when one disregards useless rules. He does not reject the Hippocratic Oath outright, for that is equally foolish. For the most part, he follows his own code, despite caring little for philosophical discourse.<br /> <br /> Besides cold hard cash, he also demands payment in the form of new things to study, the things no one else wants to be near, yet alone touch. All he asks for is assistance in entering the dark corners where marvels are waiting to be dissected (i.e. help with using Skeleton Key). He has no real home besides his Lair, where he has built a surprisingly normal house amidst all the preserved organs and anatomical diagrams of critters that shouldn't live.<br /> <br /> He is a Collector, but not because he kidnaps people and experiments on them (he finds that method laughably theatrical). The shock is caused by his pragmatism and disturbingly accurate empathy. People near him are often revealed to be sick in more than just the flesh, which he uses as leverage. His lesson, when he bothers to teach one, is that there is something ugly inside everyone, and that pretending it's not there will only make it fester.<br /> <br /> Despite all this macabre curiosity and clinical detachment, he still has a desire to be seen as a source of safety and warmth. To help with this, his Lair has a Chamber dedicated to unorthodox cuisine, which he calls &quot;medicine's more extroverted sister&quot;. There you will find things you never imagined could be edible, yet alone delicious. Good luck with getting past the unappetizing exteriors, however. Any mortal or supernatural who behaves is welcome.<br /> <br /> He probably has Kinship with Changelings and Prometheans. Atavisms would include Mimir's Wisdom, Unbreakable, Limb From Limb, Relentless Hunter and Needs Must. Nightmares would include You Must Obey and We Know All Your Secrets. I don't know what his Horror will be like at the moment.<br /> <br /> Does this sound like a viable character? Is there anything you thought was vague or confusing? What do you think is worth fleshing out (pun intended)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T13:48:23-08:00","id":823677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=818053#post818053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have three characters floating around my head<br /> <br /> The first one's Horror is a colossal snake, an Ouroboros Anakim that crawls in a desert littered with ruins and abandoned temples. It embodies the notion that nothing ever lasts, that even the greatest empires are doomed to become dust and that all the works of man will eventually be forgotten. The character itself works as an history teacher in a small school, which helps to get the lesson across but is rarely enough to sate his Hunger for destabilizing Ruin. He is torn between the fundamental truth at the core of his nature and the desire to keep the place safe and peaceful<br /> <br /> The second is a Tyrant Eshmaki, his Horror a majestic deer with the skin made of darkness and antlers covered in fire, like some sort burning bush. He's a sheriff who sees his town as a glade he has the duty to protect. As the guardian and king of the place, he keeps an eye over all the inhabitants, supernatural or not, somehow managing to exert his control from the shadow. Nobody is exactly afraid of him, it's not like he gave them reason to, but they all know he's the one who has the final word over all the issues in town.<br /> <br /> Still a bit unsure about the last one. I'm thinking about a Namtaru Nemesis with a terrifying scarecrow as Horror. She punishes those who dare to cross boundaries, but I'm still working on how to translate this to a character</div> </div> </div> </div> I like the first two better, especially the history teacher. I find his conflicting motivations very good for drama. The scarecrow dude could be a gang leader who is on his way to starting his very own mafia to protect his neighborhood against those he considers a bad influence. He could have Kinship with Werewolves and Vampires.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T14:56:43-08:00","id":823750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823666#post823666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading about the Hannibal TV series by Bryan Fuller, and that really sold me on the idea that the eponymous serial killer could be a Beast just as much as a Slasher. And I kept thinking about Beasts with vibes of medical horror. Soon a concept came to me.<br /> <br /> A Namtaru who chooses to be a street surgeon despite graduating with great honor from an admired institution, much to the disgust and shame of his family and colleagues. He simply doesn't care, because he believes true knowledge and breakthroughs are only possible when one disregards useless rules. He does not reject the Hippocratic Oath outright, for that is equally foolish. For the most part, he follows his own code, despite caring little for philosophical discourse.<br /> <br /> Besides cold hard cash, he also demands payment in the form of new things to study, the things no one else wants to be near, yet alone touch. All he asks for is assistance in entering the dark corners where marvels are waiting to be dissected (i.e. help with using Skeleton Key). He has no real home besides his Lair, where he has built a surprisingly normal house amidst all the preserved organs and anatomical diagrams of critters that shouldn't live.<br /> <br /> He is a Collector, but not because he kidnaps people and experiments on them (he finds that method laughably theatrical). The shock is caused by his pragmatism and disturbingly accurate empathy. People near him are often revealed to be sick in more than just the flesh, which he uses as leverage. His lesson, when he bothers to teach one, is that there is something ugly inside everyone, and that pretending it's not there will only make it fester.<br /> <br /> Despite all this macabre curiosity and clinical detachment, he still has a desire to be seen as a source of safety and warmth. To help with this, his Lair has a Chamber dedicated to unorthodox cuisine, which he calls &amp;quot;medicine's more extroverted sister&amp;quot;. There you will find things you never imagined could be edible, yet alone delicious. Good luck with getting past the unappetizing exteriors, however. Any mortal or supernatural who behaves is welcome.<br /> <br /> He probably has Kinship with Changelings and Prometheans. Atavisms would include Mimir's Wisdom, Unbreakable, Limb From Limb, Relentless Hunter and Needs Must. Nightmares would include You Must Obey and We Know All Your Secrets. I don't know what his Horror will be like at the moment.<br /> <br /> Does this sound like a viable character? Is there anything you thought was vague or confusing? What do you think is worth fleshing out (pun intended)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read through this and it just terrified me. So good job! For the Horror, I'm getting an image of an emaciated, vaguely humanoid creature whose mouth is full of shark-like teeth and which stretches almost to his ears. His arms (all four of them) are unnaturally long and bear long bony fingers tipped with long claws almost like scalpels. It was inspired by the Mourngul from Warhammer Fantasy. You can look up some images in Googe or on Forge World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T16:49:14-08:00","id":823865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823666#post823666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this sound like a viable character? Is there anything you thought was vague or confusing? What do you think is worth fleshing out (pun intended)?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's a really cool concept that's perfectly well rounded and fleshed out. Great job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T17:17:39-08:00","id":823870,"title":"","content":"<b>Anakim Ravager:</b> They say too much of a good thing is bad for you. So it is that this Beast satiates itself by indulging the vice of others. They are more than a drug pusher, more than a chef, they are addiction incarnate. That voice in your heard encouraging you to try one more serving. Drugs, food, sex, anything that his victims may derive pleasure from, he is happy to provide. And then, when they finally go too far and their body retaliates against them, he feasts!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's soul is a horrifying figure that appears to be made out of living candy with syringes strapped to its fingers and bottles of narcotic drugs embedded into its backside. Its skin is like ginger bread, white frosting dripping from its mouth filled with candy corn teeth and specks of red cinnamon pepper his body, completely nude for all to see. A mane of black licorice wreathes its head and it speaks with a pleasant voice and trustworthy tone. The vials in his backside pump through his arms and into his fingers, ready to empty their contents into his victim's veins if he catches them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-04-2016, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T17:27:17-08:00","id":823875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823677#post823677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like the first two better, especially the history teacher. I find his conflicting motivations very good for drama. The scarecrow dude could be a gang leader who is on his way to starting his very own mafia to protect his neighborhood against those he considers a bad influence. He could have Kinship with Werewolves and Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> They're all, at least in theory, meant ot be part of the same group. Which of course means nothing, they should be able to stand on their own legs even alone. The Makara and Ugallu are even less fleshed out than the Namtaru, nothing worth to share for now.<br /> <br /> I imagined her as a woman, partly because I needed some variety in the group and also because I really like the image of a good-looking lady (Striking Looks 1 or 2) turning into a creepy and withered scarecrow. Namtaru 101, I know, but they're essentially my premade characters. The bounduaries she patrols are intended in the widest sense, meaning she punishes not only those who cross physical but also personal ones. Some concepts include trauma support worker, social assistant, barfly vigilante, local preservation enthusiast and ranger. For physical bounduaries, she does so to protect people even from themselves, so the Scarecrow Ministry Kinship is spot on (I admit it did not came to my mind)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-04-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T17:27:29-08:00","id":823876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823870#post823870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Anakim Ravager:</b> They say too much of a good thing is bad for you. So it is that this Beast satiates itself by indulging the vice of others. They are more than a drug pusher, more than a chef, they are addiction incarnate. That voice in your heard encouraging you to try one more serving. Drugs, food, sex, anything that his victims may derive pleasure from, he is happy to provide. And then, when they finally go too far and their body retaliates against them, he feasts!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's soul is a horrifying figure that appears to be made out of living candy with syringes strapped to its fingers and bottles of narcotic drugs embedded into its backside. Its skin is like ginger bread, white frosting dropping from its mouth filled with candy corn teeth and specks of red cinnamon pepper his body, completely nude for all to see. A mane of black licorice wreathes its head and it speaks with a pleasant voice and trustworthy tone. The vials in his backside pump through his arms and into his fingers, ready to empty their contents into his victim's veins if he catches them!</div> </div> </div> </div> Slaanesh would be proud. Don't forget the painfully exaggerated sexual characteristics both primary and secondary. What if someone is addicted to adrenaline? Does he invite them to a fist fight or petty crime? He sounds like a perfect candidate for the Alien Allure Atavism and the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous Lair Trait.</b></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T17:35:09-08:00","id":823879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823875#post823875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They're all, at least in theory, meant ot be part of the same group. Which of course means nothing, they should be able to stand on their own legs even alone. The Makara and Ugallu are even less fleshed out than the Namtaru, nothing worth to share for now.<br /> <br /> I imagined her as a woman, partly because I needed some variety in the group and also because I really like the image of a good-looking lady (Striking Looks 1 or 2) turning into a creepy and withered scarecrow. Namtaru 101, I know, but they're essentially my premade characters. The bounduaries she patrols are intended in the widest sense, meaning she punishes not only those who cross physical but also personal ones. Some concepts include trauma support worker, social assistant, barfly vigilante, local preservation enthusiast and ranger. For physical bounduaries, she does so to protect people even from themselves, so the Scarecrow Ministry Kinship is spot on (I admit it did not come to my mind)</div> </div> </div> </div> I see nothing wrong with a character sharing personality or physical traits with a typical description of their X or Y splat. You can't be sure if a character concept is going to work while it stays in a vacuum. Don't beat yourself up over &quot;101-ness&quot;. In fact, I like your concept better than my mafia leader idea.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Glad you and ajf115 liked my Namtaru street surgeon! I may stat him up as an NPC or ready made PC later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-04-2016, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T18:17:30-08:00","id":823904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823876#post823876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Slaanesh would be proud. Don't forget the painfully exaggerated sexual characteristics both primary and secondary. What if someone is addicted to adrenaline? Does he invite them to a fist fight or petty crime? He sounds like a perfect candidate for the Alien Allure Atavism and the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous Lair Trait.</b></a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest, I'm thinking about possibly altering their appearance a bit. A creature with needles strapped to their fingers doesn't exactly say &quot;Let's be friends!&quot; as well as he's supposed to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:12:32-08:00","id":823946,"title":"","content":"<b>Eshmaki Predator:</b> Beasts represent a primordial fear. And what is more primordial than the fear of being eaten? Since before life was complex enough to have any semblance of thought, we have devoured each other, and it was that fear of being consumed that pushed our ancestors to evolve and conquer their surroundings. But the Beast is not some looming predator, flaunting its might at the top of the food chain. No, that attracts too much attention, too much competition for food. This Beast is a parasite, it lets others do the hunting for it, and then consumes the half digested prey from within the predator's own body!<br /> <br /> The Beast's lair is not a cave, nor a castle, it is an organism of unimaginable scale. The Beast slithers through its digestive track, finding prey swallowed up by its host and descends upon them. Its soul possesses the torso of a man, but the body of a freakishly large tapeworm. Clinging to the fleshy walls of its lair, its eyeless, sucker shaped mouth creates disgusting noises as it slurps up half digested food. When it opens wide enough to scream, its prey (if they're still alive) can see ring after ring of razor sharp teeth designed to shred them on the way down its gullet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-04-2016, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:17:26-08:00","id":823948,"title":"","content":"That sounds more like a Namtaru than an Eshmaki... certainly hit my revulsion button.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:19:13-08:00","id":823950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823750#post823750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read through this and it just terrified me. So good job! For the Horror, I'm getting an image of an emaciated, vaguely humanoid creature whose mouth is full of shark-like teeth and which stretches almost to his ears. His arms (all four of them) are unnaturally long and bear long bony fingers tipped with long claws almost like scalpels. It was inspired by the Mourngul from Warhammer Fantasy. You can look up some images in Googe or on Forge World.</div> </div> </div> </div> While I appreciate the suggestion, I'll try to avoid any overt medical visuals in favor of something more surreal, something you'd never expect to be a surgeon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:19:43-08:00","id":823951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823948#post823948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds more like a Namtaru than an Eshmaki... certainly hit my revulsion button.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Eshmaki are the fear of destruction, which is pretty much what eating somebody entails. If they were just a big, walking worm then yeah, Namtaru would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking his lair may have constrictive, acidic and slippery elements to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T06:39:08-08:00","id":824255,"title":"","content":"<b>Eshmaki Predator:</b> Plants are supposed to sit quietly and look pretty. Their sweet aroma is supposed to be alluring, not an airborne narcotic. Their vines aren't supposed to reach for you like prehensile limbs. They're supposed to drink water, not blood. And they damn sure aren't supposed to be lounge singers at the local gentleman's club!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ugallu Collector:</b> She runs an orphanage &quot;collecting&quot; wayward children off the streets. Children who have lost their parents or were unwanted by them in the first place. Maybe she had a hand in that from behind the scenes, maybe not. The official story is they suffered a terrible accident that nobody could have predicted. But her orphanage is no children's refuge, it is essentially a prison, though you wouldn't know it from the outside. A gilded cage where the owner feeds upon the fears of lost children. Their mournful sobs, their outraged cries, their in denial explanations, their pained squeals as they're disciplined for unruly behavior. Nobody gets adopted here. They just get too old for the government to care, and then she dumps them on the street to make room for their replacements!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-05-2016, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T08:50:14-08:00","id":824350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824255#post824255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>(Undecided Family) Predator:</b> Plants are supposed to sit quietly and look pretty. Their sweet aroma is supposed to be alluring, not an airborne narcotic. Their vines aren't supposed to reach for you like prehensile limbs. They're supposed to drink water, not blood. And they damn sure aren't supposed to be lounge singers at the local gentleman's club!<br /> <br /> (Can't decide between Lurker, Giant, or Leviathan)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ugallu Collector:</b> She runs an orphanage &amp;quot;collecting&amp;quot; wayward children off the streets. Children who have lost their parents or were unwanted by them in the first place. Maybe she had a hand in that from behind the scenes, maybe not. The official story is they suffered a terrible accident that nobody could have predicted. But her orphanage is no children's refuge, it is essentially a prison, though you wouldn't know it from the outside. A gilded cage where the owner feeds upon the fears of lost children. Their mournful sobs, their outraged cries, their in denial explanations, their pained squeals as they're disciplined for unruly behavior. Nobody gets adopted here. They just get too old for the government to care, and then she dumps them on the street to make room for their replacements!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Eshmaki for the plant monster. The other one is just...wrong. (In a good way mind you) I don't quite get why it's Ugallu though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:52:59-08:00","id":824447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824350#post824350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd go with Eshmaki for the plant monster. The other one is just...wrong. (In a good way mind you) I don't quite get why it's Ugallu though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I support the Eshmaki idea. Creepy plant that drugs people, grabs you with vines and drains blood? That's fear of destruction. Also quite cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-05-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T11:09:33-08:00","id":824464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824255#post824255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>(Undecided Family) Predator:</b> Plants are supposed to sit quietly and look pretty. Their sweet aroma is supposed to be alluring, not an airborne narcotic. Their vines aren't supposed to reach for you like prehensile limbs. They're supposed to drink water, not blood. And they damn sure aren't supposed to be lounge singers at the local gentleman's club!<br /> <br /> (Can't decide between Lurker, Giant, or Leviathan)<br /> <br /> <b>Ugallu Collector:</b> She runs an orphanage &quot;collecting&quot; wayward children off the streets. Children who have lost their parents or were unwanted by them in the first place. Maybe she had a hand in that from behind the scenes, maybe not. The official story is they suffered a terrible accident that nobody could have predicted. But her orphanage is no children's refuge, it is essentially a prison, though you wouldn't know it from the outside. A gilded cage where the owner feeds upon the fears of lost children. Their mournful sobs, their outraged cries, their in denial explanations, their pained squeals as they're disciplined for unruly behavior. Nobody gets adopted here. They just get too old for the government to care, and then she dumps them on the street to make room for their replacements!</div> </div> </div> </div> I like the plant monster. The part about lounge singing made me chuckle.<br /> <br /> The orphanage owner, though? That is too one-note for me. I prefer the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/beastfamily/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>sample Eshmaki</b></a> from open dev.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T11:22:38-08:00","id":824480,"title":"","content":"I think I have a good idea for the Horror of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823666#post823666\"><b>my Namtaru Collector</b></a>. He's pretty much going to be a non-humanoid Grey Alien, but strongly influenced by the more understandable critters of the Cthulhu Mythos (e.g. Mi-Go, Elder Things and Yithians). An air of otherworldly erudition juxtaposed to a repulsive exterior with virtually no familiar expressions of emotion to latch onto. Possibly lamia-shaped, bioluminescent and with several tool-like limbs. But scariest of all: totally clean and wearing actual clothes.<br /> <br /> Does that sound cool?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-05-2016, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:20:32-08:00","id":824585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824350#post824350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd go with Eshmaki for the plant monster. The other one is just...wrong. (In a good way mind you) I don't quite get why it's Ugallu though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The fun part about creating a Beast is that you can look at them from a metaphorical concept, instead of a literal one. Remember, they're living nightmares, and nightmares are more heavily influenced by your subconscious than anything else. When I wrote the orphanage lady, I imagined her to be the unfortunate circumstances that swoop in out of nowhere and drop you into a situation you're uncomfortable being in. The children's parents die from tragic, unpredictable accidents. Maybe she caused a few, or maybe it was just bad luck. Either way, the children are scared, confused, and angry, and that's how she feeds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>List of possible accidents:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Car veering off into a ravine while driving at night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rock slide during a hiking trip.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ropes snap while mountain climbing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Falling overboard during a cruise at sea<br /> <br /> <br /> Double homicide, killer didn't leave a trail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-05-2016, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:32:38-08:00","id":824594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824480#post824480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I have a good idea for the Horror of <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823666#post823666&amp;quot;]</a><b>my Namtaru Collector</b>[/URL]. He's pretty much going to be a non-humanoid Grey Alien, but strongly influenced by the more understandable critters of the Cthulhu Mythos (e.g. Mi-Go, Elder Things and Yithians). An air of otherworldly erudition juxtaposed to a repulsive exterior with virtually no familiar expressions of emotion to latch onto. Possibly lamia-shaped, bioluminescent and with several tool-like limbs. But scariest of all: totally clean and wearing actual clothes.<br /> <br /> Does that sound cool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me. I have this image of it having a spare pair of arms that constantly take notes on whatever it's doing to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:31:06-08:00","id":824698,"title":"","content":"<b>Anakim Tyrant:</b> &quot;What's with that look? Did you seriously think this was going to play out like your story books? You just come in here, swinging your magic sword and down goes the monster? I'm centuries old, you stupid son of a bitch, how many heroes do you think have tried that before you? A lot, and they had much better strategies than your Leroy Jenkins impersonation.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Beast hunts the most dangerous prey of all, Heroes. They are the horror that is stark reality, the moment of realization that a Hero is just a man fighting a creature that defies logic and science. It has several human life times worth of experience in battle, and its body surpasses human limitations. What hope does a mere mortal only a few decades old have against such a majestic creature as this? The realization that humans are not on the top of the food chain, that is who the Beast is, feeding on the shattered expectations and dreams of would be Heroes.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's lair is a combination of a trophy room and a mass grave. Each chamber is dedicated to previous Heroes that sought to slay him. Various habitats and scenery littered with skeletal remains. Artifacts and weapons that were to be used against their killer now lay rusted and broken among the corpses. And in the center of the lair, an enormous battlefield, stands the Beast itself. A fell knight clad in demonic armor, waiting for its next challenger. Once the Hero approaches, they find the landscape to be formed out of human corpses piled up to form hills and mountainsides. The amount of blood leaking from them is enough to produce rivers and the sky is tinted orange as raging fires burn in the distance, attempting to clean away the seemingly endless mass of bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-05-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:54:31-08:00","id":824713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824698#post824698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Anakim Tyrant:</b> &quot;What's with that look? Did you seriously think this was going to play out like your story books? You just come in here, swinging your magic sword and down goes the monster? I'm centuries old, you stupid son of a bitch, how many heroes do you think have tried that before you? A lot, and they had much better strategies than your Leroy Jenkins impersonation.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Beast hunts the most dangerous prey of all, Heroes. They are the horror that is stark reality, the moment of realization that a Hero is just a man fighting a creature that defies logic and science. It has several human life times worth of experience in battle, and its body surpasses human limitations. What hope does a mere mortal only a few decades old have against such a majestic creature as this? The realization that humans are not on the top of the food chain, that is who the Beast is, feeding on the shattered expectations and dreams of would be Heroes.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's lair is a combination of a trophy room and a mass grave. Each chamber is dedicated to previous Heroes that sought to slay him. Various habitats and scenery littered with skeletal remains. Artifacts and weapons that were to be used against their killer now lay rusted and broken among the corpses. And in the center of the lair, an enormous battlefield, stands the Beast itself. A fell knight clad in demonic armor, waiting for its next challenger. Once the Hero approaches, they find the landscape to be formed out of human corpses piled up to form hills and mountainsides. The amount of blood leaking from them is enough to produce rivers and the sky is tinted orange as raging fires burn in the distance, attempting to clean away the seemingly endless mass of bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div> Freaking <b><i>metal</i></b>. He sounds more like a Collector + Ravager, though. Most likely an Incarnate as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T18:24:31-08:00","id":824723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824698#post824698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Anakim Tyrant:</b> &quot;What's with that look? Did you seriously think this was going to play out like your story books? You just come in here, swinging your magic sword and down goes the monster? I'm centuries old, you stupid son of a bitch, how many heroes do you think have tried that before you? A lot, and they had much better strategies than your Leroy Jenkins impersonation.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Beast hunts the most dangerous prey of all, Heroes. They are the horror that is stark reality, the moment of realization that a Hero is just a man fighting a creature that defies logic and science. It has several human life times worth of experience in battle, and its body surpasses human limitations. What hope does a mere mortal only a few decades old have against such a majestic creature as this? The realization that humans are not on the top of the food chain, that is who the Beast is, feeding on the shattered expectations and dreams of would be Heroes.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's lair is a combination of a trophy room and a mass grave. Each chamber is dedicated to previous Heroes that sought to slay him. Various habitats and scenery littered with skeletal remains. Artifacts and weapons that were to be used against their killer now lay rusted and broken among the corpses. And in the center of the lair, an enormous battlefield, stands the Beast itself. A fell knight clad in demonic armor, waiting for its next challenger. Once the Hero approaches, they find the landscape to be formed out of human corpses piled up to form hills and mountainsides. The amount of blood leaking from them is enough to produce rivers and the sky is tinted orange as raging fires burn in the distance, attempting to clean away the seemingly endless mass of bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the classic short story, &quot;The Most Dangerous Game&quot;? Your Tyrant reminds me of the antagonist - an expatriate Russian noble looking for the ultimate thrill. Big game hunting got too easy for him (even handicapping himself), so he bought a small tropical island and turned it into his own hunting preserve. To stock it, he helps wreck ships . . . and after patching up the survivors, he hunts them across the island. And he's very, very good at it . . .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T19:04:24-08:00","id":824744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824713#post824713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Freaking <b><i>metal</i></b>. He sounds more like a Collector + Ravager, though. Most likely an Incarnate as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the lair does sound like it would make a good album cover. A 10 foot tall knight looming over a scrawny man wearing office clothes. His toupee is lopsided as he struggles to hold a sword in his shaking hands. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824723#post824723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Have you read the classic short story, &quot;The Most Dangerous Game&quot;? Your Tyrant reminds me of the antagonist - an expatriate Russian noble looking for the ultimate thrill. Big game hunting got too easy for him (even handicapping himself), so he bought a small tropical island and turned it into his own hunting preserve. To stock it, he helps wreck ships . . . and after patching up the survivors, he hunts them across the island. And he's very, very good at it . . .</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I have not read it, but I am familiar with the concept. The idea of a hunter going mad and hunting other humans has become popular enough to be well known. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T19:11:40-08:00","id":824749,"title":"","content":"An idea I've had for the Dark Era is an Eshmaki Predator/Nemesis. More specifically, he targets the various racial-motivated insurgents and terrorist groups that were common in the south at this time, a skulking predator who ambushes from the shadows with eyes like burning coals, reminding his &quot;victims&quot; that there are things far more terrifying than humans with a different level of melanin out there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T08:30:17-08:00","id":824948,"title":"","content":"Today's Beast:<br /> <br /> The Horror is a huge gray owl, the size of a small house. The owl is weird, it almost looks like it's made of marble and ebony, with strange markings on its feathers. It stays calm most of the time, moving clumsily on its claws. When he finds that someone it's not telling the truth, he agitates and suddenly it's not clumsy anymore. In front of you you have a bloodthirsty raptor bird. The spots of the feathers now clearly appear for what they are: grotesque faces that laugh and spit cruel judgements, sometimes about those around and sometimes about past victims or unidentified misgiver.<br /> <br /> The Lair resembles a mixture between a modern tribunal and an amount of buildings from ancient Rome. It's deserted, if not for many bizarre stone statues that seem to move when you don't look at them. In the main halls, every single seat is occupied by this silent public.<br /> <br /> The character works as the sort of sleazy private eye you call to spy on your spouse. He's an Ugallu Predator that hunts the liars and the betrayers. Normally, he just scares them but, sometimes, he takes a finger from them. If they react really bad to being exposed, he takes a hand. Each prey is a new feather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-06-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T10:30:12-08:00","id":824990,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">I'm expecting royalties from anybody who uses my album cover idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Namtaru Nemeses:</b> The Warden, that's what they call her. A Beast who somehow obtained control over a maximum security prison facility. Her lair is a place where criminals go to disappear, a trap made of iron and concrete. Those who obtain a map of the complex or a bird's eye view will notice the prison is built in the shape of a gigantic spider web. In the realm of nightmares, The Warden's soul is a gigantic, iron spider. Her webs are woven from steel threads, cocooning her prey in chains. In the physical world, the inmates seem to lose their will to fight back, their spirits broken from years of incarceration.<br /> <br /> <br /> The truth, however, is much more sinister. While the inmates sleep, The Warden visits their cells in their dreams, sucking the life out of them like the spider that she is. Each time they wake up, they feel a little more empty, until the day when they just stop resisting, a spiritually empty husk of their former selves. A moral person might call it cruel and unusual punishment. But the only thing The Warden cares about is the governor keeps tossing insects into her web like a sadistic child; and to accomplish that, she needs to prove she can &quot;reform&quot; these dangerous criminals.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-06-2016, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T18:26:54-08:00","id":825177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824990#post824990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I'm expecting royalties from anybody who uses my album cover idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Namtaru Nemeses:</b> The Warden, that's what they call her. A Beast who somehow obtained control over a maximum security prison facility. Her lair is a place where criminals go to disappear, a trap made of iron and concrete. Those who obtain a map of the complex or a bird's eye view will notice the prison is built in the shape of a gigantic spider web. In the realm of nightmares, The Warden's soul is a gigantic, iron spider. Her webs are woven from steel threads, cocooning her prey in chains. In the physical world, the inmates seem to lose their will to fight back, their spirits broken from years of incarceration.<br /> <br /> <br /> The truth, however, is much more sinister. While the inmates sleep, The Warden visits their cells in their dreams, sucking the life out of them like the spider that she is. Each time they wake up, they feel a little more empty, until the day when they just stop resisting, a spiritually empty husk of their former selves. A moral person might call it cruel and unusual punishment. But the only thing The Warden cares about is the governor keeps tossing insects into her web like a sadistic child; and to accomplish that, she needs to prove she can &quot;reform&quot; these dangerous criminals.</span></div> </div> </div> </div> Cue one of the prisoners becoming a Hero who leads a rebellion and escape that tarnishes the Warden's reputation. Years later, the Hero has become a crime lord and a more than credible threat to not just Beasts, but to anyone who doesn't give him what he wants.<br /> <br /> By the way, your concept gave me Superjail flashbacks. Does the Iron Spider have a fondness for purple suits and unusual glasses? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T18:33:45-08:00","id":825182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=825177#post825177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Cue one of the prisoners becoming a Hero who leads a rebellion and escape that tarnishes the Warden's reputation. Years later, the Hero has become a crime lord and a more than credible threat to not just Beasts, but to anyone who doesn't give him what he wants.<br /> <br /> By the way, your concept gave me Superjail flashbacks. Does the Iron Spider have a fondness for purple suits and unusual glasses? :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> More like dark sunglasses, bubble gum, and a tendency to put people in &quot;the hole.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T21:14:17-08:00","id":825242,"title":"","content":"<b>Anakim Tyrant:</b> The twins do everything together. At no point has anybody seen them willingly part from each other. They are always within earshot of each other unless circumstances forcefully separate them. They are physically identical too, and they do that creepy shit where they speak in unison or finish each others sentences. Most people who know about the Beasts are probably aware they share the same Lair, but only those who have actually entered it know the truth. The twins don't merely share the same Lair, they share the same Soul. Their horror takes the form of a two headed giant, an Ettin standing 20 feet tall with skin as black as pitch and eyes glowing red.<br /> <br /> Separation causes pain on their soul, and the twins will become incredibly violent in an effort to reunite with each other if they have to. They are the fear of being outnumbered, of having the odds stacked against you. Even the greatest warriors fall when presented with overwhelming numbers. If a Hero comes knocking, they will find not one Giant, but two; and they will have to face them simultaneously!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T12:11:59-08:00","id":825514,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Makara Tyrant:</b> &quot;You can't handle the truth.&quot; &quot;You don't want to do this.&quot; &quot;Beauty is only skin deep.&quot; You have heard all these phrases before, but you never really took them into consideration, never really accepted the weight they carry until now. Until you looked beneath the surface and saw what <i>they</i> don't want you to know. Most people go through their whole lives in blissful denial, they reject what they don't understand and impose their own explanations and rationality upon the world just to keep themselves happy. They never consider that their lover is dangerously unstable until something causes them to snap. They expect their leaders to be the perfect role models and are always shocked when they abuse the power entrusted to them. But worst of all, they think they know everything about how the world works.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mortals who care to look past this facade may claim the universe holds dark mysteries, but this too is a state of denial. The universe has no secrets, it offers knowledge freely to all who seek it. Humanity just doesn't want to seek it, because they're afraid of what they'll find. That is the horror of this Leviathan. It is truth, <i>the real truth</i> that humanity doesn't want to hear. Cold, pitiless and uncensored. It does not apologize, does not make excuses for itself. This is the way the world has always worked and it was <i>your choice</i> to step out of your comfort zone. If you can't handle what you learned, that's your fault, not his!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast preys on those who's sight extends beyond their wisdom, those who want to learn the truth, but haven't prepared themselves for what they'll find. Its soul is a man almost completely obscured by clothing, who's face is hidden in shadow under their hat, glasses and scarf. A trench coat wraps around their body with gloved hands tucked into the pockets, or holding a clue to some obscure mystery. Its Lair is a library overflowing with stacks of books and paper littering the floor. At times, you can't even tell if you're actually walking on the ground level, or if the paper is stacked too high. Most of the text you find here is illegible, written in a script that your mind immediately shuns as being occult or extraterrestrial in origin. But if you search hard enough, you may come across a book, scroll, note or mural that contains information related to what you're seeking.<br /> <br /> And then, when you inevitably start screaming &quot;No, that's not true!&quot; the Beast hears you, and he comes looking for who's causing such a raucous in his library.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-09-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:26:25-08:00","id":826214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=825514#post825514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Namtaru Tyrant:</b> &quot;You can't handle the truth.&quot; &quot;You don't want to do this.&quot; &quot;Beauty is only skin deep.&quot; You have heard all these phrases before, but you never really took them into consideration, never really accepted the weight they carry until now. Until you looked beneath the surface and saw what <i>they</i> don't want you to know. Most people go through their whole lives in blissful denial, they reject what they don't understand and impose their own explanations and rationality upon the world just to keep themselves happy. They never consider that their lover is dangerously unstable until something causes them to snap. They expect their leaders to be the perfect role models and are always shocked when they abuse the power entrusted to them. But worst of all, they think they know everything about how the world works.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mortals who care to look past this facade may claim the universe holds dark mysteries, but this too is a state of denial. The universe has no secrets, it offers knowledge freely to all who seek it. Humanity just doesn't want to seek it, because they're afraid of what they'll find. That is the horror of this Leviathan. It is truth, <i>the real truth</i> that humanity doesn't want to hear. Cold, pitiless and uncensored. It does not apologize, does not make excuses for itself. This is the way the world has always worked and it was <i>your choice</i> to step out of your comfort zone. If you can't handle what you learned, that's your fault, not his!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast preys on those who's sight extends beyond their wisdom, those who want to learn the truth, but haven't prepared themselves for what they'll find. It's soul is a man almost completely obscured by clothing, who's face is hidden in shadow under their hat, glasses and scarf. A trench coat wraps around their body with gloved hands tucked into the pockets, or holding a clue to some obscure mystery. It's Lair is a library overflowing with stacks of books and paper littering the floor. At times, you can't even tell if you're actually walking on the ground level, or if the paper is stacked too high. Most of the text you find here is illegible, written in a script that your mind immediately shuns as being occult or extraterrestrial in origin. But if you search hard enough, you may come across a book, scroll, note or mural that contains information related to what you're seeking.<br /> <br /> And then, when you inevitably start screaming &quot;No, that's not true!&quot; the Beast hears you, and he comes looking for who's causing such a raucous in his library.</span></div> </div> </div> </div> Another great idea. This Beast sounds like he'd be the bane of Mages...or maybe one of their best friends. However, his Hunger should be for Ruin, not Power. Also, &quot;Leviathans&quot; is the nickname for the Makara. The nickname for the Namtaru is &quot;Gorgons&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T14:42:29-08:00","id":826296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=826214#post826214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Another great idea. This Beast sounds like he'd be the bane of Mages...or maybe one of their best friends. However, his Hunger should be for Ruin, not Power. Also, &quot;Leviathans&quot; is the nickname for the Makara. The nickname for the Namtaru is &quot;Gorgons&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Woops, I meant to call him a Makara. And the power he hungers for is supposed to reflect humans limiting their knowledge out of fear and arrogance. When somebody tries to rebel and expose the truth, he moves in to prey on their horrific discovery. I'm trying to create metaphorical incarnations of Beasts. It seems to offer greater creative potential than going by literal examples. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-08-2016, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T14:45:59-08:00","id":826299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=826296#post826296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Woops, I meant to call him a Makara. And the power he hungers for is supposed to reflect humans limiting their knowledge out of fear and arrogance. When somebody tries to rebel and expose the truth, he moves in to prey on their horrific discovery. I'm trying to create metaphorical incarnations of Beasts. It seems to offer greater creative potential than going by literal examples. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So the power that he wields (or seeks to wield) is that of a censor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:08:54-08:00","id":826363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=826299#post826299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the power that he wields (or seeks to wield) is that of a censor?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Exactly. He controls the masses by keeping them ignorant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T22:03:54-08:00","id":826561,"title":"","content":"<b>Namtaru Ravager:</b> If there is one thing humans fear more than the ugly, it is the possibility of joining their ranks. Degenerative illnesses, mutilating accidents, whatever might cause unsightly blemishes or maiming. This Gorgon seeks to destroy the beauty of others, feeding upon the terror of their own hideous visage once his prey discovers what has been done to them. In the world of nightmares, his horror is that of a bloated toad the size of a man, skin covered in bumpy warts and toxic mucus leaking from his pores. A tattered, dirty loin cloth wrapped around their waist belies a sense of intelligence behind the bestial form.<br /> <br /> His lair is an infectious swamp, teaming with diseases and festering insects. Putrid water reaching thigh level attempts to slow down trespassers while dense foliage obscures the view of the sky and causes painful rashes when brushed against the skin. Luminescent gas pockets seek to lure wanderers into traps as they stumble through the swamp in search of light or shelter. And in the heart of this inhospitable environment is a squat hut built into the branches of a gnarled tree, where the Gorgon makes its home!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-09-2016, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T08:57:18-08:00","id":826857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=825514#post825514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Makara Tyrant:</b> &quot;You can't handle the truth.&quot; &quot;You don't want to do this.&quot; &quot;Beauty is only skin deep.&quot; You have heard all these phrases before, but you never really took them into consideration, never really accepted the weight they carry until now. Until you looked beneath the surface and saw what <i>they</i> don't want you to know. Most people go through their whole lives in blissful denial, they reject what they don't understand and impose their own explanations and rationality upon the world just to keep themselves happy. They never consider that their lover is dangerously unstable until something causes them to snap. They expect their leaders to be the perfect role models and are always shocked when they abuse the power entrusted to them. But worst of all, they think they know everything about how the world works.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mortals who care to look past this facade may claim the universe holds dark mysteries, but this too is a state of denial. The universe has no secrets, it offers knowledge freely to all who seek it. Humanity just doesn't want to seek it, because they're afraid of what they'll find. That is the horror of this Leviathan. It is truth, <i>the real truth</i> that humanity doesn't want to hear. Cold, pitiless and uncensored. It does not apologize, does not make excuses for itself. This is the way the world has always worked and it was <i>your choice</i> to step out of your comfort zone. If you can't handle what you learned, that's your fault, not his!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast preys on those who's sight extends beyond their wisdom, those who want to learn the truth, but haven't prepared themselves for what they'll find. It's soul is a man almost completely obscured by clothing, who's face is hidden in shadow under their hat, glasses and scarf. A trench coat wraps around their body with gloved hands tucked into the pockets, or holding a clue to some obscure mystery. It's Lair is a library overflowing with stacks of books and paper littering the floor. At times, you can't even tell if you're actually walking on the ground level, or if the paper is stacked too high. Most of the text you find here is illegible, written in a script that your mind immediately shuns as being occult or extraterrestrial in origin. But if you search hard enough, you may come across a book, scroll, note or mural that contains information related to what you're seeking.<br /> <br /> And then, when you inevitably start screaming &quot;No, that's not true!&quot; the Beast hears you, and he comes looking for who's causing such a raucous in his library.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I came up with a Beast like this once, except that it was a Nemesis that punished those who learnt that which man was not meant to know the Horror was something like a great brass clockwork spider its many legs clicking on the endless shelves. Also, the Beast worked with another one in its Brood, a Collector who collected knowledge,punishing those who violated the hoard of lore. He had a particular hatred for Loremaster Heroes and used any and all means possible to hunt them down. I came up with a Nightmare for him, You Do Not Want To Know. It basically dissuaded someone from further investigating or researching something. We came across a bunch of Mages while playing that game. I had great fun getting perpetually irritated at their constant probings at the defences of the hoard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-09-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:12:42-08:00","id":827519,"title":"","content":"Today's Beast #2:<br /> <br /> We start from the Lair. Imagine an ocean of blood, eerily clear enough to see perfectly through the &quot;water&quot;. The surface is not in sight, even if there's some source of light coming from above, though it's not clear if that's a sun or something else. Everything is distorted by the blood and assumes a red tint. If you go deep enough, you'll start noticing the skeletons of titanical beasts floating inside the gore, the deeper you go, the more you find. With some attention you'll be able to hear a distant beat, like a heart. By following it, you'll eventually get to a seafloor made of bone. Inside its chasms, you'll find the literal Heart of the Lair.<br /> <br /> The Horror resembles a classical siren as much as the creatures from the deepest abyss resemble the fish from above. Slender, vicious and covered in cartilage protrusions, the hairless monstrosity's visage has nothing in common with a human face. No mouth, no nose, just a pair of wide, milky eyes. She usually feed with the lamprey mouths located on her four clawed hands or pierces the body of her victims with the retractable bone proboscis she can grow from her arm and drains the blood.<br /> <br /> The character, a Makara Collector, works as a biologist in a renowed laboratory. She prefers to work alone and it's not the sort of person loved by the colleagues, but no one can deny that the few results she decides to share are often ground-breaking. She hoards vials of blood of people she find interesting or peculiar, no regards of their consent. She is especially fond of blood of other monster and people exposed to the supernatural, but the reason goes beyond her Hunger. You see, by analyzing their blood, the one of Beasts and Heroes more than the others, she's trying to find a trace of the Dark Mother hidden inside it, hoping to find some sort of revelation that will lead her to the Mitochondrial Eve of Fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-10-2016, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T05:49:40-08:00","id":828159,"title":"","content":"<b>Ugallu Collector:</b> While it may not be primordial, mankind does have a compelling fear of the asylum. I mean when's the last time you decided to visit the loony bin just to soak in the atmosphere? If the people aren't drugged into a stupor, they're so delirious as to be unintelligible. But in this habitat of madness, the Beast thrives. Taking the form of a doctor who roams the halls, his mere presence alone prompting the mortals to psychotic episodes.<br /> <br /> His horror is kin to those of the True Fae. He is a Jabberwocky, spreading madness wherever he goes. Men lose their capacity to speak when standing before him, babbling incoherent words and jumble sentences. How could anybody know they're trying desperately to warn you about the fork tongued Dragon with claws like razors, teeth like knives, coated in black scales and descending from the skies to prey upon those who have gone mad at the sight of him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T09:03:26-08:00","id":828250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=828159#post828159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ugallu Collector:</b> While it may not be primordial, mankind does have a compelling fear of the asylum. I mean when's the last time you decided to visit the loony bin just to soak in the atmosphere? If the people aren't drugged into a stupor, they're so delirious as to be unintelligible. But in this habitat of madness, the Beast thrives. Taking the form of a doctor who roams the halls, his mere presence alone prompting the mortals to psychotic episodes.<br /> <br /> His horror is kin to those of the True Fae. He is a Jabberwocky, spreading madness wherever he goes. Men lose their capacity to speak when standing before him, babbling incoherent words and jumble sentences. How could anybody know they're trying desperately to warn you about the fork tongued Dragon with claws like razors, teeth like knives, coated in black scales and descending from the skies to prey upon those who have gone mad at the sight of him?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, I just don't quite see how that's an Ugallu. Seems more Namtaru to me, what with the whole 'go mad at the sight of him' thing. Gave me a good idea for a Nightmare though, You Cannot Warn Them. It basically attacks a person's ability to make themselves understood, whether through speech, writing, semaphore, whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T11:42:14-08:00","id":828329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=547873#post547873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mr.Grey styled Ravager, very likely an Ugallu, who enjoys feeding his Hunger very much on the assorted people he takes back to his 'special place'. He is not fussy on what gender he takes in, though he does Feed from destroying the limits his partners have and he enjoys breaking them whilst he gets gratification from them. He is an Ugallu rather than an Anakim as it's more about making his partners exposed and embarrassed than actually causing them harm or taking their power from them. Holds You Deserve This and You Must Obey as his Nightmares (of course).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just out of curiosity, what would his Horror be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:02:16-08:00","id":828370,"title":"","content":"Ok, here's a really bastardy character.<br /> <br /> Ugallu Predator: He's an angel. Not one of these pathetic milk-and-water angels that people believe in nowadays. No, he's a full on angel of the kind that brought apocalypse to Sodom and Gamorrah with wings and swords of fire. He's the kind of angel that has to say Be Not Afraid. Except he wants people to be afraid. He feeds off of their fear and believes that it is his god-given task to rid the world of heretics and unbelievers. He believes that his kind is Nephilim, humans with the souls of avenging angels, sent to Earth for the purpose of shaping it to the will of the Creator. He hunts down those who decry the one true faith and destroys them. He has to be careful not to overfeed, but believes that God, in his infinite mercy, has given the nephilim this weakness so that sinners may have time to repent. Make no mistake though, if you have not renounced your heretical ways by the time he is ready, you have outworn his patience and God's mercy. He will have no pity for you then.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, let me make this perfectly clear: I am not some kind of screwy religious supremacist. <br /> <br /> To all those sufficiently well-adjusted to not rant at me over this, I'm sorry. It's just that I don't want to risk ironically overzealous atheists ranting at me (for the record, I'm an agnostic as well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:20:01-08:00","id":828384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=828250#post828250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, I just don't quite see how that's an Ugallu. Seems more Namtaru to me, what with the whole 'go mad at the sight of him' thing. Gave me a good idea for a Nightmare though, You Cannot Warn Them. It basically attacks a person's ability to make themselves understood, whether through speech, writing, semaphore, whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Deciding his family was tough. My first thought was Makara because I was imagining Alice in Wonder Land falling down the rabbit hole. But then most illustrations of the Jabberwocky I've seen have possessed wings, and have bodies that resemble demons or dragons, so I thought Ugallu, since they're supposed to be the flying types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:26:50-08:00","id":828389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=828384#post828384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Deciding his family was tough. My first thought was Makara because I was imagining Alice in Wonder Land falling down the rabbit hole. But then most illustrations of the Jabberwocky I've seen have possessed wings, and have bodies that resemble demons or dragons, so I thought Ugallu, since they're supposed to be the flying types.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess so. It was just that the 'madness' part of his fear seemed more essential than the flight. That might just be me though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:28:40-08:00","id":828391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=828370#post828370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, let me make this perfectly clear: I am not some kind of screwy religious supremacist.<br /> <br /> To all those sufficiently well-adjusted to not rant at me over this, I'm sorry. It's just that I don't want to risk ironically overzealous atheists ranting at me (for the record, I'm an agnostic as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ok, ajf. Making EVIL characters is part of fun and a guilty pleasure we all indulge in from time to time. You have to get their point of view to write them but I'm confident nobody around here will mistake writing a character's mentality for supporting such mentality as well.<br /> <br /> That Ugallu is a nasty piece of work, but we're cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:29:27-08:00","id":828393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=825514#post825514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Makara Tyrant:</b> &amp;quot;You can't handle the truth.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;You don't want to do this.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Beauty is only skin deep.&amp;quot; You have heard all these phrases before, but you never really took them into consideration, never really accepted the weight they carry until now. Until you looked beneath the surface and saw what <i>they</i> don't want you to know. Most people go through their whole lives in blissful denial, they reject what they don't understand and impose their own explanations and rationality upon the world just to keep themselves happy. They never consider that their lover is dangerously unstable until something causes them to snap. They expect their leaders to be the perfect role models and are always shocked when they abuse the power entrusted to them. But worst of all, they think they know everything about how the world works.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mortals who care to look past this facade may claim the universe holds dark mysteries, but this too is a state of denial. The universe has no secrets, it offers knowledge freely to all who seek it. Humanity just doesn't want to seek it, because they're afraid of what they'll find. That is the horror of this Leviathan. It is truth, <i>the real truth</i> that humanity doesn't want to hear. Cold, pitiless and uncensored. It does not apologize, does not make excuses for itself. This is the way the world has always worked and it was <i>your choice</i> to step out of your comfort zone. If you can't handle what you learned, that's your fault, not his!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast preys on those who's sight extends beyond their wisdom, those who want to learn the truth, but haven't prepared themselves for what they'll find. Its soul is a man almost completely obscured by clothing, who's face is hidden in shadow under their hat, glasses and scarf. A trench coat wraps around their body with gloved hands tucked into the pockets, or holding a clue to some obscure mystery. Its Lair is a library overflowing with stacks of books and paper littering the floor. At times, you can't even tell if you're actually walking on the ground level, or if the paper is stacked too high. Most of the text you find here is illegible, written in a script that your mind immediately shuns as being occult or extraterrestrial in origin. But if you search hard enough, you may come across a book, scroll, note or mural that contains information related to what you're seeking.<br /> <br /> And then, when you inevitably start screaming &amp;quot;No, that's not true!&amp;quot; the Beast hears you, and he comes looking for who's causing such a raucous in his library.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it, you could make this one similar to the Gate of Truth and the Gatekeeper from Fullmetal Alchemist Brotherhood. The feel of it is similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:34:30-08:00","id":828405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=828391#post828391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's ok, ajf. Making EVIL characters is part of fun and a guilty pleasure we all indulge in from time to time. You have to get their point of view to write them but I'm confident nobody around here will mistake writing a character's mentality for supporting such mentality as well.<br /> <br /> That Ugallu is a nasty piece of work, but we're cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know, it's just that I've had more than enough people overreacting to things that I've written before (I once wrote an essay-ish thing on technological singularity and how it's not necessarily a bad thing and was accused of being a nihilist trying to bring about the apocalypse) that I don't want it to happen again if at all possible. I find that a lot of people seem to be willing to abandon sensible logic when it comes to matters of faith (especially when dealing with the Abrahamic god).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:40:38-08:00","id":828412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=828405#post828405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, it's just that I've had more than enough people overreacting to things that I've written before (I once wrote an essay-ish thing on technological singularity and how it's not necessarily a bad thing and was accused of being a nihilist trying to bring about the apocalypse) that I don't want it to happen again if at all possible. I find that a lot of people seem to be willing to abandon sensible logic when it comes to matters of faith (especially when dealing with the Abrahamic god).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know the feeling. I tend to write antagonists more often than not and I'm always afraid to cross a line and offend someone. Given your past experiences, I can see why you were a bit worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:18:18-08:00","id":828461,"title":"","content":"Same here. I prefer playing the villain because there's always more freedom in doing so. Protagonists are bogged down by too many rules and expectations, yet it's hard to tell what is and isn't acceptable from a villain in between stories.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:28:32-08:00","id":828884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=824255#post824255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Eshmaki Predator:</b> Plants are supposed to sit quietly and look pretty. Their sweet aroma is supposed to be alluring, not an airborne narcotic. Their vines aren't supposed to reach for you like prehensile limbs. They're supposed to drink water, not blood. And they damn sure aren't supposed to be lounge singers at the local gentleman's club!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just had an awesome thought.<br /> <br /> Seymore is their physical form while the plant is their soul. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5ea5jKFGgUw\" data-code=\"5ea5jKFGgUw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5ea5jKFGgUw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T16:31:42-08:00","id":829013,"title":"","content":"My only problem with the angel is that it strikes me as more Anakim than Ugallu. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T00:01:55-08:00","id":829155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=829013#post829013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only problem with the angel is that it strikes me as more Anakim than Ugallu. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. I was trying to concentrate on the 'you cannot escape' thing but it might not be too clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T08:05:08-08:00","id":829251,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I was thinking of it as being overwhelmed by the power of the divine, making the victims feel like less than insects by comparison. I suppose either works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T15:03:45-08:00","id":829424,"title":"","content":"Anybody wanna try turning Undertale monsters into Beast parodies? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T16:07:58-08:00","id":829453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=829424#post829424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody wanna try turning Undertale monsters into Beast parodies? <