"> Sans (Eshmaki?), Undyne (Anakim?), Flowey (Eshmaki?), Asriel Dreemurr (Namtaru?), Chara (Hero?), </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T21:07:24-08:00","id":829556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=829539#post829539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. And honestly, the game's exploded all over the internet, so I don't think they classify as spoilers anymore. The game has been around long enough for people to get sick of seeing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game has been out for less than five months at the time of this writing. Me nearly spoiling Persona 3 for a friend six and a half years after its release is close enough to the general statute of limitations that I think of that as a gray area, but <i>less than half a year</i> is an absurdly low threshold for &quot;not a spoiler anymore,&quot; runaway popularity or no runaway popularity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Sans (Eshmaki?), Undyne (Anakim?), Flowey (Eshmaki?), Asriel Dreemurr (Namtaru?), Chara (Hero?), </div></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div>I think I can conclusively say I no longer have any idea what your notion of &quot;parody&quot; is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-14-2016, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T21:41:35-08:00","id":829574,"title":"","content":"It's only been that long? I thought with the people on the internet requesting the fandom to die off that it had been around for much longer. Plus there are like tons of blogs /tumblrs / webcomics who pretty much give away the ending.<br /> <br /> As for the parody, I meant create Beasts who are inspired by such characters, rather than a carbon copy of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, going to clarify why I think <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Asriel Dreemurr </div></div> </div> </div> is a Namtaru.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> the Namtaru are about making people feel strong reactions. I would say heart ache, pity and guilt certainly classifies. As for being a Gorgon, he kind of blasts your retinas with shimmering rainbows and exploding stars! </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T08:47:41-08:00","id":830255,"title":"","content":"What Family and Hunger do you think a Beast based off of the Reapers from the Mass Effect series would be? I was thinking either Anakim or Makara for family and either Ruin or Power for hunger? What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T10:48:01-08:00","id":830315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=830255#post830255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Family and Hunger do you think a Beast based off of the Reapers from the Mass Effect series would be? I was thinking either Anakim or Makara for family and either Ruin or Power for hunger? What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anakim for sure. They strike some Makara vibes but they're all about hopelessness and overwhelming force.<br /> <br /> For Hunger, I'd go for Ruin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:12:31-08:00","id":830448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=830315#post830315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anakim for sure. They strike some Makara vibes but they're all about hopelessness and overwhelming force.<br /> <br /> For Hunger, I'd go for Ruin.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would a Beast with that Horror feed do you think? Come to think of it, what atavisms would they have? Unbreakable for sure. You could certainly justify Mimir's Wisdom and Dragonfire (their ancient knowledge and laser cannons respectively)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T13:34:10-08:00","id":830474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=830448#post830448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would a Beast with that Horror feed do you think? Come to think of it, what atavisms would they have? Unbreakable for sure. You could certainly justify Mimir's Wisdom and Dragonfire (their ancient knowledge and laser cannons respectively)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a hard one. Ruin for hubris? Destroying what you think has gone too far? Saving people from themselves by destroying what you believe they won't be able to handle? Considering the sort of science and occult knowledge that there's in the CoD, there's potential for that, but I guess you could extend it to other things.<br /> <br /> Now that I think of it, there's some support for Hunger for Punishment as well.<br /> <br /> The Atavisms work well, but I'd also add Eye of Heaven and Siren Treacherous Song to represent mind reading and Indoctrination, and Looming Presence and Titanic Blow for, well, being colossal robots that destroy everything in their path.<br /> <br /> For Nightmares, Behold My True Form!, Everything You Do Is Worthless, Run Away and You Must Obey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T01:01:26-08:00","id":830887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=830474#post830474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a hard one. Ruin for hubris? Destroying what you think has gone too far? Saving people from themselves by destroying what you believe they won't be able to handle? Considering the sort of science and occult knowledge that there's in the CoD, there's potential for that, but I guess you could extend it to other things.<br /> <br /> Now that I think of it, there's some support for Hunger for Punishment as well.<br /> <br /> The Atavisms work well, but I'd also add Eye of Heaven and Siren Treacherous Song to represent mind reading and Indoctrination, and Looming Presence and Titanic Blow for, well, being colossal robots that destroy everything in their path.<br /> <br /> For Nightmares, Behold My True Form!, Everything You Do Is Worthless, Run Away and You Must Obey.</div> </div> </div> </div>With that kind of hunger they'd be a mage's nightmare. Literally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T06:26:31-08:00","id":831699,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Namtaru Collector: </b>Beggar, vagabond, nomad, weirdo, freak, so many names humans call him. The Beast can be seen wandering into the streets asking for handouts and tends to stick around until he is satisfied. Eventually the people have little choice but to either give him what he wants or forcefully eject him from the premises (if they can). This Beast is the ugliness that can be bribed to leave you alone. Whether it's protection money or alms, he is content to go about his merry way once he gets what he's looking for. Those who prove themselves stingy or uncharitable will find the ugly vagrant lingering around the area fouling up the atmosphere. Even if he's chased off, he keeps coming back; the bane of security guards everywhere!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Namtaru's soul is a hideous, plague stricken man who's body has withered from starvation and who's skin is covered in unsightly blemishes. They are dressed in filthy, tattered rags with shaggy, unkempt hair. Their nails and teeth are discolored with grime and they walk with a hunched gait from malnutrition. But heroes should not underestimate this Gorgon, for those nails can quickly extend into filthy claws with teeth capable of noxious bites if they feel you need to learn some humility!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's lair is a seemingly endless maze of street gutters and back alleyways with garbage cans almost every 20 feet. Travelers will find barely any food to sustain them, forced to dig through the garbage for scraps and eating whatever they can get their desperate hands on. It is a place that drives others to desperation, throwing themselves upon the mercy of others to save them from their suffering. Yet somehow, the Beast finds this despondent place comfortable enough to call it home.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-17-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T13:33:14-08:00","id":834000,"title":"","content":"? Predator: His Horror is a trickster and a deceiver. Its true form is that of a many-tailed fox but that is rarely the face that others see. The creature is a shape-shifter, capable of wearing faces and identities like masks and of abandoning them just as easily. He preys upon trust and teaches caution, targeting the naive and those who trust too easily.<br /> He uses his shape-shifting to take on forms that are easy to trust and uses them to lure his prey into situations in which he could take advantage of or harm them. He never does, no matter how his Horror pleads (he considers himself above that). He makes sure that they know he could though He always gives them a token or some kind of momento, to make sure that they remember the price of naivety in this cruel world of ours.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what family he should be though. Perhaps Eshmaki or Makara.<br /> <br /> For Atavisms I'd probably give him Alien Allure and Ten Thousand Faces (a homebrew Atavism by yours truly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T15:36:34-08:00","id":834090,"title":"","content":"Namtaru ?: A beast that feeds by indulging in the things that people condemn as immoral and wrong for no reason other than tradition and dogma. I.e. homosexuality, reading porn in public (why hello there Kakashi) etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T18:26:39-08:00","id":834173,"title":"","content":"I was reading about older portrayals of dragons in <a href=\"http://www.bogleech.com/dragons.html\" target=\"_blank\"><b>one of Bogleech's articles</b></a> (may Nurgle bless him), and I got such strong Namtaru vibes that multiple connections came to me in quick succession.<br /> <br /> The members of the Ordo Dracul are called Dragons, and their mission is to remove the weaknesses of the vampiric condition. Their mythical founder, Dracula, supposedly became a vampire as a direct curse from God, not an Embrace. The Ordo seeks knowledge both scientific and occult to benefit from this curse in explicit defiance of God's will.<br /> <br /> Dragons are also mentioned as being part of Atlantean symbolism, at least in the first edition of Mage. The Awakened are too often vainglorious and haughty, thinking of themselves as gods, explicitly or not. The Mastigos in particular use many demonic symbols in their Imagos and elsewhere (or daemonic, rather).<br /> <br /> One of the Catalysts in Genius: The Transgression, the Neids, become Inspired due to spite and scorn. In their section, the following is said about them:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In previous centuries, Neids were strongly associated with the demons of selfishness and envy. They were Satan the Dragon, and also linked with reinterpreted Norse myths of Loki or the drakes who guarded treasures. Catholic theologians classifying Leviathan as the demon of envy sealed the connections between Neids and Satanic, draconic forces, and Neids have ever since been referred to as Wyrms\u2015behind their backs, of course. </div> </div> </div>Satan is evil and a deceiver who leads mankind to sin in the Abrahamic religions, whether he is a fallen angel, djinn or something else. However, Satanism and its sub-divisions often associate him with virtues such as independence and wisdom. Depending on who you ask, this character can represent a lot of things, and how much he enjoys his job varies, as does his skill and plans for retirement.<br /> <br /> All of this got me thinking: wouldn't it be cool if there was an ancient Namtaru Nemesis + Ravager whose Horror was a great dragon, majestic to some and rotten to others? He would be an Incarnate with maxed out Lair and epic stats all around, but he doesn't confirm nor deny his origins. His current identity might be a prosecutor or something similar. He's a respected member of the community, but rumors of him abound. As overwhelming as his presence is, he's disarmingly human: if you see him, he's probably reading the newspaper while sitting on a bench in the local park, giving lectures and presentations on matters of how to improve the judicial system, or even going to church.<br /> <br /> However, this Beast takes the teaching of wisdom through suffering very, <b>very </b>seriously. I'm just having trouble imagining how he can feed his dual Hunger in a way that lives up to his archetype. I'm trying to go for something different from the visuals of the celestial rebel or man of wealth and taste. A more down to earth deceiver who has broadened his view of human nature over the years, but still wields incalculable power and knowledge. His best friend may be someone who managed to learn something from him and became a paragon among his peers, like a Mastigos with Wisdom 10, for example.<br /> <br /> Could anyone please help me flesh out this concept? I will try my best to clarify anything that might have confused you or sounded too vague.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-20-2016, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T20:17:59-08:00","id":834217,"title":"","content":"<b>Anakim Collector:</b> Since ancient times, mankind has told stories of its people vanishing into the night without a trace. Snatched up by some monster who found them in a moment of weakness. Some Begotten continue to hunt in this way, but one in particular has discovered a way to profit from it! A member of the human trafficking ring, the Beast abducts humans at night and sells them overseas, likely never to be heard from again. The fear of his prisoners sustains him, while the money he makes goes towards funding other endeavors, such as helping the Family!<br /> <br /> The Beast's true form is an enormous ogre with dark purple skin, snow white hair and wicked fangs. Standing nearly 13 feet tall and weighing 4 tons of muscle, the obese creature is garbed in lavish jewels and fine dress, all of which is paid for by his illicit business practices. He wears a robe made of white tiger pelt, though it is difficult to imagine what manner of beast produced the hide necessary to fit him.<br /> <br /> His lair is a decadent palace with marble floors, golden pillars and red carpets. The heart of the lair is the Beast's throne room, where he receives visitors. Servants patrol the halls, catering to the demands of their Anakim master. At times, he has been known to let his relatives use them as well, especially if it is part of a business arrangement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-20-2016, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T20:36:32-08:00","id":834229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=834000#post834000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">? Predator: His Horror is a trickster and a deceiver. Its true form is that of a many-tailed fox but that is rarely the face that others see. The creature is a shape-shifter, capable of wearing faces and identities like masks and of abandoning them just as easily. He preys upon trust and teaches caution, targeting the naive and those who trust too easily.<br /> He uses his shape-shifting to take on forms that are easy to trust and uses them to lure his prey into situations in which he could take advantage of or harm them. He never does, no matter how his Horror pleads (he considers himself above that). He makes sure that they know he could though He always gives them a token or some kind of momento, to make sure that they remember the price of naivety in this cruel world of ours.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what family he should be though. Perhaps Eshmaki or Makara.<br /> <br /> For Atavisms I'd probably give him Alien Allure and Ten Thousand Faces (a homebrew Atavism by yours truly).</div> </div> </div> </div> I remember that Satchel once said the kitsunes, kumihos and other mischievous fox spirits with illusion powers would be Eshmaki. The fae as a whole are similar to the Eshmaki, as they are known for being tricksters of one type or another. Also, where did you post that Ten Thousand Faces Atavism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-21-2016, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T20:47:26-08:00","id":834234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=834173#post834173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of this got me thinking: wouldn't it be cool if there was an ancient Namtaru Nemesis + Ravager whose Horror was a great dragon, majestic to some and rotten to others? He would be an Incarnate with maxed out Lair and epic stats all around, but he doesn't confirm nor deny his origins. His current identity might be a prosecutor or something similar. He's a respected member of the community, but rumors of him abound. As overwhelming as his presence is, he's disarmingly human: if you see him, he's probably reading the newspaper while sitting on a bench in the local park, giving lectures and presentations on matters of how to improve the judicial system, or even going to church.<br /> <br /> However, this Beast takes the teaching of wisdom through suffering very, <b>very </b>seriously. The problem is that I'm having trouble imagining how he can feed his dual Hunger in a way that lives up to his archetype. I'm trying to go for something different from the visuals of the celestial rebel or man of wealth and taste. A more down to earth deceiver who has broadened his view of human nature over the years, but still wields incalculable power and knowledge. His best friend may be someone who managed to learn something from him and became a paragon among his peers, like a Mastigos with Wisdom 10, for example.<br /> <br /> Could anyone help me flesh out this concept? I will try my best to clarify anything that might have confused you or sounded too vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should see <b>Witchblade</b> TV series and his main villian, <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/kenneth-irons/4005-43915/\" target=\"_blank\">Kenneth Irons</a> - he is almost exactly what you looking for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T22:48:44-08:00","id":834277,"title":"","content":"<b>Eshmaki Nemesis:</b> In the primitive days of mankind, humanity was terrified of outside threats bringing about their demise. But over the course of history, mortals became more and more powerful, to the point where a single human with a button poses more threat to the entire world than some of the most ancient creatures in history. This Beast has capitalized on that fear, becoming a personification of mankind's hubristic need to grab power.<br /> <br /> The Beast's horror is a reflection of what modern warfare may eventually become if it does not learn to reign in its thirst for power. A cybernetic super soldier who's augmented eyes glow brightly in the dark. Its sleek body armor hugging to its body like a second skin, providing freedom of movement as well as protection! The electronic voice it speaks in further enhances the intimidation value, as do the retractable blades that emerge from its forearms!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's lair is a dystopian city sacked by the ravages of war. Neon signs flicker on corner streets, advertising stores long since abandoned. There are no looters in the streets, anybody stupid enough to have remained in the city at the time of the attack are dead, their charred skeletons having been strewn about the city clinging to family members or whatever belongings they felt were more valuable than their lives.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Eshmaki feeds on those who crave more power than they need, usually those who are on top of the social ladder. Scientists, politicians, military officers, government contractors, anybody who has the potential to bring destruction to society. When it catches them, it shows them that there are some advancements mankind isn't ready for...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T00:13:46-08:00","id":834303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=834229#post834229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I remember that Satchel once said the kitsunes, kumihos and other mischievous fox spirits with illusion powers would be Eshmaki. The fae as a whole are similar to the Eshmaki, as they are known for being tricksters of one type or another. Also, where did you post that Ten Thousand Faces Atavism?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on the Other Atavism Ideas? thread, page three, most of the way down. The Satiety expenditure power has been called too powerful though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T01:11:26-08:00","id":834323,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Anakim Predator:</b></u> Her Horror is a thing of the cold. Appears as a human corpse mummified by the frigid temperatures of its lair so as to be androgynous. Its skin is frozen onto its bones and is harder than iron, its grip unbreakable. Its flesh is a pale, icy blue-white, the only splash of colour the dried blood around its mouth.<br /> <br /> The Beast works as a guide for hikers in the wilderness near where she lives. She's a good guide, making sure that they know all the dangers of the forests. She sees them safely to the next way station and sends them on their way. When she gets hungry, though, she doesn't leave. She stalks the group when they go into the wilderness again. She separates one from the group and drives them out on their own. Then she calls down the cold, letting it creep into their bones and flesh until they can go on no longer. And then she comes to them when they're on the edge of unconsciousness and tells them exactly what they did wrong. Or, if she's especially hungry, she opens a path to her lair and lets the cold and the Wendigo take them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-21-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T04:12:47-08:00","id":834350,"title":"","content":"<b>Ugallu Nemesis:</b> His Horror is a colossal bird, aquiline in appearance. Its feathers are harder and sharper than any mundane sword, its eyes are like mirrors, and its gleaming beak and talons are strong enough to rend apart steel. To those well versed in Filipino mythology, the Minokawa immediately comes to mind. But where that creature sought to devour the sun and moon, time and time again, the Raptor keeps his attention on the rest of his Kin.<br /> <br /> The Raptor is old, older than he appears, and he is one of the very few who have become a Beast Incarnate. Even before his Inheritance, he involved himself heavily with the other supernaturals of his city, stepping in whenever anyone (or anything) threatened the status quo. Now, as the Apex, he is one of the most prominent powers in this side of the World of Darkness. And while his Kinship with a number of other supernaturals often keeps him Sated, he has no problem feeding his Hunger for Punishment on whoever tries to threaten the long upheld accord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T08:59:52-08:00","id":834452,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Anakim Tyrant:</b></u> He's a detective, or a consultant at least. He's called in for the cases that no-one can solve, the ones where there's no motive, possible connections to the victim or no possible way that they could have been killed like that in that place. And he solves them Without fail, no matter how impossible, he always solves them. With some, he just looks at the crime scene and says that he did it and when they double-check, there's a connection. With others, he has to spend a little longer but he always gets them in the end.<br /> His Horror is a creature of absolute precision, silver wires and crystal circuitry powering an intellect beyond any human's. It can calculate both the future and the past, predicting the movements of its prey and extrapolating probabilities from the available data. When it leaves its silvered nest to walk free it is a terrifying opponent. No matter what you try, it knows what you'll do even before you and has a thousand counters for every possible move you could make. It is the fear of redundancy, of being made inadequate and worthless.<br /> And when the self-styled 'Hero' that came to kill it lies bleeding at its feet while it has not even a single wound upon it, it bends down and whispers in his ear.<br /> &quot;You are unnecessary.&quot;<br /> <br /> Inspired by L from Death Note.<br /> <br /> By the way, who keeps liking this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-22-2016, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T08:09:28-08:00","id":835058,"title":"","content":"<b>Ugallu Collector: </b>A complete scam artist, that's what he is! Making shady deals and offering miracle cures to people's problems. He's written 7 self help books, and the idiots are too blind to realize they're practically the same advice! The ignorant masses turn to him in desperation for a quick solution to their problems, while he rakes in their hard earned money.<br /> <br /> <br /> His horror is a majestic dragon with scales of gold and silver, encrusted with many fine gemstones including rubies, sapphires, emeralds and topazes. A truly beautiful creature who says that you can be just like him if you'll simply buy his latest product or read his book. Most people are too attracted to the silver tongue to realize there's a fork at the tip!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He doesn't trust banks, it's too easy to track his financial records that way. Instead, he hoards his money inside his lair. Piling stacks of cash high to the ceiling. If he needs to buy something, he just scoops some off the floor and goes back to the physical world. Like the dragons of old, his horror sleeps atop a pile of money when it is satiated. He's never been been forced to pay restitution, because they never found his money. What's the IRS going to do, send a collection service into people's dreams?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T08:16:38-08:00","id":835066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=835058#post835058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ugallu Collector: </b>A complete scam artist, that's what he is! Making shady deals and offering miracle cures to people's problems. He's written 7 self-help books, and the idiots are too blind to realize they're practically the same advice! The ignorant masses turn to him in desperation for a quick solution to their problems, while he rakes in their hard earned money.<br /> <br /> <br /> His horror is a majestic dragon with scales of gold and silver, encrusted with many fine gemstones including rubies, sapphires, emeralds and topazes. A truly beautiful creature who says that you can be just like him if you'll simply buy his latest product or read his book. Most people are too attracted to the silver tongue to realize there's a fork at the tip!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He doesn't trust banks, it's too easy to track his financial records that way. Instead, he hoards his money inside his lair. Piling stacks of cash high to the ceiling. If he needs to buy something, he just scoops some off the floor and goes back to the physical world. Like the dragons of old, his horror sleeps atop a pile of money when it is satiated. He's never been been forced to pay restitution, because they never found his money. What's the IRS going to do, send a collection service into people's dreams?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's always nice to read about a monster that can make me laugh. Here's a brand spanking new, straight-off-the-shelf like for you. <br /> <br /> What Atavisms would he have? I'm imagining Alien Allure, Siren's Treacherous Song and Eye of Heaven. Wondrous for sure as a Lair Trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-22-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T08:25:30-08:00","id":835070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=829453#post829453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, there's only really one or two characters that come to mind as an actual fit, and they're both spoilers.</div> </div> </div> </div> The two characters that seem Beast-like to me are the following. Spoiler box for good measure.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> The first is Undyne. She's an Anakim Predator, as Leliel pointed out in another thread. She feeds her Hunger by chasing intruders and being a demanding captain all around. The way she chases you while throwing dozens of spears is just like the Looming Presence Atavism, and she suplexes boulders with Cyclopean Strength. Even when she's trying her damn best to be friendly and welcoming, she still has mood swings and acts in a threatening manner.<br /> <br /> The second is Chara. He/she is an Anakim Ravager whose only goal is to destroy everything and everyone you love, with your help. By the end of the Genocide Route, he/she has become an Incarnate. Check out the <b><a href=\"https://youtu.be/10y7Kmyq_YM\" target=\"_blank\"> top comment on this video.</a></b> It perfectly describes why Chara is no longer human, or even an enemy to be defeated.<br /> <br /> Frisk is absolutely not a Hero. He/she is closer to a 2ED Fey-Touched, since he/she gains power by refusing to abandon a lost friend. You could say that Chara is Frisk's Horror, but if that was the case, how would Frisk feed his/her Hunger for Ruin in a Pacifist way? I believe it would make more sense if Frisk was a Sin-Eater, and Chara was the Geist. Frisk &quot;eats the sins&quot; of Flowey/Asriel by believing in him and forgiving him. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-22-2016, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T09:43:01-08:00","id":835116,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> There's also Sans who's an Eshmaki Nemeses. He kind of just follows you through the story, observing your actions and then shows up at the end to judge you for them. If you've been a sadistic little shit, he proceeds to punish you with karmic retribution. And he's really, really hard. Probably feeding on your fear of not being able to finish the adventure and see the ending.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T13:16:01-08:00","id":835981,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Eshmaki Ravager:</b></u> She works for the local Mafia as an enforcer. Not some thuggish legbreaker who goes around beating up shop owners who don't pay up. No, her targets are the rich ones, the people who think they're safe in their glass towers and hiding behind their money. She shows them that no matter how you hide yourself, debts always come back to you.<br /> The first time they don't pay, she just gets into their penthouse, sometimes by climbing the outside, sometimes taking the inside, and leaves them a message to remind them. The second time, she uses them to send a message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-23-2016, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T17:28:08-08:00","id":836119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=835981#post835981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Eshmaki Ravager:</b></u> She works for the local Mafia as an enforcer. Not some thuggish legbreaker who goes around beating up shop owners who don't pay up. No, her targets are the rich ones, the people who think they're safe in their glass towers and hiding behind their money. She shows them that no matter how you hide yourself, debts always come back to you.<br /> The first time they don't pay, she just gets into their penthouse, sometimes by climbing the outside, sometimes taking the inside, and leaves them a message to remind them. The second time, she uses them to send a message.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm imagining her Horror to be kinda like a shinobi, but with many spidery limbs to climb walls and wield many daggers. On its back is a massive treasure chest or similar receptacle of wealth, which does not impede the Horror's silent movement in any way. However, the treasure chest often has a golden necklace, intestine or similar memento dangling from its toothy maw.<br /> <br /> The Lair is a dark, labyrinthine forest slashed through with roads that lead to dead ends, traps and final warnings to pay up. No clothes, technology or magic can keep the unrelenting cold away. Apparently well-kept and safe shacks sprout from the undergrowth here and there. The flickering shadows, twisted footprints and heavy breathing of shapeless predators guide intruders and the indebted towards the shacks. This is a place of starvation, confusion, paranoia and betrayal, the nightmare of sacred hospitality being defiled for the sake of one coin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-23-2016, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T17:54:46-08:00","id":836123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=835116#post835116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> There's also Sans who's an Eshmaki Nemeses. He kind of just follows you through the story, observing your actions and then shows up at the end to judge you for them. If you've been a sadistic little shit, he proceeds to punish you with karmic retribution. And he's really, really hard. Probably feeding on your fear of not being able to finish the adventure and see the ending.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> I have to disagree. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm pretty sure his judgement and possible retribution is a one-time burst of motivation for an otherwise lazy person. Where else does he punish people? Could pranks be considered a low Satiety way of punishing stupidity and/or selfishness? Besides, what would his Horror and Lair be? A scarier skeleton and the icy woods, respectively? I, for one, agree with Leliel that Sans and Papyrus are probably Sin-Eaters. Sans' Geist is W.D. Gaster, and Papyrus' Geist is Gaster's wife. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I got that idea by watching </span></span></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rcmi_Z7Sxks\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this &quot;ask the characters&quot; blog with voice overs,</b></a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> which claims that River Person was actually Gaster's wife in disguise.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T20:57:33-08:00","id":836218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=836123#post836123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have to disagree.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm pretty sure his judgement and possible retribution is a one-time burst of motivation for an otherwise lazy person. Where else does he punish people? Could pranks be considered a low Satiety way of punishing stupidity and/or selfishness? Besides, what would his Horror and Lair be? A scarier skeleton and the icy woods, respectively? I, for one, agree with Leliel that Sans and Papyrus are probably Sin-Eaters. Sans' Geist is W.D. Gaster, and Papyrus' Geist is Gaster's wife. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I got that idea by watching </span></span></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rcmi_Z7Sxks\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this &quot;ask the characters&quot; blog with voice overs,</b></a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> which claims that River Person was actually Gaster's wife in disguise.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm, yeah, I guess that makes sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-24-2016, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T23:50:21-08:00","id":836278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=836119#post836119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm imagining her Horror to be kinda like a shinobi, but with many spidery limbs to climb walls and wield many daggers. On its back is a massive treasure chest or similar receptacle of wealth, which does not impede the Horror's silent movement in any way. However, the treasure chest often has a golden necklace, intestine or similar memento dangling from its toothy maw.<br /> <br /> The Lair is a dark, labyrinthine forest slashed through with roads that lead to dead ends, traps and final warnings to pay up. No clothes, technology or magic can keep the unrelenting cold away. Apparently well-kept and safe shacks sprout from the undergrowth here and there. The flickering shadows, twisted footprints and heavy breathing of shapeless predators guide intruders and the indebted towards the shacks. This is a place of starvation, confusion, paranoia and betrayal, the nightmare of sacred hospitality being defiled for the sake of one coin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagibed it as very spidery as well, and the Lair is v<i>ery </i>thematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T10:01:27-08:00","id":836502,"title":"","content":"Aww, now I wish I had thought of this one earlier. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Eshmaki Ravager:</b> Ask yourself, what is it that you want most in this world? Then ask yourself what you are willing to give up to obtain it. Would you quit your job, distance your friends, give up your life savings? Or would you just keep giving things until you had nothing left? This Beast is the fear of sacrifice, it is the glittering prize that waits at the end of a long road of self destruction and misery. By the time you finally get your hands on the prize, you finally realize that you gave up everything important to you in order to get it. There is nobody to share the spoils with, leaving you a broken, lonely individual with nothing but a shiny bauble to keep you company.<br /> <br /> The Beast's horror is an honest to god Mimic. When at rest, it looks like an enormous treasure chest filled with gold and jewels. But when it senses prey and rouses itself, it transforms into a hideous creature. Retractable teeth sprout from the chest's rim and the treasure is immediately swallowed to reveal its insides are a writhing mass of slimy tentacles. Arms and legs burst out from the sides of the box as it skitters towards its unwary victim. The prey was so focused on the treasure, it failed to recognize the trap, and now it will feed the Beast for the night!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's Lair is a dungeon filled with traps and puzzles that wanderers must overcome before heading deeper. Along the way, they are teased with glimpses of wealth or power at the end. Just enough to keep them moving onward. Maybe they lose some people or supplies along the way, but the reward at the end will be worth it. When they finally reach the end, however, they usually don't have enough supplies to make a return trip, assuming they even survive the Beast's attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-24-2016, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T17:49:05-08:00","id":836765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=836502#post836502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, now I wish I had thought of this one earlier. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Eshmaki Ravager:</b> Ask yourself, what is it that you want most in this world? Then ask yourself what you are willing to give up to obtain it. Would you quit your job, distance your friends, give up your life savings? Or would you just keep giving things until you had nothing left? This Beast is the fear of sacrifice, it is the glittering prize that waits at the end of a long road of self destruction and misery. By the time you finally get your hands on the prize, you finally realize that you gave up everything important to you in order to get it. There is nobody to share the spoils with, leaving you a broken, lonely individual with nothing but a shiny bauble to keep you company.<br /> <br /> The Beast's horror is an honest to god Mimic. When at rest, it looks like an enormous treasure chest filled with gold and jewels. But when it senses prey and rouses itself, it transforms into a hideous creature. Retractable teeth sprout from the chest's rim and the treasure is immediately swallowed to reveal its insides are a writhing mass of slimy tentacles. Arms and legs burst out from the sides of the box as it skitters towards its unwary victim. The prey was so focused on the treasure, it failed to recognize the trap, and now it will feed the Beast for the night!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's Lair is dungeon filled with traps and puzzles that wanderers must overcome before heading deeper. Along the way, they are teased with glimpses of wealth or power at the end. Just enough to keep them moving onward. Maybe they lose some people or supplies along the way, but the reward at the end will be worth it. When they finally reach the end, however, they usually don't have enough supplies to make a return trip, assuming the even survive the Beast's attack.</div> </div> </div> </div> I love how the Horror and Lair of this Beast are quite similar to those I suggested for the previous Beast, yet the fear and lesson are totally different.<br /> <br /> Goes to show you that recycling character concepts can indeed work.<br /> <br /> Also, your version gave me <a href=\"http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/darksouls/images/4/47/Tumblr_lt8n59tMwH1qaavgho1_500.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20120118034613\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Dark Souls flashbacks</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-24-2016, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T13:51:38-08:00","id":839410,"title":"","content":"Ugallu Ravager: He calls his Horror the Gremlin. Doesn't sound very intimidating does it? Nevertheless, those with secrets to hide fear both him and it. Unlike the Horrors of his boodmates, his is not some kind of dragon or giant of the kind that terrified neolithic cavemen and Sumerian villagers. His is a new fear. That of the ghost in the machine, of your helpers becoming your foes and the devices you trust your secrets to betraying you.<br /> <br /> In the world of flesh he's a hacker, one of the best. He can crack systems in minutes that others spend days chipping away at. He's in high demand from dozens of factions in the city, from the mafia to the police even to supernatural clades and covenants. Others would be long-gone, sacrificed to keep the secret. He's made sure that he knows his employer's secrets though. He keeps dozens of copies of them. Some on hard drives, some tucked away in the dark corners of the web. He uses them as a combination dead-man's switch and Sword of Damocles. They're his insurance, because if they off him he won't be there to stop the programs posting all of those juicy, juicy secrets for the world to see. He gorges on the fear that he causes, the fear of everything coming crashing down around you.<br /> <br /> And all it would take would be the press of a button.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T14:47:43-08:00","id":839444,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Namtaru Ravager:</b> We've all known someone like them at one point in our lives, the one who always seems to get out of trouble. Some crocodile tears, a cute face or some feigned ignorance and suddenly they're off the hook. Only their victims know the truth, but their victims aren't the ones in charge of rendering the verdict.<br /> <br /> Anyone with a basic knowledge of survival skill can tell you that the most beautiful things in nature can also be the deadliest. In fact, the more enticing something appears to be, the more dangerous it is to predator and prey alike. So it is that this Beast preys on the fear of misplaced trust and betrayal. People come up to it, thinking them to be harmless and charming, only to be caught off guard when it begins to destroy their livelihood from the inside. Worst of all, they are an expert at creating scapegoats, causing others to take the blame for their actions because they're just too nice to have ever done something so malicious.<br /> <br /> In the physical world, they are the patsy of the group. The one who doesn't know any better; they've been swept up by the charismatic ring leader. Or they're just following orders like a good little servant and can't be held responsible because of their master's tyranny. Nobody realizes that they are actually the puppet master in the relationship, orchestrating chaos and misery from behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's horror is the most adorable Gorgon you will ever meet. An anthropomorphic rabbit, it stands as big as a child with cotton candy pink fur that sparkles with glitter. It's voice is high pitched and childish like a cartoon and you just want to scoop them up and give them a big hug. That's when it pulls a knife from behind it's back and coerces you to do some very naughty things on its behalf!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-29-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T15:25:58-08:00","id":839473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=839444#post839444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Namtaru Ravager:</b> We've all known someone like them at one point in our lives, the one who always seems to get out of trouble. Some crocodile tears, a cute face or some feigned ignorance and suddenly they're off the hook. Only their victims know the truth, but their victims aren't the ones in charge of rendering the verdict.<br /> <br /> Anyone with a basic knowledge of survival skill can tell you that the most beautiful things in nature can also be the deadliest. In fact, the more enticing something appears to be, the more dangerous it is to predator and prey alike. So it is that this Beast preys on the fear of misplaced trust and betrayal. People come up to it, thinking them to be harmless and charming, only to be caught off guard when it begins to destroy their livelihood from the inside. Worst of all, they are an expert at creating scapegoats, causing others to take the blame for their actions because they're just too nice to have ever done something so malicious.<br /> <br /> In the physical world, they are the patsy of the group. The one who doesn't know any better; they've been swept up by the charismatic ring leader. Or they're just following orders like a good little servant and can't be held responsible because of their master's tyranny. Nobody realizes that they are actually the puppet master in the relationship, orchestrating chaos and misery from behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's horror is the most adorable Gorgon you will ever meet. An anthropomorphic rabbit, it stands as big as a child with cotton candy pink fur that sparkles with glitter. It's voice is high pitched and childish like a cartoon and you just want to scoop them up and give them a big hug. That's when it pulls a knife from behind it's back and coerces you to some very naughty things on its behalf!</span></div> </div> </div> </div> I think their cute voice would be the same as <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rnZdiR7YbN4\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Catbug's</b></a>, and their serious voice is the same as <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ugp5xqUgI_4\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Boingo's</b></a>. If there is a Beast that would make me root for a Hero, it's probably this one. Nice work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T06:39:54-08:00","id":839859,"title":"","content":"Dunno if I already suggested this, but how about a Morgana le Fey style character? Kinship with changelings. A Sorceress with powers that even the True Fae would fear. And instead of a keeper--YOU WOULD HAVE A QUEEN!! Not dark but beautiful and terrible as the Morn! Treacherous as the Seas! Stronger than the foundations of the Earth! All shall love me and despair!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/_S0BAOVlaEpQ/TFsaa6AUSlI/AAAAAAAAA4c/M9oSx6FVy84/s1600/Galadriel_green_3.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T21:44:20-08:00","id":840391,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Anakim Ravager:</b> The boom of a thunder clap, the shockwave of an explosion, the violent shaking of an earthquake. They are the Beast's offspring, its lovers, its siblings, maybe even its parents. Most terrors in this world merely cause destruction, but this particular Beast <i>is destruction</i>. It is the unstoppable force of nature that defies mankind's attempts to leash it. Its fellow Giants revere it as one of their great grandsires, an ancient progenitor of their kind. It is perhaps one of the few Beasts in the world old enough to remember The Dark Mother's face.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's soul is a monumental creature of the elements. A colossus of earth and wood with thunder clouds for hair and volcanic magma for blood. Its very footsteps crack the earth's crust beneath it's weight and its heavy breathing can dismantle the feeble constructions of man. It sees mankind as mere ants with a shocking level of accuracy. It can flatten their towns and villages in the blink of an eye, but it would only be a matter of days before the pitiful humans started to rebuild what was lost. That's okay, it just means he gets to do it all over again!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-02-2016, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T13:58:00-08:00","id":843129,"title":"","content":"I have a vague idea of a beast that preys on anti-vaxers, the more irrational anti GMO types and pretty much any one who buys into the appeal to nature too much. It's basically the Weaver from WtA, with a touch of the Wyrm to reflect it being the fear of being out of touch with nature, as a Beast, complete with a techno spider horror form, a lair that looks like a polluted but orderly cyberpunk city , and kinship with a bunch of technology minded supernaturals that run a megacorp. The main difference is that said Beast truly believes in the potential for good that the technologies that the appeal to nature demonizes and finds the constant attempts of Heroes to try to ally with more hippie granola type supernaturals to be a pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> This idea mostly comes from the an autistic person with a mother who is a sucker for the appeal to nature (she is not an anti vaxer herself, but she claims that they are allowed to have their opinion (she's a sucker for the false balance fallacy too.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T17:30:24-08:00","id":843207,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=835066#post835066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's always nice to read about a monster that can make me laugh. Here's a brand spanking new, straight-off-the-shelf like for you.<br /> <br /> What Atavisms would he have? I'm imagining Alien Allure, Siren's Treacherous Song and Eye of Heaven. Wondrous for sure as a Lair Trait.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wouldn't know. I don't have access to the Beast PDF, so I don't know what any of the lair traits, atavisms, or nightmares are.<br /> <br /> I did, however, just now come up with a terror for him: <i>The Fear of Failure</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Eshmaki Ravager:</b> War is hell, or at least that is what sound minded individuals who have actually taken part in it will tell you. They lost friends and loved ones, watched as men, women and even children degenerated into savages just to survive another day while their cities were ransacked between two clashing armies. This Beast embodies the fear of conflict, and preys upon the tension that comes before all hell breaks loose. Centuries ago, it served as the adviser to kings and tyrants, dripping poisoned whispers into their ear as they manipulated them into skirmishes with foreigners. In the modern world, it serves as a weapons manufacturer, supplying tools between foreign powers that would result in mutual destruction, should they come to blows. It's most recent achievement was instigating the Cold War between America and Russia by supplying both countries with nuclear arms. Woe be to mortals when it's next scheme gets off the ground!<br /> <br /> <br /> The first thing Heroes will notice when they see the Beast's true form is that they may actually be able to kill it. But in exchange, they will be sacrificing their own lives in the process. The Beast is covered in natural weaponry. Poisonous mandibles grow from its mouth while needle sharp spines protrude from its chitinous exoskeleton. Serrated talons are attached to its arms and legs while a dagger length stinger caps its bulbous tail. The Beast is not afraid to take damage in a fight, because it knows that it's opponent will injure itself in the process. The Beast may die, it knows this is always a possibility; but if it's going to die, <i>it's going to take you down with it!</i></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-06-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:43:43-08:00","id":843488,"title":"","content":"Wrong thread,sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 03-07-2016, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T12:57:29-07:00","id":849407,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Makara Tyrant:</b> Not all trappings are physical in nature, as this Beast has come to understand. When it comes to being a Leviathan, his eyes are like the sea, easy to get lost in. His voice is like the waves, washing over listeners with a siren's allure. In public, he has a menagerie of girls from his school following him around and hanging on his every word! Occasionally, one of the Ex-boyfriends will show up as a Hero trying to win their girl back through violence and brutishness. It never fails to bring a smile to his face when he exposes them as jealous, possessive individuals in serious need of anger management.<br /> <br /> The Beast's horror is a strange entity. It has the head and torso of an Asian male possessed of bishounen levels of beauty and speaks in a calm, seductive voice. But from the waist down, it is comprised of a writhing mass of tentacles that it slithers around on like snakes. The technical term for his species is &quot;Roper,&quot; but he has been called a few less pleasant names in the past by Heroes.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Eshmaki Nemeses:</b> Some people have trouble coming out of their shell. They mostly keep to themselves, rarely speaking up and just trying to get through the day without incident. Unfortunately these people are often the ones who get pushed around the most. Which is exactly what this Beast is hoping for! They are the one who eventually snaps and exacts retribution for being singled out as a victim. It tries to starve its soul when possible, but sometimes that's just too hard. When it goes hungry for too long, the Beast gets irritable; and should its abusers manage to run into them on those days, it usually doesn't end well for them!<br /> <br /> The Beast's horror is an anthropomorphic snapping tortoise. Its mouth is a sharpened beak while its limbs end with reptilian claws. It's shell is lined with spiked ridges around the sides and top, giving it a more ornery appearance than other tortoises. It's usually not aggressive and tries to go about its business, but mess around in its territory or agitate it too long and it starts hitting back!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-02-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T17:45:47-07:00","id":849940,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Eshmaki Ravager:</b> A fear that heroes and villains are all too familiar with is the possibility of a good intention going horribly wrong. That somewhere down the line, you lose sight of what you're trying to achieve and become a corrupted mockery of what you once were. This Beast knows that fear because they have lived it, they thought that humans and monsters could co-exist peacefully with one another; only to be met with violence and misunderstanding. Now it encourages others to stray from their path, to give into temptations and watches with glee as their morals and ethics crumble in the face of inconvenience. It lives by the motto that in this world: It's kill or be killed!<br /> <br /> The Beast's horror is a tragic creature. It possesses the wings and halo of an angel with snow white hair and the body of an anthropomorphic goat dressed in purple robes. The wings are tattered and frayed while the halo is cracked and chipped. their body is wrapped in a network of thorny briers and although it speaks with the gleefulness of a psychopath, its dark eyes reveal the pained sorrow that it carries within itself.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T17:06:26-07:00","id":850324,"title":"","content":"Matt Murdoch: Eshmaki/nemesis<br /> <br /> Legend: Brutal <br /> Life: Kind<br /> <br /> When one first enters his lair they are greeted by complete darkness and the cries of agony. They stand in unseen pools of blood in order to travel to the next camber they take the blood and put it into their eyes they then are given a vision of an invisible city visible only for the blood pouring down it.<br /> Where Matt's horror, a devil made of spilt blood and broken bone, roams <br /> <br /> Matt lost his eyes to chemical Burns while a child and resigned himself to it until his devouring when the horror gave him clarity it didn't fix his eyes but it strengthened his other ones to the point that it doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","name":"Quinn H.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T23:39:09-07:00","id":852843,"title":"","content":"<b>Eshmaki Predator:</b> They say that those who fight monsters should watch themselves so as to not become what they fight. Many Hunters know this all too well, but one of them didn't listen. The Traitor, as it is commonly known among the Begotten, was a Hunter who rejected all that made Man vulnerable so as to become perfect at its calling. And it got what it wished for, to the expense of all that which was dear to it. Its eager patriotism faded as went from nation to nation, seeking the monsters that were corrupting the halls of power from within. Its chivalry and camaraderie atrophied, as it started to see genders as just disguises to take and allies as tools. Resources and safe houses were used and discarded quickly so as to not become liabilities. Its hobbies and friends became distant memories that no longer entered its dreams. Its faith in God became less than nothing.<br /> <br /> As more and more of its anchors to humanity were abandoned, the Thing in its nightmares grew closer. When the Thing came for the Traitor, they embraced each other with more purpose than any parent, child or lover. The Traitor used its new powers to study monsters up close, finding out every single weakness they thought they could hide. While Heroes concerned themselves with glory and petty grievances, it made sure to destroy any supernatural community it saw as dangerous from the roots. Common mortal criminals were dispatched just as ruthlessly. Vampire Elders and Slashers, an Archmage here and a True Fae there, it all blurred together. No calling cards were left, no melodrama before or after each beautifully heartless murder. Some were glad, others went mad with hatred, and quite a few just carried on. Their reactions soon became indistinct as well. <br /> <br /> The Traitor knew very well it would never last like this. It searched during decades for a way to make it impossible for others to remember its appearance, only its actions. It found an unspeakable rite inscribed with a part of the Dark Mother's true name, and carried it out beneath the eclipsed moon. The Hunters who used to work with it only recall terrifying glimpses of cautionary nightmares. &quot;Do not follow my steps&quot;, the nightmares would say. &quot;I cannot go back, enjoy the company of what you fight for while you still can&quot;. The Traitor's profiles in the data banks of Conspiracies and the Libraries of monsters have little else to say about it.<br /> <br /> The Thing that gave the Traitor all it could hope for has grown strong. So very strong.<br /> <br /> The Traitor has no one to call Kin among Man or Monster. No place on Earth or any realm to call Home. It has become lonely. So very lonely.<br /> <br /> It keeps on killing. No one is safe from it. The world has not changed much since it started, but the lessons it teaches were never forgotten. Man must keep Monster at bay to grow, and Monster must contain Man lest it destroy us all with its endless appetites and ambitions. The truth is that the Traitor is becoming obsolete. They are used to the Darkness.<br /> <br /> The Traitor wants to find an ending. Maybe it can abandon the bloodshed long enough to settle down somewhere and make others' lives a bit happier before it too fades away. Perhaps it will find where the Dark Mother sleeps, kill her and destroy the world's need for fear. It might finally give up and take down all it can along with itself.<br /> <br /> While that doesn't happen, you better watch how long you stare into the Abyss. The Traitor is the one inside looking back at you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date"