doesn't work that way regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:26:00-07:00","id":853016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853009#post853009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural Merit and therefore inaccessible to non-mortals, Family Resemblance is already about as close to an omni-Unseen Sense as you can get short of Peripheral Mage Sight, and Unseen Sense doesn't work that way regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence houserules. it's not the sort of thing that you'd put in all games but if you want to run a game in which beasts can see Ephemerals, go ahead. So long as the Players and Storytelller agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T17:45:37-07:00","id":853247,"title":"","content":"<b>Namtaru Ravager:</b> They call him The Doctor, but any mortal institution would have stripped his medical license from him centuries ago if they knew what sort of malpractice he indulges in. He does not cure sickness, he spreads it! From deep within his lair, he concocts vile toxins and deadly pathogens before releasing them upon the unsuspecting public. He lives for the chaos brought upon by social collapse, and one of the best ways to collapse society is with a highly contagious disease entering the city!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's horror is a putrid thing. A giant rat that walks upright like a man and clothes itself in tattered, filth covered rags. Its fur is mangy and unkempt, it's skin is covered in blisters and pustules, foam drips from the corners of its mouth. Physical contact with the creature causes paint to peel, metal to rust and infections to set, while it's fetid breath can knock all but the strongest constitutions out cold! Anyone who engages in unprotected sex with the Beast is guaranteed to contract something that will take more than lotion to get rid of.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Doctor's lair is a subterranean laboratory filled with canisters and pipes that contain brightly colored liquids and gases. Bubbling vats of poison and hissing steam vents fill visitors with dread if they attempt to wander without an escort, fearing that one wrong step will cause them to be exposed to whatever sick experiments The Doctor is working on now. If he gets his claws on any Heroes wandering the area, he always takes perverse glee in throwing them into one of the churning vats and watching them spend the last few moments of their life trying to climb back out before they sink to the bottom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-29-2016, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T05:36:11-07:00","id":853428,"title":"","content":"As much as I like the Nurglian imagery, this one is a bit too cartoony in its wickedness for me. What sort of lessons would he teach? If it happened, it would be accidentally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:32:19-07:00","id":853493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853428#post853428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I like the Nurglian imagery, this one is a bit too cartoony in its wickedness for me. What sort of lessons would he teach? If it happened, it would be accidentally.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does there have to be a lesson? I thoughts Beasts were supposed to represent fears, not morals.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose his lesson could be that when faced with the possibility of extinction, humanity embraces chaos over order?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:35:36-07:00","id":853498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853493#post853493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Does there have to be a lesson? I thoughts Beasts were supposed to represent fears, not morals.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose his lesson could be that when faced with the possibility of extinction, humanity embraces chaos over order?</div> </div> </div> </div>That, or encourage the finer points of good hygiene... ya filthy mon-keigh. &gt;;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:52:26-07:00","id":853508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853498#post853498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, or encourage the finer points of good hygiene... ya filthy mon-keigh. &gt;;3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (off topic here for a moment)<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the idea of them having to teach people lessons is <i>even worse</i> than them just being the embodiment of fear. If they're living terrors, then that draws attention to the personal horror that nWoD seems to focus on. You're a blood thirsty monster, but that doesn't mean you have to take pleasure in it.<br /> <br /> But if the theme of the game is about teaching people morals and common sense, then it kind of justifies being a monster. It's like &quot;Hey kid, didn't your parents tell you not to trust strangers? Guess I need to show you why!&quot;<br /> <br /> At that point it becomes less about personal horror and more about the process of natural selection.<br /> <br /> (End rant)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:57:05-07:00","id":853513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853508#post853508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> (off topic here for a moment)<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the idea of them having to teach people lessons is <i>even worse</i> than them just being the embodiment of fear. If they're living terrors, then that draws attention to the personal horror that nWoD seems to focus on. You're a blood thirsty monster, but that doesn't mean you have to take pleasure in it.<br /> <br /> But if the theme of the game is about teaching people morals and common sense, then it kind of justifies being a monster. It's like &amp;quot;Hey kid, didn't your parents tell you not to trust strangers? Guess I need to show you why!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> At that point it becomes less about personal horror and more about the process of natural selection.<br /> <br /> (End rant)</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that the 'teaching morals' is decided by the Beasts themselves, not by their nature. It's like a vampire refusing to kill people to feed or a changeling refusing to feed off of fear. It's a personal choice, one that lets the Beast give himself some flimsy justification for his actions. Personally I would have preferred it if the 'teaching lessons' thing had been left out of the main book and a few pages should have been devoted to talking about the way that Beasts justify their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:00:38-07:00","id":853519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853508#post853508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> (off topic here for a moment)<br /> <br /> Personally, I think the idea of them having to teach people lessons is <i>even worse</i> than them just being the embodiment of fear. If they're living terrors, then that draws attention to the personal horror that nWoD seems to focus on. You're a blood thirsty monster, but that doesn't mean you have to take pleasure in it.<br /> <br /> But if the theme of the game is about teaching people morals and common sense, then it kind of justifies being a monster. It's like &quot;Hey kid, didn't your parents tell you not to trust strangers? Guess I need to show you why!&quot;<br /> <br /> At that point it becomes less about personal horror and more about the process of natural selection.<br /> <br /> (End rant)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just kidding! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:04:01-07:00","id":853520,"title":"","content":"Oh, good. Was worried it was some kind of requirement.<br /> <br /> By the way, I'm a little unclear about this. Is the book finished yet, or is it still in testing phases? I wanted to know when I could get my hands on a physical copy that won't be subject to revisions every couple months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-26-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:05:18-07:00","id":853522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853520#post853520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, good. Was worried it was some kind of requirement.<br /> <br /> By the way, I'm a little unclear about this. Is the book finished yet, or is it still in testing phases? I wanted to know when I could get my hands on a physical copy that won't be subject to revisions even couple months.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As far as I know, It's finished. There's a PDF version out for the Kickstarter backers so the full version should be out in a week or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_15233