orum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853592#post853592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Agreed. While I do appreciate that they included the idea of wisdom through fear, I think it was too emphasized. I imagine most Beasts as embracing their role. The tone varies according to the particular Beast, of course, and even from day to day. But making the teaching of that wisdom a significant part of their culture sounds rather defensive on part of the Begotten. Looking for justifications so often is the main flaw of Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that they mention it an awful lot for an optional, but they do at least once note that some Beasts just retroactively call the assorted murders/assaults/homewrecking/etc they were going to do anyway &quot;lessons&quot; if anyone asks them about it, and some Beasts honestly just don't bother with the facade at all. There's room for not being a teacher, the setting's fine with that. The issue - and this is a general one - is getting a table on-board with all playing Beasts who have enough troupe cohesion to actually run the game. The guy who teaches middle-class families to appreciate their blessings by spooking them from time to time, promoting close-knit bonds of love and gratitude, and the gal who likes to play home invasion with her least favorite political demographic, leaving nothing but broken-eyed ruin behind, can't really co-exist. What I've found is that despite most other lines letting you run 'monsters,' the lack of a Morality stat in Beast somehow facilitates all kinds of ethical argument and sniping. I guess the game doesn't let you make the argument that you're &quot;acceptable&quot; if you're a diablerist but I feel like there isn't really an argument anyway. Still, some folks like having them.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, I want to run a Lovecraftian psychiatrist who terrorizes scientists, occultists, and private detectives into nervous breakdowns and then REALLY puts the screaming to them, an embodiment of Things Man Was Not Meant to Know. Those who seek knowledge beyond what they need to survive and live normal lives must be shown the limits of their kind; those who stargaze will learn never to raise their eyes again; et cetera et cetera. Someone who styles themselves as a gnostic tyrant, but is actually just bitter that they weren't smart enough to cut it before their Devouring, they only finished out their degree by supernatural compulsion and strength of fear, and searches for someone with the will and gumption to hold them off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:55:41-07:00","id":853631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853626#post853626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> All hail the one true God of the Onyx path Forums! All hail the almighty STCHL!</div> </div> </div> </div> <b>Logic for the Logic God! Likes for the Like Throne!</b><br /> <br /> (OK, I've had my fill. Next post will be on topic.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:11:40-07:00","id":853644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853630#post853630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that they mention it an awful lot for an optional, but they do at least once note that some Beasts just retroactively call the assorted murders/assaults/homewrecking/etc they were going to do anyway &amp;quot;lessons&amp;quot; if anyone asks them about it, and some Beasts honestly just don't bother with the facade at all. There's room for not being a teacher, the setting's fine with that. The issue - and this is a general one - is getting a table on-board with all playing Beasts who have enough troupe cohesion to actually run the game. The guy who teaches middle-class families to appreciate their blessings by spooking them from time to time, promoting close-knit bonds of love and gratitude, and the gal who likes to play home invasion with her least favorite political demographic, leaving nothing but broken-eyed ruin behind, can't really co-exist. What I've found is that despite most other lines letting you run 'monsters,' the lack of a Morality stat in Beast somehow facilitates all kinds of ethical argument and sniping. I guess the game doesn't let you make the argument that you're &amp;quot;acceptable&amp;quot; if you're a diablerist but I feel like there isn't really an argument anyway. Still, some folks like having them.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, I want to run a Lovecraftian psychiatrist who terrorizes scientists, occultists, and private detectives into nervous breakdowns and then REALLY puts the screaming to them, an embodiment of Things Man Was Not Meant to Know. Those who seek knowledge beyond what they need to survive and live normal lives must be shown the limits of their kind; those who stargaze will learn never to raise their eyes again; et cetera et cetera. Someone who styles themselves as a gnostic tyrant, but is actually just bitter that they weren't smart enough to cut it before their Devouring, they only finished out their degree by supernatural compulsion and strength of fear, and searches for someone with the will and gumption to hold them off.</div> </div> </div> </div> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=825514#post825514\">Nyrufa had a similar idea earlier in this thread.</a></b> <br /> <br /> I don't wanna sound like a backseat mod, but there's another thread about Beasts and morality going on that is much better suited for this discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T17:57:38-07:00","id":853771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853626#post853626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All hail the one true God of the Onyx path Forums! All hail the almighty STCHL!</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853644#post853644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't wanna sound like a backseat mod</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/bokusaatchi.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I mentioned Alan Webster way back in the earlier chunks of this thread as the Tutor, and he's developed a fair bit since then. He's become an econ major with a gambling fixation, a fascination with prophetic verse, an abiding conviction that the Dark Mother is spoiling her Children, and a stubborn adherence to the middle of the Satiety ladder. His clocktower Heart touches one or two places in the Hedge and he's learned enough to start hunting for Avernian Gates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T08:16:07-07:00","id":865952,"title":"","content":"By day he works as a zookeeper, more specifically as a keeper for the tigers at the local zoo. They seem to listen to him, as if he's one of them. He seems to like them too, even staying after hours to feed and watch them. In fact, it's probably because he's there at night that the zoo hasn't had the same troubles as others in the area. There have been a rash of violent break-ins or animals escaping their cages and enclosures, even sometimes quite dangerous ones. They're never found after the escape either, seeming to vanish. Every now and again, though, someone spots a cougar drinking at a stream or something and the media frenzy starts all over again. A while ago, they even found a body that looked to ahve been stripped clean by some kind of big predator...<br /> <br /> In truth, of course, the zookeeper is an Eshmaki Ravager whose Horror is a great tiger the size of a horse and who instigates the 'breakouts' as a method of destroying the complacency of the populace. His Lair is a vast jungle in which he keeps his dangerous 'pets', letting them out when they need to hunt. Sometimes he joins them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:25:32-07:00","id":866079,"title":"","content":"Admittedly more of a methodology than a concept, but it might be an interesting setup for an antagonist. <br /> <br /> Okay, first, you have to be a Tyrant. Second, you need to have the Nightmare Tabula Rasa, which can erase memories, and generally have a high Satiety. Then you either need to have a Lair that can be farmed, or have access to bulk supplies of food. Then in the real world, you hunt someone down, stalking them and taking pains to cut at the ties binding them to their life. Then, when they're all alone, you lead them somewhere you can open a Pathway and pull them into your Lair. You gloat and gleefully tell them what's going to happen and how they can't stop it (this feeds the Horror) and then hit them with Tabula Rasa, using the High Satiety effect to erase their entire life's memory and the Satiety expenditure to make it permanent; if you wish, you may set it to when they next sleep and then use You Will Never Rest, if you wish for more time to set the stage. Use the circumstances, copious amounts of supernatural force, and your social skills to convince them that the reason they can't remember anything is because you are a god who just forged them into being, and that your Lair is the whole world. Repeat as needed.<br /> <br /> Congratulations, you now have a cult who depends on you for survival that you can farm Satiety from! You are also a total scumbag, and the pcs are likely to end up ruining your plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:40:32-07:00","id":866090,"title":"","content":"What about a Nightmare that makes the person think they're someone else? Complete with different personality and interests?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:08:01-07:00","id":898009,"title":"","content":"I've got two I've made so far as NPCs for my upcoming campaign:<br /> <br /> Anakim Ravager - a Minotaur that works as a shift leader for a janitorial company. He's got keys to a couple important buildings in town, and has found an easy way to feed, though he never feeds deep any longer. He calls it his &quot;diet.&quot; <br /> <br /> Ugallu Collector - a Coautl waitress who uses her Atavisms to steal cats and dogs from the suburbs and lets them live in one of her chambers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5985-jessel","name":"Jessel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:47:14-07:00","id":898111,"title":"","content":"<b>Makara Collector</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You always dreamed of being a wizard. Well, technically you dreamed of being chased through a sunken castle by a massive serpent whose eyes betrayed centuries of cunning and wisdom, but what you <i>wanted</i> was to be a wizard, a magnus who had the knowledge to move heaven and earth. Really you figured the universe owed you it. After all, you had to work and sweat and struggle for everything while your sister, the favorite of your parents and everyone else, coasted through life on a wining smile.<br /> <br /> Eventually, you left to go to college, where you finally confronted the serpent that was you and claimed your birthright. You were upset when your realized this blocked you from your power, but you grew somewhat content, becoming as much of an expert on the sorceries of your Kin as an outsider could. Eventually you were called home to help provide for your parents (because of course the Golden Child couldn't be bothered), and for a time the world was good.<br /> <br /> But then you met your sister again, and when she flared with the light of Kinship, you grit your teeth and bore it. When her Nimbus shone with the shimmering coloration of the Primal Wild, it took all that you had not to bash her pretty perfect head into the nearest wall. Now you aid her in the investigations that plague her soul, her using you for your knowledge and skill and you using her to gain an in with her fellow Mages and the Satiety you need. But as the days go on you become more and more aware that you're nothing more than her <i>assistant</i>, her on-demand Yantra, her <i><b>familiar!</b></i> Now you grow bitterer and bitterer, and soon you fear you'll do something you regret... or worse, something you won't regret in the slightest.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 06-16-2016, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T13:02:17-07:00","id":898132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=898111#post898111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Makara Collector</b>*<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You always dreamed of being a wizard. Well, technically you dreamed of being chased through a sunken castle by a massive serpent whose eyes betrayed centuries of cunning and wisdom, but what you <i>wanted</i> was to be a wizard, a magnus who had the knowledge to move heaven and earth. Really you figured the universe owed you it. After all, you had to work and sweat and struggle for everything while your sister, the favorite of your parents and everyone else, coasted through life on a wining smile.<br /> <br /> Eventually, you left to go to college, where you finally confronted the serpent that was you and claimed your birthright. You were upset when your realized this blocked you from your power, but you grew somewhat content, becoming as much of an expert on the sorceries of your Kin as an outsider could. Eventually you were called home to help provide for your parents (because of course the Golden Child couldn't be bothered), and for a time the world was good.*<br /> <br /> But then you met your sister again, and when she flared with the light of Kinship, you grit your teeth and bore it. When her Nimbus shone with the shimmering coloration of the Primal Wild, it took all that you had not to bash her pretty perfect head into the nearest wall. Now you aid her in the investigations that plague her soul, her using you for your knowledge and skill and you using her to gain an in with her fellow Mages and the Satiety you need. But as the days go on you become more and more aware that you're nothing more than her <i>assistant</i>, her on-demand Yantra, her <i><b>familiar!</b></i> Now you grow bitterer and bitterer, and soon you fear you'll do something you regret... or worse, something you won't regret in the slightest.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you've seen the Primordial Sorcery stuff Deionscribe and I did, this character would love that, I think. Especially the curses. It's not the easy power of a mage's magic though. He'll still have to work for it, and I doubt the sister will recognise his powers as anything special. He can't conjure storms, create life and weave reality to the pattern he wants after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 05-24-2016, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:39:53-07:00","id":898234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=898132#post898132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you've seen the Primordial Sorcery stuff Deionscribe and I did, this character would love that, I think. Especially the curses. It's not the easy power of a mage's magic though. He'll still have to work for it, and I doubt the sister will recognise his powers as anything special. He can't conjure storms, create life and weave reality to the pattern he wants after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>True; honestly this idea has been floating around in my head for a while. Anyway, a couple more less developed ideas.<br /> <br /> \u2022A Stigmatic turned Ugallu Ravenger with an insane hatred for the G-M. Reluctantly allies themselves with a Ring of Saboteurs and finds themselves actually beginning to regard these not-Kin as a sort of family.<br /> <br /> \u2022A Namtaru Nemesis, a pastor/&quot;Praying Mantis&quot; who is driven both by his hunger and his belief that anyone can be redeemed to scare the wicked into the arms of God.<br /> <br /> \u2022An Ugallu Predator who works with abuse victims by day and stalks the Hedge by night, with a special enjoyment in hunting the Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> \u2022An Anakim Collector who's a loyal member of a Mummy Cult, stealing Relics in the name of his &quot;god&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u2022A Nemesis whose Devouring saved them from the ravages of Soul Loss, and who now punishes those hubristic enough to steal or damage that precious numinal organ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Added one 05-24-2016, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:40:57-07:00","id":917466,"title":"","content":"Again, sorry about the double post, but I think a few days short of a month makes it okay. <br /> <br /> Anyway, after being inspired by a comment <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/907934-sell-me-on-beast?p=917226#post917226\">here</a>, I like the idea of an Eshmaki who takes the form of a strange pumpkin creature, a Nemesis or Tyrant who feeds by terrifying intruders into dangerous places, like the graveyard where he tends the grounds and serves as a guard for the Avernian Gate there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T22:11:41-07:00","id":936422,"title":"","content":"Fire is the great protector, the purifier. Literal gods walk the land, blessings those they choose, destroying others on a whim. In the Neolithic Era, she's a shaman - a wise woman who sits on the fringes of society and counsels those who seek her out.<br /> <br /> Or so they say. <br /> <br /> Really, the People truly know the only reason why one would visit her: revenge. She hears the pleas of wronged supplicants, using the power of the great Horror within to judge the truth of their words. If their words ring true and they pay her price, she'll hunt down and punish the guilty, throwing their soul into the darkest depths of the ocean.<br /> <br /> Basically, she's a Makara Nemesis, with her Horror a titanic sea-serpent known as the Terror of Death that swims through the Ocean Beyond Life and the Primordial Dream. Her fear - and lesson - is that you cannot escape what you have done, and even death is not a release. For when her Horror claims your life, it drowns your soul within the ever-swirling currents of its Lair, forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There was a signature here. It's gone now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8730-pandorym","name":"Pandorym","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8730_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T13:31:33-07:00","id":939750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=853493#post853493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Does there have to be a lesson? I thoughts Beasts were supposed to represent fears, not morals.<br /> <br /> Although I suppose his lesson could be that when faced with the possibility of extinction, humanity embraces chaos over order?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the doctor could easily teach a lesson that the Beast I posted would agree with. The lesson being, don't get your medical advice from former playboy playmates. In this, the plauge rat image would represent both literal plague rats that spread infectious diseases but also human &quot;mental plauge rats&quot; that carry and spread ideas that are just as infectious and dangerous to society as a literal disease.<br /> <br /> In fact, my weaver wyrm-spider would gladly let your beast build his laboratory lair under his polluted city lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T14:07:15-07:00","id":939774,"title":"","content":"<b>Anakim Tyrant:</b> He's got the eye of the tiger... a nemean tiger, to be exact! He showed up in the ring years ago and achieved one victory after the next, all the way up to the championship. He rules undefeated, his opponent's blows glancing off his body with barely any impact, and no matter how many drug tests the committee demands, he always passes, so they have no evidence to accuse him of cheating. He was almost choked into submission by a challenger seeking to earn his belt, but managed to slip free of his hold before losing consciousness and went flying into the offensive.<br /> <br /> Since that match, he's been training constantly. He knows that his opponent will show up again one day, looking for a rematch. And next time, there won't be any tap outs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T17:09:05-07:00","id":940943,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a Beast that just sort of tumbled out of my head: Ingrid Frost, twitchy conspiracy theorist (who &quot;collects&quot; mysteries) with the soul of a mothwoman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T19:14:34-07:00","id":955357,"title":"","content":"<b>Anakim Tyrant:</b> To say that he casts a long shadow over the city would be an understatement. Before his devouring, he felt like he never had any control over his life, always following orders and being powerless to follow through on his own decisions. But once he stood tall, he saw just how small and insignificant those who oppressed him truly were. On that day, he decided that not only was he going to be in control of his own life, he was going to take control of everyone else's life to make up for the humiliation he endured!<br /> <br /> Now, he rules the city, nothing gets approved in it without his say so. His shadow looms over the heads of the common rabble, watching their every move and taking swift action to silence any dissension in the ranks. He laughs at the notion of being called &quot;mayor&quot; behind closed doors. King would be a more appropriate title, and he's not relinquishing the crown as long as he continues to draw breath!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:14:32-07:00","id":960851,"title":"","content":"Meg is a naturally protective sort, naturally growing from the kid who stood up to bullies to a potent activist advocating for abuse victims on her college campus. The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood saw that she was a force for good and brought her in to help them keep the local girls safe from vampires, and was happy to hold a Vigil against mundane assholes and nocturnal terrors. <br /> <br /> Then one of the Furies stepped out of Greek myth and into a ragged hole in her chest, and she found that she now had the power to actually hurt the predators out there instead of just speaking out against against them. <br /> <br /> Now Meg's torn in all directions, trying to balance a normal college life full of study and political activism even as she hides her newfound nature as an unholy spirit of vengeance from her Hunter sisters, and that's before she catches word that the vampires are muttering about their dark goddess sending them a messenger...<br /> <br /> She's an Ugallu Nemesis, and I'd play with being torn between mortal obligations and unwanted supernatural Kinship as well as the idea of having a notable and infamous Horror, namely Megaera the Fury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:32:58-07:00","id":961131,"title":"","content":"I'm making an Eshmaki Predator who is a bartender.<br /> Her favored prey are those who are about to give up on something as many of her patrons do. She uses her position to find out more about them, their worries...their fears and then she destroys their life from the shadows. The unseen hand of fate slowly destroying their lives, and she makes it more and more clear someone is doing this to them. In the end, she spares the ones who fight to get their lives back, returning as much as she can that was taken from them. It usually succeeds, she plans her prey well, but when it fails, she kills them and considers it a mercy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T13:24:19-07:00","id":962465,"title":"","content":"<b>Namtaru Nemesis:</b> The absolute strongest adversary to overcome is yourself. This Gorgon is the manifestation of the self, bringing with it doubt, fear and weakness. From a casual observation, the Beast appears to be an identical copy of its victim, but a closer inspection will reveal the truth. The monster's body is composed of reflective glass and polished metal, like an anthropomorphic mirror reflecting the image of those it preys upon. It studies its victim, learning to move and act as they do. When it feels confident that it can replicate their behavior, that is when it attacks. Infiltrating their dreams and claiming to be their subconscious emotions. Envy, hatred, lust, pride, greed, the Namtaru is the guilty conscience that tears you up inside.<br /> <br /> <br /> The monster's lair is a house of mirrors, each one of which is a window into the soul. A monitor through which to view the most humiliating, painful, and terrifying moments of a person's life. The monster herds its prey through the mirrors, forcing them to watch one scene after another, as their spirits are crushed beneath fear and despair. But the Namtaru must take great care not to go too far with their sadism.<br /> <br /> <i>A Hero capable of forgiving themselves is a terrifying opponent, indeed.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-05-2016, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T13:36:41-07:00","id":962473,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> , would you mind if I make a Beast in associated with yours?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T15:05:12-07:00","id":962518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=962473#post962473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> , would you mind if I make a Beast in associated with yours?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Go right ahead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T17:31:29-07:00","id":962589,"title":"","content":"Makara Tyrant (from my Savannah setting): Normally the potential to become a beast doesn't run in human bloodlines, her father's is one of the exceptions. Supposedly he and his many half-siblings were born devoured, the spawn of an ancient incarnate who reached a state beyond that. The ancient sea serpent's spawn became the apex incarnates of their own hives, all of them linked into their father's primordial empire<br /> <br /> She on the other hand was devoured after birth, by her father of course, and her horror looks much like his, a loch ness monster type creature that swims through the swamps and rivers of the primordal dream in her father's domain. Her tyrant nature mostly takes the form of being the smartest kid in the room, the one who knows how her peers' schemes will blow up in their faces before they even begin and enjoys asserting her mental superiority over the other local children, and making her owns plans that use them as pawns. That being said she isn't above playing the &quot;spoiled princess of the apex&quot; form of tyrant either. Her main kinships are with some local changeling kids with aquatic kiths and with a boy who.... she actually doesn't know what he is, to tell the truth, except that he is both incredibly dumb, absurdly lucky and somehow never stays dead while never remembering his deaths from their misadventures.<br /> <br /> in human form, she is a biracial 9 year old girl, capable of passing for white if she takes care not to let her Gullah accent slip and uses enough hair products. When she isn't wearing her school uniform, she usually wears the sort of clothes little rich girls usually wear, with subtle accessories drawn from her Gullah heritage.<br /> <br /> Her lair takes the form of a sunken amusement park in brackish water, not unlike if an amusement park in Orlando sank back into the swamp, with chambers made from the various places she's mentally dominated and terrified the other children of Savannah, though the latest chamber comes from the Disney Cruise her father took her on over the summer as a promised reward for straight As last year in school, the ship's counterpart in her lair a capsized wreck on the marsh floor.<br /> <br /> Quotes:<br /> (Upon seeing the results of her idiot kin's latest failed scheme) &quot;I don't even... Look, just... explain to me what you were <b>trying </b>to do when this happened.&quot;<br /> <br /> (intimidation) &quot;Do you want me to tell daddy what you're doing in his turf? because he will be much harder on you than I would if you let me in on this.&quot;<br /> <br /> (impressed) &quot;I hate to admit it, but the idiot has a point.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Bratty) &quot;But Daddy, you said I could land the death blow on that hero!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-02-2016, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T23:26:53-07:00","id":962721,"title":"","content":"Honestly, despite my assorted misgivings and gripes with Beast seeing people's character ideas has kept me interested. Plus, I really want to play Ingrid some day, she's one of my favorite characters that I've created. Plus she has something a personal connection my own fears in a way that most monsters don't- I heard about the mothman and Indrid Cold when I was pretty young, and the story (and the drawings of the mothman I saw online) freaked me out in a way that not much else ever has. For a significant period in my life, my main fears were the mothman, Indrid Cold, and dementors coming out of the toilet. <br /> <br /> Also, I retooled a Leviathan character I had into a Beast and made her part of a cross-splat Mummy cult I was working on. She's a Makara Tyrant and the owner of a small New Jersey-based and heavily mafia-connected construction company. Basically, if the Cloverfield monster had more arms and took fashion tips from The Situation. I also came up with a nasty Kinship Nightmare for her that came from the casino-owning business magnate Mummy she worked for- it's called Everyone Has A Price, and it forces the target to think of things- including themself- as commodities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T01:20:00-07:00","id":962738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=962518#post962518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go right ahead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Anakim Tyrant:</b> Where his friend shows her prey their own failings, he shows them how far they are from what they want. He preys upon those who desire to be perfectly beautiful or attractive. He shows them that there is always someone <i>more</i> perfect, <i>more</i> attractive, that even supermodel-looks won't stop the company that you model for Photoshoppping you to be better.<br /> <br /> Entering his Lair, even Heroes are overawed by the utter, impossible beauty of the rainforest that greets them, of the exquisite placement of the impossibly green leaves, of the droplets of water which fall like diamonds from every frond and leaf. Even the storms that sometimes roll in overhead are beautiful, tempestuous cathedrals in the sky. The entire place has a crystalline, unearthly allure to it, as if it were a living, growing artwork.<br /> <br /> He calls his Horror the Peacock Serpent and it takes the form of an enormous, feathered serpent. Every inch of its plumage is spotless and gleaming, iridescent in countless shades of red, blue and green. Its eyes are like yellow gems in its face and even its deadly, venomous fangs look beautiful and shapely. When he feeds, he brings his prey into his Lair, usually making it seem as if it is a dream. In serpent-form, he is almost pleasant and genial at first, if prideful, offering to guide the bewildered mortal around his domain. Over time, though, as its prey becomes more and more overawed with its surroundings and the Serpent itself, its words become crueller, more cutting. It begins by commenting on the mortal in relation to its glorious self, and how they must be envious and it's so sorry it can't help. Then it moves on, letting the prey consider their own place. Eventually, when they sit down and despair over themselves, it simply devolves into a tirade of insults and deriding comments as the Serpent coils ever-tighter around them.<br /> <br /> Those who can push past this and gather the will to leave (and live) are guided to the exit and wake up, unharmed and, perhaps, made wiser. Those who cannot are either devoured whole by the Serpent or remain within its Lair. A few have survived, feeding upon the fruits and beasts within the Lair and have created almost a 'cult' of sorts, venerating the Serpent as the most beautiful thing in the universe, slowly forgetting their original lives within the mind-bending beauty of the Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T06:44:57-07:00","id":962799,"title":"","content":"Actually, I would say that my mirror Beast has a kinship with Prometheans. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Ugallu Ravager:</b> When asked about why he became a monster, he'll tell you that he was born to do it. Prior to his devouring, he served as a bomber pilot, dropping explosive ordinance upon enemy troops from the sky. After his devouring, he became a dragon of old, and now soars through the sky on great black wings. Searing hot flames blasting from his maw and igniting enemy encampments as they scramble for safety. As one of the incarnate, he was forced to go awol for obvious reasons. But he doesn't let his dishonorable discharge bring him down. How could it, when he no longer needs a plane to take flight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-03-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T06:53:05-07:00","id":962804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=962799#post962799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I would say that my mirror Beast has a kinship with Prometheans. What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of the shared 'identity' thing? Absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:00:39-07:00","id":962806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=962804#post962804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of the shared 'identity' thing? Absolutely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep. Learning to impersonate humanity, except it focuses on the bad parts. Only those who can accept the bad with the good, instead of running from it can overcome his horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T12:36:16-07:00","id":962947,"title":"","content":"Ugallu Tyrant<br /> <br /> The man in the aviators regards you coolly. Your eyes keep being drawn the patches on his jacket, covered in eagle insignia for branches of the military you've never heard of. You don't know how he knew about the affair, you were so careful. He has pictures though, and he's here to give them to you. He doesn't want money and he doesn't make threats. They're a gift, and a reminder that someone is always watching. He says he hopes he can call on you in the future, he doesn't say what for, and that you're prepared to do your patriotic duty. He is everything that ever frightened you about surveillance, about spy satellites, about drone strikes, about the invisible data in the air around you, and now you belong to him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T12:58:11-07:00","id":962952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=962947#post962947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugallu Tyrant<br /> <br /> The man in the aviators regards you coolly. Your eyes keep being drawn the patches on his jacket, covered in eagle insignia for branches of the military you've never heard of. You don't know how he knew about the affair, you were so careful. He has pictures though, and he's here to give them to you. He doesn't want money and he doesn't make threats. They're a gift, and a reminder that someone is always watching. He says he hopes he can call on you in the future, he doesn't say what for, and that you're prepared to do your patriotic duty. He is everything that ever frightened you about surveillance, about spy satellites, about drone strikes, about the invisible data in the air around you, and now you belong to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that... is bloody terrifying. Good job!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T18:11:54-07:00","id":963025,"title":"","content":"As much story seeds as potential characters:<br /> <br /> 1)They know that tonight, one of them will be destroyed, and in spite of this, because of this, here they are.<br /> She's just a comedian, doing stand up in a seedy bar, but on the stage, she's so much more. She's a superpredator, the unchallenged mistress of her tiny domain. Everynight as part of her show she chooses someone, usually the more confident person in the room, and tear them apart right there in front of the audience, cruelly mocking, gleefully humiliating, striking at weak points, unveilling embarassing secrets, while the others laugh at her victim's misfortune, partly in relief at having been spared. This time.<br /> Even so, helplessly, inexorably, they come back night after night to see her, so irresistibly funny and charming, as she feeds on the ego of one of them, ripping it apart with cutting words and razor wit. Strangely, there hardly ever are any hard feelings, or so briefly they're barely worth mentioning. Maybe they forgive her. Maybe they love her. Or maybe, they're deprived of the very ability to resent her. She doesn't know. She doesn't care. She merely accepts the offered sacrifices as her due and feasts on the altar of her stage, under the applause of the herd.<br /> <br /> 2)Hearts have been disappearing. It took a while for the police and the press to understand what was going on, to find the link uniting the theft of trinkets, work of art and other objects to the gruesome mutilated animal corpses found recently. The culprit steals hearts or representations of hearts. Nobody ever saw anything. No picture, no video exists of the thief, even thouh some of the crimes were comitted in public places in broad daylight.<br /> It could be anybody. They could be anywhere. They could stike anytime. And what if objects or animal organs weren't enough for them anymore? Paranoia is spreading. People are taking more precautions. Tempers flares. The police increased its presence. In vain.The mayor's main adversary for the next election, a charismatic new politician, leaner and hungrier than the norm, is criticizing his lack of results, exacerbating tensions. Some civilians have decided to take matters into their own hands. From the shadows the thief watches, smiling. The municipal elections are in a few weeks. If all goes well, he'll steal the heart of the city.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T19:54:19-07:00","id":963057,"title":"","content":"<b>Namtaru Collector:</b> It is said that the original Gorgon had the power to turn men to stone if they gazed upon her visage. While this descendant may not actually petrify people, she has other ways of making men hard as rock. Gorgeous in human form and fiendishly sexy in your dreams (she is a succubus, after all), the Namtaru uses her sex appeal to swindle men out of their belongings. Her strategy is simple; after choosing her victim, she convinces them to partake in some light S&amp;M play, After tying them blindfolded to the bed, she rummages through their clothes and steals their valuables before sprinting off into the night! The men, she leaves naked and bound to be discovered in the morning, much to their shameful humiliation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T19:35:57-07:00","id":963489,"title":"","content":"The main antagonist from the cross over chronicle I'm STing is an Incarnate Ugallu Nemesis. Orphaned during the Second Intifada, she has come to embody the fear of collateral damage during war. Her Horror is a great bio mechanical hawk forged from implements of death, razor wire knits her flesh together, her talons are spears, and her screech an air raid siren. Targeting war profiteers, she makes them feel what it's like to live in the constant anxiety of a city under siege where a stray air strike could mean death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:48:54-07:00","id":966565,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering, what would be a good Family/Hunger for a con artist-type character? Maybe Ugallu, because of the &quot;knowing all the angles&quot; concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T21:36:06-07:00","id":966605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=966565#post966565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering, what would be a good Family/Hunger for a con artist-type character? Maybe Ugallu, because of the &quot;knowing all the angles&quot; concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any family, really: Anakim can be very cunning, Eshmaki and Namtaru very sneaky, Makara terribly silver-tongued, Ugallu very perceptive.<br /> As for Hungers: Tyrants might enjoy outwitting their prey, Ravagers might enjoy ruining them, Collectors would just be after the loot, Nemesis could swindle only bad guys, Predators could be about machinations and schemes targetting a specific person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T21:54:13-07:00","id":966613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=966565#post966565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering, what would be a good Family/Hunger for a con artist-type character? Maybe Ugallu, because of the &quot;knowing all the angles&quot; concept?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I actually posted that very character concept back on page 12 at the top, if you want to review my take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:02:32-07:00","id":966615,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I was thinking more of an old-time traveling flimflam artist, though. Probably someone who isn't as interested in making money as in the thrill of pulling a con.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:22:03-07:00","id":966811,"title":"","content":"I'd say Ugallu or Makara Tyrant with a focus on perception, charm and deception.then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:06:48-07:00","id":968983,"title":"","content":"Ivey knew he wanted a career in law enforcement from his fifth birthday onward, and dedicated his life to that goal; the FBI recruited him before he was even done with his college studies, and he had a prestigious road ahead of him... or would have, if he'd been willing to keep his nose out of trouble. Agent Ivey couldn't let justice get away from him, and after too many investigations into &quot;animal attacks&quot; and &quot;cold case missing persons reports&quot; that the higher-ups were too skeptical or too paid-off to humor, he faced a transfer to the crackpot Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit, to ride a desk with all the Mulders who believe in Bigfoot serial killers and UFO abductions. This didn't stop him from chasing the impossible, and when he was offered the chance to undertake the Wintergreen Procedure, he lept at the chance to become a better detective.<br /> <br /> The procedure was supposed to awakened his psychic potential; instead, it woke his true self up.<br /> <br /> It was a strangely comfortable homecoming, the monster replacing his heart settling in like an old friend instead of tearing its way through his soul. It's oddly patient for a Horror, willing to wait for the ideal moment to pass judgment and eat the guilty. Ivey wants to bring the criminals in for a fair trial and usually wins the battle of wills, but sometimes things spiral out of control and he has to kill in self-defense. Sometimes the especially weird cases tug at the threads of kinship, but those feelings make him incredibly uncomfortable, and he throws that disgust into being the best at his job he possibly can be.<br /> <br /> Even for a team full of psychics, nutjobs, and weirdos, Ivey stands out as the strange one. He's intense and laser-focused on bringing the bad guys in, and his knacks sure don't feel like the regular Teleinformatics to the rest of the team, but he gets the job done and is polite doing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:12:25-07:00","id":968988,"title":"","content":"That is awesome. What does his Horror look like, though? Oh, and what sort of lair does he have? Maybe something like a dungeon or courtroom, for the &quot;justice&quot; theme.<br /> <br /> It's also fun to take a folkloric monster and come up with a character who'd match with that as their Horror. A Book of Creatures is an awesome source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:16:26-07:00","id":968992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=968988#post968988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is awesome. What does his Horror look like, though? Oh, and what sort of lair does he have? Maybe something like a dungeon or courtroom, for the &quot;justice&quot; theme.<br /> <br /> It's also fun to take a folkloric monster and come up with a character who'd match with that as their Horror. A Book of Creatures is an awesome source.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I want him to have something so on-the-nose as a great big Anpu/Anubis or Ammut, but it's admittedly tempting. The Lair is equal parts crushing oubliette and harshly-lit, exposed plain with nowhere to hide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:22:06-07:00","id":968995,"title":"","content":"Speaking of combining Beast with conspiracies: a former chemtrail-sprayer pilot whose Horror is an aerial poison-spewing stingray. <br /> <br /> Just anything involving aerial poison-spewing stingrays, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:42:37-07:00","id":969004,"title":"","content":"This thread is making me realize that I don't have nearly enough pictures of fleshy classical monsters. Most of my collection is robots or abstract stuff, which works great for GMC but not so much for Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T08:57:26-07:00","id":975082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=968992#post968992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if I want him to have something so on-the-nose as a great big Anpu/Anubis or Ammut, but it's admittedly tempting. The Lair is equal parts crushing oubliette and harshly-lit, exposed plain with nowhere to hide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mental Image (may or may not fit):<br /> <br /> Their Lair is a glimmering glass tower rising over a blasted plain/desert. The approach leads one through a cramped, twisting labyrinth of tunnels that also double as dungeons. Rising up into the tower itself, a traveler finds darkness swapped with near-blinding light, refracted through the transparent glass walls. Inside the walls, visions of the observer's prior crimes play out, and accusations of those they've wronged seem to dance upon the wind. At the summit, a terrifying sphinx-like beast passes judgement with its two faces - one grim and stern, the other cruel and predatory. At its feet lay a pit of impossible darkness, where it throws the guilty... or perhaps the innocent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T23:37:39-07:00","id":978243,"title":"","content":"<b>Ugallu Predator:</b> The vampires know him all too well, for he counts them among his closest of kin. Nocturnal hunters that awaken with the setting sun, emerging to feed on the blood of their prey. He is not so different from his undead cousins, although perhaps a bit less subtle about it.<br /> <br /> His horror is a chiropteran monstrosity. A man sized bat that walks on two legs, using its needle sharp fangs to pierce its victim's flesh and sip at the blood that pools from their wound. With its attack successfully carried out, it spreads its wings to take to the sky, leaving no footprints with which to track its whereabouts.<br /> <br /> It's lair is like something out of a bad horror film. The moonless night leaves travelers in nearly pitch black darkness. A forest surrounds them in all direction, but the lack of foliage growing from the branches indicate it might be mid autumn, or perhaps winter seasons. There is only one noticeable building in the entire forest, a dilapidated church standing upon a hill. Unfortunately for those who attempt to seek shelter within, the Beast makes its nest inside the bell tower, and they're heading straight for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-29-2016, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:52:36-07:00","id":981632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=839410#post839410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugallu Ravager: He calls his Horror the Gremlin. Doesn't sound very intimidating does it? Nevertheless, those with secrets to hide fear both him and it. Unlike the Horrors of his boodmates, his is not some kind of dragon or giant of the kind that terrified neolithic cavemen and Sumerian villagers. His is a new fear. That of the ghost in the machine, of your helpers becoming your foes and the devices you trust your secrets to betraying you.<br /> <br /> In the world of flesh he's a hacker, one of the best. He can crack systems in minutes that others spend days chipping away at. He's in high demand from dozens of factions in the city, from the mafia to the police even to supernatural clades and covenants. Others would be long-gone, sacrificed to keep the secret. He's made sure that he knows his employer's secrets though. He keeps dozens of copies of them. Some on hard drives, some tucked away in the dark corners of the web. He uses them as a combination dead-man's switch and Sword of Damocles. They're his insurance, because if they off him he won't be there to stop the programs posting all of those juicy, juicy secrets for the world to see. He gorges on the fear that he causes, the fear of everything coming crashing down around you.<br /> <br /> And all it would take would be the press of a button.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just read the playtest version yesterday, and I was thinking up a gremlin-inspired Ugallu Ravager of my own, though she does like handing out Ruin as a form of Punishment. Might as well do <i>some</i> good with her powers.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> He looked up into the piercing light, trying to spot his assailant. White was all he saw. The ground, the sky. The omnipresent light burning his eyes denied him even the cover of shade. Something was lurking in the empty sky, but he couldn't look up for more than a glimpse, and at most he'd catch a form leaping between... what? The tops of buildings? Trees? White on white was all he saw, and everywhere he reached, he could only feel an endless expanse of polished white stone, without even a horizon to mark where it transitioned to sky.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm here to teach you a lesson. 'What are you?' CEO?&quot; She grinned at the fearful figure from her perch, &quot;Not anymore. Poisoning the locals' drinking water wasn't a wise move. Saving money isn't any good if the world knows you'd kill their precious children to buy another yacht. That's why I told them.&quot;<br /> <br /> He blubbered the usual insincere promises of atonement. This was not something to be forgiven.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nobility? There are no peasants here to serve you, and none of your friends from that club to pat you on the back for being born in the right family. What is a lord, or a count, or a duke if no one follows them?&quot;<br /> <br /> He finally discovered a pillar and began orbiting it by touch, trying to hide in its shadow. She leaped to the top of the short piece of cover, finally providing the darkness he was looking for. It would be no hiding place. He recoiled and ran, staggering in the void, flailing for something to hide behind.<br /> <br /> &quot;A business man? You were born into wealth! The only reason you're rich is because you were handed everything. You may have made calls and badgered people into doing your will, but you never made anything with your own hands. All you ever did with the companies you owned was strip away expenses, including the ones that made a profit in the long run.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't do this!&quot; He finally protested.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why not? Are you going to <i>sue</i> me? I don't see your army of lawyers. I don't see the judges you bought or the crooked cops you paid to look the other way. Even they don't want anything to do with you, anymore.&quot; But they'll get their turn, she thought. &quot;Let's try this from another angle. What do you have? You don't have friends like those lawyers to protect you. No advisors to tell you what to do for your own good or steer you away from your own stupidity. No kind strangers, since everyone knows what you did. Since they froze your accounts, you don't have any money. Those off shore accounts they don't know about? They're mine, now.&quot;<br /> <br /> She rushed towards him, bounding between feet and knuckles, and started tearing at his expensive clothes, &quot;No million dollar power suit to awe me into submission, Iron Man. No weapons. No body guards. I've stripped that all away from you. Without the accounts, these cards are just meaningless plastic. Your pocket change won't buy any mercy from me. Without all those illusions of power and wealth, you're just a weak. naked. monkey. All I see is a frail collection of skin and bones... Let's see what, <b>if anything</b>, is left after I strip you of <b>that. </b>My guess? Underneath it all, you're <b>nothing.</b> Look around. Nothing is my field of expertise.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:00:20-07:00","id":981640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=981632#post981632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just read the playtest version yesterday, and I was thinking up a gremlin-inspired Ugallu Ravager of my own, though she does like handing out Ruin as a form of Punishment. Might as well do <i>some</i> good with her powers.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> He looked up into the piercing light, trying to spot his assailant. White was all he saw. The ground, the sky. The omnipresent light burning his eyes denied him even the cover of shade. Something was lurking in the empty sky, but he couldn't look up for more than a glimpse, and at most he'd catch a form leaping between... what? The tops of buildings? Trees? White on white was all he saw, and everywhere he reached, he could only feel an endless expanse of polished white stone, without even a horizon to mark where it transitioned to sky.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm here to teach you a lesson. 'What are you?' CEO?&quot; She grinned at the fearful figure from her perch, &quot;Not anymore. Poisoning the locals' drinking water wasn't a wise move. Saving money isn't any good if the world knows you'd kill their precious children to buy another yacht. That's why I told them.&quot;<br /> <br /> He blubbered the usual insincere promises of atonement. This was not something to be forgiven.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nobility? There are no peasants here to serve you, and none of your friends from that club to pat you on the back for being born in the right family. What is a lord, or a count, or a duke if no one follows them?&quot;<br /> <br /> He finally discovered a pillar and began orbiting it by touch, trying to hide in its shadow. She leaped to the top of the short piece of cover, finally providing the darkness he was looking for. It would be no hiding place. He recoiled and ran, staggering in the void, flailing for something to hide behind.<br /> <br /> &quot;A business man? You were born into wealth! The only reason you're rich is because you were handed everything. You may have made calls and badgered people into doing your will, but you never made anything with your own hands. All you ever did with the companies you owned was strip away expenses, including the ones that made a profit in the long run.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't do this!&quot; He finally protested.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why not? Are you going to <i>sue</i> me? I don't see your army of lawyers. I don't see the judges you bought or the crooked cops you paid to look the other way. Even they don't want anything to do with you, anymore.&quot; But they'll get their turn, she thought. &quot;Let's try this from another angle. What do you have? You don't have friends like those lawyers to protect you. No advisors to tell you what to do for your own good or steer you away from your own stupidity. No kind strangers, since everyone knows what you did. Since they froze your accounts, you don't have any money. Those off shore accounts they don't know about? They're mine, now.&quot;<br /> <br /> She rushed towards him, bounding between feet and knuckles, and started tearing at his expensive clothes, &quot;No million dollar power suit to awe me into submission, Iron Man. No weapons. No body guards. I've stripped that all away from you. Without the accounts, these cards are just meaningless plastic. Your pocket change won't buy any mercy from me. Without all those illusions of power and wealth, you're just a weak. naked. monkey. All I see is a frail collection of skin and bones... Let's see what, <b>if anything</b>, is left after I strip you of <b>that. </b>My guess? Underneath it all, you're <b>nothing.</b> Look around. Nothing is my field of expertise.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool character design. Kudos to you. What kind of shape does her Horror take, out of curiosity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:12:07-07:00","id":981646,"title":"","content":"I was thinking a sort of hybrid arboreal beast, part gorilla to remind humanity of their origins and the raw animalistic strengths they gave up in favor of layers of social and technological strength, and how easily those things can be stripped away. Combines fear of exposure to the elements with the destruction of all the infrastructure that comfortably protects us from the savage world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:18:58-07:00","id":981650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=981646#post981646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking a sort of hybrid arboreal beast, part gorilla to remind humanity of their origins and the raw animalistic strengths they gave up in favor of layers of social and technological strength, and how easily those things can be stripped away. Combines fear of exposure to the elements with the destruction of all the infrastructure that comfortably protects us from the savage world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of like a gibbon-gorilla hybrid? Perhaps a baboonish head? Those fangs are bloody terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:36:47-07:00","id":981662,"title":"","content":"Namtaru or Eshmaki Predator - a creature that steals people's pets, never to be seen again, and feeds off their fear and grief for the beloved animal.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a Namtaru that robs from well-loved graves and violates places of worship, drawing on the fear and disgust from the desecration of the sacrosanct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:02:57-07:00","id":981679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=981646#post981646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking a sort of hybrid arboreal beast, part gorilla to remind humanity of their origins and the raw animalistic strengths they gave up in favor of layers of social and technological strength, and how easily those things can be stripped away. Combines fear of exposure to the elements with the destruction of all the infrastructure that comfortably protects us from the savage world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wings optional, for flying monkey?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:57:27-07:00","id":982150,"title":"","content":"So, has anyone done a crowded city as a take on the Cramped and/or Currents traits? The pressing mass of people are obviously just animate scenery, but they should be able to simulate the prior effects.<br /> <br /> Any other ideas for Traits or just narrative aspects that could be tacked on to a Lair that is &quot;populated&quot; by bland or faceless crowds of people?<br /> <br /> Or what the Horror of such a Lair might be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:47:12-07:00","id":982581,"title":"","content":"<b><u>I came up with this character during my Homecoming story I posted up here a while ago. But didn't really flesh out what his hunger was.</u></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Makara Collector:</b> Mysteries both ancient and occult are the forte of this abhorrent creature. Though it is no mage, it has its own breed of dark magics that were never intended to be wielded by mortal hands. At times, the mages have even come to seek its counsel on their own research, an honor that it takes great pride in, despite its attempts to maintain a stoic front about it. Its lair is a city of stone carved into unnatural architecture. The city itself is completely submerged inside cloudy, green water that obscures the vision of anything beyond your immediate surroundings. The water allows for movement along both the X and Y axis, which is required in order to navigate the stone architecture. Clearly this city was not built with idea of humans maintaining residence, but something more alien and complex.<br /> <br /> <br /> Humans don't have a name for his Horror yet, it is to obscene for it to have been classified as an identifiable species. It's skin is pale green and clammy with sea slime. It walks upon four legs with webbed feet that end in needle sharp claws. An elongated, flexible torso grows up from the center where the four legs join together. Atop the torso is a bulbous head shaped like that of an octopus with solid black eyes and a clacking beak for a mouth. Along the length of the torso is a swarming mass of tentacles so dense that it frequently obscures the body from view. Possessing so many limbs allows it to multitask on a level that no natural human could replicate. Reading dozens of books at a time, concocting multiple scientific formulas, or performing complex rituals that are beyond the limits of human anatomy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T08:02:57-07:00","id":986767,"title":"","content":"Head's up: this will later be Edited into more coherent/Detailed descriptions.<br /> <br /> One of mine is a pretty straightforward example: an Anakim Predator thug for the mob who feeds by breaking people (preferably their bones, but their home and property is fine, too) and who also is very ambitious and extremely loyal to his Family.<br /> His Horror is a Giant metal golem, his Lair an industrial forge, with huge fires and vats of acid. Atavisms are Looming, Unbreakable and relentless.<br /> I started with some Full metal Alchemist and X-Men's Collosus (Shows in e.g. Names and loyalty), but later switched to T-1000 and Went From there.<br /> <br /> What about the Ugallu investigative Reporter who Ruins politicians, corrupt cops and ceos by uncovering their secrets? He is Not a nemesis, but a ravager, since the goal is not the punishment of wicked deeda, but rather the loss of trust and following Paranoia of the community. His Horror, a Manticore, is just as poisonous as the words he uses to discredit his victims. If legal means are not available, he won't shy away from breaking in through unlikely routes, and making pictures if necessary, Like some evil Peter parker.<br /> The Lair is a Sahara-like , blinding desert whipped by strong winds with a Single steep stone in the middle, atop which the manticore rests, keeping a lookout for prey to stalk to death.<br /> <br /> Another one is the Petty Beast, A Eshmaki ravager who feeds by ruining The festive Mood Of People by stealing or breaking Anything That Is representative of the festival, Teaching that evil does never stop, and that even during the Holy days, there is no respite or reason To Feel save.<br /> yes, it's a Grinch-Beast ^^&quot;<br /> The Lair is a dark cave, the tiniest Sound creating a cascade of echoes, the floor strewn with tripping stones and stalagmites.<br /> <br /> Sorry for weird typing and short sentences, I am writing on my phone and not liking it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  next edit 10-14-2016, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T16:43:41-07:00","id":987006,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> Ah shucks, you took part of my idea. Great minds must think alike. I was just working on an Anakim Predator thug who kills people for the mob too. His Horror is a terrible pseudo-reptilian behemoth shrouded in an impenetrable darkness. His Lair is a deep, lightless pit filled with the stench of his victims' half-eaten corpses from which none can escape - as if it were the creature's maw. Atavisms are Cyclopean Strength, Looming Presence, Shadowed Soul, and Unbreakable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:15:30-07:00","id":987022,"title":"","content":"<b>Eshmaki Ravager:</b> Change is something that everybody fears, even if they don't admit it. Normalcy makes people feel comfortable, and when you introduce something new to the equation, they reflexively become agitated and paranoid. This Beast feeds on that fear, visiting nice, orderly environments and introducing something new, something that did not exist before. And when his victims realize something is out of place, they get scared. Maybe not enough to cause a panic, but enough to keep him satisfied.<br /> <br /> His horror is a chimera, an amalgamation of different species that should not exist together. But unlike the classical Greek interpretation, where the animals are simply merged onto the same body, his parts blend seamlessly together. To an untrained eye, it becomes difficult to tell where one species ends and the other begins, as it exists in a perfectly hybridized state. He appears to have the genetic makeup of a tiger, a gorilla, a crocodile, and a bull.<br /> <br /> <br /> His lair is as equally confusing as his horror. An outdoor habitat which blends together environments that should not exist together in the real world. To those not experienced in traversing it, the unnatural landscape becomes disorienting to navigate, much less survive in. How do you know what plants are safe to eat when the plants are taken from over a dozen ecosystems? You think you can hear a pack of wolves howling along the sea bed floor at night. And is that a school of sharks moving through the clouds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-13-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:15:25-07:00","id":987336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=987006#post987006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Ah shucks, you took part of my idea. Great minds must think alike. I was just working on an Anakim Predator thug who kills people for the mob too. His Horror is a terrible pseudo-reptilian behemoth shrouded in an impenetrable darkness. His Lair is a deep, lightless pit filled with the stench of his victims' half-eaten corpses from which none can escape - as if it were the creature's maw. Atavisms are Cyclopean Strength, Looming Presence, Shadowed Soul, and Unbreakable.</div> </div> </div> </div>:-D I am always happy when others have ideas like me; I'm pretty New to all this, so it makes me feel I'm on the right track, therefore thanks! <br /> Also, I like your concept and feel like there is even enough of a difference to have them in the same brood!<br /> After all, mine is more an unstoppable thug sent to collect money/sent a message. Yours feels more like the love Child of L\u00e9on the professional and Killer Croc, an unseen hitman sent to make the targets into a message themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T15:50:43-07:00","id":987473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?view=stream&p=987336#post987336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> :-D I am always happy when others have ideas like me; I'm pretty New to all this, so it makes me feel I'm on the right track, therefore thanks!<br /> Also, I like your concept and feel like there is even enough of a difference to have them in the same brood!<br /> After all, mine is more an unstoppable thug sent to collect money/sent a message. Yours feels more like the love Child of L\u00e9on the professional and Killer Croc, an unseen hitman sent to make the targets into a message themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually frightfully compatible. Which is awesome, because it shows how even Beasts of the same Family and Hunger can achieve interesting synergy without too much overlap through differences in feeding preference, out-of-Family Atavism choices, and Lair Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T02:26:53-07:00","id":988193,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hq6DaeO6SCw\" target=\"_blank\">So i Saw this.. A Beast with a Mirror into the Human Soul for a Face?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T04:34:32-07:00","id":988207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?view=stream&p=988193#post988193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hq6DaeO6SCw\" target=\"_blank\">So i Saw this.. A Beast with a Mirror into the Human Soul for a Face?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. A Namtaru for sure, with Behold, My True Form! and Tabula Rasa for Nightmares. I'm not sure about Atavisms though. Perhaps Mimir's Wisdom and Shadowed Soul, for how she knows exactly where the room is and for how it darkens before she uses Behold, My True Form!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 10-16-2016, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T06:26:57-07:00","id":988223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?view=stream&p=987473#post987473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is actually frightfully compatible. Which is awesome, because it shows how even Beasts of the same Family and Hunger can achieve interesting synergy without too much overlap through differences in feeding preference, out-of-Family Atavism choices, and Lair Traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I think in General the character concept and how it is fleshed out is more important than the x y z splat axis (same atavisms and hunger, but one feeds through illegal activities Like our concepts, while another does so legally as a fighter or soldier). However that would lead to less synergy and more conflict within a brood (sweet, sweet conflict xD)<br /> Even with in-family atavisms, there is a big difference between a physical anakim with a Titanic blow and Cyclopean Strength combination (fits with e.g. thugs, bankrobbers) and a social focused one with Mimir's Wisdom and Looming height (Interrogating cop or a lawyer could make use of that).<br /> <br /> Btw, our brood was to have another anakim (tyrant) who would have been a corrupt cop who'd feed on lording over others. Your hitman, my thug, that cop... Throw in an Anakim tyrant lawyer, and we're good :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:36:38-07:00","id":990559,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.scified.com/articles/yet-more-monsterarts--shin-godzilla-revealed-set-for-release-this-december-19.png\" target=\"_blank\">What would the King of Monsters be?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:44:43-07:00","id":990567,"title":"","content":"Eshmaki or Makara, probably. <br /> <br /> &quot;Evil ringmaster&quot; would be a great Beast concept. It has a lot of crossover potential, in the ringmaster assembling a group of monsters and weirdos as &quot;talents&quot;. We talked about a ChroD version of the midnight circus on the forum, and one of the ideas I liked for that was having a really twisted Beast in charge. Maybe a Namtaru, because the &quot;creepy carnival&quot; theme goes well with shock and revulsion as methods of inducing horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-20-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:48:50-07:00","id":990571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?view=stream&p=990559#post990559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.scified.com/articles/yet-more-monsterarts--shin-godzilla-revealed-set-for-release-this-december-19.png\" target=\"_blank\">What would the King of Monsters be?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a Ravager.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T00:56:21-07:00","id":990842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?view=stream&p=990559#post990559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.scified.com/articles/yet-more-monsterarts--shin-godzilla-revealed-set-for-release-this-december-19.png\" target=\"_blank\">What would the King of Monsters be?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly a Ugallu Nemesis or Tyrant. Of the 2 I'd go for Nemesis for the Original and Tyrant for the later incarnations.<br /> This is mostly because of the themes of the original were more in line with that.. what with being the Embodiment of &quot;What man has Wrought&quot;, The later versions/ones only really woke up or went on a Rampage when something else was harming it's &quot;Territory&quot;... behaviour of a Apex Tyrant i'd say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T04:54:13-07:00","id":990898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?view=stream&p=990559#post990559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.scified.com/articles/yet-more-monsterarts--shin-godzilla-revealed-set-for-release-this-december-19.png\" target=\"_blank\">What would the King of Monsters be?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Anakim Ravager with Anakim, Eshmaki, Namtaru and Makara Atavisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:10:39-07:00","id":991940,"title":"","content":"He's a psychopath. That's what the psychiatrist said when he was 12, before she was paid a truly magnificent son by his parents to keep it quiet. She just wrote 'genius' on the psych evaluation, and that was true as well. He's just thought of the whole thing like a cosmic joke. Make him a genius so that any intellectual entertainment is short-lived and then a psychopath so that emotions don't offer any interest either. He entered the corporate sphere, just as his parents had hoped, but not for their sake. He just did it hoping that the Board might make his life a bit harder, provide him something to play against. That lasted all of a month, before he'd bankrupted each and every one of them and replaced them with people who actually did their jobs. Then he went for the top spot. Becoming CEO consumed half a year - the longest he'd ever had fun for - and then that was it. Then he went on to working on other companies, hoping that they'd put up a challenge. Some did, but the ones he could go for lasted only so long. He seemed to be cursed to while away his life in utter boredom.<br /> <br /> Until <i>It</i> came. <br /> <br /> That night, when the thing he'd always seen in his dreams, the giant-king, finally ate him up and became him. Finally, he had something to <i>do</i>. Where before he had simply been empty, now he was <i>hungry</i> . And hunger could be sated. He'd take the utmost pleasure in doing so.<br /> <br /> Anakim Tyrant, obviously, probably with Looming Presence and Mimir's Wisdom for Atavisms and You Must Obey and a reskinned You Can't Take It With You for Nightmares, the latter reflecting the fact that the victim <i>knows</i> that no matter what they do, the monster has the money and power to counter it, so they don't even try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:41:08-07:00","id":992465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?view=stream&p=547449#post547449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of a few character concepts:<br /> <br /> -A vigilante Eshmaki Nemesis working at a women's shelter. She makes sure that abusive partners are punished for their actions, again and again. She never kills them, not even when they beg her to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, I came up with a character just like this! There are differences though; my version is a devout christian whose beast is a vicious, demonic hellhound, hungry to punish those who betray their obligations and responsibilities. She tries to mesh her faith with her new nature, eventually coming to terms with it, realizing that she and Beast like her are Gods way of punishing the wicked, reminding them that sins have consequences. Her favorite prey are domestic abusers. She volunteers at a womens shelter, listening to the stories of the women and children in her care. She remembers them, and when her Hunger begins to gnaw at her, she goes into the night, says a prayer and reminds the abuser that that God is always watching, and his servants are everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T22:30:06-07:00","id":994414,"title":"","content":"This Makara Tyrant is really good with computers, and working at the college 's IT support provides a lot of opportunity to feed and teach the importance of Being prepared. Having basically unrestricted access to any Laptop on campus, he deletes Files at his leisure, often targeting documents carrying &quot;Thesis&quot; in their title (Especially if there is no backup), but installing a thousand toolbars or cutting off your Internet access during a game are not beneath him, either. If you have only minimum protection, he will log into your social media and do emberassing things there, or simply share your 'private' conversations and information. Occasionally, he goes all the way, causing permanent bluescreens, regular Crashes and the like. When inevitably they come to him for help, he will restore everything back to normal - While Holding A Sermon on IT security. If you are a repeat offender though, you might have to start working on your paper from scratch- no one said lessons are cheap.<br /> <br /> His Horror is a brain-sucking slug, his Lair a dusty, dark library, books half-rotten strewn And stacked on the ground. He has the &quot;all your teeth are falling out&quot; and &quot;you will never rest&quot; nightmares and the Monster from the deep and Relentless Hunter atavisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  typo 10-28-2016, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T17:44:48-08:00","id":1002406,"title":"","content":"He had always been a man of God, and he sought to lead his flock by example. His lifestyle was frugal, he acted with honesty in all affairs and all were welcome in his church. Despite all of this, he suffered from recurring nightmares where his church would be overtaken by an all-seeing demonic figure. His former followers would sign their names on a book the demon was carrying in exchange for having the chains around them broken.<br /> <br /> At first he was unable to interpret the meaning of this nightmare, and brushed it off. But the people who followed him diminished in number as the years passed, some under mysterious circumstances. When he went to investigate what had happened to them, he discovered the once faithful had turned to witchcraft and displayed terrifying reality-altering powers. Unable to convince them to abandon this heresy, he began researching what aspect of the occult attracted his lost lambs. Each night he'd stay awake in libraries and online, until he found out that his city was a nexus of occult phenomena. Fearing that this was caused by the dwindling number of faithful, he took it upon himself to eliminate these mysteries and bring back people to the righteous path.<br /> <br /> However, try as he might, it was impossible to fight back witchcraft with the tools of common men. He decided to fight fire with fire and started a Mystery Cult with the intent of gathering Relics in the hopes of banishing the curse from his city. What happened instead was that his cult attracted the attention of a Beast who worked with the witches. The Beast invited the priest to an occult gathering, promising to show him the truth if priest would hand over his relics and cultists to the witches. After much deliberation, the priest accepted, and the Beast returned the favor by Devouring him. That night, the priest dreamt of the demon again, but recognized that it was no servant of the Devil, but a part of his own being that represented his urge to control other people.<br /> <br /> Accepting that this monster was him, he merged with it, becoming an Ugallu Tyrant. His talent for leadership was noticed by a Mastigos who belonged to a group of witches called the Silver Ladder. They offered him the chance to prove himself so he might join their ranks and keep protecting the members of his flock, which he managed to do. Nowadays, his view of religion has been both expanded and confused, and he struggles with maintaining his honor while feeding his Hunger. Despite this, he is determined to teach a lesson to whoever falls into Hubris: you lead by example, not force.<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Mimir\u2019s Wisdom, Needs Must, Eye Of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Nightmares: We Know All Your Secrets, You Must Obey","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-12-2016, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T01:17:01-08:00","id":1003285,"title":"","content":"<b>Anakim Tyrant: </b>Speed. That's all that mattered, once upon a time. He was a racer, but not good enough to get into the big leagues. He made do, though, with the thrill of speed from backstreet racing, pushing his second-hand Mercades as fast as it could go and revelling in the acceleration. That lasted until the accident. A misjudged turn, a foot just a hair too far down on the accelerator and he was waking up in hospital with an amputated leg and a cocktail of chemicals bringing him in and out of consciousness.<br /> He lay there in the hospital bed, half alive, and wondered. What would he do now? When he slept, though, he dreamt of driving and of the huge beast in the rear view mirror, a vaguely feline outline with exhaust smoke curling from its jaws and white LED headlights for eyes. He dreamt of driving as fast as he could and yet it always caught him, ending the dream with a steel claw tearing his little vehicle in two.<br /> Eventually, though, after he'd ben discharged with a carbon fibre leg and gotten hold of a car he could drive, he tired of running. That night, he turned the car around and charged the beast, thinking that if he was going to go out again, he'd make it hurt this time. Instead, he saw the joy in its eyes, that he had finally faced it and this time when it devoured him, he looked out through its eyes and roared in the voice of a living engine.<br /> Now it's not speed he cares for, but beating others, showing them that even though he's down a leg, he's still better than them.<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Looming Presence, Inescapable, Unbreakable, Relentless Hunter<br /> Nightmares: You Must Flee, You Cannot Run","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T11:30:13-08:00","id":1005040,"title":"","content":"Inspired by the eternal 'the homeless won't be missed and are prey for the monsters of the night' trope.<br /> <br /> <b>Ugallu Predator:</b> He's been on the streets for as long as he can remember, and he's seen everything that hides in the shadows. He's spoken with vampires, informed mages, pointed werewolves on their way and hidden from monsters that chase half-men through the night. He's dealt with spirits and counselled the ghosts of less fortunate vagrants. And that was all before the bat-monster ate up his soul and made a nest in the remnants.<br /> Now he's got the strength to deal on an equal footing with the other denizens of the night and he makes use of it. He protects the rest of the guys on the streets, as best he can. He can't keep them all safe, but he can teach them to keep themselves from harm. By day he tells them what he wishes he knew when he was younger, the stuff he had to learn the hard way. How to ward of a ghost and what names to drop when a fella with pale skin and too-sharp teeth comes wandering around.<br /> By night, though, he notes the ones who don't believe him and gives them an introduction to the shadow world. He waits til they're asleep, then he opens up his lair, a crumbling, gothic city, and brings them in. He watches them wake up to a neverending moonlit night and burning eyes watching them from the rooftops. He watches them run from him until they can run no more until, when they collapse from exhaustion, he gives them a bite to remember him by and dumps them out in the waking world, scared but hopefully wiser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T13:40:36-08:00","id":1005085,"title":"","content":"[Anakim or Ugallu]: Its lair is a labyrinthine warren of tattered house walls, brick, drywall, and plaster all blending into one another. Amidst the dimly lit debris, you can smell something almost sickly sweet. Right when you think you've found the way out, the Horror bursts through the walls as if they were cardboard. It stands before you, corpulent, rounded, with transparent flesh and filled with sloshing red liquid. As it sees you, it gloats:<br /> <br /> <sup><sub><b><i>Oh, yeah!</i></b></sub></sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T13:50:26-08:00","id":1005087,"title":"","content":"<b>Anakim Tyrant + Collector:</b> The wisdom he he wants to share is simple: raw supernatural power doesn't make you a giant among men. It's the capacity to get back up after taking a beating and learn from your mistakes that separates you from the common folk. Case in point, he works as a martial arts instructor for anyone who is willing to suffer through his demanding but rewarding methods. He watches his pupils closely for signs of both physical and psychological weakness, and hones them into warriors. Not a single one of his pupils have been used to mop the floor when faced with an opponent who relies on supernatural tricks to impose their will on others. <br /> <br /> But that is not enough to satisfy his dual Hunger. He holds a secret tournament inside his arena Lair. Only supernaturals and mortals in the know are allowed to enter. Those who make it to the finals get to fight the instructor himself in his Horror form, a towering multi-armed ogre with a single piercing eye that knows your next attack before you do. Those who lose must give an object they worked extremely hard to obtain, though he prefers supernatural weapons that some think are enough to beat him. Those who win are allowed to pick anything from his hoard and have their faces carved on the walls of fame inside his Lair. All who participate later enjoy a feast cooked by the instructor himself, so they can restore their energy and share what they have learned. He uses this feast as an opportunity to bring people together and create new Family Ties. After all, all warriors are his Kin.<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Looming Presence, Cyclopean Strength, Relentless Hunter, Needs Must, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> Nightmares: Behold My True Form, You Cannot Kill It, Your Tools Betray You","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T21:01:26-08:00","id":1005968,"title":"","content":"<b>Makara Nemesis:</b> She lives in the woods. Some say she is a secretly a witch, and they're not too far off. Choosing to make her home there wasn't a whim. Hungry and alien shades lurk just beyond the sight of mortals, and the barrier that separates their realm from ours is weaker in the places that are farther away from civilization. She acts as a diplomat and law enforcer for both realms. To mortals, she is a guardian of esoteric laws and verges of spiritual activity, always on the lookout for those who would disrespect or desecrate them. To the spirits, she is a rogue element who knows their names and weaknesses, and is more than willing to put her knowledge to use in banishing them should their predation go too far.<br /> <br /> The lesson she wants to teach is that people have become too prone to dismissing evidence of the unseen on their lives. She wants people to know that the gods and fiends are all too real, and teach them the difference between superstition and the true laws of the other side. This duty she imposed upon herself attracted the attention of the local Uratha, who have come to see her as a useful if strange ally.<br /> <br /> When not protecting the balance between the realms, she makes a modest living by selling fruit, wood carvings and remedies she growns in her own garden. She does take in visitors, and likes it when people listen to her retellings of folklore that most have forgotten. Just be careful when you ask her about the Fetishes. She does sell them, but God help you if you misuse them.<br /> <br /> Her Horror is a humanoid tree covered in lurid carvings of powerful spirits. Occult items of bone, leather and stone dangle from its many limbs, each one a Fetish given to her by werewolves whose hunts she assisted. The bark is pitch-black, save for the eyes, which glows like twin moons that emit a ghastly mist.<br /> <br /> Atavisms: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817829#post817829\"><b>Witchwood</b></a>, Monster From The Deep, Unbreakable, Looming Presence, Eye Of Heaven","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-27-2016, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T23:37:32-08:00","id":1006022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1005968#post1005968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Makara Nemesis:</b> She lives in the woods. Some say she is a secretly a witch, and they're not too far off. Choosing to make her home there wasn't a whim. Hungry and alien shades lurk just beyond the sight of mortals, and the barrier that separates their realm from ours is weaker in the places that are farther away from civilization. She acts as a diplomat and law enforcer for both realms. To mortals, she is a guardian of esoteric laws and verges of spiritual activity, always on the lookout for those who would disrespect os desecrate them. To the spirits, she is a rogue element who knows their names and weaknesses, and is more than willing to put her knowledge to use in banishing them should their predation go too far.<br /> <br /> The lesson she wants to teach is that people have become too prone to dismissing evidence of the unseen on their lives. She wants people to know that the gods and fiends are all too real, and and teach them the difference between superstition and the true laws of the other side. This duty she imposed upon herself attracted the attention of the local Uratha, who have come to see her as a useful if strange ally.<br /> <br /> When not protecting the balance between the realms, she makes a modest living by selling fruit, wood carvings and remedies she growns in her own garden. She does take in visitors, and likes it when people listen to her retellings of folklore that most have forgotten. Just be careful when you ask her about the Fetishes. She does sell them, but God help you if you misuse them.<br /> <br /> Her Horror is a humanoid tree covered in lurid carvings of powerful spirits. Occult items of bone, leather and stone dangle from its many limbs, each one a Fetish given to her by werewolves whose hunts she assisted. The bark is pitch-black, save for the eyes, which glows like twin moons that emit a ghastly mist.<br /> <br /> Atavisms: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817829#post817829\"><b>Witchwood</b></a>, Monster From The Deep, Unbreakable, Looming Presence, Eye Of Heaven</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I feel flattered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T15:22:45-08:00","id":1006881,"title":"","content":"an Ugallu Nemesis paparazzi, who enjoys taking down the careers of celebrities who think their fame and wealth make them immune to punishment. Normally he just sneaks around and takes film of them at their absolute worst, raking in the cash and feeding his horror as their most terrible sins are exposed, but in one case he pretended to be a teen idol's friend and helped her escape from his fellow paparazzi before kidnapping her and selling her as meat to a dark mother worshiping cannibal cult in the mountains, but his defense she was twisted in a way the press and courts wouldn't be able to deal with. She isn't the only famous sinner he has punished in a permanent fashion, but does prefer that his prey's sins be public knowledge, as his horror does love seeing his prey exposed and defenseless from the angry mobs, police investigations and lawsuits that follows it's exposes.<br /> <br /> His horror is a giant predatory insect with segmented camera lenses for eyes and razor segmented arms holding microphones in the top two claws, that stalks it's prey from the towering heights of the dark reflection of Los Angeles that is it's lair, a literal fly on the wall just watching and recording, waiting to scoop up and devour it's famous prey and make them another one of Hollywood's public meltdowns or unsolved crimes before he writes a book about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 11-22-2016, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T08:57:19-08:00","id":1011105,"title":"","content":"<b>Ugallu Ravager:</b> Susan used to be normal. Just another small-town girl with lower-than average grades looking for a way in the world. She dreamed, though. In her dreams, she ran across an endless plain, grass as far as the eye could see, with a firestorm chasing at her heels. Then, one night on the way back from remedial classes, she saw Adam, a transfer from someplace no-one had heard of getting beaten on by a bunch of the steroid-using 'jocks'. Except that didn't last long. Adam was usually a nice, quiet kid, but this time he'd had enough. Eyes burning, he grabbed one of the jocks and sent him flying, before lightning peeled away his skin and revealed the sewn-together horror beneath. Two of the jocks spent the next few moths in a body-cast and another never made it back home. He didn't notice her, though, and she went to sleep that night with her mind whirling.<br /> When the flames came, though, this time she didn't run. She faced them and raged with fury to match them. The two blazes joined and merged, blazing all the higher for their union, and when she awoke again it was with of fire and storm in her soul.<br /> The next day she went to the camper where Adam was staying. She talked to him and he told her about what he was, a stitched-together man made from corpses and lightning, with a soul that burned too hot. So she showed him the fire in her soul, and within the week they were gone together, on their way to the next town over with a pocket full of cash.<br /> <br /> <u>Atavisms:</u> Dragonfire, Storm-Lashed, Untouchable<br /> <u>Nightmares:</u> Run Away, You Deserve This<br /> <br /> <u>Lair:</u> Extreme Heat, Burning<br /> <br /> Susan Brand's Lair has two Chambers, besides the Heart. The Heart of her Lair is the same burning plain that she once ran across, while the other two Chambers are the farm of a farmer who Adam once worked for and who tried to kill him once the Disquiet set in, while the other is her old house, which she occasionally uses to return home.<br /> <br /> <u>Horror:</u> Susan's Horror is a formless, blazing mass of fire and the gale-winds it kicks up, almost indistinguishable from the fires of the Lair itself. Sometimes faces of ravenous beasts or claws stretch out of the conflagration. Ultimately, her Horror is more a force than it is a creature, and it is more than happy to blaze its way out of her soul and into the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T15:28:42-08:00","id":1015870,"title":"","content":"<b>Ugallu Punisher:</b> Spider-Man, Spider-Man, does whatever a spider can!<br /> <br /> Spins a web, any size. Catches thieves just like flies!<br /> <br /> Look out, here comes the Spider-Man!<br /> <br /> <br /> Is he strong? Listen bud, he's got radioactive blood!<br /> <br /> Can he swing, from a thread? Take a look, overhead!<br /> <br /> Hey there, there goes the Spider-Man!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the chill of night, at the scene of a crime!<br /> <br /> Like a streak of light, he arrives just in time!<br /> <br /> Spider-Man, Spider-Man, friendly neighborhood Spider-Man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-11-2016, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T08:19:28-08:00","id":1017080,"title":"","content":"<b>Namtaru Ravager:</b> She's a witch, I tell you! No, not like those Awakened folks, I mean the kind of witch that backwoods peasants tell their children about to keep them from misbehaving. They say the filthy hag lives deep in the woods, but nobody's ever been able to find out exactly where. <i>Not unless she wants you to find her.</i> <b>Not unless she drags you there, herself!</b> But she's not just any practitioner of the dark arts, oh no, that would be far too convenient for us! You see, she's become rather addicted to the black arts, and uses it on the good people of this town purely for the sake of her own entertainment. A prankster at the best of times, and a sadistic fiend at any other, the lucky ones manage to get off with simply being tormented or killed. The unlucky ones, those poor bastards, they're the ones she decides to take home with her, the ones she transforms with her magic, <b>turning men into Beasts!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T21:54:28-08:00","id":1017496,"title":"","content":"Went ahead and ordered Beast and 2nd Edition Core book for Christmas presents. Hopefully I'll be able to think of some more fleshed out characters in a few weeks. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T17:00:58-08:00","id":1018263,"title":"","content":"<b>\u200bAnakim Tyrant</b><br /> <br /> He sits across the desk from you. He's leaning back in his seat, one foot resting on the other knee, fingers steepled, his expression relaxed and mildly curious. &quot;Tell me why you think you deserve to keep your job.&quot; Some people sit in horror of this modern-day king, stammering out limp excuses, trying to appeal to the better nature that doesn't exist. These people are fired on the spot, dismissed with a mocking, &quot;Have a nice day.&quot; Some others manage to work up the courage to respond, pointing to their accomplishment, fighting for the right to keep getting paychecks. These people get to keep their jobs- for now. Sooner or later, the company will have to make tough decisions, and he'll be the one sitting in judgement of the unlucky. And they'll have to prove themselves again- or suffer the consequences. <br /> <br /> He teaches people that they have to be their own heroes. Nobody is coming to save you, and power cannot be appealed to, only defied. <br /> <br /> His horror is a hulking ogre, cunning and cruel, holding court over a massively-scaled castle made of skeletons, filled with doors only he is strong enough to open, and traps that only he is clever enough to avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T00:22:38-08:00","id":1018368,"title":"","content":"This was inspired by the fairies from <i>Jonathan Strange and Mr. Norrel</i>, as well as their realm of Lost Hope.<br /> <br /> <b>Makara Nemesis:</b> His Horror takes the form of an ethereal fae lord and his Lair is the ruins of an ancient mansion, every flat surface bedecked with candles whose flames burn in impossible colours while faerie dancers twirl and waltz across the cracked floors and through the mirrors which bedeck the place, dancing between reality and reflections with no distinction made. Invaders to the Lair are swept into the dance, passed from one dancer to another in an endless waltz. Trying to strike out at one of them yields nothing, as no matter what is done they placidly twirl away from the assault.<br /> In the real world, he's a lawyer who gets brought in when contracts and deals are transgressed against. He's the one that makes sure that those who break their word never do so again, no matter their reasons or motivations for doing so. It might be childish, but he's always believed that a promise given is a promise true, and such covenants should be kept. He holds himself to the same standards, after all, so he can't be called a hypocrite. When he gets really hungry, though, he'll take one of the oath-breakers into one of his mirrors, and he'll leave them there, trapped in a reflection-realm until they agree to whatever he asks them to, in order to get out. Then he watches them, and if they break their word, he takes them again, this time into his Lair, and they join the dance, never to leave.<br /> <br /> <u>Atavisms:</u> Alien Allure, Through the Looking Glass*<br /> <br /> <u>Nightmares:</u> You Cannot Run, You Made a Deal**<br /> <br /> <u>Lair:</u> Currents, Mirages<br /> <br /> *<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><u><b>Through the Looking Glass (Ugallu)</b></u></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Reflections are everywhere in the modern world. Windows, video screens, puddles after rainfall, everywhere. People spend years looking into mirrors, making sure that their face is just right, that they are \u2018beautiful\u2019. People trust mirrors, because when you look into one, you know that what looks back at you is just a reflection.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Except when it\u2019s not. When you look into a mirror and something <i>other </i></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">looks back. When all of those reflections are the </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>thing\u2019s </i>eyes and every mirror is a door that it can step through. When that happens, where can you hide?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> None</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Action: </span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">None</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast can step into any reflective surface which is large enough to fit him, entering a world which such Beasts call Mirrorspace. Mirrorspace itself is completely black and empty, the only points of light being the Beast himself and other reflective surfaces, which appear as \u2018windows\u2019 looking out into the real world. These \u2018windows\u2019 are in the same position as they would be in real life (a puddle is on the floor, a bathroom mirror hangs suspended in the air at head height) and show what they would reflect in the real world (the mirror would show a bathroom, the puddle the sky). While the Beast is looking out of a mirror, his reflection appears in its real-world counterpart. </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Beast can only enter and exit Mirrorspace through the same reflection that he used to enter it and always knows the direction and distance to that reflection. Each Beast enters their own Mirrorspace and never encounters another Beast within it. Items can be brought into Mirrorspace so long as the beast is holding them. Items <i>can</i> be left in Mirrorspace but only last a number of days equal to the Beast\u2019s (Lair + Composure) before vanishing. It is unknown where these items go. The exception to this is within the Lair, where items can remain within a mirror for as long as desired by the Beast.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Beasts can only exit Mirrorspace via the same reflection through which they entered and should that reflection be destroyed the Beast is immediately ejected from Mirrorspace and is subject to the Stunned tilt. A Beast inside Mirrorspace can smash one of the 'windows', destroying its real-life counterpart.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Low Satiety:</b> As the Beast's hunger grows, he becomes able to access aspects of the Mirrorspace that he otherwise could not. In this case, he gains the ability to exit Mirrorspace through any reflection big enough to fit him. He still has to travel to the mirror physically but is no longer ejected if the point of entry is destroyed.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Satiety Expenditure: </span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">With the expenditure of a dot of Satiety, the Beast can bring another with them into Mirrorspace, leaving them trapped there until the Beast retrieves them. Mortals in Mirrorspace do not need food, drink or sleep and do not age. However, after a number of years equal to the Beast's Lair at the time when the victim was trapped, the victim is ejected from Mirrorspace into a random world. They could end up in the mortal world, Arcadia, the Shadow, the Hedge or any other world.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> **<br /> <br /> <b><u>You Made a Deal (Changeling or True Fae Kinship)</u></b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <i>You made that bargain, and now it hangs around your neck like a chain. You know what will happen if you try to break your word. You know how you'll suffer.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dicepool: </b>Manipulation + Satiety vs Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> This Nightmare can only be activated immediately after the intended victim has made a promise, deal or vow, although it need not be with the Beast himself. When activating this Nightmare, activate another simultaneously. The second Nightmare will hang over the victim's head like the proverbial Sword of Damocles for (Lair + Satiety) days, taking effect if the victim attempts to go against the letter of his word. The Nightmare will only take effect the first time the victim tries to transgress against the bargain.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety: </b>The Beast is automatically made aware when the victim tries to break his word.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>For every dot of Satiety spent, the Nightmare 'attached' to this one gains another 'charge', meaning that if three dots are expended, the Nightmare will take effect the first, second, third and fourth times that the victim attempts to break his word.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>On an Exceptional Success, the victim must roll Resolve + Composure to attempt to transgress against the bargain, as he gains a bone-deep certainty that if he does so, he will suffer some horrific retribution.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-17-2016, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T13:48:51-08:00","id":1018570,"title":"","content":"<b>Makara Predator:</b> &quot;Dude, you've got to relax, just go with the flow...&quot; it's a motto that he's all too familiar with preaching to others. For a vicious, blood thirsty monster, he's shockingly laid back and calm; preferring to take life as it comes and not get worked up about the details. Ironically, this Leviathan works as a lifeguard, soaking up the sun's rays amidst white sandy beaches and cool, rippling waves. Life is good for the care free monster of the deep, though not so much for his feeding victims.<br /> <br /> He is the unseen terror of the deep. The one you don't even notice until it's right beside you brushing against one of your extremities. His horror takes the form of an enormous jellyfish, it's translucent body nearly invisible beneath the water as it drifts amidst the currents. It's toxin filled tentacles lazily reaching out for a victim they can ensnare before the feeding commences. He doesn't particularly care who he feeds on, just as long as they're satisfying. Perhaps it is because of this lax attitude that he's been known to spawn the occasional Heroes from nearly any background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T14:13:34-08:00","id":1018577,"title":"","content":"Beasts don't spawn heroes anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T15:01:39-08:00","id":1018596,"title":"","content":"<b>Makara Tyrant:</b> Turns out old nightmares can learn new tricks. It's actually really embarrassing for him. All the other Beasts are things from ancient mythology, monsters that have been hunting forever, werewolves and simurghs and gashadokuros.<br /> <br /> He's definitely sure he's never seen another Horror that has a <i>copyright</i> on it.<br /> <br /> But, this is where our young Leviathan stands. His soul is an aboleth, straight from the pages of the Monster Manual. It has a certain number hit points and can cast a so many spells per day and gives you a nice amount of experience points if you kill it. Maybe that's why he seems to draw all the really nerdy Heroes to him, the ones who don't think of themselves as Beowulf or Odysseus but as Drizzt Do'Urden or Harry Potter.<br /> <br /> But he'll show them. They'll have to find him first, get past the little cult he's been gradually building in a sleepy coastal town, uncover layer after layer of deception and rumor, venture down into the perilous sea caves, fight his ichthyous Kin, and dive, deep, deeper than their lungs can bear, and find, what, exactly?<br /> <br /> Oh, he'll show them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T16:20:58-08:00","id":1018606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1018577#post1018577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts don't spawn heroes anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Didn't know that. Well hopefully I'll be more informed when I unwrap that sexy player's book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T18:33:25-08:00","id":1018636,"title":"","content":"A woman wearing a long coat walks to you from the other side at a narrow ally. Strange, you thought that no one was over there, and you certainly didn't hear any footsteps. On a closer look, she's wearing a mask. A red mask, but the color seems... off. A bit too dark, and moist. She calls you, and stops you in your tracks. For some reason, you find yourself obeying her. With a strangely melancholic voice, she asks you a question; &quot;Am I beautiful?&quot; You take a close look at her face. Fair skin, long and glistening black hair, deep dark eyes with a trace of sepia brown... She reminds of your first love, so of course you say yes. Hell, maybe she likes you too. Then her sweet voice suddenly changes to a raspy cackle. &quot;Then how about this?!&quot; She tears off that red mask, and reveals a mouth slashed wide open across her cheeks and up to her ears. She grins, and you see dozens of needle-like teeth. You faint in terror as you see her mouth open up into a huge, snapping maw.<br /> <br /> <b>Horror</b>: The Red Mask<br /> <b>Family</b>: Namtaru<br /> <b>Hunger</b>: Prey<br /> <hr /><br /> Just something from an urban myth that used to be quite a hit back a few years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T08:03:23-08:00","id":1020403,"title":"","content":"It was the middle of the night when the luxuriously hand crafted doors to the exotic shop were reduced to splinters as they were blown off their hinges. From the wreckage emerged a young boy, possibly between the ages of 12 and 14. The owner of the store, a handsome looking man with a full beard and dressed in middle eastern style apparel didn't even bat an eyelash at the destructive display. Rather, he folded his arms over his chest, leaned back in his chair from behind the counter and waited as the boy stormed up to him and slammed a fist on the counter, cracking it beneath his strength.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;What did you do!?&quot;</i> the boy roared, his face contorted into raw fury as he was struggling not to tear the entire building apart. The store owner quirked an eyebrow at him before unfolding one arm and absently waving it through the air.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You wished to be a super hero, so that's what I made you.&quot;</i> he said nonchalantly, <i>&quot;Are you unsatisfied with the results?&quot;</i> he asked, his demeanor was completely devoid of snark but rather suggested he truly didn't understand why the boy was so upset.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;My parents!&quot;</i> the boy bellowed, slamming his fist again, this time splitting half way through the counter. <i>&quot;WHY!?&quot;</i> he demanded. The man folded his arms over his chest again before he responded.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Oh, that.&quot;</i> he quipped, <i>&quot;Well, from my research, super heroes always have an element of tragedy in their origin stories. Soooo in order to make things more authentic, I had to kill your parents.&quot;</i> the next strike from the boy was aimed directly at the owner of the store, but just as it was supposed to make impact, the man dissipated into a cloud of smoke.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Be careful what you wish for, boy!&quot;</i> the man's voice came from within the cloud before it and the entire store began to vanish out of existence. Soon, the super powered youth was left standing in a vacant lot, with no evidence to the store or its owner having ever been present.<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> The Malicious Djinn<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Ruin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T11:01:19-08:00","id":1020953,"title":"","content":"'Honest&quot; Gregory Loomis (the car salesman from hell) Eshmaki Collector<br /> <br /> Gregory Loomis had just inherited his father's car dealership when he underwent the devouring, and quickly began to indulge his collector nature by tricking people in need a of a car into paying large sums of money, or even better, trading beloved older vehicles for cars that were often lemons. Despite what you might expect, he is actually more likely to feed by screwing a customer on a new car than a used one, which he will tell other beasts is because a new car has more middlemen that need to be paid off than a used one, though he does love nothing more than selling a used lemon, even a recalled one, to someone he feels deserves it.<br /> <br /> <br /> His horror is a 6 eyed, four nostriled serpentine dragon wearing ostentatious jewelry, with leathery wings flapping and his forked tongue flicking as he scents out potential new vict... I mean customers. Gregory's horror wears jewelry made from hood ornaments, hubcaps and other notable parts of famously bad cars. The deadly fuel tank of a pinto converted into a bag he keeps his treasure in, the doors of a Deloren become armor for his wings as the scandalous grill of an Edsel became the base for a cod piece of all things for the serpentine Horror, made all the more sleazy by the addition of the lethal steering column for a 1961 Corvair.<br /> <br /> His Lair is something of a museum of horrible cars, the famous lemons carefully put on proud display on alters in a junk yard littered with the sharp rusty ruins of much better cars taken from his victims, with flows of battery acid, large angry junkyard animals and flaming rivers of gasoline providing hazards to any intruders along with with a security system his son Alan, a Beast himself with a similar horror (though Alan is more of a computer salesman from hell) made from the infamous computerized electronics of the 1976 Aston Martin Lagonda and the clunky iDrive system of a 2002 BMW 7-series.<br /> <br /> Gregory, being at lair ten, has decided to seek the incarnate inheritance via the spawn a legend method, in which he plans to drive one of the great auto makers out of business by tricking their executives into making the worst car EVER and letting all their out of work former employees and dealers know who did it.<br /> <br /> Lair Traits: maze, corrosive, toxic , slick, burning , jagged (representing scattered junk on the ground) and razored.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will add Alan later if you guys want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 12-23-2016, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T20:25:20-08:00","id":1021123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1020953#post1020953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I will add Alan later if you guys want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:31:02-08:00","id":1021154,"title":"","content":"Alan Loomis (the computer salesman from Hell) Eshmaki Ravager<br /> <br /> Alan Loomis, like his father before him, is an eshmaki who feeds by being a sleazy salesman who sells shoddy products. The difference being that while Gregory inherited a car dealership to work out of, where as Alan had to make do selling computers at the mall as a teenager in the 80s. It was slow feeding at first, but then he discovered the Coleco Adam, a computer that only routed the power supply through the often defective printer, but went so far as to release an electromagnetic pulse that would wipe any floppy disk inside it when turned. After modifying the store's stock of Adams to make the EMP stronger, he sold them all to the city government and fed deep as the EMP wiped all the data that wasn't written down and fried the radios emergency responders relied on.<br /> <br /> Over the next few decades, Alan repeated that strategy on multiple scales, selling computers that seem too good to be true to households, businesses and governments, and then, as soon as the extended warranty the customer paid oh so much money for runs out, they begin crashing, losing files and dropping connections, and then the customer is horrified to learn that the backups failed, all their precious photos, important financial documents, drafts of their screenplays, all of it lost forever.<br /> <br /> He also does a side business in spyware, putting various software out on the net that inexperienced users install to turn their cursor into a dragon, only for it to send all their personal information to Loomis, who then milks it for all it's worth and leaves the victim in rags. In these days of much more reliable computers, the identity theft strategy for feeding is his go to, but he is also expanding into shoddy smartphones, having recently unloaded a warehouse full of those exploding Samsung phones to various suckers.<br /> <br /> His horror is much like his father's, a great serpentine dragon decked out in finery made from the parts of famously bad computers, transistor earrings hang from his horns and a power mac G4 cube hangs from a heavy chain necklace as the chiclet keys of a Texas instruments TI-99 are set into rings on his clawed wings as his bronze armor, made from copper taken from the faulty power supplies of Dell Dimension 4600s, protects the horror's wings and body.<br /> <br /> His Lair is a computerized urban sprawl straight out of an 80s/90s era cyberpunk novel, electric currents fry intruders' bodies as EMPs from the various Coleco Adams in the lair fry any electronics they bring' into the lair. CRT monitors provide insufficient light for intruders to see and constantly ringing smartphones deafen them as the walls made from the aluminum casings of Apple threes and the heat from the various devices slowly cook them<br /> <br /> Lair Traits: Poor Light, Thunderous, Electrified, Extreme Heat, Disruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 12-23-2016, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T13:31:40-08:00","id":1021383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1021154#post1021154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alan Loomis</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I regret my decision. Somebody tell the Heroes where to find this ass hole! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T13:36:02-08:00","id":1021384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1021383#post1021383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I regret my decision. Somebody tell the Heroes where to find this ass hole! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was pretty tired when I wrote him, might need to punch him up a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:11:16-08:00","id":1021426,"title":"","content":"(Might be in bad taste, but I slept on it, and still had a nagging urge to write this character up.)<br /> <br /> <br /> A confirmed sex offender and child killer, Harold Kreemz was on his way to either a life time in prison, or a very brutal death at the hands of other inmates. Or at least he would have been, had he not used the insanity plea to get himself acquitted. of his crimes. Instead of the rigors of life in prison, he was placed under mandatory therapy sessions to help him overcome his sick cravings. But instead of curing Harold, it turned him into something much, much worse. Discovering more about his inner self with each session, Harold's last visit to therapy resulted in his homecoming, finally transforming him into the monster he's always been on the inside. He has always targeted children, but now he reaps more tangible benefits for doing so. And now, with the ability to escape into the realm of nightmares, the police will have a significantly harder time capturing Harold then they did before!<br /> <br /> <br /> His horror is a distorted blob of vanilla and strawberry ice cream. Large, bubble gum eye balls are set within drooping eye sockets as his partially melted features congeal puddles on the ground beneath him. Sprinkles, nuts, gummy bears and other assorted toppings are embedded throughout his creamy flesh like sickly sweet skin blemishes. Licorice hair dangles from his scalp like dreadlocks, limp and slick with chocolate syrup dribbling through them. His gaping mouth features splintered popsicle sticks for teeth, while his fingers and toes are tipped with waffle cone claws. Its voice is disturbingly high pitched and cheerful, singing enchanting music that causes children to flee from their parents in the hopes of getting a refreshing treat from the ice cream man.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> The Ice Cream Man<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-23-2016, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T05:27:28-08:00","id":1021950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1021426#post1021426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Might be in bad taste, but I slept on it, and still had a nagging urge to write this character up.)<br /> <br /> <br /> A confirmed sex offender and child killer, Harold Kreemz was on his way to either a life time in prison, or a very brutal death at the hands of other inmates. Or at least he would have been, had he not used the insanity plea to get himself acquitted. of his crimes. Instead of the rigors of life in prison, he was placed under mandatory therapy sessions to help him overcome his sick cravings. But instead of curing Harold, it turned him into something much, much worse. Discovering more about his inner self with each session, Harold's last visit to therapy resulted in his homecoming, finally transforming him into the monster he's always been on the inside. He has always targeted children, but now he reaps more tangible benefits for doing so. And now, with the ability to escape into the realm of nightmares, the police will have a significantly harder time capturing Harold then they did before!<br /> <br /> <br /> His horror is a distorted blob of vanilla and strawberry ice cream. Large, bubble gum eye balls are set within drooping eye sockets as his partially melted features congeal puddles on the ground beneath him. Sprinkles, nuts, gummy bears and other assorted toppings are embedded throughout his creamy flesh like sickly sweet skin blemishes. Licorice hair dangles from his scalp like dreadlocks, limp and slick with chocolate syrup dribbling through them. His gaping mouth features splintered popsicle sticks for teeth, while his fingers and toes are tipped with waffle cone claws. Its voice is disturbingly high pitched and cheerful, singing enchanting music that causes children to flee from their parents in the hopes of getting a refreshing treat from the ice cream man.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> The Ice Cream Man<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey guys, forget the computer salesman from hell. We need to kill this one ASAP. And also call in those more-human monsters you happen to know. I'm sure at least one of them has a heart.&quot;<br /> <br /> - A Hero after finishing his research on this Beast, talking to his fellow Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T01:07:56-08:00","id":1023150,"title":"","content":"They call her the crazy cat lady, because of all the cats she keeps around herself. But she is no collector of felines, no matter what her victims might tell you. Anybody who stops to observe her pets will notice that they consist entirely of black cats, solid black cats! This elderly grandmother is a bringer of misfortune to the community. When night falls, she and her beloved kitties go prowling the streets, inflicting bad luck upon anyone unfortunate enough to cross their path. The lesson she imparts upon those she feeds from is simple in its deliverance: whether your good or bad, shit happens, and you can't be prepared for everything life throws at you.<br /> <br /> Her horror is an old witch sporting the ears, tail, claws, eyes and fangs of a black cat. She walks with a hunched gait, dressed in patchwork rags and always surrounded by a group of her black coated pets. Her passing causes supersitious people to throw up every counter hex their grandparents ever taught them as a child in an attempt to counteract the bad luck. Sometimes, if she's feeling coy, she'll leave them alone for doing so... unfortunately, that playfulness seems to be what draws in the Heroes who think they can ward off bad luck.<br /> <br /> Her lair is a superstitious nightmare full of jinxes and bad omens. Ladders, broken mirrors, roads leading past grave yards, spilled salt shakers, cracked mugs, burning ears, anything and everything that people associate with bad luck can be found in abundance. Visitors to her realm will find themselves hard pressed to maneuver through it without contracting 7 years bad luck, possibly more if they're careless. But it's not just the decorations that haunt them, the lair itself appears to be cursed, causing all manner of unfortunate accidents to befall unwelcome guests who dare to intrude upon her territory. Even should a Hero manage to find their way into her lair, the Beast will laugh as they are made to look utterly incompetent at their mission to destroy her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> the Crazy Cat Lady<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Ruin<br /> <br /> <b>Kinship:</b> Undecided<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Everybody knows the story of the Little Mermaid. A young mermaid sees a man for the first time and makes a bargain with a sea witch to trade the only life she's ever known for the chance to spend the rest of her life with him. She does this before they even have one line of dialogue between them, claiming that it's love at first sight. In the Disney version, this story has a happy ending, with the mermaid marrying the man of her dreams. But the real story is much more tragic. The man was already betrothed and had no romantic attachments to the little mermaid, thus prompting her to die as a result of the sea witch's magic. This particular leviathan thought the original was much better, and taught a powerful message that young girls and boys can both learn from. Love at first sight doesn't exist!<br /> <br /> Having chosen to model herself after the popular folk tale, the Sea Witch's Horror is one that most people would easily recognize. She possesses the head and torso of a woman, but instead of legs, she has a mass of octopus tentacles with which to propel her through the water. She freely associates with Changelings, and has acquired a bit of mystical knowhow from them. She uses her magical expertise to offer bargains to those she feeds upon. Typically, such bargains are horribly stacked against her victim's favor, but the potential rewards are too good to refuse. Or at least that's what her victims think before signing away their livelihoods for the chance to follow their dreams.<br /> <br /> The Sea Witch's lair is a homely and welcoming place at a casual glance. An underwater cave with an air pocket for those land lubbers who don't have the gills necessary to survive otherwise. Potions and other magical reagents are lined against the wall on top of coral shelves, with an enormous cauldron in the center of the room, bubbling with a mysterious concoction. In the corner of the cave, one can see a side pathway leading into a bedroom of some kind, complete with a vanity mirror and make up kit so the cave's resident can make herself look presentable. Nobody who knows the resident personally comes to visit, however, not unless they need something from her. Then she welcomes them in with a cheery disposition and begins to negotiate the terms of their contract.<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> the Sea Witch<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Makara<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Ruin<br /> <br /> <b>Kinship:</b> Changelings<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Lovecraft once wrote that the oldest and most powerful fear of mankind is fear of the unknown. Perhaps that may have been the case for a long time, but now mankind is getting wiser, more advanced, and with that advancement comes knowledge, and with that knowledge comes a brand new fear that threatens to shake man to the core. Nihilism, the realization that all of existence is ultimately meaningless. With all their scientific achievements, mankind has predicted that somehow, someday, the universe is going to die and everything in it will die, too. This Beast is a constant reminder of that knowledge, always looming over the heads of his victims with the realization that no matter what we do, we are all born to die.<br /> <br /> Their Horror is a pathetic and tragic sight to behold. A withered old king dressed in tattered robes and wearing a rusty crown upon his brow. His features are sunken and hollow, a clear sign that the rigors of time have stripped him of the hope he once carried in his youth. He sits apathetically upon his throne, watching the universe decay around him. He doesn't chase after his victims, there's no reason for him to do so, anymore. But when an enemy shows up trying to kill him, he rises from his seat and prepares to teach them that their struggle is futile. Nobody can fight death forever.<br /> <br /> His lair is a dead world within a dead universe. There are no stars in the sky, they burned out long ago, covering the world in perpetual darkness and freezing temperatures. All species of plants and animals have gone extinct and any food that might have been left has long since decayed, or been eaten by scavengers who eventually died off anyways. The land itself is a towering monument to mankind's failures. A graveyard built on top of a city, built on top of a graveyard, built on top of a city, built on top of a grave yard, built on top of a city, and so on. The king's throne sits on the upper most lair of this cycle of death and rebirth. He can't build the next lair anymore, he has no more subjects left to aid him!<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> the Fallen King<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Tyrant<br /> <br /> <b>Kinship:</b> Geists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-28-2016, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:51:39-08:00","id":1023191,"title":"","content":"Really loving the Fallen King and the Crazy Cat Lady =D<br /> <br /> Reading Lovecraft made me think of &quot;Shadow over Innsmouth&quot; and a despicable type of character, probably better suited as a (villainous?) NPC than PC.<br /> <br /> One really scary aspect about Shadow over Innsmouth is that people willingly reproduce with fishpeople from the deep seas. Partly, that was in return for blessings and riches, but it was their free choice. You read that right, they were not forced, they simply did it as a service to their religion and/or out of greed. Over time, this left a mark on the town, and the majority of people were part of the 'family' with the characteristic Innsmouth look, and basically no one could escape this hellhole.<br /> <br /> The Deep One's desire likewise cannot be quenched. Despite not looking great, he has charisma, connections - and money. He long lost count of how many cuckoos he's planted, and how many relationships destroyed. He somehow became a trusted advisor for a few celebrities, and used to work a number of jobs before finding his &quot;calling&quot;.<br /> To keep a steady income, he started a cult, and some people revere him as a prophet of Mother Hydra. Despite it's size, the people are very devoted, and even those who are unhappy with their life stick to their choices, because they have nothing else to return to after burning all bridges to join.<br /> However, he is never forceful nor does he even initiate anything, be it a rendezvous or a conversion; he simply goads people into doing what he wants, and when they complain about what happened to them, confronts them with the fact that it was their own free choice that led them down this path. This manipulated 'realization' of being responsible for your own misfortune, having no one to blame and having to face the consequences by yourself is what sustains his Horror. His cult is growing, and one of his cuckoo kids just recently had a homecoming and joined his brood and cult.<br /> Now, he is looking to make the local city his headquarters - with all that entails.<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Cult Leader<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> Deep One<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Makara<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Ruin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Typo: Fallen Kind. I of course meant the Fallen KinG 12-28-2016, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T20:05:11-08:00","id":1023555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1023191#post1023191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading Lovecraft made me think of &quot;Shadow over Innsmouth&quot; and a despicable type of character, probably better suited as a (villainous?) NPC than PC.<br /> <br /> One really scary aspect about Shadow over Innsmouth is that people willingly reproduce with fishpeople from the deep seas. Partly, that was in return for blessings and riches, but it was their free choice. You read that right, they were not forced, they simply did it as a service to their religion and/or out of greed. Over time, this left a mark on the town, and the majority of people were part of the 'family' with the characteristic Innsmouth look, and basically no one could escape this hellhole.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, well the Great Old Ones seemed just as willing to fornicate with humanity as they were to devour it. Me thinks Lovecraft may have had some serious issues he needed to work through in his writings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wouldn't necessarily call it a hellhole, though. I've never read the story, but I've heard that one of the blessings they received for this pact was immortality. So it's not like the people of Innsmouth weren't reaping some benefits for their devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T21:04:59-08:00","id":1023572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1023555#post1023555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, well the Great Old Ones seemed just as willing to fornicate with humanity as they were to devour it. Me thinks Lovecraft may have had some serious issues he needed to work through in his writings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wouldn't necessarily call it a hellhole, though. I've never read the story, but I've heard that one of the blessings they received for this pact was immortality. So it's not like the people of Innsmouth weren't reaping some benefits for their devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovecraft is pretty notable for his racism. I think the most common interpretation of Shadow Over Innsmouth is a condemnation of mixed race marriages <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Lovecraft had issues&quot; is probably one of the least controversial statements it's possible to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T22:20:42-08:00","id":1023594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1023572#post1023572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lovecraft is pretty notable for his racism. I think the most common interpretation of Shadow Over Innsmouth is a condemnation of mixed race marriages <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Lovecraft had issues&quot; is probably one of the least controversial statements it's possible to make.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, didn't know Lovecraft was such a racist until I saw some online videos finding quotes in his writing (<i>&quot;the blackest of African voodoo circles&quot;</i>.) As I understand it, he was starting to get over that just before he died.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I finally got my hands on the Beast book, so hopefully, I can come up with better ideas, now!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T01:01:12-08:00","id":1023621,"title":"","content":"This is something of an evolution of my first real Beast character; only in the past while have I gotten the inspiration to really get Cormack to a more complete whole, and I figured I'd share him here. Let me know what you guys think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Cormack was originally just a football player; he was big even at a young age, he was strong and eager, and his dad pushed him to become part of the big leagues. Everything seemed to be going well, and he got interest from various scouts looking for talent. This ended when a rival tackled Cormack into a back breaking injury that sent him into the hospital. Recovery went well, barring a lasting pain in his back, but in that time Cormack learned about the injuries various football legends went through, particularly with damage to their brain. That, more than anything else, killed his interest in football and through it ruined his relationship with his father. With his monetary and family investments in ruins Cormack tried to reinvent himself by using his looks, but though he had some talent acting he had problems remembering the lines, and he found himself verging on homelessness for it.<br /> <br /> His luck changed when the dreams came back to him. Throughout his life, Cormack had been subject to odd dreams he could never place. What had started as spirographs that spiraled out of control, and turned into wild fractals that hurt his mind to remember, had re-manifested in his time at the hospital as a face. It never said anything, but it appeared in his the dreamscape in place of others' faces, in reflections that should have been his, in the dark. Every other time he woke up in a sweat; however, the night of a particularly bad interview, he dreamed of the stage he had been thrown off from. In what seemed like an eternity, the spirographs and fractals returned, subsuming the stage and its props, tearing the audience and seating away, and leaving just him standing in madness, with just the face staring at him from the void.<br /> <br /> That is, until he realized he was looking at himself from that void, from the face. His face.<br /> <br /> The next day, Cormack returned for another interview. The difference in his performance was staggering, and he was taken on, albeit in a background part considering his first attempt. His reputation swiftly grew from there.<br /> <br /> Even compared to other Beasts, Cormack finds his Horror, The Fractal King, rather unusual. Outside of its body being tall, warped and angular, the Fractal King's form almost looks like a piece of animation rather than something flesh and blood. Light and shadow doesn't play quite right across it, an afterimage trails after every movement and a layer of something like static skitters over its form. It is obviously three dimensional and yet flat looking, though the distinction between the two varies when it slips through cracks in its domain. Painful ripples of white, black and red run across its body, with wings like blades protruding from its shoulders and its face is a smooth, rounded but expressive trapezoid decked with two horns on top of a similarly shaped head. Its realm initially appears to be a normal room, though one colored much like the King itself, with eye straining patterns that make it hard to tell where things actually are, and what is actually a door and what isn't; chambers accepted into its lair adopt these same properties, though those welcome find the patterns shift to something easier to bare. The Fractal King actually enjoys company and, provided it is respected, indulges in their pleasures with its illusions, but it is equally eager to share the terrors of its lair, leaving guests wondering just what is real even when they've been allowed to leave.<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Charismatic Stage Actor<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> The Fractal King<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Ugallu<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Power<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Seductive. Cormack's good looking, and he's long known it. When normal and even supernatural avenues fail, it's not too hard to find someone receptive to his charm to.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Noble. Cormack may be seen as a flirt, but he'll listen and help however he can to make life a bit better. Being able to tell lies from reality helps.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Poor Lighting, Sealed Exits, Mirages<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Needs Must, Mimir's Wisdom<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Flying and Falling, You Must Obey<br /> <br /> <b>Inspiration: </b><a href=\"http://xaravald.deviantart.com/art/Fractal-monster-531613519\" target=\"_blank\">http://xaravald.deviantart.com/art/F...ster-531613519</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 01-07-2017, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T02:54:52-08:00","id":1023641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1023555#post1023555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, well the Great Old Ones seemed just as willing to fornicate with humanity as they were to devour it. Me thinks Lovecraft may have had some serious issues he needed to work through in his writings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wouldn't necessarily call it a hellhole, though. I've never read the story, but I've heard that one of the blessings they received for this pact was immortality. So it's not like the people of Innsmouth weren't reaping some benefits for their devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, there were some tangible benefits (getting fish and gold so you don't friggin STARVE since there's no fish left, for starters). But from the description, people's lifes weren't very joyful, and it was basically a dictatorial regime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T08:50:57-08:00","id":1023785,"title":"","content":"Some believe there is no punishment greater than the one we inflict upon ourselves when we feel like we deserve retribution. This Beast would like very much to test that theory, and so they have refined their feeding habits to accommodate it. They don't physically harm their victim, at least not directly, but what they do resort to is sending them on a nightmare powered guilt trip, the likes of which can drive a man to martyrdom.<br /> <br /> Their horror is the scrawny, helpless kid who always got bullied by others because they felt he was too weak to defend himself. He's the captain of a boat, or a train, or a plane, or sometimes it's just a car. Whatever it is, he'll be your driver for the night, while you, the unlucky passenger, are strapped tightly into your seat with no perceivable way to undo your bindings. He limps into view covered in wounds and bandages as he informs you that he is here to ferry you to the afterlife. That's when the lights dim, he retreats from sight, and the ride starts moving.<br /> <br /> His lair is reminiscent to Willy Wanka's tunnel from the original movie. Those who take the ride through it are assaulted on all sides by exaggerated recreations of the consequences for their actions. The people they've hurt are screaming in blinding agony and wailing in despair like damned souls who can not escape their torment. A slow motion replay of the Beast's victim is shown violently assaulting them with a sadistic glee only matched by demons etched across their face. Visions of medical treatments come next, but they're way beyond anything the victim might have actually done. Disgusting bruises that turn the flesh dark purple or decayed brown, and shattered bones that protrude through the skin. The Beast's victim hasn't simply attacked their victim, they've brutalized them, all to make themselves feel powerful (this particular lesson doesn't ingratiate himself with Tyrants). The next series of visions are an endless bombardment of obscenities and humiliating scenarios. Every insult they've ever thrown at others, or prank they've ever pulled is now directed at them a thousand times over without pause. Most victims end up screaming to get off by the time this starts happening. And just as the victim's psyche has reached its limit, a glow begins to form over the horizon, with the vehicle getting closer as is gets brighter. The victim has to strain their vision at first, but then their eyes go wide and they start thrashing as the image becomes clear. The glow is produced by an endless sea of flames, and they're drifting straight for it!<br /> <br /> The ride usually ends before the flames start licking the victim's skin and with the Beast having suitably gorged itself upon their mind numbing terror. His family has repeatedly encouraged him to go on a stricter diet, but he can't help himself. These people never showed him an ounce of mercy when he was human. Now that he's a monster, he feels no inclination to do so, either. <i>The people he punishes have only themselves to blame!</i><br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> the Ferryman<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Punishment<br /> <br /> <b>Kinship:</b> Mummies<br /> <br /> <b>Lesson:</b> Caution - Some day, it might be you who's begging for mercy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-23-2017, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:37:22-08:00","id":1023926,"title":"","content":"<b>Ugallu Ravager:</b> She was voted in scarcely a month ago, and since then she's been on a crusade, not to push her own agenda through, but to uncover all the dirty laundry of her 'peers', exposing it to the public eye and watching their careers crash and burn. To her colleagues, she's a threat, a monster which they can only hope doesn't turn its gaze on them until they've had time to clear away the things they don't want dragged into the light. To the public she's an avenging angel, a paragon upholding the right and the just and punishing the wicked. The fact that she's survived more than one assassination attempt and disproven a number of false claims that she is just as corrupt as those she tears down hasn't hurt her reputation either.<br /> <br /> In truth, she's both: a monster <i>and </i>an angel.<br /> <br /> In her childhood, her family, friends and neighbours suffered under the uncaring boot of far-distant corporation owners and politicians, just another blot on the urban landscape, another set of miscreants and layabouts without jobs, as if that was a choice they made. In school, she pushed herself harder and further than her peers, desperate to rise above where she was born and to whom, to stand on a level with their 'lawful' oppressors and cast them down, to help the people like her. In dreams, she found herself under the vast and pitiless regard of the creature she called the Watcher and - later, after she learned Latin - the Grigori, a thing of a thousand wings and a hundred thousand judgemental eyes, each scourging her nightly with their contempt for her weaknesses. With each step she made towards her goal, though, another pair of wings unfurled, until eventually, on the night after she won her campaign, the last pulled back and she saw the one who stood beneath the wings, the face of that seraph - her own.<br /> <br /> Since that day, she has continued her crusade, feeding on the destruction of the careers and lives of the leeches who think themselves kings. She only wishes that she could pretend that it was the justice and the punishment that set her heart beating faster, not the looks of despair and horror on their faces as they realise that all they have built is for nought.<br /> <br /> <u>Lair Traits:</u> Exposed, Blazing Light<br /> <br /> <u>Atavisms:</u> Eye of Heaven, Mimir's Wisdom, Wings of the Raptor, Dragonfire (manifests as a scourging, burning radiance)<br /> <br /> <u>Nightmares:</u> You Deserve This, Everything You Do Is Worthless<br /> <br /> <u>Lesson:</u> What you do can ruin you (she doesn't really focus on teaching this as much as she does on actually <i>bringing</i> that ruin)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T20:44:31-08:00","id":1024616,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>I wrote this character idea up waaaaay back on Page 7.<br /> <br /> Beast has been more fleshed out and refined since then, and now that I've gotten my hands on the official book, I've decided to revise my previous version. So here it goes!</b></i></span><br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------</span><br /> <br /> Bottom feeders, scum suckers, ass kissers, parasites, these are words society often attributes to people who prefer to stick close to power, without assuming any responsibility. They praise and venerate those above them in hopes of being shown nepotism when they need a favor done. Timothy Blight knows these kinds of people all to well, for he used to be one before his devouring. Now, he wishes to show these boot lickers just how disgusting they truly are.<br /> <br /> <br /> Timothy Blight's horror is a horrifying cross between a tape worm and a centipede that has been grown to nightmarish proportions. Its mouth is shaped like sphincter, and opens to reveal multiple rows of needle sharp teeth. It skitters across the walls, floor and ceiling on countless spindly legs, while it's long antennae dangle around in the air, sensing for prey as it lacks proper eyes to see with. When it detects one nearby, it detaches from the wall with a blood curdling screech before charging in for the attack.<br /> <br /> His lair is not so much a place, as it is a thing. A living creature of unimaginable size, and Timothy resides inside its guts. More specifically its digestive track, where he feeds on the partially digested meals that find their way down there. Partially digested meals, like the victims who's dreams he torments. He's not the only parasite to be found here, either. Timothy has laid thousands of eggs throughout the creature's intestines, which have hatched into miniature versions of himself, and threaten to attack those who come within reach. Their best chance at survival here is to feed on the host's left overs. But that's something they should be comfortable with, already. After all, they've been feeding on society's hard work for years; so why get squeamish now?<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Basilisk's Touch, Infestation, Shadowed Soul, Heart of the Ocean<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Bugs Everywhere, You Must Obey, Everything You Do Is Worthless<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Stench, Flooded, Slick, Corrosive, Swarm<br /> <br /> <b>Lesson:</b> Don't manipulate others to support your livelihood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-26-2017, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T09:56:35-08:00","id":1031633,"title":"","content":"<b>The Frosts:</b> while all Begotten see themselves as family on some historical level, some of the children are family in a more literal sense. The Frosts are one such example, a Brood who are related to one another by blood. It consists of five members including the father (Anthony Frost), the mother (Heather Frost), and their three lovely children (Michael, Winter, and Lily).<br /> <br /> Interesting of note is that despite all being related to each other in the human world, their Horrors actually trace their lineages to different family origins. Each member of the Frosts are a different kind of Beast, with a different kind of Hunger. And while this gives them a significant advantage when it comes to fending off Heroes, it also makes family dinners more problematic when everybody in the family wants something different.<br /> <br /> The collective Lair shared by the Frosts resembles a frozen mountain range surrounded by arctic tundras spanning in all directions. Each member of the family claims a different part of the mountain as their lair, and those attempting to scale it will progressively encounter the entire family by the time they reach the top. The family's locations are as follows.<br /> <br /> Anthony - Outer Base<br /> <br /> Lily - Inner Base<br /> <br /> Michael - Outer Surface<br /> <br /> Heather - Inner Surface<br /> <br /> Winter - Mountain Peak<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Anthony Frost, Makara Nemesis:</b> The patriarch of the family and founder of the Brood, Anthony's career as a S.W.A.T officer enables him to dispense uncompromising justice upon the heads of those who abuse society. He deeply cares about his family and will go any lengths to ensure their safety. Unfortunately, this love is hard to appreciate at times, when it forces him to commit heinous acts for the greater good. The most recent example being when he forced the Devouring upon Lily, after she exhibited no potential connection to the Primordial Dream on her own. The Frost children seem to have inherited their Horrors from Anthony, as demonstrated by their winter-themed motif.<br /> <br /> Looking astoundingly healthy for a man in his late 40's, Anthony law enforcement training has combined well with his Begotten capabilities. He stands 6'2 in human form, weighing 217 lbs. His hair is kept short above the ears and still retains its healthy chestnut coloration from his youth, instead of fading like other men his age are known to do. His deep blue eyes have a piercing gaze that speaks of having witnessed the worst the world has to offer, and yet he's still prepared to keep fighting.<br /> <br /> Anthony's horror is a sea dragon, with a serpentine body that moves gracefully through the water and burrows caverns through the ice with its webbed claws. Its lair is an arctic landscape where platforms of slick ice drift upon frigid waters, threatening to plunge the unwary into instant hypothermia should they lose their balance. He is also the oldest and most powerful Beast in the family, although Michael's raw strength does make him a decent competitor.<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Reconcile with Lily (long term), Take down a criminal operation (short term)<br /> <br /> Hunger: Punishment<br /> <br /> Lair 4: Extreme Cold, Slick, Flooded, Unstable<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Heart of the Ocean, Monster of the Deep, Limb from Limb, Storm Lashed<br /> <br /> Nightmares: Fear is Contageous, You Deserve This, Everything You Do is Worthless, You Cannot Run<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Heather Frost: Namtaru Predator:</b> Time has not been as kind to Heather as it was for her husband. Before meeting Anthony, Heather was a vicious serial killer who gorged herself by mutilating her victims into shredded meat. It was with his help that she learned to control her appetite and they eventually fell in love. Today, Heather displays a much more subdued attitude and plays the role of doting housewife in front of the neighbors. But behind this motherly facade lurks the mind of a predator. Even her own family have learned by now that they are better off not knowing the secret ingredient to her family recipes.<br /> <br /> In her human form, Heather sports bright green eyes and medium cut, cherry blond hair. Being only a few years younger than Anthony, age has siphoned off much of the sex appeal she once had in her younger days. Standing at 5'7 tall and weighing 156 lbs, Heather's skin has begun to show the signs of wrinkling and her hair is not as vibrantly healthy as it used to be. She also dresses a couple decades out of date, as if she is trying to emulate the stereotypical housewife, but doesn't know how.<br /> <br /> In her Horror form, Heather is a gargantuan ice worm who's body is protected by an armored caripace as she burrows her way through ice and stone that composes the family's mountain. When her mouth opens, it reveals a ring shaped maw filled with several rows of needle sharp teeth ready to swallow her victims whole. Heather dwells inside the upper regions of the mountain, hunting down anyone who attempts to seek shelter from the weather by hiding inside one of the many cave systems she's burrowed out over the years.<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Have another child with Anthony (long term), Get Lily to laugh (short term)<br /> <br /> Hunger: Prey<br /> <br /> Lair 3: Poor Lights, Maze, Jagged<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Unbreakable, Monster From The Deep, Shadowed Soul<br /> <br /> Nightmares: Behold, My True Form, You Are Not Alone, You Will Never Rest<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Michael Frost, Anakim Tyrant:</b> A regular party animal, Michael is the eldest of the Frost children and the one who's closest in power to that of his parents. Michael has moved out of his parents' house in order to attend college, but the Lair shared by his Brood allows him to quickly pop over and visit them whenever he wants. Michael revels in his heritage and flaunts his power whenever he sees an opportunity to get away with it. Of course, being a giant means that Michael has plenty of opportunities to get away with it!<br /> <br /> At 18 years of age, Michael's human form has all the obnoxious rowdiness of a college fratboy. Which is fitting, considering that he actually is one. He's a big boy, standing just shy of 7 feet tall and weighing 240 lbs of athletic muscle. Michael takes after his father, having inherited the chestnut hair and blue eyes that Anthony possesses. However, he's also inherited Heather's drive to make the rest of the family happy and gets quite protective around his younger sisters.<br /> <br /> In the Primordial Dream, he takes the form of a great yeti, with icy blue skin, thick white fur, glowing red eyes and sharpened teeth. His lair spans the surface of the mountain which his Brood calls home. The strong winds and unstable terrain makes travel extremely dangerous for those not accustomed to mountain climbing, and yet Michael seems to be a natural at maneuvering through the environment. Much to the chagrin of those attempting to flee his pursuit.<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Graduate College (long term), Find a girlfriend (short term)<br /> <br /> Hunger: Power<br /> <br /> Lair 3: Extreme Cold, Unstable, Crosswinds<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Cyclopean Strength, Titanic Blow, Storm-Lashed<br /> <br /> Nightmares: You Will Never Rest, All Your Teeth Are Falling Out<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Winter Frost, Ugallu Collector:</b> The middle child of the Frost family, Winter broke the mold of traditional sibling roles by becoming one of the most popular girls in town, as opposed to being over shadowed and neglected by the attention given to her older brother and little sister. Unfortunately, her popularity comes at the expense of being a shameless flirt who manipulates both males and females into doing what she wants. Indeed, Winter's hoard is a veritable harem of admirers who will gladly do whatever is in their power to please her, so long as her demands are not too extreme. Winter is especially attracted to those who play hard to get, and her Hunger is stirred by the thought of adding them to her collection.<br /> <br /> At 16 years old, Winter has developed nicely as a voluptuous young girl. The kind that turns the heads of the sports team's star player and leaves the cheerleaders seething with jealousy. And she flaunts this sex appeal to the furthest extent that is legally tolerable in public. She stands 5'5 and weighs 130 lbs. Wearing skin tight, revealing outfits and bright, colorful fashions designed to lure in her prey. She's inherited Heather's cherry blond hair and bright green eyes, but she has Anthony's tenacity for getting what she wants.<br /> <br /> Winter's horror is an ice dragon with majestic white scales across her primary body. Her underside (and membrane on her wings) are a crystal blue hue, making her appear stunningly beautiful for a creature out of mankind's nightmares. Her lair is an ice cave that has been carved into the peak of her family's mountain. Sub zero temperatures combined with a lack of fresh air outside her cave leaves Winter's captives few options for survival beyond remaining trapped inside with her. And even then, their survival depends entirely upon whether or not they continue to please their mistress.<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Seduce a celebrity (long term), acquire a new lover (short term)<br /> <br /> Hunger: Collector<br /> <br /> Lair 2: Blizzard, Extreme Cold, Thin Air<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Wings of the Raptor, Alien Allure, Storm-Lashed<br /> <br /> Nightmares: You Must Obey, Flying and Falling<br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Lily Frost, Eshmaki Ravager:</b> it's official, every household has to have the one family member who makes everything more difficult than it needs to be. The youngest member of the Frost family, Lily did not exhibit any natural affinity to the Primordial Dream and would probably have gone through life as an ordinary human. But Anthony, fearing the worst possible outcome, decided to force the Devouring upon her, turning Lily into a monster without her knowledge or consent. Lily did not appreciate the well intended gesture, and has emotionally withdrawn herself from the world. Now, she is the most quiet and reserved member of the family, having focused most of her energy on self contemplation until she can determine where she stands on her current situation.<br /> <br /> At 12 years old, Lily's human form is a shy and soft spoken girl as far as outward appearances go. Inwardly, she struggles to come to terms with what's been done to her, leaving her mind a jumbled mess of raw emotion that strains to lash out. Due to her youth, she stands 4'6 tall and weighs 92 lbs. She has the chestnut colored hair of Anthony, and the bright green eyes of Heather, but prefers to dress in plain, muted outfits so as to draw as little attention to herself as possible. So far, her hunger for destruction can be waved off as a rebellious phase she's going through; but that excuse won't work forever, once she's older.<br /> <br /> Lily's horror is a sabertooth cat; large and savage, with fangs as long as a man's hand. Her lair is a network of cave systems that span beneath the foot of the mountain shared by her family. There are many exits to these caves, but they all deposit travelers into the frozen wastes that the rest of her Brood calls home. Trespassers must choose which is the better option; being torn apart by Lily, or risk freezing to death on the surface. And should her victims prove lucky enough to escape her pursuit within the mountain, there's still the chance they'll encounter her mother on the upper levels of the caves!<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Come to terms with her new life (long term), Relieve some pent up aggression (short term).<br /> <br /> Hunger: Ruin<br /> <br /> Lair 1: Jagged, Darkness<br /> <br /> Atavisms: From the Darkness, Limb from Limb<br /> <br /> Nightmares: Behold, My True Form, You're Not Alone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-23-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T23:52:05-08:00","id":1032020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=826561#post826561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Namtaru Ravager:</b> If there is one thing humans fear more than the ugly, it is the possibility of joining their ranks. Degenerative illnesses, mutilating accidents, whatever might cause unsightly blemishes or maiming. This Gorgon seeks to destroy the beauty of others, feeding upon the terror of their own hideous visage once his prey discovers what has been done to them. In the world of nightmares, his horror is that of a bloated toad the size of a man, skin covered in bumpy warts and toxic mucus leaking from his pores. A tattered, dirty loin cloth wrapped around their waist belies a sense of intelligence behind the bestial form.<br /> <br /> His lair is an infectious swamp, teaming with diseases and festering insects. Putrid water reaching thigh level attempts to slow down trespassers while dense foliage obscures the view of the sky and causes painful rashes when brushed against the skin. Luminescent gas pockets seek to lure wanderers into traps as they stumble through the swamp in search of light or shelter. And in the heart of this inhospitable environment is a squat hut built into the branches of a gnarled tree, where the Gorgon makes its home!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Lair 4:</i> Stinging, Diseased, Flooded, Stench<br /> <br /> <i>Atavisms:</i> Basilisk's Touch, From the Darkness, Monster from the Deep, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <i>Nightmare:</i> All your teeth are falling out, Behold my true form, You are alone<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>NOTE:</b> I imagine that Monster from the Deep allows his horror to ensnare victims with its extendable tongue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T05:29:07-08:00","id":1036555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1031633#post1031633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Frosts:</b> while all Begotten see themselves as family on some historical level, some of the children are family in a more literal sense. The Frosts are one such example, a Brood who are related to one another by blood. It consists of five members including the father (Anthony Frost), the mother (Heather Frost), and their three lovely children (Michael, Winter, and Lily).<br /> <br /> Interesting of note is that despite all being related to each other in the human world, their Horrors actually trace their lineages to different family origins. Each member of the Frosts are a different kind of Beast, with a different kind of Hunger. And while this gives them a significant advantage when it comes to fending off Heroes, it also makes family dinners more problematic when everybody in the family wants something different.<br /> <br /> The collective Lair shared by the Frosts resembles a frozen mountain range surrounded by arctic tundras spanning in all directions. Each member of the family claims a different part of the mountain as their lair, and those attempting to scale it will progressively encounter the entire family by the time they reach the top. The family's locations are as follows.<br /> <br /> Anthony - Outer Base<br /> <br /> Lily - Inner Base<br /> <br /> Michael - Outer Surface<br /> <br /> Heather - Inner Surface<br /> <br /> Winter - Mountain Peak<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A literal family of Beasts - why couldn't I think of that faster?? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, and just how did the Devouring of this family of fear go? Did one member become a Beast first and then proceeded to invite the others in, or were they catalyzed by some outside influence at the same time? The latter alone might be a potent story hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:04:39-08:00","id":1036593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1036555#post1036555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A literal family of Beasts - why couldn't I think of that faster?? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, and just how did the Devouring of this family of fear go? Did one member become a Beast first and then proceeded to invite the others in, or were they catalyzed by some outside influence at the same time? The latter alone might be a potent story hook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Anthony and Heather underwent their Devourings separately. They met roughly 2 weeks after Heather's and teamed up together, eventually deciding to marry. Michael and Winter underwent their Devourings naturally in their youths (thanks to living in such close proximity to their parents' Horrors all their lives), but Lily had it forced upon her. Anthony fully believes he did the right thing for Lily's sake, even if she doesn't understand or appreciate it right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, just noticed I forgot to detail the heights and weights of the kids. :P<br /> <br /> Went back and edited that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-23-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:13:51-08:00","id":1036598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1036593#post1036593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Anthony and Heather underwent their Devourings separately. They met roughly 2 weeks after Heather's and teamed up together, eventually deciding to marry. Michael and Winter underwent their Devourings naturally in their youths (thanks to living in such close proximity to their parents' Horrors all their lives), but Lily had it forced upon her. Anthony fully believes he did the right thing for Lily's sake, even if she doesn't understand or appreciate it right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet - they come pre-baked with story hooks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T20:33:55-08:00","id":1041086,"title":"","content":"<b>Eshmaki Nemesis:</b> What do you know about ninjas? Not a god damn thing if your information comes from kung fu movies, comic books and video games! But that's okay, because The Shadow is here educate you on the proper way of ninjutsu. That is to say, he's so good at concealing his presence that nobody even knows he exists! Well, there are some exceptions, the Brood for one. And then there's the Heroes that try to hunt him down, chasing him all over the city with a katana strapped to their back like they were in some wire fu action movie. But to mainstream society, he's unheard of; not even a whisper upon the lips of others.<br /> <br /> Like the shinobi of old, The Shadow is a revolutionary. He targets the corrupt and powerful, those who abuse their authority over others and he deals with them appropriately. He carries out his feeding with the utmost professionalism, killing non essential targets only as a last resort, and leaving forensics investigators tearing their hair out as they search the crime scene top to bottom in search of any evidence that can identify the culprit. <br /> <br /> <br /> Their Lair a Japanese ghost village under a moonlight night and with a heavy fog rolling through the streets. The misty atmosphere can easily turn the inexperienced visitor around as they run in circles trying to navigate the village. And the creepy atmosphere has been known to play tricks with the mind as unwelcome visitors lose their wits and begin to hallucinate. Not so for The Shadow, however, for this is their village and they know every nook and cranny. They've stashed supplies and traps all over the place, and they can eliminate trespassers before they even realize he's there!<br /> <br /> The true identity of their Horror is unknown to everybody but The Shadow, himself. Nobody has ever gotten a clear enough look at it to provide more than a hazy description at best. Collaborating reports state that it is shaped like a man and has a face that reminds them of a snarling demon, but anything beyond that is unconfirmed speculation. Even his own Broodmates remain frustrated by his insistence to remain hidden in the mists of his village when he hosts their company in his Lair.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> 4 (Poor Light, Mirages Fog, Maze)<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> From the Darkness, Shadowed Soul, Relentless Hunter, Limb from Limb<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You Deserve This, They Are All Around You, You Will Never Rest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T02:36:01-08:00","id":1041157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1036593#post1036593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Anthony and Heather underwent their Devourings separately. They met roughly 2 weeks after Heather's and teamed up together, eventually deciding to marry. Michael and Winter underwent their Devourings naturally in their youths (thanks to living in such close proximity to their parents' Horrors all their lives), <b>but Lily had it forced upon her. Anthony fully believes he did the right thing for Lily's sake, even if she doesn't understand or appreciate it right now.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, just noticed I forgot to detail the heights and weights of the kids. :P<br /> <br /> Went back and edited that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is supposed to be incredibly disturbing and alarming and sad, right? I'm getting strong child predator vibes from this writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:13:51-08:00","id":1041240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1041157#post1041157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is supposed to be incredibly disturbing and alarming and sad, right? I'm getting strong child predator vibes from this writeup.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it's done right, it can come across as tragic, yes. Lots of parents do something harmful to their kids under the belief that it will benefit them in the long run. Anthony's method of helping Lily was just a touch more extreme than others. Yes, he tore her soul to pieces and replaced them with a monster that compels her to destroy everything she touches.<br /> <br /> <b>But look at the alternatives:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> 1 - A normal human in a family of Beasts, Lily would have likely been driven insane with terror.<br /> <br /> 2 - One (or more) of the family members loses control one day and Lily ends up hurt or killed as a result.<br /> <br /> 3 - Lily accidentally finds out about her family's dark secret and inadvertently becomes a Hunter (possibly even a Hero) as she tries to stop them.<br /> <br /> 4 - Lily never discovers her family's true nature and goes through life unaware they have been lying to her since birth.<br /> <br /> <br /> All of these possibilities, Anthony considered, and he figured his solution was the best option.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:44:32-08:00","id":1041286,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it was very disappointing that Lily didn't respond to the grooming as well as her older siblings, and the family was very worried that she would tell a teacher (or worse, the cops!) and chose to force the issue. But that doesn't really change the fact that violating your own child with a soul-eating monster from Astral Nightmare Zone isn't a thing that sympathetic characters usually do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T10:22:34-08:00","id":1041332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1041286#post1041286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it was very disappointing that Lily didn't respond to the grooming as well as her older siblings, and the family was very worried that she would tell a teacher (or worse, the cops!) and chose to force the issue. But that doesn't really change the fact that violating your own child with a soul-eating monster from Astral Nightmare Zone isn't a thing that sympathetic characters usually do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;She's only 12, she'll understand once she's older.&quot;</i> - that's pretty much his argument on the subject.<br /> <br /> Anthony's not inherently a jackass, he took no pleasure in what he did to Lily and has been trying to make amends for it ever since. And she's not alone during this transitional period, she has four blood relatives who are perfectly willing to offer their support and guidance, should she ask for it. He's less of a child predator and more of an overbearing parent who's already planned their child's life out for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> In Lily's case, however, she is on the verge of puberty, when her hormones kick in and her emotions run wild. That was already stressful enough without having to worry about feeding a Ravager on top of everything else. She might be able to forgive her father for the thing's he's done, eventually.... but right now, she's too angry to see the big picture, or the reasons for her father's actions.<br /> <br /> Not much different from most teenagers going through their rebellious phase, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-31-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T03:42:18-08:00","id":1048157,"title":"","content":"<b>Carl, the Goblin King:</b> A bitter and cynical man, Carl's childhood was filled with empty promises and broken dreams. All throughout his youth, people told him dreams came true and that he could be anything he wanted. So when reality kicked in, Carl was crushed and retreated into his own fantasy realm as a way of coping with the disappointment and anger he felt towards the world. On the day of his 21st birthday, however, Carl's dreams really did come true; but not the kind that anybody wanted!<br /> <br /> Almost immediately following the events of his Devouring, Carl became ravenous to learn as much about the supernatural as he could. He began devoting all his time and energy into tracking down occult knowledge, magical trinkets and artifacts of power, which for a normal person would probably have turned up bunk. But as a member of the supernatural community, Carl achieved a surprising level of success in his hunts. Eventually, he discovered a way to contact the True Fae, and that is where Carl's legend truly begins, for he realized that Arcadia held nearly limitless magical potential, and he wanted it for himself. Carl is now the head of a human trafficking ring that caters to the denizens of Arcadia. Those who are kidnapped by his organization are sold off to the highest bidder in exchange for magical items and secrets. Changelings can no longer bring themselves to utter Carl's name without spitting in disgust, so they simply call him the Goblin King!<br /> <br /> It probably comes as no surprise that Carl has his sights set on Incarnation, at which point he plans to take up a more permanent residence near Arcadia. In fact, he's already figured out a way to solidify his Legend as the Goblin King; he plans to sell an entire band of Heroes to the True Fae as slaves. It's a dangerous plan that borders on the realm of suicidal, but it will be so deliciously exquisite if he can pull it off.<br /> <br /> Carl's Lair is a vast, torch lit goblin market held deep underground where slaves are bartered for with magic. Black iron cages built into the walls, floors and celing house a variety of mortals waiting to be sold off to the highest bidder. There are dozens of such captives, but most of them are simply illusions generated to inspire fear in unwanted visitors. Only prisoners who actually get sold off are real, and they only comprise maybe a tenth of the Goblin King's monthly stock. Those who aren't locked in cages are paraded through the streets in chains, their hands, feet and necks shackled together as whips are cracked against their exposed flesh. The market is shielded by several hundred feet worth of rock in any direction, which prevents electronic devices from functioning properly due to poor signal coverage and magnetic interference. As with any slave market, the atmosphere is constantly noisy, and filled with the sounds of excited bidding, rattling chains, and wailing captives.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Power<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A foul and ugly goblin, Carl's horror stands six feet tall and is morbidly obese at 462 lbs. His ears are gnarled and floppy like a pig's, while his nose is bulbous and his skin is a mottled orange. His yellow eyes are too large for human sockets and a protruding overbite reveals his sharp teeth to onlookers. He dresses himself in wolf pelts, with an assortment of accessories made from human bones. The most prominent of which is the belt made of skulls he wears around his waist.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: Honest - If Carl has any redeeming qualities, it's that he prides himself on being a fair and honest businessman. Treat him with respect, and he will do the same to you, provided you're not currently up for market. Carl has even developed a multitude of powers dedicated to appraising others and deciphering truth from falsehoods.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Relentless - Carl's hunger for power is all consuming, and once he finds something he wants, he won't just give it up without a fight. Of course, this also means that he will go to nearly any lengths to satisfy the terms of an agreement, regardless of who gets hurt along the way.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Enslave a band of Heroes (Long Term), Capture a red haired virgin (short term)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> 8 (Disruption, Cramped, Mirages, Stinging, Poor Light, Echoing)<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You Must Obey, Everything You Do Is Worthless, You Can't Wake Up, You Cannot Run<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Eye of Heaven, Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must, Unbreakable, Shadowed Soul, Looming Presence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-15-2017, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T08:44:10-08:00","id":1049309,"title":"","content":"Two little ideas that cropped up due to reading Lovecraft again...<br /> <br /> <b>Francis Thurston: </b>A likeable professor, knowledgeable on anthropology and the occult as well as a lover of art, who takes care of his chosen students. He can be harsh when it comes to work, and working with him leaves people feeling drained and exhausted, but it also often ends up their best work yet. He considers it in human's best interest to stay away from vampires and werewolves and the like, and will scare them off if possible. On the other hand, he can be a cruel opponent that gives people searching too strongly for the supernatural exactly what they were looking for, to show them that they cannot handle that at all, and feeds by breaking their world, even if that means driving them quite literally insane. The lesson he teaches is a simple one: &quot;Ignorance is bliss. Don't look too hard at the darkness.&quot;<br /> Professor Thurston used to run with a small Krewe and gets along quite well with the local Kindred due to the amount of cover-up work he does, and likes to go diving in his free time.<br /> Unlike many other Beasts, he likes to stay fed and relies more on his Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Makara<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> Cthulhu - an gigantic abomination of man, dragon and kraken. With three sets of eyes, a greenish gelatinous body and flabby claws it is a mind-numbing monster that simply should not be. The Chambers are the island with alien geometry and the city of R'lyeh itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: Parental- Thurston deeply cares for his prot\u00e9g\u00e9s, and goes to quite some length to make sure they stay safe.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Vicious- Thurston doesn't believe in half measures. When he gets serious, he leaves lifes (and minds) in shambles.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Mirages, Slick, Unstable, Exposed / Darkness, Flooded, Diseased<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold, My True Form!, You Can't Wake Up, Flying and Falling, They are all around you, You can't take it with you<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Mimir's Wisdom, Heart of the Ocean, Relentless Hunter, Looming Presence, Cyclopean Strength, Eye of Heaven<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Richard Upton Pickman:</b><br /> The Pickmans were a rich and respected family. Along came Richard, and things got complicated: diagnosed early on with a variety of derangements, he had always been sort of a creepy child. His devouring made everything worse. His family was helpless, and on the verge of giving up, when they met a therapist claiming to have a solution: While he most likely would never be able to take over the family business, Richard might be able to channel his... 'urges' in a creative manner. To his surprise, Richard found he liked that idea very much, and ever since found his very own niche. A crazy artist creating absurd, partly abstruse and always shocking pieces, Pickman is a sort of a fringe celebrity. However, unbeknown to most, each of his paintings are based on real situations: some Pure hunting humans, a Mummy punishing a would-be thief, kindred dueling each other, a Hero slaying a broodmate, the same Hero being taken down in revenge - he seeks out places and scenes where someone loses their most important posession: their live. From each scenery, he takes something to turn into his paintings (which are not on sale, just showcased). This could be actual blood for a painting, a brush or braiding made from a werewolf's hair, kindred teeth turned into tiny figurines, Promethean hide for binding a book, the strange symbols he saw in a mages book making up the edging, human bones crumbled and used as colouring, jewlery with inlaid soulstones etc.<br /> Of course, if there is no murder or similar loss he can feed upon, he simply has to make his own food.<br /> He recently started a new project: &quot;Facebook&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Collector<br /> <br /> <b>Horror: </b>A humanoid with a freakishly large, canine head and long limbs with horrifying claws, the Ghoul is a rotten creature that manages to disgust with its sight alone, let alone its smell of rotten meat and feces. It has no fur, so you can see it is practically blueish-green skin and bones, and has weird spiky growths on its spine. It would seem a dangerous animal if not for its eyes, betraying an abundance of cunning and intelligence and turning it into a far more scary monstrosity.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: Cautious - Pickman is a right bastard, one who knows how to stay out of trouble, and he won't hesitate doing anything necessary to stay safe.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Watchful - He is there, watching you. He sees what is happening to you, he might even be responsible for it, and if you are very unlucky, the last thing you'll see is his face.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Poor Light, Extreme Cold, Rotting / Stench, Toxic, Decayed<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Run Away, Fear is Contagious, Your Rage consumes you, You are Lost, Tabula Rasa, They are all around you<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Needs Must, Limb from Limb, Shadowed Soul, Basilisk's Touch, From the Shadows","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T08:41:56-08:00","id":1049873,"title":"","content":"A Set of 2 idea's I've had<br /> <br /> <b>Terrance Jones:</b> Terrance has always had problems fitting in. He has a dark sense of humor that comes from a long period of having really bad stuff happen to him and his family for years, what made it worse for him was the ability to see what was going to happen in Dreams before hand and no-one ever believing him. He grew up jumping from household to household as not many families have been able to deal with his Twisted sense of humor. He never meet any Children or much of the Supernatural before his own Self Devouring. After abit of traveling and seeing what the world is really like Terry decided to settle down and open a Hotel that provides a Unique selling point, &quot;If you Sleep here you will have Nightmares&quot; It has became a local Tourist trap and a minor Landmark in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Ruin<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> (Shadow Giant) A Hulking Great shadow that hunches over and is wearing a faded old red Ringmasters outfit. It might not be the most Horrific of Monsters, But it is not his look that makes him horrific.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Loyal - &quot;See I can live with you trying to wreck my stuff... but you hurt my staff.. That I cannot Allow you to get away with.&quot; If you are his friend or part of his staff he will move heaven and earth for you. Betray his trust... and he will end you.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Seductive - &quot;Come one, come all, see the Truth of the World as it is... Unfiltered&quot; seeing all things as nothing but a playground of the mind he loves to Whisper secrets to people and let them come to there own Ruin from it.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Blinding Light, Darkness, Cramped, Echoing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Markus &quot;Tulip&quot; Henry:</b> Markus hates people, they are nasty, stupid and petty. He would rather a life less ordinary then deal with the idiocy of people who don't know what they actually want, He would rather sit on his computer playing games in another world and shut out the world then deal with people. Sometimes however he finds himself unable to ignore them for long as they keep pestering him about things. &quot;Why aren't you Working?&quot; &quot;Why aren't you dealing with the bills?&quot; &quot;You need to help me with this and that! Get up!&quot;. After finally getting booted from his apartment he has meet up With Terrance and managed to get a job.... He's only slightly miffed that he needs to meet up with people in their dreams. Ow.. and there's the Fact his Horror is Female......<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Ugallu<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Punishment<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> (Yuki-Onna) White Haired, Fair Faced, Icy Demeanor and ultimately enticing, &quot;Tulip&quot; is lovely to encounter and will bring you into her garden and let you watch the weather with her. She is Intoxicating to be around and a brilliant face to talk too... Except she doesn't Give a Shit about you. She just wants to too keep talking... And let you harm yourself in her Garden.<br /> <br /> <b>Life: </b>Shy - &quot;Why can't you just leave me alone... I don't want anything to do with you....&quot; People annoy Markus, he loathes them. He doesn't want to share much with people if he can help it.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Judgemental - &quot;Everyone has done Something that has harmed someone else. You need not tell me.. I Know. I KNOW.&quot; Everyone has some secret they keep... Those secrets are your damnation. Tulip will treat you like shit and make you suffer, atleast untill you melt her Heart.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Blizzard, Fog, Extreme Cold, Razored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":". 02-16-2017, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:19:20-08:00","id":1049883,"title":"","content":"<b>Anthony Gote:</b> If the Begotten consider each other to be part of one extended family, then Anthony is the black sheep who behaves inappropriately at family gatherings. For as long as anyone can remember, Anthony has lived a life of decadence. He wasn't incredibly wealthy, but he also showed no interest in becoming a productive member of society. A hedonist and a lech, Anthony squandered his potential in favor of satisfying his base urges. After his Devouring, this personality became more destructive, because Anthony is no longer content to ruin his own life, but now feels the need to ruin the lives of others, as well!<br /> <br /> Anthony Gote has built his legend around being a creature of temptation. When he finds a victim, he offers to help them get what they want out of life, often with little or no charge. It seems harmless at first, but over time, they come to depend on Anthony, to the point where they can no longer take care of themselves because they're used to having everything handed to them on demand. Once he feels they can't live without him, he severs contact and feeds on the terror that comes with them struggling to survive without his assistance.<br /> <br /> In his attempts to provide people with what they think they need, Anthony came into the company of a cabal of morally dubious mages and formed a kinship with them. It was from their tutelage that he learned about the occult, as well as a number of supernatural methods in which to obtain resources, or perform deeds that would be difficult (if not impossible) by mundane methods.<br /> <br /> Anthony's Lair is a place of debauchery and shame. It takes the shape of a densely overgrown forest, with a thick fog rolling through the trees to confuse the senses of those who pass through it. The pungent scent of musk fills the air. Visions of beautiful, naked men and women flit in and out of sight through the fog, the sound of playful laughter and sensual moaning can be heard off in the distance, enticing wayward travelers to head towards its direction in hopes of finding somebody to talk to. Unfortunately, those who take the bait have a better chance of encountering the forest's baphomet, than they do finding a trail guide!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Ugallu<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Ruin<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> Baphomet - Possessing the head and legs of a goat, the torso of a large breasted woman and the genitals of a well endowed man, Anthony's horror is immediately recognized as a creature of lust and desire. A pentagram star has been branded into his forehead, while his eyes are red like hot coals and his fur is as black as a starless night. A pair of black feathered wings grow from their backside, and look strong enough to support him in flight.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Selfless - Anthony is a man of the people, or so he would have you believe. He potrays himself as being incredibly generous towards others and is willing to offer his aid without asking for anything in return. At least until he gets hungry, that is.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Seductive - Anthony prefers to avoid hostilities, especially when there's a chance he can turn a potential enemy into an ally. Rather than bring them to ruin personally, he prefers to subtly lead them down the path of self destruction, feeding once his victims realize they've caused their own downfall!<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Become a Cult Leader (Long Term), Seduce a Wiccan (short term)<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> 6 (Undergrowth, Fog, Stench, Mirages, Echoing)<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> The Void Is Waiting, Flying and Falling, You Must Obey, You Are Better Than Them,<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Wings of the Raptor, Alien Allure, Eye of Heaven, Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must, Siren's Treacherous Song<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Victor Marls:</b> From the snowy regions of Canada, Victor Marls was once a member of the mounted police force and had a decently successful career at the time. That changed, however, when he was sent out to arrest what he assumed to be another dangerous criminal who had a history of murder. Long story short, the trail turned cold, and pretty soon after that, everything else began to turn cold as well. Despite his training with the mounties, Victor mysteriously became lost in the forest at night and was facing the threat of freezing to death, accompanied by starvation. Alone and on the edge of death, Victor closed his eyes for one last dream, and that's when his quarry appeared before him. For reasons Victor still doesn't understand, they saved his life that night, but condemned him to a fate even worse than the one he would have faced.<br /> <br /> Victor has convinced everybody from his previous life that he died in the forest, and with good reason. He wouldn't want anybody he cared about to see him in the state he's become; a monster with an eating disorder, who spends more time commiting murders than solving them. Adding to the problem is the fact that Victor tries to deny his hunger for as long as he possibly can, which causes him to be in a nearly constant state of low satiety, which is a very dangerous state to be around when predators are involved. Thankfully he's met a brood that helps him deal with the changes that have occured in his life, but it's still a rocky transition.<br /> <br /> A self loathing Beast, Victor secretly has a death wish that he keeps from the rest of his brood. He would love nothing more than to be human again, but at the same time, he knows he doesn't deserve that life anymore. The deaths of too many people weigh on his conscience, and you don't go back to a happy life after that. Victor has recently begun harboring a fascination with the Retreat. If his horror were confined to the Primordial Dream, then at least he could prevent it from physically harming people (or so he believes). But he's hesitant to go through with it at this time. Lulling his Horror to sleep would require <i>a lot</i> of murders, and he's just not sure he can go through with it, even if it would save more lives in the long run. Such is the tortured dilemma of Victor Marls.<br /> <br /> Victor's lair is a grueling endurance test that mirrors the snowy forests he almost died in. Strong winds and heavy snowfall create an atmosphere of frigid air. Even those who protect themselves against such temperatures will find that the slick ice permeating the environment adds yet another complication to traversing the land. Fatigue and hunger rapidly sets in, draining victims of their strength to carry on as they prepare to lay down in the snow and await death.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> Windego - An impossibly tall monstrosity, Victor's horror possesses the head of a deer, the legs of a horse, the body of a man, the claws of a bear and the teeth of a wolf. It stands almost 15 feet tall, but is so horribly malnourished that it's nearly anorexic in body mass. It's ravenous eyes dart about in search of meat, any meat, with which to satisfy the unending hunger that plagues its gut.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Shy - Victor does not do very well around new people, and even his own brood have a tough time bonding with him in public. This shyness causes him to be quiet and withdrawn, unless circumstances compel him to take action<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Vicious - Because of the perpetual state of starvation in which he keeps himself, Victor finds it almost impossible to restrain himself when he feeds. By the time he's finished with his prey, the only plausible explanation for the state he leaves his victims in is that there was some kind of wild animal attack!<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Undergo The Retreat (long term), Kill a fat man (short term)<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> 7 (Extreme Cold, Blizzard, Slick, Crosswinds, Heavy )<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Fear is Contagious, Behold My True Form, Run Away, You Are Lost<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Unbreakable, Storm Lashed, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, Limb From Limb, Looming Presence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-16-2017, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T03:31:21-08:00","id":1050405,"title":"","content":"Another 2 Lovecraft-inspired Beasts (those stories are a treasure trove! more is sure to come)<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Sans-Serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Sans-Serif\">&quot;I have seen the dark universe yawning<br /> <img src=\"http://www.hplovecraft.com/pics/PixelClear.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>Where the black planets roll without aim\u2014<br /> Where they roll in their horror unheeded,<br /> <img src=\"http://www.hplovecraft.com/pics/PixelClear.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>Without knowledge or lustre or name.&quot;</span></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <b>Robert Blake: </b>An author of crime and horror short stories, Robert Blake is a shy intellectual, with an interest in architecture and history. His Devouring was unusual insofar as it seemingly was triggered by an artifact. The rush of power was underwhelming, actually, but the sense of fulfillment, of being something other than just a shy author was enourmous, and even though Bob leads his life pretty much a lot like he used to, there are some changed habits, of course.<br /> He hunts cults - after having decided on any group that keeps isolated, exploits their members and/or refuses them the right to leave, he starts researching on who the most important people are. He starts with the recruiters: when they sleep, he draws symbols on their forehead, with blood (he gets it from a butcher). Then, he goes after the higher ups: indoctrinators, people with pull and rights. They get a haircut, or just a shallow cut, whatever he feels like. Finally, he turned to stalking the higher ups... sometimes, their bodies turn up, hit by lightning in their own house. Should anyone attempt to repair the cult, take leadership, after all this, he disappears.<br /> The lesson Blake teaches is a simple one: &quot;They can't protect you - they can't even protect themselves.&quot; He prides himself on the idea that he helps people get back on with their life.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> The Haunter of the Dark. A dark, bat-winged, semi-material creature with a huge three-lobed burning eye for a head, the <a href=\"http://s.hswstatic.com/gif/stufftoblowyourmind-23-2014-04-haunterofthedark2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Horror</a>'s touch is corrosive and deadly.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: Shy - Blake is not the most social of people, and tends to hold back a lot.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Relentless- If Blake has decided you are his next victim, nothing will stop him from seeing things through.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair: </b>Blakes Lair is an old abandoned church, the different rooms the chambers. The Heart is the uppermost tower chamber and contains the Shining Trapezohedron. the Lair traits are Poor Light, Corrosive, Decayed, Thin Air (Dusty) and Electrified.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Robert Blake is in possession of a powerful artifact: The Shining Trapezohedron. This &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Sans-Serif\">nearly black, red-striated polyhedron with many irregular flat surfaces&quot; is a </span></span>4-inches big spherical crystal which grants him access to &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=1050370#post1050370\">You must have it</a>&quot; and &quot;Mimir's Wisdom&quot;, and can be used to watch past or future events where the stone was present. As long as in the posession of a Beast, it adds +1 to its effective Lair. However, the Trapezohedron must be kept in a poorly lit place (which is why he keeps it in his Lair most of the time) and once a month, a life must be ceremonically extinguished in its presence. Otherwise, it's effects turn on the owner (Lair -1, if that would reduce Lair to 0 the Beast gains the Slumbering condition. Furthermore, she is affected by You must have it for a scene every day until either the gem changes ownership or the ceremony is held). There is some connection between Nephren-Ka and the polyhedron, and Blake assumes Nemes Hamadi must have created it.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold, My True Form!, Fear is Infectious, You are not alone<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Needs Must, Shadow-Souled, Wings of the Raptor, Storm-Lashed, Limb from Limb<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nemes Hamadi:</b><br /> Nemes is a scientist from Egypt, but also a highranking diplomat. In addition to being highly charismatic and having a lot of pull in governments and tons of resources, the industries are crazy for his inventions. Little do they know that the star-eyed idealistic do-gooder has a nefarious plan: ultimately, the relationships he makes possible will come crashing down, his inventions will cause new problems... and everyone will look to him for help. Eventually, they all will realized they are but toys in his hands. When he feels particularly vicious, he doesn't just destroy someones career, but their sanity as well. He rarely feeds deeply by killing though, since it seems less lasting, and he wants his quarry to know and remember. The lesson he teaches is &quot;You are not enough&quot;.<br /> Every now and then, someone like Randolf Carter comes along, and reaches his goals despite Nemes' adversity. The Ugallu simply applauds them, considering them a chosen few, and carries on, because he knows something they dont: He will get to them some other time. Right now, his eyes are on a different goal: Inheritance is in his grasp.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Ugallu<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Tyrant<br /> <br /> <b>Horror: </b>Nephren-Ka. A humongous pitch-black man with shining eyes dressed as a pharao, buth instead of a head he has a giant tentacle with a mouth.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: Honest- Nemes does not lie, if only because he doesn't have to. He will get you to do his will just fine like this.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Seductive- Nemes makes people do things they come to despise.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Mirages, Maze, Extreme Heat, Blazing Light, Disruption, Engulfing, Crosswinds<b> - </b>a desert patch where Nyarlathothep can just watch his prey lose all hope, running around disoriented and helpless, before taking care of them, exhausted and weak, one by one.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Fear is Contagious, You must obey, Everything you do is Worthless, You are alone, You deserve this, They are all around you, You can't wake up<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Eye of Heaven, Alien Allure, Siren's Treacherous Song, Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must, Storm-Lashed, Looming Presence<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:56:22-08:00","id":1053323,"title":"","content":"I challenge someone to recreate Strahd von Zarovich's realm of Barovia--and/or Castle Ravenloft--as a Beast Lair! &gt;x3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:56:11-08:00","id":1053357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1053323#post1053323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I challenge someone to recreate Strahd von Zarovich's realm of Barovia--and/or Castle Ravenloft--as a Beast Lair! &gt;x3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not even that hard;<br /> <br /> The Lair of Stanislav Zaguche, the ancient Apex of Transylvania, puts the truth to his frequent claim that he is as much a part of the land as the land is part of him; more than once, only the manifestation of a fellow Beast's Horror is any indication you have left the physical world and are now within his soul. Due to careful and precise claiming and generation of Chambers (the Count is excellent at subtle, precisely targeted psychological torture), the Lair is an almost perfect replication of his hometown, the surrounding forest, and the castle in which the Anakim dwells. It even has people in it, though they're more extensions of the Lair than anything self-aware. Scratching the surface, though, reveals the truth; the real Barovia, while certainly not winning any First World Lifestyle awards any time soon, is aware the world around it is changing, and almost reluctantly keeps up with the world enough to survive in a modern Romania; the actual villagers love their cheap smartphones (it's what they can afford) and have AC units next to their fireplaces. The villagers of Lair-Barovia seem to living fossils from at least 80 years back, if not further; most of them don't have the slightest clue what a phone <i>is, </i>and they are utterly flabbergasted by modern clothing, let alone internal heating. While the earthly woods have been thinned out by loggers and the slow expansion of the town, the Dream's forest actively resists any attempt to make it more tame, and the dream-animals regularly patrol at the edge of the light, almost completely unafraid of humans. Above all is the mist; Barovia is foggy, but Stanislav's version might as well be a flightless cloud. Sometimes, it even gets so thick, you start to suffocate-there's too much water for lungs to extract oxygen from the cloudy air. This is, of course, entirely the result of the owning Beast's own personality; the Count is an old, old man, and his nostalgia for the heady days of pre-WWI Transylvania infects everything in his heart, let alone his Family's inherent nature as the Fear of Power; on some level, the Dread Lord of Ravenloft wants anyone modern to feel the distinct discomfort that comes from being out of their own time. It only becomes more obvious as any intruder or guest nears the family's castle, the inner Chambers surrounding his Heart; the castle is remarkably well-preserved in the real world, but the Primordial Dream's imitation is pristine and new, a call-back to its master's childhood and young adulthood before the Great War. Entering, however, gradually reveals the fractal patterns of regrets, psychological issues, and entitlement that drives Stansilav; the castle is borderline empty of any inhabitation, minus what ghosts and revenants the Count lets dwell within. Dust gathers, rooms stand unattended and eternally ready for guests and family that never seem to arrive-a profound sense of loneliness and emptiness pervades every single cubic centimeter of the Dream's version of Castle Ravenloft. Of course, anyone who has figured out the crazed obsession that drives the Count's nercomantic experiments may start to wonder if the castle is the &quot;too quiet&quot; levels that generally proceed a mad ambush. They would be right; Besides the batlike Dread Lord itself, the castle is infested with tiny little monsters born from the dream itself, each one born from a self-justification and cruel action the Count has done in his mad quest to reclaim Tatyana-to say nothing of the aforementioned ghosts and revenants, who become rather irate at anyone invading their landlord's soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T13:49:03-08:00","id":1053408,"title":"","content":"You're amazing. &lt;3<br /> <br /> So would the revenants and ghosts be real, or are they constructs of the lair itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:55:51-08:00","id":1053511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1053408#post1053408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're amazing. &lt;3<br /> <br /> So would the revenants and ghosts be real, or are they constructs of the lair itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>I Would say Both. Some are Trapped souls of visitors, others are born whole stuff of the Dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:22:49-08:00","id":1053557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1053511#post1053511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I Would say Both. Some are Trapped souls of visitors, others are born whole stuff of the Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another question would be if Barovia were a collection of different lairs, with the Apex being the lord of Castle Ravenloft. The Fog would most likely then be the shared trait amongst them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T19:05:34-08:00","id":1053576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1053511#post1053511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I Would say Both. Some are Trapped souls of visitors, others are born whole stuff of the Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less. The revenants are well, revenants, though-they're vampire spawn WoD!Strahd lets live in his Lair in return for help with him hunting. They're the actual vampires to his Beast-That-Looks-And-Acts-Like-One.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As for the Fog, yeah. That's the Hive's Lair Tilt, representing the fear that comes from <i>knowing </i>something's out there, but not what-they live in <i>Transylvania </i>after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 02-22-2017, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:54:23-08:00","id":1055293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1053576#post1053576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More or less. The revenants are well, revenants, though-they're vampire spawn WoD!Strahd lets live in his Lair in return for help with him hunting. They're the actual vampires to his Beast-That-Looks-And-Acts-Like-One.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As for the Fog, yeah. That's the Hive's Lair Tilt, representing the fear that comes from <i>knowing </i>something's out there, but not what-they live in <i>Transylvania </i>after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm trying to picture the setting in CoD terms, and some of the ideas are indeed tempting to try. What if Baba Lysaga was a Circle of the Crone who knew <s>Strahd</s> Stanislav before his Devouring? What if the Amber Temple was somehow connected with either the Underworld, or was an Awakened Mystery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:05:51-08:00","id":1055336,"title":"","content":"<b>[Ugallu]The Eyes Sees All:</b> He's a normal-seeming man, 'till you realize he works at a store that sells surveillance equipment, learn that he 'worked for the government' overseas and has no records going back farther than a decade ago. He <i>watches</i>, too, watches <i>everything</i> and <i>everyone</i>. He knows more than he should. He makes cryptic remarks regarding others' personal lives. He knows their daily routines. He talks to nobody, yet he <i>knows</i> things.<br /> <br /> But...in his Lair, hidden in his soul, he is an artificially intelligent program running the obsessively-detailed automated security of a nightmarish apartment complex. Wherever you go, he has an eye watching, or a bug listening or a motion sensor to note your passing. He sees <i>everything</i> here, and has no tolerance for rules breakers.<br /> <br /> His Lesson is simple: <i>no one is truly invisible, anymore, and everything you do has a data trail.</i> He finds criminals who commit insurance fraud, steals and uses credit cards, misrepresents themselves to others for profit, and so on---<i>and he hunts them</i>, first in the material realm then in his Lair.<br /> <br /> He finds <i>everything</i> about you, but he never reveals it. He feeds on the fear that he's <i>watching</i> you, he knows all your misdeeds, and, at a moment's notice, <i>he can bring it all crashing down.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 02-26-2017, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:53:30-08:00","id":1055375,"title":"","content":"<b>[Dark Eras 1500 AD {Ugallu}]The Prince of the Forest:</b> In ancient times Beasts such as he were honored as gods. Now, as the year 1500 AD approaches, this Beast is the Thing in the Forest, the elf-lord who rides out with the Wild Hunt to scourge the Earth of sinners. He represents the unknown factors of nature: the ravening wolf, the murderous boar, the defiant stag. Under the shadow of his wings, his forest has become a source of constant terror.<br /> <br /> Among humans, the Prince of the Forest is a wildman, barely civilized, purposefully living at the outskirts of human habitation. But, there is <b>another</b> forest, a <b>hidden</b> forest, where gigantic owls hold enigmatic parliaments and where witches come to barter away their souls. The Beast's Horror is a kaballistic angel, a gargantuan thing of wheels of fire and knives for feathers, casting light as other things cast shadows. It speaks in a billion voices and its gaze is terrifying in its scrutiny.<br /> <br /> You see, the Prince of the Forest makes...<i>pacts</i> with mortals: an occult favor in return for a mundane favor. But these 'mundane' favors end up exposing hidden secrets, unveiling adultury and acts of brutality no one suspected was there. The Prince of the Forest trades away petty sorcerous tasks done on your behalf---and in turn, <i>he sets your world on fire.</i><br /> <br /> He is a metaphorical demon. He associates with imps and witches and mediums whose souls are wrapped in the embrace of hoary ancient shades. He has no mercy. And he <i>will</i> collect on what he's owed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 02-26-2017, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T05:49:05-08:00","id":1055606,"title":"","content":"<b>Anakim Nemesis, the Spider Goddess:</b> Ask anybody who knows about dreams and they'll probably tell you that they're symbolic depictions of your subconscious. If you dream about spiders, it means you're trying to run from your problems, or so the theory goes. This Beast has chosen to capitalize on this fear by preying upon those who attempt to shirk their responsibilities. Whether it's family, work, religion, governance, medicine, convicted criminals or public servants, everybody must make personal sacrifices in their life to ensure that society continues to function. And if they will not offer themselves willingly, then she will drag them to the altar by force!<br /> <br /> <br /> In her human form, she is a <i>Loyal</i> member of the community who recognizes that the needs of the many outweigh the needs of the few. At times, she's even put needs of others above herself, like when she found out her own daughter was a dangerous slasher who needed to be taken off the streets. In the days since her Devouring, the Spider Goddess has become a judge within the judicial system, one who does not play favorites and resists all attempts at bribery and extortion. No singular person or family is above society, a fact you will become acutely aware of, should you find yourself in her courtroom.<br /> <br /> <br /> In her monster form, she <i>Relentlessly</i> hunts down those she deems irresponsible. The torso of a beautiful woman attached to the body of a gargantuan arachnid. Eight eyes adorn her face, while her silky white hair spills down to her waist. A mouth of fangs with paralytic venom and a carapace thick enough to deflect bullets. The heart of her lair contains a stone altar, splattered with dried blood. When she captures her target, she places them bound and gagged upon it before conducting the painful ritual of sacrificing them. Hopefully the victim understands the symbolism behind her theatrics, or she may feel the need to pay them additional visits!<br /> <br /> <br /> The rest of her lair takes place in a sweltering jungle with unfeasibly large spider webs laced throughout the trees and bushes. Victims find navigating through the jungle to be exhausting as no matter how far they run, they never seem to make as much progress as they would like. The weight of the world bares down on them, and some claim they have difficulty breathing, due to anxiety. Like all spiders, the Spider Goddess can sense the vibrations of her web, and she knows when another insect is traipsing through her lair.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Undergrowth, Thin Air, Heavy, Extreme Heat<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Needs Must, You Cannot Run, You Must Obey<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Looming Presence, Basilisk's Touch, Unbreakable, Relentless Hunter<br /> <br /> <b>Lesson - Humility:</b> We all must make sacrifices for the good of society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:24:46-08:00","id":1055784,"title":"","content":"<b>[Void Moment Insatiable]The Grand Maw:</b> Was it human, once? It no longer remembers: gender, sexuality, empathy, binary existence---all flotsam long since forgotten. It is the echo of the oblivion that sprawled over the heads of earliest Homo sapiens, the nothing that seemed so monstrous and unending. It is a sphere made of the night sky and gravity lenses in its presence. Everything is consumed; nothing is ejected. Not light, not life, and certainly not dreams and fears.<br /> It moves about, seemingly at random, drawn to Beasts the way wandering black holes are inexorably drawn towards stars. It no longer remembers any life prior to becoming its Moment; in human form it is mutilated and without genitals or other sexual identifiers. It drifts into town and hunts---waiting!---'till its prey makes a mistake...and then it zeroes in.<br /> The Beast's Lair slowly collapses under the Grand Maw's crushing gravimetric embrace, and light dims and sounds are consumed. The Grand Maw eats messily, and knows no restraint. Eventually, it will have consumed everything...<br /> ...<i>and then, it just moves onwards.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T02:05:46-08:00","id":1056026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1055784#post1055784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>[Void Moment Insatiable]The Grand Maw:</b> Was it human, once? It no longer remembers: gender, sexuality, empathy, binary existence---all flotsam long since forgotten. It is the echo of the oblivion that sprawled over the heads of earliest Homo sapiens, the nothing that seemed so monstrous and unending. It is a sphere made of the night sky and gravity lenses in its presence. Everything is consumed; nothing is ejected. Not light, not life, and certainly not dreams and fears.<br /> It moves about, seemingly at random, drawn to Beasts the way wandering black holes are inexorably drawn towards stars. It no longer remembers any life prior to becoming its Moment; in human form it is mutilated and without genitals or other sexual identifiers. It drifts into town and hunts---waiting!---'till its prey makes a mistake...and then it zeroes in.<br /> The Beast's Lair slowly collapses under the Grand Maw's crushing gravimetric embrace, and light dims and sounds are consumed. The Grand Maw eats messily, and knows no restraint. Eventually, it will have consumed everything...<br /> ...<i>and then, it just moves onwards.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNice. A sort of monstrous inevitability. +1 to you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:24:55-08:00","id":1056237,"title":"","content":"More Lovecraftian Characters! <b>Alfred De la Poer:</b> Alfred used to be a smart guy. Sensitive, intellectual, he was however struck with a strong interest in genealogy which would prove his doom. Having served in Afghanistan, he barely survived an attack and re-evaluated his priorities. He started studying medicine and picked up genealogy, mainly because his own father (living out his life in an asylum) would never talk about his ancestors or why he left Ireland. Upon his father's death, Alfred was approached by a lawyer who broke the truth to him: he was old aristocracy! The last of a long line to be precise. His father broke with the rest of the family, thus he never found out about the tragic accident that killed most of them, and due to his situation was unable to accept the inheritance.<br /> This was a revelation without equal, and Alfred decided to find out more about this family of his. He went to Ireland to claim Exham Priory, the ancestral estate. Soon, the Dreams started.<br /> Alfred has gone batshit-insane after finding out about his late family's secrets: among every of his ancestors' generations, there was a Beast, and they all had the same Horror. The Rats are... different. They cannot be satisfied with cutting someone, or beating someone up.<br /> No, their Hunger is quite literal - they need to consume. As the ancient Apex, and a more than just debauched influential family, the De la Poers managed to create a cult, and a secret chamber in which they did unspeakable things to humans, until they ceased to be humans and became cattle.<br /> It wouldn't do for nobility to feed on their subordinates, after all.<br /> Alfred went crazy, and has long periods of blacking out. All he knows about that time is that the Rats indulged in their Hunger to the point of slumbering, and him having to run away and keeping a low profile. At some point, the black outs became less, but the brutality stayed the same, as Alfred adapted to his new lifestyle, even started enjoying it. Under his Horror's Tutelage, he developed quickly, and after years became a fearsome force. Many a hunter met his end at the swarm's teeth, and a few Heroes met the same fate.<br /> At some point, he attacked a man on the street, and started chewing his face off right then and there.<br /> People didn't know that it was a Hero looking to kill him, and Alfred felt justified in defending himself. But now, he has all manner of people after him: heroes, the police, unhappy Kindred, neglected cultists and other hunters.<br /> For all his might: his time is running out, slowly but surely, and he knows that.<br /> But for some reason, he doesn't really care. All he can think of is making sure those after him never find out about his illegitimate son, because the bloodline must live on...<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> Rats in the Wall.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: Intellectual - Chess, history debates, correcting the museum guide: Alfred loves stimuli that challenge his mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Devouring - Alfred takes away and consumes pieces of people, and he wants them to be aware of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair: </b>Exham Priori, the old estate of the De la Poers. While the mundane thing is a pretty enough, albeit slightly scary place, the Lair version of it is downright sickening.<br /> Rotting, Diseased, Echoing, Cramped, Toxic, Maze, Poor Light, Stench, Swarm, Unstable.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold, My True Form!, Fear is Contagious, You are not alone, All your Teeth are Falling Out, Rat's Everywhere!, You cannot Run<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Infestation, Cavernous Maw, Limb from Limb, Relentless Hunter, Basilisk's Touch, Shadowed Soul, From the Shadows<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: Ancient Horror 5, Fast Refleces (advanced), Fist of Nightmares, Danger Sense (advanced), Direction Sense (Advanced), Encyclopedic Knowledge (Genealogy), Epic Potential (Dexterity), Guilty Pleasure (Cannibalism), Indomitable, Iron Skin, Iron Skin (epic), Iron Will, Killer Instinct (advanced), Parkour 5, Relentless Assault 5<br /> <br /> <br /> Next one up will be Erich Zann and/or the scary old man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T06:50:02-08:00","id":1057575,"title":"","content":"the whole &quot;needing to actually consume people&quot; thing seems more like an Insatiable though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T17:20:15-08:00","id":1057845,"title":"","content":"<b>The Fickle Mistress:</b> It is often difficult to please a Collector, but none are quite as vexing as the one who calls herself The Fickle Mistress. A frivolous and aloof creature, The Fickle Mistress desires something for no other reason than she does not already have it in her possession. Once she obtains the object of her desire, it quickly turns to trash in her hands, and she finds herself turning to new prospective treasures that she may add to her growing collection. Many have risen to greatness because of her, and just as many have fallen to ruin for the same reason. Once she's had her fun with them, she loses interest, causing them to suffer without her continued protection.<br /> <br /> Her horror is a thing of great beauty and merciless cruelty. A radiant goddess who shines down from the heavens, casting a smile upon those she favors. Her presence banishes that which would see you harmed; but the second she turns her gaze elsewhere, the dangers that threaten you sense their opportunity to strike. That is when you find yourself surrounded on all sides by the evils of the world.<br /> <br /> Her Lair is the place where all treasures go to be forgotten. Things and places which once meant the world to her now lay abandoned, falling prey to the ravages of nature as plants entangle them in a mass of crawling vines. Nothing lasts long within her realm, as decay rapidly sets in, turning even the most sparkling of treasures into rusted junk. Destructive weather conditions sweep through periodically, demolishing whatever is too brittle to remain intact any longer, and making way for new treasures to be added to the collection. And, of course, there is the celestial gleam of The Fickle Mistress that shines down from the heavens, threatening to blind those who deign to venture through her Lair unprotected.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> <i>Parental</i> - as long as The Fickle Mistress desires something (or someone), she will use everything in her power to keep them safe. Even fighting on their behalf, should they need it. Such passionate love has fooled many into believing her to be a lady of fortune, naive to the fact that everybody's luck runs out at some point.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> <i>Unexpected</i> - when The Fickle Mistress loses interest in one of her treasures, she abandons it cold turkey, regardless of the consequences involved. To be treated with such love and kindness one moment, only to be left helpless and alone in the next has caught many victims off guard, as they were not prepared to find themselves without her aid when they needed it most.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Ugallu<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Hoard<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Undergrowth (vines), Blazing Light, Decayed, Hurricane<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You will never rest, Flying and falling, You deserve this<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Eye of Heaven, Needs Must, Basilisk's Touch, Storm-Lashed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T22:01:47-08:00","id":1057931,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.bogleech.com/creepy/creepy16thedaddyface.html\" target=\"_blank\">Donny Reynolds</a><br /> <br /> Inspired by a story by Rakshasarani that is one of the creepiest damn things i have ever read. If you have issues with abusive parental figures, be warned, cause this guy is a piece of work. I would never use him as anything other than an antagonistic foil to responsibly-feeding PC Beasts, and only if I cleared it with all other players first. Anyway, tw: child abuse and here goes.<br /> <br /> <b>Father</b>: Sure, most people are lucky enough to be able to say they loved their parents. But can they deny that there was at least one time in their life when they feared them? Maybe they broke a precious item and feared their wrath? Maybe you declined an invitation to a party because you were just sure they would know? Regardless of how its used, it's undeniable how much power a parent can have over a child, and a person who has power over you is someone you cannot help but fear. And how much is a parent feared when love has no place in their household?<br /> <br /> The Father is everything you feared about your parents. He sees all, he knows all and he knows you deserve. You never know wh itat will set him off next time, only that he demands you be good boys and girls and get Daddy his newspaper quickly. His Horror is simple to imagine. Just imagine the kind of picture a small child would draw of a violently abusive father: bulging eyes, sharp teeth set in a screaming mouth, a blood-red face (turned inside out in this case) and not a trace of mercy.<br /> <br /> The man himself though, is pathetic. Too scared to truly fulfill his calling as a Nemesis and risk prosecution, he sates his Hunger by terrorizing his step-children and their friends. Get on his bad side and he'll show you the daddy face. And if you've seen it once, you never want to see it again.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: <i>Paternal - </i>He'll tell you day in and day out that he punishes them because he loves them and wants them to grow up into productive members of society. And if that requires traumatizing them into complete compliance with his exacting standards of good behaviour, so be it.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend</b>: <i>Powerhungry - </i>In the end though, everything else is just a pretext for the sick thrill of having power over those weaker than himself.<br /> <br /> <b>Family</b>: Ugallu<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger</b>: Punishment<br /> <br /> <b>Lair</b>:, Unstable, Maze, Sealed Exits, Cramped (one chamber only, based on his SUV)<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: Behold My True Form, You Deserve This, You Must Obey, The Daddy Face (Kinship: Nosferatu Vampire)*<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Looming Presence, Mimir's Wisdom, In My Image (from the forums), Dragonfire (KND references for the win, even when highly inappropriate)<br /> <br /> *uncertain on effect, but i wanted a less-lethal but still harmful and terrifying counterpart to Behold My True Form<br /> <br /> This is my first try at this. how did it turn out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 03-29-2017, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T03:20:09-08:00","id":1057981,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> That's truly a nasty piece of work. Good job!<br /> Don't know about Insatiables, so can't comment on that. But basically, his Horror wants to eat Prey to really be satisfied. Just a finger might do the trick when hungry, but when he's gorged...<br /> Similar to how some Predators need only beat up their Prey when hungry to feed, but need to break bones when sated, or outright kill them when gorged.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:41:12-08:00","id":1059759,"title":"","content":"So, i am trying yo create a Anakin.<br /> I am thinking in one that drain the power of it's victims, in other words he is not giants, he shrinks you.<br /> This would be reached with manipulation and psychological attacks, he would destroy your soul in a way you just lost the will to fight.<br /> But i don't know what would be a good Hunger to him and i don't think the atavisms in the book cover this.<br /> Suggestions?<br /> <br /> I thought in a hunger, i would be a collector that collect broken dreams and lost futures, i would take a mememto of it.<br /> <br /> About the Atavism, i would need something that brake the victim soul, maybe something that give a condition or something that take away willpower (or maybe both atavisms)<br /> <br /> I just need to think in a lesson... Maybe that you need to care about your dreams and your destiny?<br /> <br /> I found a monster called Baku, it's a dream eater.<br /> Ok, the only thing here is that they can sometimes eat all dreams (including dreams of the future)<br /> But it's just it.<br /> Maybe i should create my won horror, i want a Japanese horror... So i was thinking in a horror that would take a form of a old wise man (a hermit), he would talk to you and give advices, but if he see that you have a dream or a future opportunity that you are letting away he will eat this, destroying your dream or potential future. When he will eat your future he changes his face to a more monster like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13077,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","user":"draxdeveloper","date":". 03-07-2017, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13077-draxdeveloper","name":"draxdeveloper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T11:29:38-08:00","id":1060952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>draxdeveloper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1059759#post1059759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i am trying yo create a Anakin.<br /> I am thinking in one that drain the power of it's victims, in other words he is not giants, he shrinks you.<br /> This would be reached with manipulation and psychological attacks, he would destroy your soul in a way you just lost the will to fight.<br /> But i don't know what would be a good Hunger to him and i don't think the atavisms in the book cover this.<br /> Suggestions?<br /> <br /> I thought in a hunger, i would be a collector that collect broken dreams and lost futures, i would take a mememto of it.<br /> <br /> About the Atavism, i would need something that brake the victim soul, maybe something that give a condition or something that take away willpower (or maybe both atavisms)<br /> <br /> I just need to think in a lesson... Maybe that you need to care about your dreams and your destiny?<br /> <br /> I found a monster called Baku, it's a dream eater.<br /> Ok, the only thing here is that they can sometimes eat all dreams (including dreams of the future)<br /> But it's just it.<br /> Maybe i should create my won horror, i want a Japanese horror... So i was thinking in a horror that would take a form of a old wise man (a hermit), he would talk to you and give advices, but if he see that you have a dream or a future opportunity that you are letting away he will eat this, destroying your dream or potential future. When he will eat your future he changes his face to a more monster like.</div> </div> </div> </div>See.. I'd have him actually be a Collector of Heights.... I.E he doesn't Just shrink you... He Takes your Height and adds it to his own... so starting out... he's Small. but given time and several victims, he is a Giant, a Patchwork Giant of different skin tones and stances.....<br /> <br /> <br /> But then i'm abit of a weirdo like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T11:35:41-08:00","id":1060956,"title":"","content":"How would he do that though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T14:28:12-08:00","id":1061026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1060956#post1060956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would he do that though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dreams. The 'You Are Meat' and 'All Your Teeth Are Falling Out' Nightmares. The Looming Presence Atavism. Horrors work on dream-logic. It's only when they reach into the more physical realms that they become more limited by their laws. Atavisms and Nightmares are mutable, and can represent many things. It says in the book that Nightmares can easily be reskinned. AYTAFO could easily represent shrinking, or age, or degenerative disease, or a crippling weakness that falls upon one like a tidal wave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T16:35:47-08:00","id":1061379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1061026#post1061026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dreams. The 'You Are Meat' and 'All Your Teeth Are Falling Out' Nightmares. The Looming Presence Atavism. Horrors work on dream-logic. It's only when they reach into the more physical realms that they become more limited by their laws. Atavisms and Nightmares are mutable, and can represent many things. It says in the book that Nightmares can easily be reskinned. AYTAFO could easily represent shrinking, or age, or degenerative disease, or a crippling weakness that falls upon one like a tidal wave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he Trades with you... Or Intimidates you.. you feel yourself giving him power...and with that he takes your Size. (Or part of it) after many meetings your little more then a couple of Inches tall and part of his Collection. He doesn't need you anymore. Welcome to the Zoo.. That's the chamber he uses to store people away when he's done with them. Tall walls, tiny Furniture, housing for people.<br /> <br /> Maybe he Challenges himself sometimes and doesn't use his collected Size sometimes, he starts out like he was... and he works for every inch. Taking what he wants, gaining it step by Step, piece by piece. Those he Collects this way... he keeps in places of honor in his gallery.<br /> <br /> He Approaches as a Friend, gives you what you need (&quot;Just a taste, enough to see what I can offer&quot;) helping those that need it with things that shouldn't need to deal with. Part of the fear here would be that he can give you everything you desire/need with a &quot;Small&quot; price... But anything worth doing/earning is worth doing it yourself. Not getting it given to you... who knows when debts given are to be paid... and what is the price of having a simple life....?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:39:54-07:00","id":1063809,"title":"","content":"Erich Zann and the scary old man are on hold for now, cause I need to figure out some stuff there first.<br /> However, here you have a simple concept that should be alright to use for an early character.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> #istilllikeourconceptmore<br /> <br /> <b>Alexander Johnson: </b>A rock singer touring around. He teaches a lesson of \u201eYour loved ones are not safe (enough)\u201c by entering houses and cutting some resident's hair (preferably, the youngest child's), then leaving a letter including the hair and the words \u201eI could have\u201c to call upon the residents' Adult Fear. He prides himself on helping these people realize the threat of break-ins before something really bad happens and improving their security drastically. He is very satisfied if his sprees lead to reduced rates of break-ins and related accidents/offences. Sometimes, he takes his sweet time by visiting the same house over a period of days and doing little things first - misplacing books, keys, furniture, turning on the tv, whispering to or even touching people when they pass him by in the dark- to 'get their attention' before his great 'lesson'. He calls it his warm-up gig. That something like this could potentially end up traumatizing doesn't enter his equation, because hey - &quot;<i>Nothing bad actually happened, amirit?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Ravager<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> The Banshee mourns the death of a family member before his time is due, making her a bad omen. Alexander tries to fulfill her desires with a twist, turning it into a warning rather than a dooming message. Usually, the Banshee is satisfied by the resident's fear of what potentially could have transpired. Sometimes, it hungers for more, though - times like these, the residents will be left devastated by loss, and the whole neighbourhood will be horrified and in mourning.<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: Proud \u2013 Alex has always been proud of himself, of his ability, his hard work, and now, his lessons, too. Anything he does that allows him to boast freely to someone about it satisfies this cornerstone of his identity. Boasting about break-ins isn't exactly smart, though, despite how well-intentioned you may come off, and the moment someone takes the time to compare the 'strange break-ins' and his tours will most likely be a bad day for him.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend: </b>Watchful - Alexander feeds by dangling the possibility of what he could have done infront of his victims, letting them fully know he could've done something. He likes seeing them squirm, even more so when he is close.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair: </b>A moonlit forrest with a lake.<br /> Fog, Echoing, Poor Light.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You are not alone, You deserve this<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> From the Shadows, Siren's Treacherous Song, Shadowed Soul","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T17:06:30-07:00","id":1064085,"title":"","content":"<b>Jaad al-Shahin:</b> don't call him a terrorist, he gets very irritated when people use words they don't understand the proper definition of. He's actually more of a hitman, one who doesn't particularly care about collateral damages once he's been given a contract. Jaad, if you couldn't tell by his name, is a middle eastern man who has come to embody one of the urban legends of his people, the Ifrit. An incarnation of smoke and flames, the Ifrit is heralded as a spirit of vengeance, which is what Jaad has chosen to capitalize on. When somebody feels they have been wronged, they get in touch with him. They speak their grievances to him, offer the payment he requires and then turn him loose upon society. He doesn't just go after his contracted target, he goes after their supporters, their loved ones, their property and businesses. He burns everything to the ground so that nobody will dare follow in his victims footsteps. Sometimes, though, the lesson doesn't always stick; and that's when he receives yet another contract from a wounded party.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Shy - Assassins typically don't go around announcing themselves to the public. If somebody needs to get in contact with them, then they should already know the proper channels for doing so.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Vicious - More than a hitman, the Ifrit is a spirit of vengeance and fiery retribution. Once a target has been designated, its punishment is spectacularly brutal in its performance. Destroying his victim's livelihood, as well as their lives in general.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Punishment<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> Pitch black smoke and fiery embers coalesced into the silhouette of a man, the Ifrit is horrifying to look upon, much less approach. Its touch leaves anything smeared with greasy black soot, assuming it doesn't burst into flames. It is unbarred by mortal security measures, for it lurks in the shadows like a wraith, emerging from the dark pits and unleashing fiery hell upon everything in sight. Then, when its work is complete, it fades into the night, leaving nothing but smoldering ashes in its wake.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Fog (smoke), Thin Air, Burning<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Dragonfire, Shadowed Soul, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You deserve this, You can't wake up, You are not alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T04:03:54-07:00","id":1066226,"title":"","content":"<b>Samantha Wade: </b>Samantha is a young teenager that has only recently accepted her nature as one of the Begotten. Having had to suffer because she rejected her nature upon her Homecoming/Devouring at a very young age, he Horror often ran rampant, which lead to her spending a year in an asylum, under close observation of what seemed like a group of scientists that studied her (actually, docs trying to figure out what the hell is wrong with her to help). She escaped, killing all of them, and hid. After some time, she met someone who helped her accept what she is, and that she can use it for good.<br /> Now, she goes after people abusing children (alcoholic fathers, pedophiles, uncaring doctors, drug pushers and gang leaders, and everything in between), often stalking them, then luring (or chasing) them into her lair. Most don't make it out again. Those who do know to stay away from children, and are often traumatized and mutilated. Her lesson seems to be\u201eStay away from children\u201c, as she tells herself, but it really is \u201eWhat looks helpless could still kill you\u201c.<br /> Despite her young age, Samantha is a force to be reckoned with, having been a Beast for the majority of her life.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A pale, tall, gauntly-muscled humanoid with a featureless 'face' that opens like some sort of carnivorous flower, extending five petal-like mouth flaps to reveal a huge lamprey mouth.*<br /> <br /> <b>Life</b>: Loyal \u2013 If Samantha considers you family, you have nothing to worry about.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend: </b> Relentless \u2013 Once the Hunt is on, the prey WILL be hunted down.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> A spore-infested dark Forest, and a factory basement covered in Meat Moss.<br /> Darkness, Toxic, Disruption (Electronics), Echoing<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You are not alone, All your Teeth are Falling out-reskined to You cannot Move, Bugs everywhere-reskined to Slimy Slugs Everywhere. Behold my true form- reskined to My Mind over your Matter, You cannot wake up<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Relentless Hunter, Unbreakable, Shadowed Heart, Limb From Limb, Cyclopean Strength<br /> <b>Merits</b>: Advanced Direction Sense<br /> <br /> *<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Have I been reading the TV tropes section of Stranger Things, specifically the Character Entry on the Demogorgon? Why, yes, I have, how did you know? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Yes, this is a poor attempt at making an 11-inspired Beast. 11 would be better as a Deviant, I know, but her close relationship with the Demogorgon, some of the kids' early suspicions and the Upside Down making an awesome version of a lair just were too temptative not to try to turn into a Beast.<br /> The Atavisms are mainly meant to represent the sturdiness and danger of the Demorgon. Some Atavisms, the Nightmares and the Advanced Direction Sense merit are mostly used to re-create effects from the series: Eleven's ability to track people, her Psychokinesis to harm (Beholdmytrueform) or subdue (All your teeth are falling out) people, the Slug-thing visions, the general paranoia of <i>something</i> being out there, the flickering of the lights.<br /> Oh, and I pieced the Demogorgon's description from lines I stole from TV Tropes. In case I wasn't clear enough on that. Always state your sources, guys! =)<br /> P.S: The Demogorgon's need to go after blood was actually placed on it \u2013 it's an Anathema =P</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:07:35-07:00","id":1066589,"title":"","content":"I'm Musing about Making Sans as a Begotten..... Afterall he does have a Hunger for Prey. And Vengance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","c