egacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T02:32:51-07:00","id":1076866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1076861#post1076861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... now that's not going to get off my mind for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Welcome.<br /> <br /> *Proceeds to Steal Boat*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:50:08-07:00","id":1077001,"title":"","content":"<b>EDITED LAIR DESCRIPTION AND TRAITS</b><br /> <br /> <br /> the<b> Wyrm of the Ring:</b> Under normal circumstances, a single guardian wouldn't be enough to deter the Prince from persecuting the Circle of the Crone within their domain. But when that guardian exhales fire and has the power of flight, it's not a good idea to go poking it with a stick. The one who kindred have come to call the Wyrm of the Ring is a dangerous and tempermental creature who can swoop down from the sky at any moment and set fire to the Prince's holdings. Whether or not they'd ever actually do so is irrelevant, the point is that the Prince believes they would. the Wyrm of the Ring has no respect for the carefully orchestrated politics of vampire society. If it wants something done, it makes its intentions known, often quite loudly. The first time he came to their aid, he kidnapped the Prince's touchstone right out of her bed and threatened her life in front of the Prince's very eyes. The Wyrm of the Ring is not an enemy that the Prince can afford to antagonize, and so they have thus far backed off their mistreatment of the Pagans.<br /> <br /> But what could the Circle have that would move such a creature to defend them? Some binding ritual, some mystic artifact, maybe even a king's randsome? No, none of these things would sway the Beast to put their life on the line for somebody else. The truth is the Wyrm has a childhood friend within the local Circle. Someone who they've known practically their whole life and grew up together with. Now that they're both monsters, they don't have to hide anything from each other; they're free to be open about themselves. And that is worth more than any bribe you can offer!<br /> <br /> The Wyrm of the Ring's Lair is a raging forest fire. Gnarled roots and thick foliage grasp and scratch at anybody who tries to maneuver through without a proper travel guide. Embers dance upon the wind as flames lick the trees; choking the air with smoke and threatening to incinerate those caught in the blaze. And yet, if one wishes to meet the master of this realm, they must move towards the flames. Locating the center point of the destruction, where the Wyrm of the Ring sits within a glade of ash and charcoal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Ugallu<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Destruction<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A great, winged dragon with body scales as black as ink and underscales that reflect the color of nightshade. Their eyes gleam like red rubies in their sockets and wisps of black smoke leak from the corners of its maw.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Loyal - the Wyrm of the Ring takes care of those close to them and is willing to flout the rules if it means keeping them safe from harm. He's definitely the kind of guy you want on your side.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Unexpected - when moved by aggression, the Wyrm of the Ring has all the grace of a bomber pilot. Swooping in from out of nowhere and unleashing chaos and devastation upon their targets<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Undergrowth, Thin Air, Stinging, Burning<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Dragonfire, Wings of the Raptor, Limb from Limb, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold my True Form, Run, Fear is Contagious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-29-2017, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T01:26:50-07:00","id":1077572,"title":"","content":"Another Suggestion for one.... The Blair Witch. A Local Incarnate that's lair is slowly crossing over with the Real world in one area of the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"