forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T08:54:03-07:00","id":1077757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1077649#post1077649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ....stolen!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Help, police! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1077661#post1077661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I hate to pick holes, but wouldn't it make more sense to have Choking rather than Thin Air as Lair Traits? I assume you're using Thin Air to represent the smoke?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That is what I was going for, yes. Basically encouraging people to remain low to the ground, which only serves to reinforce the Undergrowth trait. </span></span></span><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1077633#post1077633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the burning part mean that using enough Dragonfire can let him impose his Lair basically anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a strong possibility. Heh, heh!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-13-2017, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T04:02:41-07:00","id":1078263,"title":"","content":"<b>Countess Amber:</b> <i>&quot;Alright, cocksucker. What was so important you felt the need to interrupt my meal?&quot;</i> the countess may hold sway among the Autumn Court, but her temperament is as curt and direct as a member of Summer. She's seen the so called 'nightmares' of Arcadia and she's got to say that she's not impressed. Somebody needs to teach these people what real fear is and the court of Autumn was practically fawning over her for proper instruction in the art of sowing terror.<br /> <br /> Countess Amber does not see anybody without an appointment; unless somebody is really insistant on speaking with her without one. When that happens, she makes it very clear that they will NOT be doing that again. She lives in a private, luxury estate bought and paid for by her Changeling allies and guarded by Autumn courtiers. In addition to comfortable living arrangements, it also grants her the privacy needed to conduct her work with as little stress as possible. Truly, Countess Amber feels like a member of the pampered nobility!<br /> <br /> Amber's Lair is like a reflection of a fairy forest, tormenting its victims with confusion and distractions. Strangling vines lined with barbed thorns crawl across the environment while a dense mist drifts between the foliage and hides the dangers from sight. There is a sweet, narcotic scent in the air that clouds the senses and makes wanderers hallucinate things that aren't there. Those who become lost within the forest rarely make it back out again, for one reason or another.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Makara<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Power<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> The image of a beautiful, naked woman carved into the trunk of a great tree. Or perhaps that's not quite accurate, it's more like the tree's trunk grew around an actual woman, fusing her to its bark! The wood resists attempts to cut it, as if it has petrified over time; but when successfully damaged, it seeps blood, rather than tree sap. The tree is alive, in more ways than one; it is conscious and capable of free movement. A teeming mass of writhing vines serves as its prehensile limbs with which to manipulate the world around it, and enchantingly sweet aromas disorient the minds of those exposed, drawing their focus towards the imprisoned woman and away from the dangers of the tree. Rotting corpses hang from the tree's branches, the physical remains of those who tried to oppose it in the past now meant to serve as a warning to any future adversaries.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Shy - Countess Amber is a private woman who prefers that others seek her out, rather than the other way around. But they'd better do her the courtesy of announcing their visit in advance!<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Seductive - There are many species of deadly flora who appear beautiful and alluring to those they prey upon. Countess Amber is one such species!<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Undergrowth, Mist, Jagged, Mirages.<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Monster from the Deep, Alien Allure, Unbreakable, Looming Presence<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You are Lost, You Must Obey, You are Alone, Everything you Do is Worthless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  found a typo! 04-14-2017, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T08:35:03-07:00","id":1078378,"title":"","content":"Does she have more powers than that from other sources? The atavisms, lair and nightmares don't really show me why the Autumn Court adores her so much","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T09:48:13-07:00","id":1078405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1078378#post1078378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does she have more powers than that from other sources? The atavisms, lair and nightmares don't really show me why the Autumn Court adores her so much</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She might. I'm not exactly sure how non-Mages get their hands on magic, or how it operates for them. Just went with the books I had available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T10:16:37-07:00","id":1078413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\