 stuff like exorcisms and minor luck trinkets I think.<br /> <br /> Oh, and look up <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/864954-primordial-sorcery-homebrew\">Primordial Sorcery</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:47:11-07:00","id":1078635,"title":"","content":"<b>The Night Drinker:</b> A literal Apex Predator, the thing now known as The Night Drinker achieved their Incarnate state some time ago and has since been leaving a trail of unsolvable murders in her wake. There are no signs of forced entry, no signs of a struggle, no signs the victim knew they were in danger of any kind. All the investigators have is a dehydrated corpse and an estimated time of death somewhere between 12:00 PM and 6:00 AM. Fortunately, the lack of hard evidence has so far prevented authorities from discovering the truth of what's going on. But everyone in the Hive is nervous about how much longer she can keep this up. She's bound to make a mistake sooner or later, and she just might end up exposing the rest of them in the process!<br /> <br /> Her Lair is both one of familiarity and disoritentation. Victims pulled in may find the surrounding environment to resemble the inside of a house, or an office complex, or some other place that one might ordinarily feel safe and secure. It is heavily storming outside, with rain coming down in sheets and booming thunder claps at irregular intervals which always seem perfectly timed for a jump scare. It is the middle of the night and the power is knocked out, leaving victims to rely on their night vision as they fumble around the environment looking for some place to wait out the storm. Unbeknownst to them, however, they are not alone. There is a killer in the building with them and it has no problems navigating around in the dark! And to make matters worse, nobody's bothered to recharge any of the batteries around here, leaving electronic and digital equipment to be unreliable when needed most!<br /> <br /> As the Apex, The Night Drinker's Lair imposes the Poor Light trait onto the Hive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A possible cousin to the Moth Man, The Night Drinker resembles a giant, bipedal mosquito with a spear-like appendage growing out of her face, which she uses to siphon the blood of her prey until her abdomen is swollen with fresh blood. Its sleek, sinewy body moves about with insect agility and its large, purple eyes gleam like reflectors in bright light. Like a normal mosquito, she moves through the environment with barely a sound. Most of the time her prey has no idea she is even present until after she's begun to feed on them!<br /> <br /> <b>Myth:</b> A silent killer who comes in the night.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Poor Light, Sealed Exits, Downpour, Thunderous, Disruption, Maze<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Wings of the Raptor, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, From the Shadows, Needs Must, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You Cannot Run, Behold my True Form, You Can't Wake Up, You Will Never Rest, Fear is Contagious, You are Not Alone<br /> <br /> <b>Beast Shape:</b> Flight, Piercing Sight, One with the Shadows, Superior Atavism (From the Darkness, ) Unnatural Healing, Uncanny Speed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-19-2017, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T18:26:38-07:00","id":1080681,"title":"","content":"<b>B. Jillian Eyes: </b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Nothing, I repeat NOTHING gets by her. She has eyes everywhere!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I've been watching you from the moment you crossed the border into my territory; and I've already counter planned around you.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Jillian Eyes, or 'Bajillion Eyes' as she's known around the supernatural community is a nosy woman who has her hands in virtually every social circle the Hive has to offer. You name a clique, organization, gang or movement and she's got connections there. She has the entire hive and possibly even more than that under her personal supervision. This makes her a dangerous threat, but also an invaluable asset. If you need to get in touch with a more reclusive or hostile faction, she's the one who can get you a meeting. If you're trying to hunt down an elusive adversary, she's the one who can give you a complete itinerary about their operations and the up to date blueprints for their hideouts. Jillian is a world class information broker, easily one of the best in the business!<br /> <br /> As a Tyrant, Jillian uses her vast information network to remain several steps ahead of the competition. She does not care for premature gloating and veiled threats, she saves her monologues for the sweet, savory moment when her enemies discover she had a head start on them days ago and now they're playing catch up!<br /> <br /> Jillian's Lair is a paranoid schizophrenic's worst nightmare. A sprawling city of moist flesh and putrescent fluids with eyes of all different shapes and sizes embedded around the environment. Buildings, vehicles, street signs and everything else that clutters the streets and alleyways is constantly watching you from all directions. Physical contact with these eyes causes them to water and rapidly blink the pain away, but it soon refocuses its attention on you, its lids narrowing to portray is agitation. But being constantly observed is only part of the problem, for trespassers also must deal with assaults on their audio and visual senses. Hallucinated sounds and images plague their travels through the Lair; hopefully depriving them of their ability to tell what is real and what is fake. Getting separated for even a moment is thought to be a death sentence for any hostile groups moving through the area!<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Power<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A beholder, that's the only way to adequately describe this entity that seems to be literally made out of visual sensory organs. It doesn't have a head, instead there is a horrifically large and empty eye socket atop its shoulders. Instead of lashes, the lids sport a row of carnivorous teeth, and the inside of the socket is a cavernous black hole with a trio of flailing tongues emerging from its depths. The rest of its body is an amalgamated, vaguely humanoid shape of compound eyeballs, while its torso writhes with prehensile eye stalks that branch out to gaze upon distant locals and events happening elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Cautious - Jillian doesn't like to move until she knows exactly what the situation is and where it's heading. Attempting to catch her off guard is practically a fool's errand.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Watchful - Jillian is omniscient, she sees all and knows all. Or at least that's what she appears to be to anyone that goes prying into her business.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Stench, Exposed, Mirages, Slick, Echoing<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Shadowed Soul, Eye of Heaven, Mimir's Wisdom, Looming Presence, Needs Must<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold my true form, Everything you do is worthless, They're all around you, We know all your secrets, You must obey<br /> <br /> <b>NOTE:</b> If used as an Apex, Jillian imposes the Exposed trait upon the Hive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-31-2017, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T20:57:27-07:00","id":1083316,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Paindeer:</b> Technically, he calls himself 'the Red Nosed Paindeer,' but that was too long, so everybody just shortened it. Regardless, the Paindeer has established himself as an almost comical terror who wanders the land at night and gores anybody who crosses his path. He generally prefers to hunt solitary prey, those who have been cut off from the rest of the herd. But if he's feeling particularly famished, he'll go after groups and pick them off one by one. For him, it's all about the thrill of catching his victims completely off guard. He moves through the night without leaving a trace, and the only way his prey knows he's nearby is a subconscious tension they feel in the environment. That's when the Paindeer races out of the shadows to impale his victim upon his rack, carrying them screaming off into the night to feast upon their warm entrails.<br /> <br /> Prior to his devouring, the Paindeer was a serial killer by the name of Kyle Toddens. He fancied himself as the next Jack the Ripper and hunted the streets of the city at night, killing his victims and fleeing the scene before anybody could arrive to help. But unlike Jack, Kyle was almost caught thanks to the wonders of modern day forensics investigation. The police had compiled the evidence and were prepared to conduct a raid on his house that night while Kyle was sleeping. But the Dark Mother got to him first. She gave him a vision of the police raid, as his devouring came in the form of a hail of bullets. He awoke just in time to leap out the third story window before the police kicked in his door. If Kyle had attempted to escape on foot, he would surely have been caught that night, but instead he took to the skies, flying over the heads of the unwary officers who to this day believe somebody tipped Kyle off and convinced him to flee before they arrived.<br /> <br /> The Paindeer's Lair is a dark, shadowy forest of twisting pathways and dense foliage. It is a moonless night, so anybody not relying on technology is left fumbling around in the dark and becoming hopelessly lost in the process. The forest appears to be set in the winter months, as the plants are in hibernation and there is a strong chill in the air that becomes gradually less tolerable the longer one is exposed to it. None of this would seem particularly frightening to a casual traveler, but those who bring along a light source or fumble around long enough can see the terrible truth. There in the branches of randomly selected trees, are the decaying bodies of past hunts. They have been impaled through the torso with shafts of wood as bite marks in their flesh allow the blood to drip from their bodies, staining the ground crimson, as well as anybody else who happens to cross under them at the time. The looks upon their faces make it clear that these people died in agony! And once they happen upon one of these corpses and realize what they are, that's when the panic sets in. That's when the Paindeer riles itself for the hunt as it takes to the air once more!<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> The Red Nosed Paindeer is a malicious counterpart to the beloved Rudolph. It takes the form of a great buck with fur that possesses the blackness of charcoal. Its nose has been stained red with the blood of victims both fresh and old and its antlers are sharpened to ten spear-like points. Like the reindeer who pull Santa's sleigh, the Paindeer has the power of wingless flight, allowing it to travel soundlessly across the land and catch its prey in the dark of night before they even see it coming!<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Cautious - Like most deer, the Paindeer is skittish and constantly alert for signs of danger.<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Unexpected - A black deer who stalks the forests in the dead of night can be pretty hard to see coming. Even more so when it leaves no tracks with which to follow!<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Downpour (blood), Darkness, Maze, Extreme Cold<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Shadowed Soul, Wings of the Raptor, Limb from Limb, Relentless Hunter<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Run, You will never rest, You are alone, You are Lost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-31-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:50:44-07:00","id":1083663,"title":"","content":"Has anyone actually turned Hannibal Lecter into a Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T18:53:14-07:00","id":1085269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1083663#post1083663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone actually turned Hannibal Lecter into a Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Coincidentally, I was watching Bryan Fuller's Hannibal series a while back, and I was starting to write a sheet for him as a Genius Slasher. As a Beast, I believe he'd have the following traits. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Makara (For luring you in with a false sense of security and other mind games)<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Tyrant + Predator (For using his immense intellect and charisma to control others and get the next exquisite meal, all while seeming innocent)<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A male version of <a href=\"http://orig05.deviantart.net/d5e4/f/2014/340/9/4/elesh_norn__fanart_of_art__by_kaps_world-d7tjigi.png\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Elesh Norn</b></a>. However, it wears a fine crimson suit instead of flowing robes. Also, its mouth is covered by a pair of skeletal hands that resemble the metal mouth restraint he wears along with a straightjacket in the Silence Of The Lambs version. When it feels like being polite and charming, the hands stay in place, occasionally letting their fingers click and wriggle like the mandibles of a spider. When the hands part, the Horror's angelic voice disappears and its countless, pristine, ornate fangs shine in a demonic smile.<br /> <br /> <b>Life: </b>Cautious<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Seductive + <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/833639-custom-legends-and-lives\"><b>Deceitful</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> A baroque, decadent mansion-church made in his own image, filled with sensual architecture and ammenities of a subtly sinister design. You are welcome to try out anything you want, as long as you have time for a chat with the host...he'd really like to know you better.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous</b></a>, Blazing Light, Sealed Exits, Mirages.<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Alien Allure, Eye Of Heaven, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=589702#post589702\"><b>Draining Kiss</b></a>, From The Shadows, Limb From Limb, Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold My True Form, Organs Everywhere, We Know All Your Secrets, You Are Better Than Them, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=540663#post540663\"><b>No Masks For You</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T03:50:28-07:00","id":1085415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1085269#post1085269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coincidentally, I was watching Bryan Fuller's Hannibal series a while back, and I was starting to write a sheet for him as a Genius Slasher. As a Beast, I believe he'd have the following traits. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Makara (For luring you in with a false sense of security and other mind games)<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Tyrant + Predator (For using his immense intellect and charisma to control others and get the next exquisite meal, all while seeming innocent)<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A male version of <a href=\"http://orig05.deviantart.net/d5e4/f/2014/340/9/4/elesh_norn__fanart_of_art__by_kaps_world-d7tjigi.png\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Elesh Norn</b></a>. However, it wears a fine crimson suit instead of flowing robes. Also, its mouth is covered by a pair of skeletal hands that resemble the metal mouth restraint he wears along with a straightjacket in the Silence Of The Lambs version. When it feels like being polite and charming, the hands stay in place, occasionally letting their fingers click and wriggle like the mandibles of a spider. When the hands part, the Horror's angelic voice disappears and its countless, pristine, ornate fangs shine in a demonic smile.<br /> <br /> <b>Life: </b>Cautious<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Seductive + <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/833639-custom-legends-and-lives\"><b>Deceitful</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> A baroque, decadent mansion-church made in his own image, filled with sensual architecture and ammenities of a subtly sinister design. You are welcome to try out anything you want, as long as you have time for a chat with the host...he'd really like to know you better.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous</b></a>, Blazing Light, Sealed Exits, Mirages.<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Alien Allure, Eye Of Heaven, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=589702#post589702\"><b>Draining Kiss</b></a>, From The Shadows, Limb From Limb, Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Behold My True Form, Organs Everywhere, We Know All Your Secrets, You Are Better Than Them, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540642-homebrew-nightmares?p=540663#post540663\"><b>No Masks For You</b></a></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this a lot, except that to me, Hannibal has always been more of an Anakim than a Makara, because of the 'you can't stop me/ I am better than them' theme, and the way he mostly killed people he considered rude/beneath him. His whole cat-and-mouse game of season two was him proving that he is the best (trying not to spoil anything here), and even when comparing himself with other killers, he considered himself superior. Kind of has an Anakim vibe to me.<br /> <br /> Makara fits well with his curiosity and the knowledge etc, though. Hm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Atavisms are chosen very fittingly. I'd add You must Obey to the Nightmares though. Representing his... unorthodox treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T07:23:55-07:00","id":1085445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1085415#post1085415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this a lot, except that to me, Hannibal has always been more of an Anakim than a Makara, because of the 'you can't stop me/ I am better than them' theme, and the way he mostly killed people he considered rude/beneath him. His whole cat-and-mouse game of season two was him proving that he is the best (trying not to spoil anything here), and even when comparing himself with other killers, he considered himself superior. Kind of has an Anakim vibe to me.<br /> <br /> Makara fits well with his curiosity and the knowledge etc, though. Hm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Atavisms are chosen very fittingly. I'd add You must Obey to the Nightmares though. Representing his... unorthodox treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>He certainly works as an Anakim, especially considering that a lot of mythological giants also ate human flesh. It could go either way.<br /> <br /> I deliberately left out You Must Obey because what he does is <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MoreThanMindControl\" target=\"_blank\"><b>more than mind control.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T22:15:41-07:00","id":1085700,"title":"","content":"Anyone else remember Avatar: The Last Airbender? Do you remember the episodes with the Great Library? Here's my concept: An Ugallu Collector, his Liar a vast Library, his Horror resembling an enormous Tito Owl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T23:09:18-07:00","id":1085713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1085700#post1085700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else remember Avatar: The Last Airbender? Do you remember the episodes with the Great Library? Here's my concept: An Ugallu Collector, his Liar a vast Library, his Horror resembling an enormous Tito Owl.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea. Wan Shi Tong was a marvellous character in my opinion. Koh would make a good Beast as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T00:57:19-07:00","id":1086515,"title":"","content":"Early Toph would make a good Anakim, with her need to prove herself the best fighter and so on. And Badgermoles do work well as Horrors.<br /> <br /> <br /> You know who else works awesomely well as a (conflicted) Beast? Jackie Estecado, host of The Darkness! I'd say Eshmaki Prey, with Atavisms like Monster from the deep, Relentless Hunter, Unbreakable, Shadowed Soul and From the Shadows. For Nightmares, at the very least Behold My true Form, you are not alone and Fear is contagious. <br /> Throw in a Minion maker ability for good measure, and voila. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T03:21:36-07:00","id":1086535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1086515#post1086515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early Toph would make a good Anakim, with her need to prove herself the best fighter and so on. And Badgermoles do work well as Horrors.<br /> <br /> <br /> You know who else works awesomely well as a (conflicted) Beast? Jackie Estecado, host of The Darkness! I'd say Eshmaki Prey, with Atavisms like Monster from the deep, Relentless Hunter, Unbreakable, Shadowed Soul and From the Shadows. For Nightmares, at the very least Behold My true Form, you are not alone and Fear is contagious. <br /> Throw in a Minion maker ability for good measure, and voila. <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe let Jackie have high dots in the mage 'Familiar' Merit---but instead of one uber-powerful spirit, Jackie has <i>tons</i> of Rank 1 spirit-goons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T05:00:26-07:00","id":1086554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1086535#post1086535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe let Jackie have high dots in the mage 'Familiar' Merit---but instead of one uber-powerful spirit, Jackie has <i>tons</i> of Rank 1 spirit-goons?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have to make some changes to the Familiar Merit. At two dots it grants a Rank 1 familiar. At four dots it grants a Rank 2 familiar. So you can't have one uber-powerful familiar since it's capped at Rank 2, and even if you do split up a maxed familiar you only end up with two Rank 1 familiars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T05:35:44-07:00","id":1086563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1086554#post1086554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd have to make some changes to the Familiar Merit. At two dots it grants a Rank 1 familiar. At four dots it grants a Rank 2 familiar. So you can't have one uber-powerful familiar since it's capped at Rank 2, and even if you do split up a maxed familiar you only end up with two Rank 1 familiars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, s**t. Well, ''twas an idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T06:42:15-07:00","id":1086590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1086563#post1086563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, s**t. Well, ''twas an idea!</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a Merit on the Beast Merit thread based around having Ephemeral minions living in your Lair. I forget the name of it, but it's a comparatively recent one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T06:46:51-07:00","id":1086595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream\"> Nightmares &amp; Dreamscapes: Incursions from the Primordial Dream - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The title is pretty much self-explainatory: this is a thread I made to post all sorts of critters and oddities born from the Primordial Dream. Think Intruders: </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> not from that thread, but was it the Night Terrors from this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T06:51:04-07:00","id":1086599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1086595#post1086595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...imordial-dream</a><br /> <br /> not from that thread, but was it the Night Terrors from this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Here it is. It's a little crude and could do with some 'tuning up', though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Court of Nightmares (o-ooooo)<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Spirit Kinship.<br /> <br /> Mostly the layers are empty save for the horror itself and any pests generated by the layer. However, some Beasts tend to enjoy company and fill their homes with various beings. Sometimes, the various beings may wonder into the layer on accident and be stuck/settle there.<br /> Effect: Layer is populated by a number of beings equal to the Combined Rank=2 xMerit dots (e.g. A 3-dot version of this merit can support 2 3rd rank or 6 1st rank beings). The beings generally live in the Lair and only leave it when accompanied by the Horror. </div> </div> </div>I think we'll have to excuse the grammar and spelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:04:22-07:00","id":1086605,"title":"","content":"I also think that a stipulation on maximum Rank might be necessary, perhaps with an advanced version allowing a Beast to have a higher-Rank being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:09:32-07:00","id":1086609,"title":"","content":"Maybe a Beast has a Chamber of their Lair in the Shadow Realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:15:56-07:00","id":1086612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1086609#post1086609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a Beast has a Chamber of their Lair in the Shadow Realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:18:22-07:00","id":1086615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1086612#post1086612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's certainly possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That <i>could</i> explain Jackie Escatado's horde of minions; they're just Rank 1 darkness-spirits he's coerced into aiding him!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T11:51:09-07:00","id":1086727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1086515#post1086515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early Toph would make a good Anakim, with her need to prove herself the best fighter and so on. And Badgermoles do work well as Horrors.<br /> <br /> <br /> You know who else works awesomely well as a (conflicted) Beast? Jackie Estecado, host of The Darkness! I'd say Eshmaki Prey, with Atavisms like Monster from the deep, Relentless Hunter, Unbreakable, Shadowed Soul and From the Shadows. For Nightmares, at the very least Behold My true Form, you are not alone and Fear is contagious.<br /> Throw in a Minion maker ability for good measure, and voila.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1019276#post1019276\"><b>a sheet for Jackie Estacado as a Beast.</b></a> What do you think? I believe all that is missing is a Condition that makes his Darkness more independent than most Horrors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:56:33-07:00","id":1086988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1086515#post1086515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early Toph would make a good Anakim, with her need to prove herself the best fighter and so on. And Badgermoles do work well as Horrors.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At 12 years old, took on most of the earth kingdom's imperial guard and in the comics she fought King Bumi as an equal, nearly tearing apart an entire mountain range in their friendly sparring match. I'd say Giant suits her perfectly!<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what about Shendu? Clearly an Eshmaki Collector<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/jackiechanadventures/images/7/78/Shendu_7.png/revision/latest?cb=20120412040734\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-03-2017, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:58:47-07:00","id":1088230,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> Right, that seems pretty much spot on! I do prefer Hunger for Prey over Power here, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hey, what about the Defenders?<br /> Luke Cage, Daredevil etc. reimagined as a Brood doesn't seem that farfetched to me (although Deviant or a microtemplate is probably better if you wanna be more accurate, but they'd just be an inspiration here).<br /> Haven't seen Jessica Jones yet, but I think they'd fit the bill:<br /> <br /> Luke Cage is an Anakim Ravager who has a bone to pick with people that treat others poorly and drag them into their dirty world. He's coming at them with Unbreakable, Iron Skin and its upgrades to represent his taking hits, and Cyclopean Strength to show his increased power, as well as Looming Presence since he's tall and can threaten a lot of people without them even knowing about his skillset. Lait traits probably include things like Decayed, Cramped and maybe Extreme Heat.<br /> <br /> Daredevil would be an Eshmaki Ravager out to destroy criminal activity, with Shadowed Soul to represent his Super-Senses/Blind-Sight, Relentless Hunter to represent his repeated taking of a beating and getting up again and again and again, and Eye of Heaven and Needs Must to account for his people skills and ability to find trouble. Maybe add in From the Shadows. Lair Traits would likely be Darkness or Poor Light and something like Echoing or Mirages (Noises making people think he is somewhere he isn't.) His Horror would probably be a literal Version of his Daredevil suit. He definetly knows some parkour.<br /> <br /> Iron Fist comes pre-packed with a Horror: Shou-Lao, the undying Dragon. Imo, he's a Makara Nemesis out to defend Rand from anything that would mar his father's legacy, with Limb from Limb, Titanic Blow, and Alien Allure. His Lair Traits include Blizzard and Extreme Cold, as his Lair is the Pass outside K'un-Lun. Lots of different fighting styles.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T18:44:45-07:00","id":1088585,"title":"","content":"What do you guys the the Family would be for a Beast inspired by the Maenads? Themes would include the fear of madness, or the potentially horrible results of excess.<br /> <br /> The strength of the Maenad's would seem to suggest Anakim, but loss of control so total that you would rip apart your family members while mad seems repulsive enough to go with Namtaru too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T18:59:15-07:00","id":1088588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1088585#post1088585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys the the Family would be for a Beast inspired by the Maenads? Themes would include the fear of madness, or the potentially horrible results of excess.<br /> <br /> The strength of the Maenad's would seem to suggest Anakim, but loss of control so total that you would rip apart your family members while mad seems repulsive enough to go with Namtaru too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that either could work. Depending on which metaphors you wish to use, Makara could work as well. Think about how many songs describe madness, an inability to control yourself, and being unable to regulate your emotions as a sea in which you are drowning, or a cloistering, suffocating feeling. That's practically all of Linkin Park's early discography right there. Eshmaki could represent it as the darkness and chaos within you seeping out. Hell, you could even justify the fear of exposing what you truly feel and letting yourself act the way that you wish. Or fear of exposure to the societal/political repercussions you would face if you acted to excess. <br /> <br /> Tl;dr/not helpful enough: What type of Maenad do you want to play? That will inform your family. You can justify any of them for the fear you have chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T02:57:42-07:00","id":1089050,"title":"","content":"Could the titular character from the TV series <i>Lucifer</i> be a Beast?<br /> Nemesis, obviously, but I don't know about a Family. Makara, possibly, for the 'depths of Hell'. Ugallu might work, as might Anakim (punishing unseen sins and the insurmountable might of divinity).<br /> <br /> For Nightmares, he's obviously got Behold, My True Form! and possibly some kind of unique one which makes people tell him what they desire (I Know What You Want?), although that might be a peculiar manifestation of Eyes of Heaven.<br /> <br /> For Atavisms, Unbreakable, Cyclopean Strength, Relentless Hunter and Alien Allure, definitely.<br /> <br /> His Lair is Hell itself, with Mirages of your past sins to punish and deride you. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 05-07-2017, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T18:25:03-07:00","id":1090078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1088585#post1088585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys the the Family would be for a Beast inspired by the Maenads? Themes would include the fear of madness, or the potentially horrible results of excess.<br /> <br /> The strength of the Maenad's would seem to suggest Anakim, but loss of control so total that you would rip apart your family members while mad seems repulsive enough to go with Namtaru too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say they would fall under the Namtaru category; not all Gorgons are hideous to look upon, but they do have a tendency to make others feel uncomfortable. Maenads are described as being psychotic cannibals who exist in a perpetual state of mind shattering ecstasy. And they <i>want to be that way, </i>considering it a gift from their patron, Dionysus. That definitely sounds like something that would give many people cause to avoid them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Also, I had this idea:</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette4.wikia.nocookie.net/americanmcgeesalice/images/d/d6/Walrus_sitting_on_the_main_Oyster_Starlet.png/revision/20160530043246\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-08-2017, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:29:11-07:00","id":1090146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1089050#post1089050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the titular character from the TV series <i>Lucifer</i> be a Beast?<br /> Nemesis, obviously, but I don't know about a Family. Makara, possibly, for the 'depths of Hell'. Ugallu might work, as might Anakim (punishing unseen sins and the insurmountable might of divinity).<br /> <br /> For Nightmares, he's obviously got Behold, My True Form! and possibly some kind of unique one which makes people tell him what they desire (I Know What You Want?), although that might be a peculiar manifestation of Eyes of Heaven.<br /> <br /> For Atavisms, Unbreakable, Cyclopean Strength, Relentless Hunter and Alien Allure, definitely.<br /> <br /> His Lair is Hell itself, with Mirages of your past sins to punish and deride you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Ugallu or Anakim fit him best.<br /> You must Obey! is in his repertoire, he just usually uses it to make people tell him their deepest desire.<br /> Otherwise, I agree^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T10:11:38-07:00","id":1090345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1088230#post1088230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> Right, that seems pretty much spot on! I do prefer Hunger for Prey over Power here, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hey, what about the Defenders?<br /> Luke Cage, Daredevil etc. reimagined as a Brood doesn't seem that farfetched to me (although Deviant or a microtemplate is probably better if you wanna be more accurate, but they'd just be an inspiration here).<br /> Haven't seen Jessica Jones yet, but I think they'd fit the bill:<br /> <br /> Luke Cage is an Anakim Ravager who has a bone to pick with people that treat others poorly and drag them into their dirty world. He's coming at them with Unbreakable, Iron Skin and its upgrades to represent his taking hits, and Cyclopean Strength to show his increased power, as well as Looming Presence since he's tall and can threaten a lot of people without them even knowing about his skillset. Lait traits probably include things like Decayed, Cramped and maybe Extreme Heat.<br /> <br /> Daredevil would be an Eshmaki Ravager out to destroy criminal activity, with Shadowed Soul to represent his Super-Senses/Blind-Sight, Relentless Hunter to represent his repeated taking of a beating and getting up again and again and again, and Eye of Heaven and Needs Must to account for his people skills and ability to find trouble. Maybe add in From the Shadows. Lair Traits would likely be Darkness or Poor Light and something like Echoing or Mirages (Noises making people think he is somewhere he isn't.) His Horror would probably be a literal Version of his Daredevil suit. He definetly knows some parkour.<br /> <br /> Iron Fist comes pre-packed with a Horror: Shou-Lao, the undying Dragon. Imo, he's a Makara Nemesis out to defend Rand from anything that would mar his father's legacy, with Limb from Limb, Titanic Blow, and Alien Allure. His Lair Traits include Blizzard and Extreme Cold, as his Lair is the Pass outside K'un-Lun. Lots of different fighting styles.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to that, Fisk as an Anakim Tyrant (A terrifying, indestructible kingpin), Cottonmouth as a Makara Nemesis (a vengeful ruler of a criminal underworld), Diamondback as either an Anakim Ravager, or possibly Nemesis (He wants to fuck Luke up, but he seems to really like destroying things), or possible a Hero after Luke. Kilgrave is an Anakim Predator, or possibly Tyrant or Ravager if you want to focus on the powerlessness or loss of control, and Punisher is an Anakim Nemesis.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd actually peg the &quot;enhanced individuals&quot; as mostly Deviants, but you could look at them through a Beast lens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T20:01:17-07:00","id":1090567,"title":"","content":"How well would you say the Slender Man works as an Incarnate Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T05:04:58-07:00","id":1090679,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, <b>Daredevil</b> could be an Ugallu. I mean, how often do you expect a blind lawyer, much less a blind lawyer who beats the crap out of dangerous criminals on a nightly basis? Plus, he jumps around on roof tops and I think he's even got a grappling hook for quick access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-28-2018, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:40:08-07:00","id":1091060,"title":"","content":"They call him '<b>Ronin,' </b>supposedly because he's a disgraced warrior. Something about being exiled from his original hive and now he can't find anywhere to truly call home. Instead, he travels the world, looking for something to occupy his time. He's lost count of how many humans he's defeated, many of them being professionally trained hunters. He's even taken out some unruly siblings who were making life miserable for the rest of the family. The hoard he collects are trophies from battle, the very weapons that his enemies sought to use against him. His most coveted trophies are those of former Heroes, adding their so called 'chosen blades' to his arsenal and using them against future Heroes. But these trophies are very rare and difficult to acquire, so he keeps them under lock and key until he needs them.<br /> <br /> His lair takes the form of a Japanese village set in an nondescript medieval period. It is a moon lit night and it is raining quite heavily. Not many people would be walking the streets at this time, save for Ronin. The storm doesn't bother him, in fact, it helps him. Anybody brave or foolish enough to go walking around in the rain in the middle of the night is probably asking for trouble, and Ronin is happy to provide! Like something out of an action movie, he appears with a flash of lightning. For a moment, his shadow appears impossibly large before it fades to reveal his actual image.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Collector<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A warrior dressed in feudal Japanese gi, along with a necklace of thick prayer beads, a straw hat, and wooden sandals. His skin is the same shade of blue as moonlight and his teeth bare a set of sideways curving fangs that force him to keep a perpetually sneering expression. he has a full set of hair both on the scalp and facial area. It grows in spiked tufts and is black as the night's sky. Even beneath his gi, it is obvious that he is packed with muscle, being in peak physical condition.He is also usually carrying a weapon, which he wields with one hand, no matter how heavy it may appear to be!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Downpour, Poor Light, Thunderous<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Titanic Blow, Cyclopean Strength, Storm-Lashed, From the Shadows<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Fear is Contagious, You are not Alone, Run Away","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-04-2017, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T10:17:26-07:00","id":1093318,"title":"","content":"How about Jack Skellington from a Nightmare Before Christmas as a Namtaru Predator who has Kinship with Changelings, Sin-Eaters and likely more? He is probably the Apex of whatever game he is in. Halloween Town is his Lair, with Chambers being shared with other Beasts of his Brood. He would impose the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous (Halloween Decorations And Monsters)</b></a> Lair Trait on the Hive. His plan to kidnap Santa Claus was due to his identity crisis over being a monster that has to spread fear over and over, but he eventually embraced who he was and defeated a much worse Beast (Oogie Boogie), possibly earning his Incarnate Inheritance in the process. Santa might have been a high level Changeling who was kidnapped through the use of cold iron and his Frailties. I'm thinking of making Jack's mortal identity be a party organizer and wise aristocrat, as a reference to how much he loves holidays and books, as well as that classy look he has. I'll rewatch the movie and write a character sheet for him. Anybody interested?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-17-2017, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T19:11:09-07:00","id":1093492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1090679#post1090679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, <b>Daredevil</b> could be an Ugallu. I meant, how often do you expect a blind lawyer, much less a blind lawyer who beats the crap out of dangerous criminals on a nightly basis? Plus, he jumps around on roof tops and I think he's even got a grappling hook for quick access.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Deviant seems like a better fit to me, you are correct about the grappling hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T13:39:46-07:00","id":1097610,"title":"","content":"Has this been posted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://iguanamouth.tumblr.com/post/126286516207/bertb0t-antique-symbolism-bertb0t\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/a3fd118604d1603004ef122580498805/tumblr_inline_nsu5j4kakx1qmoaae_640.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://iguanamouth.tumblr.com/post/126286516207/bertb0t-antique-symbolism-bertb0t\" target=\"_blank\"> go wash your hands </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://iguanamouth.tumblr.com/post/126286516207/bertb0t-antique-symbolism-bertb0t\" target=\"_blank\"> http://iguanamouth.tumblr.com/post/126286516207/bertb0t-antique-symbolism-bertb0t </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> scribbles </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>antique-symbolism:</b> Imagine a dragon at Antiques Roadshow, appraising its hoard<br /> <br /> <b>bertb0t:</b> Imagine the dragon hoards monetarily worthless things like newspapers or old bones and the person appraising it getting more and more nervous about telling the dragon their stuff isnt worth anything<br /> <br /> <b>antique-symbolism:</b> Imagine that the dragon knows this and just likes watching the person squirm.<br /> <br /> <b>bertb0t:</b> The dragon actually hoards uncomfortable situations </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/ec8323d4711dd46d9a5b6e8425d0bd4d/tumblr_inline_nsu5jtwijI1qmoaae_500.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/2d0d718afc7be12dbc78fb9bd45ea88b/tumblr_inline_nsu5kmxjIE1qmoaae_500.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/4f9e0a3bbd7c71707167d98e6068273b/tumblr_inline_nsu5l0bYTU1qmoaae_500.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/d09b39efa03d996e6058728512eaadf3/tumblr_inline_nsu5ldqFZA1qmoaae_500.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T22:40:07-07:00","id":1100018,"title":"","content":"You know how <a href=\"https://youtu.be/EQB6ctBXNzs\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Saitama from One Punch Man suffers from boredom because he can't experience conflict?</b></a><br /> <br /> I was thinking of creating an Incarnate Beast who is in a similar situation to Saitama, but in order to prevent their Myth from being Destabilized, they teach people not to seek victory and power for their own sake. Instead, they act as this martial arts master and spiritual guru of sorts who no one can beat but is said to be very wise, so people seek them out for all sorts of advice. They get to Feed their Horror by demonstrating their immense fighting skill and cunning, and teach the Lesson of &quot;embrace your conflicts for they will make you stronger&quot;. And if anyone threatens their students over this Lesson, they show up to protect the students. Think Mister Miyagi and Master Shifu. They would be an Anakim Tyrant.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-04-2017, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T01:57:28-07:00","id":1100052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1091060#post1091060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They call him '<b>Ronin,' </b>supposedly because he's a disgraced warrior. Something about being exiled from his original hive and now he can't find anywhere to truly call home. Instead, he travels the world, looking for something to occupy his time. He's lost count of how many humans he's defeated, many of them being professionally trained hunters. He's even taken out some unruly siblings who were making life miserable for the rest of the family. The hoard he collects are trophies from battle, the very weapons that his enemies sought to use against him. His most coveted trophies are those of former Heroes, adding their so called 'chosen blades' to his arsenal and using them against future Heroes. But these trophies are very rare and difficult to acquire, so he keeps them under lock and key until he needs them.<br /> <br /> His lair takes the form of a Japanese village set in an nondescript medieval period. It is a moon lit night and it is raining quite heavily. Not many people would be walking the streets at this time, save for Iado. The storm doesn't bother him, in fact, it helps him. Anybody brave or foolish enough to go walking around in the rain in the middle of the night is probably asking for trouble, and Iado is happy to provide! Like something out of an action movie, he appears with a flash of lightning. For a moment, his shadow appears impossibly large before it fades to reveal his actual image.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Collector<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A warrior dressed in feudal Japanese gi, along with a necklace of thick prayer beads, a straw hat, and wooden sandals. His skin is the same shade of blue as moonlight and his teeth bare a set of sideways curving fangs that force him to keep a perpetually sneering expression. he has a full set of hair both on the scalp and facial area. It grows in spiked tufts and his black as the night's sky. Even beneath his gi, it is obvious that he is packed with muscle, being in peak physical condition.He is also usually carrying a weapon, which he wields with one hand, no matter how heavy it may appear to be!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> Downpour, Poor Light, Thunderous<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Titanic Blow, Cyclopean Strength, Storm-Lashed, From the Shadows<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Fear is Contagious, You are not Alone, Run Away</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd swap out Titanic Blow and Cyclopean Strength for Looming Presence and Limb From Limb. &quot;Super strength&quot; doesn't really seem something like a ghostly swordsman would have, but &quot;overwhelming aura&quot; and &quot;tear people apart&quot; does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T02:22:24-07:00","id":1100055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1100052#post1100052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd swap out Titanic Blow and Cyclopean Strength for Looming Presence and Limb From Limb. &quot;Super strength&quot; doesn't really seem something like a ghostly swordsman would have, but &quot;overwhelming aura&quot; and &quot;tear people apart&quot; does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was going for an Oni (one of my favorite eastern monsters) style for him, who's mythology basically translates to being <i>'stronger than strong' </i>or <i>'excessively strong.' </i><br /> <br /> That's how they can swing those gigantic weapons around with one arm. The crooked fangs, spiked hair and skin coming in shades of red / blue are common themes among them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-04-2017, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T02:47:55-07:00","id":1100056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1100055#post1100055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Was going for an Oni (one of my favorite eastern monsters) style for him, who's mythology basically translates to being <i>'stronger than strong' </i>or <i>'excessively strong.' </i><br /> <br /> That's how they can swing those gigantic weapons around with one arm. The crooked fangs, spiked hair and skin coming in shades of red / blue are common themes among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doh! The fangs should've been a hint. Silly me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:56:22-07:00","id":1111787,"title":"","content":"Spun off my own personal opinions of how Beast!!Daredevil would work, though this isn't meant to be a direct re-creation. I just really like the religious imagery in certain DD stories, and, well....<br /> <br /> Family: Ugallu<br /> <br /> Hunger: Nemesis<br /> <br /> Horror: A winged and horned gargoyle, which from a distance appears to be made of weather-stained pinkish marble. Up close, however, its skin looks more like a half-healed acid burn, with black fluid oozing perpetually from its empty eye sockets.<br /> <br /> Lair: Maze-like, Echoing, Poor Light. A city-sized Gothic cathedral designed by M. C. Escher. Interlocking pointed arches soar up into shadows, and the only light sources are flickering clusters of votary candles or blazing stained glass windows that dazzle and confuse the eye.<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Needs Must, Wings of the Raptor, From the Shadows<br /> <br /> Nightmares: You Deserve This, Eating You from the Inside Out (from the Homebrew folder)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:44:07-07:00","id":1117215,"title":"","content":"The Leader is a curious Beast. An Ugallu Collector, he is a vicious businessman, hard but fair, and feeds himself by collecting companies.<br /> His Horror is a Dragon just the size of a truck, and even though he himself is mainly a social player, he can defend himself if necessary. By now he has become one of the more poweful Begotten around just by himself. Taking all his Social Contacts into account, he might well be able to challenge the Apex for the position.<br /> So far, he has not shown an interest in that position, though. He seems happy with becoming one of the most powerful corporate executives in the history of manking.<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Wings of the Raptor, Siren's Treacherous Song (FUS RO DA!), Dragonfire, Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must, Allien Allure, Eye of Heaven [in sequence of Acquisition]<br /> <br /> Nightmares: You are alone, You cannot wake up, You are not alone, All your teeth are falling out, You Deserve this, Run away [in sequence of Acquisition]<br /> <br /> Lair: The top of a mountain, basked in sunlight. It's a dangerous climb, but the view is breath-taking. The Chambers are various levels of the Mountain, with the Burrows being passages on the way.<br /> Thin Air, Exposed, Extreme Cold, Jagged, Hurricane. [in sequence of Acquisition]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T02:42:53-07:00","id":1117651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1117215#post1117215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Paarthurnax, is that you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:53:05-07:00","id":1117775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1117651#post1117651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paarthurnax, is that you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you mean Lofwyr? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:32:37-07:00","id":1117869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1117775#post1117775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you mean Lofwyr? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI can only imagine what the CofD version of Dun's will is like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T14:59:35-07:00","id":1117943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1117651#post1117651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paarthurnax, is that you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pssst! That's a secret!<br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously though, glad you identified the inspirational source =) Kudos!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar974_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"974\" data-vbnamecard=\"974\">MrParaduo</a> Huh, that one fits really well. However, I am unfamiliar with Shadowrun, had to look him up. I'd actually imagined my humanoid Paarthurnax Beast quite like that. Would you look at that. Weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T08:22:31-07:00","id":1123026,"title":"","content":"Alright, have a new one that will soon see use.<br /> <br /> Samuel Byers is a young, successful therapist who loves helping people, and who uses most of his earnings to support his food-stamp family, since he is the first in generations to make it out the trailer park. However, he has a problem: he is no human. Not really. What has taken the place of his soul is dark, and evil, and hungry. Sustaining it forces him to do horrible things he would never have thought of, such as abusing his position of trust with his patients, preying on them when they are at their weakest and thus need him the most. He was betraying his oaths. He tries to justify it to himself by pointing out that his newly gained abilities let him help people more effectively - he is sacrificing some for the good of all. And he tried picking either people who he had little hope on saving anyway, or strong people who he hoped could grow stronger from the experience.<br /> But when he was honest with himself, he felt less and less bad about it. He enjoyed the rush of power. He enjoyed pulling the rug from under people's feet, leaving them disoriented, wondering how they could have ended up this way. Wondering who manipulated them.<br /> Just what did that make him?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Makara<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Tyrant<br /> <b>Horror:</b> A slim Deep One, covered in lustrous, chromatic, shiny scales. A captivating sight, to be sure, and able to produce wonderful, if clearly inhuman music.<br /> <b>Lair: </b>A swampy plain, filled with stinging, painful rain. Lair Traits: Downpour, Corrosive<br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Alien Allure, Siren's Treacherous Song<br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You cannot wake up, They are all around you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T14:54:07-07:00","id":1124486,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the doublepost, but I feel the time difference justifies a new one rather than an edit. <div align=\"center\"><b><u>At long last...</u></b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> I had promised these ages ago, but somehow never managed to make a concept stick. Finally, some things clicked into place for me, and I am content with how they turned out.<br /> Enjoy. <div align=\"center\"><i>Erich Zann</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/25/33/5f/25335f6847f64518a39c208472a0b978.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> <br /> <br /> Erich Zann is a gatekeeper: he keeps people safe by making them stay away from bounderies to other places, like the Hedge or the Twilight. When he was younger, he was more vicious in his punishment of trespassers into the supernatural dimensions, but with time, he has come to see himself as someone with a mission to educate humans on the dangers they are facing: he was by far one of the least malovelant inhabitants of the supernatural, so they should be glad they get away with a slap on the fingers rather than the ultimate punishment of delving too deeply into things not meant for man. Should they be able to keep up with him, he conceded they might have a chance, but that didn't happen often, and hadn't happened in decades. Whenever his cousins find a weak spot in the Gauntlet, a open Avernian gate or a place where it is particularly easy to traverse into the Hedge, they call in the specialist. Erich, they knew, would guard the place and make sure no human gets more than a peak. That much was acceptable for him to feed The Polyp. The lesson he teaches is &quot;Do not put your nose where it doesn't belong&quot;.<br /> The old man has acquired a lot of experience doing this by now. This way, he kept the humans save from lasting harm, and got them out of his cousins' hair.<br /> In his spare time, the retired musician teaches playing the violin as well as the piano, and composing. Since he was quite successful in his earlier career, touring around the world, some of his chambers are located in other countries<br /> <b>Family:</b> Makara<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Nemesis (Although Predator works just as well)<br /> <b>Horror: </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/09/bb/de/09bbdecc2d8a1983993ff4cbed5319d6.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> The Polyp is a tentacled mass without a face or discernible mainbody, and is actually made up of trillions of tiny slimy organisms that bind together, specialize as bodyparts, and move as one.<br /> <b>Lair: </b>As can be seen in the image above, the heart is an endless void filled with tiny stars with a Burrow connecting it to a hotel room, the next burrow is the Staircase leading to the exit, where the next chamber is the street before a bakery. The other chambers are a concert hall and a museum's Egypt department.<br /> Darkness, Poor Light, Suffocating, Crushing, Extreme Cold, Sealed Exits.<br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Siren's Treacherous Song, Eye of Heaven, Shadowed Soul, Storm-Lashed, Infestation<br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Tabula Rasa, You are Lost, You Cannot wake up, They are all around you, Tentacles everywhere!, Run away! <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <i>The Terrible Old Man</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/33/41/93/334193a397a047fb7316a703d0982915.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> <br /> <br /> The Terrible Old Man is a local legend, old enough that no one remembers ever having seen him young, and abhorred by the locals for his poor hygiene, lack of body care, strange mannerisms and just general unpleasentness. Him being filthy rich did not help matters, and many suspect he was a pirate when he was younger, since he occasionally went to the jewler to exchange foreign and sometimes artistic coins of pure gold for money. A jewler ripped him off once, and soon the city had a vacancy.<br /> In his house, the Terrible Old Man has a shed, filled with jars of varying sized and a pendulum inside: quite pretty to look at. However, they have one thing in common: one dark, brownish dot on the bottom, that might have been liquid and red once. He talks to them, giving them names of people who disappeared or died.<br /> Sometimes, someone (usually an outsider) thought a feeble, old and rich man would make a perfect victim, and soon, the sea would wash a mangled body ashore.<br /> The Terrible Old Man has had enough time to build relations with many supernatural denizens, and some Spirits are particularly fond of him. In addition, he has good connections to some nasty mages that are as abhorred by their society as he is by the mortal populace - and possibly as long lived. They sometimes do him a favour and make his collection more interesting - after all, storing blood satisfies him, but storing a Soul in a Jar is so much better. Even he needed someone to talk to, once in a while, after all.<br /> People underestimate his size, since he bends over a lot and thus looks kind of small, but him pulling himself up to his full size is usually the moment his adversaries realize they made a huge mistake. This Apex is on the verge of becoming an Incarnate.<br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Collector (Predator alternatively)<br /> <b>Horror: </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/564x/85/eb/bf/85ebbf7a097bee8f4c76ee5f73c59fbc.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> The gigantic, multilimbed Star-Spawn can lay waste to whole landscapes at a time.<br /> <b>Lair: </b>A shipgraveyard is the heart of the Lair, with many ship wrecks still carrying their treasure and secrets. The shore of an acidic sea is his first acquired chamber, and his garden is another. The Jewlerie is the probably most recent addition, and the bar he occasionally goes to for having a bottle of rum is yet another chamber. His last chamber is the shipyard.<br /> Flooded, Corrosive, Currents, Undergrowth, Fog, Disruption.<br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Limb from Limb, Unbreakable, Cyclopean Strength, Relentless Hunter, Monster from the Deep, Looming Presence<br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You cannot run, You are not alone, Behold, my True Form!, All your Teeth are falling out, Fear is Contagious, You cannot kill it, Death is a Prison, You are better than them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-03-2017, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T09:19:11-07:00","id":1134154,"title":"","content":"Came up with an idea? A Beast SlumLord but would like ideas on what Family or Hunger they should have<br /> <br /> thinking &quot;Keep to your place mind your own business dont do or deal drugs, or engage in prostitution.&quot; as the lesson they teach<br /> <br /> so hunger for punisdhment maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\"