container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1135275#post1135275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas what he can do when Feeding gets to be problematic?<br /> <br /> Family Dinner?<br /> <br /> a region that complacent will make an ideal hunting territory for Vamps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In that case, has he really helped his tenants at all?<br /> <br /> I think you see where my point about the downfalls of trying to solve problems as a Beast is going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T16:08:21-07:00","id":1135287,"title":"","content":"Still arguably better then gang leaders, drugs and murder on the streets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T20:29:35-07:00","id":1135336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1135287#post1135287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still arguably better then gang leaders, drugs and murder on the streets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many Hunter organizations would disagree with you (Because at least they are human).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T21:33:04-07:00","id":1135344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1135336#post1135336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many Hunter organizations would disagree with you (Because at least they are human).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And those hunters would be idiots, because those 'humans' don't have any incentive to keep their victims alive.<br /> <br /> At least a Beast will try to keep the death toll to a minimum. Most street level criminals are too stupid to care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-30-2017, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T22:02:02-07:00","id":1135351,"title":"","content":"thoughts on the idea? of the slum being a peaceful, but subtly creepy community, for some hunters , or just mortal PC's coming finding the people welcoming, but finds their almost too straight and narrow? <br /> <br /> seems like a good start to many horror movies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T02:50:38-07:00","id":1135378,"title":"","content":"Slum and welcoming does not really fit together for me. Make it a suburb, 50's style idyillic with a creepy undertone for that imo.<br /> <br /> But a somewhat clean slum, with healthy-ish looking people, and many more valuables outside than normal due to not fearing being stolen from, sure. And over all of this, a sense of oppression, of bottled-up desires and needs, of having-to-behave-good rather than being good - you can still see that in some of their eyes. Some hat this new life, where they lost all their Status, and Wonder how they can bring the good old times back. Others adapt: put out very valuable stuff in the hoped of making their neighbour jealous (&quot;Look how good we have it!&quot;) And if he steals that, even better- now the Lord will deal with him!<br /> <br /> Human beings are a creative bunch. They find loopholes in any system. This will be a less - obviously miserable slum, but miserable it still will be.<br /> Because the Beast oppresses, he does not enable further than that. <br /> At least, That'd be my take","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:14:05-07:00","id":1135475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1135351#post1135351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thoughts on the idea? of the slum being a peaceful, but subtly creepy community, for some hunters , or just mortal PC's coming finding the people welcoming, but finds their almost too straight and narrow?<br /> <br /> seems like a good start to many horror movies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said, slums are typically the most run down, shitty places of the city. They're the place you go when you've hit rock bottom and have no other options for survival. It would be an oxymoron for the 'slums' to be a peaceful, decent place to live. It should be riddled with crime, corruption and condemned architecture in order to qualify as a slum.<br /> <br /> This would be why the slumlord trying to expand the slum would be so terrifying. Its victims would be afraid of being forced to live there, and would thus fight to keep the city a decent place to live. Their lesson to the people could be <i>&quot;treat each other properly, or this is where you'll end up.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-30-2017, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T11:44:19-07:00","id":1135523,"title":"","content":"Hmmn just thought, would a Drug Dealer, Pimp, gangster or prostitute work for a Hero?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T12:15:11-07:00","id":1135532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1135523#post1135523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmn just thought, would a Drug Dealer, Pimp, gangster or prostitute work for a Hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the above, so long as they can justify why they're still doing what they're doing. Justification is the heart of the antagonistic Hero. Of course, the justification doesn't have to be especially mystical. It could be something as simple as 'the gang will kill me if I try to leave, and then I won't be able to bring down the monsters'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T15:02:16-07:00","id":1135616,"title":"","content":"The Survivalist - Namtaru Tyrant<br /> Jonathan Monroe is everything Bear Grylls would like to be when it comes to Survival: no matter where he is dropped off, this guy manages to come through. Expeditions to the Antarctic, the Jungle, the Desert? Been there, done that. He was not well known, however, since he went as far as living completely on his own in the woods for a few years. Recognition was not what he was after: being self-reliant, and enjoying the world, and making sure he can last long, was what he was about. And that was before his Devouring.<br /> Now, with his soul a swarm of buzzing, hungry scarabs, the man managed to make friends with honest-to-goodness Ancient Mummies. Monroe is even a honorary member in one such illustrious group, with certain responsibilities but also rights. He helps his friend with the memory problem, but has to admit he is very curious about the ability to return from the dead. Might there be a way to get something similar for himself?<br /> He is traveling, but ever since, the desert stayed a special splace for him.<br /> Jonathan needs to feed this new hunger, though, and what better way than to put people into situations where he as a guide is no longer available, where they are forced to do something they think is ugly or disgusting to survive? Realizing their dependence on someone else, the fear of facing a situation one is not equipped to handle wakes people up to the fact that they are not fit to live on their own. That satisfies the Beast's desire to teach a lesson. Them realizing they are capable of things they would otherwise recoil from in revulsion, that satisfies the Namtaru desire to revolt and disgust. People also begrudingly admiring Jonathan for his abilities and superiority, that satisfies the Tyrant in him. And so, the Beast feeds on his customers every once in a while - preppers, survivalists, survivalist-wannabes, soldiers, hunters and city people wanting a taste of adventure.<br /> <br /> Becoming better at survival in any meaning of the word, that satisfies all of him. After all, this Beast wants to last as long as he can in this dangerous, beautiful world...<br /> <br /> <br /> Horror: Swarm of Scarabs<br /> Lair: A desert scene, with &quot;burning sand&quot;, a blinding sun, the disgusting stench of carrion, and slithering snakes. One of his chambers is a street corner in NYC, with the street lights being on fire, the windows reflecting the desert sun, snakes hanging from street signs and dead and dying pets laying on the wayside filling the air with a horrible smell of decay. One cave in Peru is also a tomb, a strange mix of jungle and Sahara, with burning sand trickling down from above, illuminating the cave-tomb.<br /> Lair Traits: Blazing Light, Stench, Burning, Noxious Gases<br /> Atavisms: Infestation, Looming Presence, Relentless Hunter, Unbreakable, Shadowed Soul, Storm-Lashed, Wings of the Raptor<br /> Nightmares: Run Away!, Fear is Infectious<br /> Merits: Epic Potential (Stamina), Epic Orientation, Hardy, Survivalist, Eidetic Memory, Advanced Danger Sense, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Poisonous plants), Advanced Fast Reflexes, Hunger Management, Trained Observer, Patient.<br /> <br /> <br /> Jonathan is geared towards surviving, as can be seen. With Infestation and Unbreakable alone, incoming damage is highly reduced unless Aggravated, especially when spending satiety, and Relentless Hunter and Looming Presence (+Epic Potential Stamina) only increase this resilience. Shadowed Soul gives him a way to outright evade notice or damage, and helps with vision in dark places. Storm-Lashed helps with weathering the weather, Wings of the Raptor with unwelcoming terrain. Storm-Lashed and Wings of the Raptor help with inflicting a debuff/Tilt like Knockdown and escaping. Which is needed, since he has little abilitites when it comes to DEALING damage - Jonathan wants to teach people about themselves, about their reliance on others. Once they are aware of that, they need to decide for themselves in how far they want to change that or adapt to that. He has no interest in causing physical harm directly.<br /> His Nightmares are similarly meant to make people freak out (so they end up in troublesome situations) and/or leave him alone (Looming Presence helps here, too).<br /> In his chosen field, his Training makes him good (Hardy, Survivalist), which is only enhanced with his new abilities (Looming Presence for more Stamina on rolls, Relentless Hunter against Fatigue, Toxic for Poisons, Infestation for movement/lack of air, Stench/Noxious Gases for resilience against that, Epic Orientation to find his way at all times + improve his tracking)<br /> Of course, he can call down Lightning Bolts with Storm-Lashed, and even a vicious sand storm if he spends the Satiety.<br /> <br /> Jonathan has goals, despite having come a long way: He wants to become even more resilient (Iron Skin Merits), but even more important to him is to master the art of Parkour! After all, free movement is a thing with him, and there are situations where turning into a bunch of scarabs is not the approrpriate response. He is also looking for ways to steel his mind: being part of a cult makes it necessary to be able to hold a conversation, not something he is very accostumed to. Being able to stand his ground here is important, even more so considering the mind-bending abilities of some of his cousins (Iron Will and Indomitable). Finally, while not interested in inheritance, really, he is looking for a way to extend his time on this earth - The Descent seems to be his best bet so far. Studying Irem's culture (he relies on his Mummy friend for this) might help with that. Making Friends with Shamans might not be a bad call, either.<br /> Essentially, he searches for a form of immortality - Reinkarnation, to be exact. After all, he was the Scarabs. And the Scarab was the symbol of rebirth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T17:43:20-07:00","id":1135642,"title":"","content":"I feel like the survivalist would be better suited as a Makara, as I imagine their primordial fear to be that of somebody being immersed in an environment they aren't adapted to. Traditionally being a human dropped in the middle of the ocean, but more modern interpretations allow for other sorts of environments, such as the desert. (ooh, a giant scarab that burrows amidst the sand dunes!)<br /> <br /> Also, Namtaru do not desire to revolt and disgust people, they are inherently disgusting to be in the presence of. The Namtaru merely figured out how to weaponize that revulsion and make it a part of their horror. A Namtaru would be more appropriate to a survival game show in which they make people compete in gross out challenges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-30-2017, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T07:00:52-07:00","id":1135754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1135642#post1135642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the survivalist would be better suited as a Makara, as I imagine their primordial fear to be that of somebody being immersed in an environment they aren't adapted to. Traditionally being a human dropped in the middle of the ocean, but more modern interpretations allow for other sorts of environments, such as the desert. (ooh, a giant scarab that burrows amidst the sand dunes!)<br /> <br /> Also, Namtaru do not desire to revolt and disgust people, they are inherently disgusting to be in the presence of. The Namtaru merely figured out how to weaponize that revulsion and make it a part of their horror. A Namtaru would be more appropriate to a survival game show in which they make people compete in gross out challenges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum, good point. Would also go better with the quest for knowledge. Hm...<br /> No Makara Atavism fits him well, really, though. Maybe a refluffed Heart of the Desert? An ability to 'swim' in sand instead of breathing in water, and instead of destruction by water, it is destruction by Sandblasting?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Another Idea: Disney Princesses as Beasts! Or rather, characters similar to and derived from Disney princesses =D<br /> We had that already, e.g. posted images in the inspiration thread, but still:<br /> <br /> Mulan:<br /> A Dragon Horror. Mushu in Scary, basically. Challenging Societal norms, proving women to be as capable as men. Does so by hiding among men. Eshmaki Tyrant?<br /> Has Cyclopean Strength and Dragonbreath. Has the Poor Light and Burning Lair Traits, where the latter is realized through massive fireworks explosions.<br /> <br /> Merida:<br /> Considering the prominence of Bearification, a big-ass bear like Mor'du as a Horror seems fitting. For added Horror, and due to the Freedom theme and association with birds, let's give that Bear WINGS. Ugallu Tyrant, proving herself above tradition and rules, and the equal to any guy.<br /> Eye of Heaven and Needs Must are Atavisms that would be fitting (and helpful with bow shooting), though she is also an excellent climber and has Wings of the Raptor.<br /> Her Lair includes the traits Mirage (Will-O-Wisps), Exposed and Poor Light, and her lair is a cave on top of the mountain she climbed to drink straight from the waterfall.<br /> <br /> Ariel:<br /> Doubtlessly a Mermaid Horror. Makara for sure, with Alien Allure. Challenges the Racism of her people. Collector of all things human (from shipwrecks, though), so Makara Collector imo.<br /> Has Storm-Lashed, as she creates the storms that wreck ships, and Alien Allure to befriend the survivors as newest additions to her collection.<br /> Electrified, Decayed, Flooded, Downpour and Hurricane make for a horrible lair, that is meant to destroy and take down ships to the bottom of her sea.<br /> Also, probably has Heart of the Ocean and/or Suffocating.<br /> <br /> Alice (yes, would make an excellent Changeling, still):<br /> Cheshire Cat is her Horror, and she focuses much more on Nightmares than the others. Among them, causing unrational fear (They are all around you, Cursed-Object-Nightmare), Loss of Memory and Identity Crisis (Tabula Rasa, You are an Imposter), a Time-stretching nightmare that makes minutes feel like an eternity, a sudden loss of and inability to comprehend sociatal rules and norms, and a nightmare that reduces mental understanding, so that even simple tasks look like ridiculous, illogical puzzles. She does, however, have Looming Presence, and From the Shadows. An Eshmaki Ravager that endulges in creating chaos, be it the Queen of Hearts' games or a public press conference: she loves causing a panic. Favored Traits include Mirages, Cramped, Sealed Exits and Crushing.<br /> <br /> Tarzan (also works as a changeling):<br /> Has a giant Gorilla as his Horror, and as Anakim Nemesis punishes people that attack his family/friends mostly. Looming Presence and Cyclopean Strength, lair traits are slick, undergrowth, toxic and disruption to resemble a Jungle.<br /> <br /> Snow White:<br /> Anakim Tyrant with Infestation and Alien Allure. Her Horror is a group of seven deadly dwarves. Focuses on being the most pretty person around. For added fun, Siren's Treacherous Song if anyone tries to challenge her to a sing-off - or a hero tries to get too close.<br /> Her Lair is actually the mines in which the dwarves toil away, with Cramped, Darkness and Jagged as Lair Traits.<br /> <br /> Tiana:<br /> Voodoo-styled giant humanoid frog as her Horror, this Namtaru Nemesis protects her chosen spot - her cafe - from anything. Limb from Limb and Monster from the Deep are very helpful in that regard. Flooded and Slick represent the swamp, Razored the giant alligator.<br /> <br /> Dr. Facilier (works better as a Demon, but here goes):<br /> Eshmaki Collector with his shadow being his Horror. Teaches people to value what they have. Uses nightmares to create ming-bogging effects where people believe they are attractive or a frog. From the Shadows and Shadowed Soul are his Atavisms. His Lair is a the Other Side (him being 'beaten' is him retreating after having taught his lesson) with Darkness, Mirage and Currents as Lair Traits (Currents manifest as those spirits pulling on you).<br /> <br /> Belle:<br /> A Anakim Predator, The Beast is her Horror, obviously, the Castle her Lair. Despite Limb from Limb and Cyclopean Strenght, she relies more on Mimir's Wisdom and her Lair traits to harm her prey.<br /> Jagged, Engulfment, Closed Exits and Mirages (essentially, the animated furniture of the castle) soften the targets before she finishes them.<br /> <br /> Pocahontas:<br /> A speaking wooden tree as her horror, this Eshmaki Nemesis is basically an eco-terrorist. With Witchwood, Storm-Lashed and Wings of the Raptors, she is fairly capable of causing quite some mayhem. Her Traits of Undergrowth, Flooded, Crosswinds and Hurricane support it further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T08:27:52-07:00","id":1135778,"title":"","content":"The Heart of the Desert take sounds pretty cool, actually.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call Mulan a tyrant, as she didn't really do anything tyrannical during her story. She'd probably be a nemesis, given that she joined the military to help drive back the Mongolians, who were invading China at the time. She also buried their forces under an avalanche, pretty much leaving them to a slow, gruesome death.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Ariel, I agree, she's a Makara. It comes back to my point of being immersed in an environment you have no idea how to survive in. Ariel is pretty god damn oblivious to the ways of humans, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not going to say the Cheshire cat isn't a possibility for Alice (especially not after American McGee), but you might say that the Mad Hatter also works. If we take the &quot;6 impossible things&quot; and apply it to the Hatter's mindless babbling during tea time. As for her horror, she is definitely a Makara. She didn't just peek behind the looking glass, she dove right into it!<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Snow White, I have to say she's Namtaru. Don't forget that not all gorgons are hideous and vile. Some are actually quite attractive and charismatic. The important thing is that they invoke an emotional response from those around them. In her case, the queen was overcome with maddened jealousy, the woodsman couldn't bring himself to slay her, despite it being a direct order from the queen herself, and the dwarves were practically falling over themselves to earn her affections when she showed up. Men want her, women want to be her, and there are many ways she can exploit that in order to feed her hunger.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-31-2017, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T09:05:44-07:00","id":1135800,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> I originally had Snow White as Namtaru, actually! Don't know why I changed that. I guess the revulsion part, since it is not quite clearcut that anything other than revulsion is their thing from the write-up. So what is revolting about Snow White? How about how she makes everyone go along with her every want and need? And she doesn't force them; she makes them want to do so.<br /> <br /> I like Alice as Makara better, I admit. Didn't occur to me then but it's perfect.<br /> <br /> Mulan was tricky, as I hadn't seen the movie in ages and didn't look anything up. So yeah. Forgot about the avalanche even. Blizzard as a Trait would befitting to include that...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T10:58:13-07:00","id":1135841,"title":"","content":"I came across an idea while talking to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a>: A collector who collects broken bits and pieces of Infrastructure. Seems like a fun setup for accidently turning your lair into infrastructure!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T19:51:42-07:00","id":1136062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1135800#post1135800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> I originally had Snow White as Namtaru, actually! Don't know why I changed that. I guess the revulsion part, since it is not quite clearcut that anything other than revulsion is their thing from the write-up. So what is revolting about Snow White? How about how she makes everyone go along with her every want and need? And she doesn't force them; she makes them want to do so.<br /> <br /> I like Alice as Makara better, I admit. Didn't occur to me then but it's perfect.<br /> <br /> Mulan was tricky, as I hadn't seen the movie in ages and didn't look anything up. So yeah. Forgot about the avalanche even. Blizzard as a Trait would befitting to include that...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I thought there was a part in the write up saying they didn't have to be ugly. They just had to make people feel uncomfortable, such as making the queen feel envious that she wasn't as beautiful as Snow White.<br /> <br /> Plus, she's supposed to be 14 in that movie... meaning that the Prince is either a hell of a lot younger than he looks, or he's a pedophile... same goes with those dwarves!<br /> <br /> As for making people want to go along with her, then yes, there is massive potential for her to be a Namtaru if you use that correctly. I would like to point out Rick Sanchez as evidence of how to do that properly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T14:21:17-07:00","id":1137037,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Description:</u></b> [LEGION] is a clan legendary in the hacking community for not only holding back doors into the computer systems of over a dozen multinational corporations and more than a few governments - and proving that those back doors exist, as well - but also for never having had even one of their identities exposed. Even more legendary, though, is their leader, a programmer who goes only by Aleph. Aleph is said to have been at the head of every major hack ever carried out by [LEGION], to have conquered the systems of more than a dozen nations and to have been employed by twice as many, although every such tale also includes their 'price' - a lingering program they insert into the systems of their employers, just in case they try to pull something.<br /> <br /> In reality, Aleph is not only a master hacker and programmer but also a powerful Beast. He has not yet undergone Incarnation - he is loath to leave behind the friends he's made, both in his brood and in [LEGION] - but he knows that he could. Paraplegic in the 'real' world, Aleph spends far more time using his Ghost In The Machine Atavism to explore the internet, a datascape which, to him, at least as magnificent as reality. <br /> <br /> Aleph also holds kinship with a Free Council techno-shaman, who introduced him to the Shadow and its denizens. Following this discovery, Aleph swiftly gathered a following of the data-wraiths that inhabit his 'sanctum sanctorum', a penthouse suite paid for with penny-shaved money and which is equipped with the very best in information technology. He offers these spirits a haven within his Lair in exchange for their aid and, if necessary, defense.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Family:</b></u> Ugallu<br /> <br /> <u><b>Hunger:</b></u> Tyrant - Aleph satisfies his hunger with his hacking, making sure that his victims know precisely who got into their system and what he could have done. They should be glad that he only stole <i>some</i> of their money instead of all of it, and should take his attack as a heads-up to tighten their security. It's not that it'll <i>stop</i> him, but if they make a good show on his return visit he'll leave them alone unless they bring themselves to his attention. If they don't, well. That's the price you pay in this digitized world.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Horror:</b></u> Aleph's Horror is a code-dragon within the cyberspace of its lair, its every feather-scale a polygon scintillating with viruses and firewalls both. Its exact appearance varies from moment. A frill of horns expands behind its head in an intimidation display when it roars, only to shift into a sleek, smooth neck as the creature dives in to bite. <br /> <br /> <u><b>Lair:</b></u> Aleph's Lair appears at first glance to be a classical dragon's lair - a vast mountain, within which a labyrinth of tunnels connect the Chambers to the Heart. As you ascend through the guts of the mountains, though, you begin to realize that everything is not as it seems. Those aren't vines, they're cables. Holograms conceal hidden traps and dangers. Those aren't shiny crystals in the ceiling, they're cameras. Technology rebels against its users. If an intruder survives the innards of the mountain and its guardians - data-spirits who are <i>more</i> than happy to possess the animatronic monsters scattered around the Lair - the Heart is a pristine server-farm, all blue lights and white surfaces. The temperature is frigid, just perfect for computers.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lair Traits:</u></b> Extreme Cold, Maze, Disruption, Mirages, Exposed, Sealed Exits, Poor Lighting<br /> <br /> <u><b>Atavisms:</b></u> Eyes of the Heavens, Ghost in the Machine, Basilisk's Touch, Unbreakable, Looming Presence, Needs Must, Ten Thousand Faces, Wings of the Raptor<br /> <br /> <u><b>Nightmares:</b></u> You Are Not Alone, You Must Obey, Everything You Do Is Worthless, Fear is Contagious, They Are All Around You, You Will Never Rest<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T19:54:16-07:00","id":1137167,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><u>Description:</u></b> Claudia Hopf is a simple woman and her life was largely uneventful. Raised by devout Christian medical doctors, she was taught from a young age about the trade of healing and the virtuous path. As much as she tried her very best to be a good professional, she was the least loved among her three sisters for her lack of social grace and perfunctory adherence to Christianity. Her Devouring came on the night she gained a prize for academic excellence in dentistry which failed to get so much as a smile from her parents. Full of bitterness and disgust, she retreated deep into her dreams, where she met her Horror. She would try her best to feed its dozens of gnashing maws with pile after pile of exquisite food and grandiose praise, only for it to demand more. Just when she was about to break down from exhaustion, she screamed in defiance and leaped at the Horror\u2019s slimy, bloated form and exchanged blows with it until the Devouring was complete. From that night onward, she never again allowed her worth to be defined by others or used sweet words when brutal honesty was necessary.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Family:</u></b> Namtaru<br /> <br /> <u><b>Legend:</b></u> Judgmental<br /> <br /> <u><b>Life:</b></u> Parental<br /> <br /> <b><u>Hunger:</u></b> Tyrant \u2013 Claudia gains Satiety not just by scaring people straight when it comes to oral hygiene, but also by taking away the metaphorical sweetness out of their mouths. She is a good listener despite her rough exterior, and is more than capable of being fully honest with patients who are being too na\u00efve or smarmy. She wasted many years being a sweetheart and had little to show for it, so she tries to show people that there is a time for being blunt.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Horror:</u></b> A garish, rainbow colored blob of syrup covered in fanged maws of hardened sugar. Many elephant-like feet are formed and then absorbed noisily as it quickly and messily crawls around, its massive form heaving and sloshing. What passes for its head is a luminous pyramid made of the same substance as the fangs. Around the head is a halo of flying bugs that serve as sensory and communicative organs. Many polymorphic appendages extend from just above the feet, clicking and dripping. Its stomach is transparent, and a hideous mess of alien organs can be seen producing an endless flow of liquid and solid treats that are excreted and replaced like the teeth of a shark.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lair:</u></b> An obese wonderland of the most decadent level, where every piece of the landscape is edible and delicious to the point of being addictive. Rivers of honey, mountains of chocolate and forests of chewing gum and a dozen other painfully inviting sights go as far as the eye can see. There is no sun, stars or moon, for the whole sky is covered in titanic clouds of flying bugs, leaving the rare glowing fauna and flora as the only sources of light. This is where people are brought to understand precisely why too much sugar is bad for their health or grow enough of a backbone to stand up to the foul Horror.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Lair Traits:</u></b> Poor Light, Sealed Exits, Swarms, Exposed, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous</b></a>, Viscous<br /> <br /> <b><u>Atavisms:</u></b> Alien Allure, Basilisk\u2019s Touch, Eye Of Heaven, Infestation, Limb From Limb, Looming Presence, Mimir\u2019s Wisdom, Needs Must, Relentless Hunter<br /> <br /> <b><u>Nightmares:</u></b> All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, Behold My True Form, Bugs Everywhere, We Know All Your Secrets, You Must Obey</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bOtMizMQ6oM\" data-code=\"bOtMizMQ6oM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/bOtMizMQ6oM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-03-2017, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T16:01:58-07:00","id":1139572,"title":"","content":"2 more ideas based on occupations associated with Fear<br /> <br /> INS agent, KNOW this is political<br /> <br /> not sure what he can teach other then &quot;Dont come into the country uninvited&quot;<br /> <br /> And Repossesion.<br /> <br /> Which can teach &quot;Pay your bills in a timely manner!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T11:33:47-07:00","id":1139979,"title":"","content":"Dragon Fire + Wings of the Raptor + Relentless Hunter + Infestation + Looming Presence<br /> <br /> <i>Somebody have fun with that....</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T12:30:31-07:00","id":1139987,"title":"","content":"Does it have to be fire-based, or can it some sort of mod of dragonfire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T13:10:09-07:00","id":1139991,"title":"","content":"Two connected character ideas, both possibly Incarnate or close just to have the power level needed. Very crossover-heavy and inspired by Beasts' effect on the Hedge<br /> <br /> An Eshmaki Collector who does the ludicrously dangerous job of stealing Changelings from Arcadia. His hoard is the support network of Changeling Kin he puts together from the survivors. He will definitely need from the shadows. He teaches the lesson that people are not toys.<br /> <br /> And his darker counterpart, an Ugallu Nemesis based off the dark truth that True Fae are kin too. Basically, he's a privateer who punishes Changelings for breaking the pacts they made with the True Fae by escaping. He teaches other people the lessons of &quot;stick to your word&quot; and &quot;don't mess with the fae world in the first place&quot;<br /> <br /> Have I mentioned I love making evil Nemesis Beasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T13:44:59-07:00","id":1139999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1139987#post1139987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it have to be fire-based, or can it some sort of mod of dragonfire?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be plasma, focused solar energy, laser beams, with a little reskinning it could work for shooting lightning or an entropic breath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T14:46:58-07:00","id":1140321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1139987#post1139987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it have to be fire-based, or can it some sort of mod of dragonfire?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I modded it for a banshee's scream myself.<br /> <br /> Edit to add to the thread:<br /> <br /> A brood that is a Judge (Anakim Tyrant), a Sheriff (Ugallu Nemesis), and a Jailer (Namtaru Collector).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 09-14-2017, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T15:51:01-07:00","id":1140344,"title":"","content":"My character concept is about an hacker ravager, he feed his horror by infecting and damaging computers with virus and malawares. And usually his victims are people who use internet to do lewd things or greedy corporations. He could be a Eshmaki since hackers as well lurks in the shadow when they attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:08:14-07:00","id":1140632,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda poking around an old idea that I need help refining. Mostly just need help with powers and what not.<br /> <br /> Concept: Empress of Mars.<br /> <br /> Description: You see her upon her rusted throne, floating above a ruined keep. Tall and thin with grey skin, obsidian hair, and black voids for eyes. She sits there regally, surveying her kingdom of ruin and dust. Somehow you know, with a gesture she could crush you, but for now you are beneath her attention. A mere ant in the presence of a Queen from beyond the stars.<br /> <br /> Powers: This where things start fall apart.. I want her to be something of a telekinetic/psychic.. while hunger is easy enough I keep bouncing between ungallu and anakim... as the latter's strength could be re-skinned as touch range telekinesis.. but the former also has bits that fit nicely... Though I heavily favor Anakim. Its just a matter of hashing out atavisms and nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T09:40:09-07:00","id":1140841,"title":"","content":"The story of <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/0Tefh\" target=\"_blank\">Jimmy C</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T04:26:42-07:00","id":1141364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1140632#post1140632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda poking around an old idea that I need help refining. Mostly just need help with powers and what not.<br /> <br /> Concept: Empress of Mars.<br /> <br /> Description: You see her upon her rusted throne, floating above a ruined keep. Tall and thin with grey skin, obsidian hair, and black voids for eyes. She sits there regally, surveying her kingdom of ruin and dust. Somehow you know, with a gesture she could crush you, but for now you are beneath her attention. A mere ant in the presence of a Queen from beyond the stars.<br /> <br /> Powers: This where things start fall apart.. I want her to be something of a telekinetic/psychic.. while hunger is easy enough I keep bouncing between ungallu and anakim... as the latter's strength could be re-skinned as touch range telekinesis.. but the former also has bits that fit nicely... Though I heavily favor Anakim. Its just a matter of hashing out atavisms and nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An Anakim Tyrant with Ugallu Atavisms. Give her Cyclopean Strength (Anakim) to represent telekinetic power, Mimir's Wisdom (Anakim) for preternaturally superior intelligence in general, and Eye of Heaven (Ugallu) to represent mind-reading. Her regal presence could be represented by either Looming Presence (Anakim) or Alien Allure (Makara), depending on which aspect you want to emphasize (maybe even both). Other Atavisms such as Wings of the Raptor and Unbreakable could be added on, representing things like telekinetically flying around on her throne and force shields. No idea on Nightmares, though. I'm not yet savvy with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1140841#post1140841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story of <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/0Tefh\" target=\"_blank\">Jimmy C</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Everything about that guy just screams Beast. Either a Makara or Ugallu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T09:54:07-07:00","id":1141444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1141364#post1141364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Everything about that guy just screams Beast. Either a Makara or Ugallu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds more like a low-Synergy sin-eater to me personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T14:22:44-07:00","id":1141541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AberrantEyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1141444#post1141444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds more like a low-Synergy sin-eater to me personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not savvy enough in Geist - would you mind explaining a bit more?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Is it the &quot;jumped off a bridge&quot; and &quot;we&quot; part? Those could be read as metaphor for the Devouring and the presence of the Horror, and the surreality of the whole experience look more in line with the blurring of reality and dream that Beasts tend to provoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 09-18-2017, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T07:38:59-07:00","id":1141742,"title":"","content":"Zuroch, the Iron Bank. Makara Nemesis who is the gilded halls, the piles of money, the chains and gnashing of teeth; as well as the terrible Goblin who keeps its ledger. You wouldn't think something so small, so decrepit, so devoid of heart could be so terrifying and yet: home after home, business after business, every hope and every dream find their way into his ledger next to a number. Zuroch embodies the fear of drowning in debt and punishes those who reach beyond their grasp with terrifying collection tactics. Those who &quot;default&quot; find themselves torn from their loved ones working off their debt in the Iron bank itself. Worse of all, debt is considered a familial burden.<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Mimir's Wisdom, ???<br /> Nightmares: You Must Obey, They Are Watching You<br /> Lair Traits: No Escape, ???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:29:09-07:00","id":1141973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1141742#post1141742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zuroch, the Iron Bank. Makara Nemesis who is the gilded halls, the piles of money, the chains and gnashing of teeth; as well as the terrible Goblin who keeps its ledger. You wouldn't think something so small, so decrepit, so devoid of heart could be so terrifying and yet: home after home, business after business, every hope and every dream find their way into his ledger next to a number. Zuroch embodies the fear of drowning in debt and punishes those who reach beyond their grasp with terrifying collection tactics. Those who &quot;default&quot; find themselves torn from their loved ones working off their debt in the Iron bank itself. Worse of all, debt is considered a familial burden.<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Mimir's Wisdom, ???<br /> Nightmares: You Must Obey, They Are Watching You<br /> Lair Traits: No Escape, ???</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that! Like Gringott's on meth. For his Makara atavism... maybe Monster From the Deep, representing animating parts of his hoard to to act as Security? Or Alien Allure, to show the seductive draw of glittering gold?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:20:44-07:00","id":1142115,"title":"","content":"I forgot Alien Allure was Makara. Almost definately that. Although ugly himself, his gold is quite shiny.<br /> <br /> On that note, bright light (glittering gold) may make a good second lair trait. Need one that is easy to apply. Maze and Crushing are also thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:31:40-07:00","id":1142117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1141973#post1141973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that! Like Gringott's on meth. For his Makara atavism... maybe Monster From the Deep, representing animating parts of his hoard to to act as Security? Or Alien Allure, to show the seductive draw of glittering gold?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Needs Must, for tracking the prey.<br /> <br /> Edit: Now I realize that it was specifically a Makara Atavism that was needed. My apologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 09-20-2017, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T10:43:56-07:00","id":1142214,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1157\" data-vbnamecard=\"1157\">SoulGambit</a> If I may propose an alternative interpretation, assuming homebrew from the forum is a thing you are okay with:<br /> Take <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a>'s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1029982#post1029982\">Endless Depths</a> Atavism to represent the unrelenting hardheadedness of the Iron Bank's Goblin: they will not be swayed, and no matter the tricks you try to pull, they will get their due!<br /> To represent the shiny gold, take Blazing Light, sure. And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a>'s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait#post649174\">Wondrous</a> Lair Trait, because that fits really, <i>really </i>well here.<br /> <br /> Alien Allure is an Atavism, and as such should reflect the Horror, not the Lair, which is why I thought it might not be fitting (unless there is something alluring about the Goblin itself). Siren's Treacherous Song might work well, too, for the times the Goblin makes sweet, sweet promises.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and btw, totally love the concept!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T10:49:39-07:00","id":1143843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1139999#post1139999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be plasma, focused solar energy, laser beams, with a little reskinning it could work for shooting lightning or an entropic breath.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, great...<br /> <br /> Now I'm imagining some kind of giant disco ball shooting laser beams in all directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T11:05:36-07:00","id":1143846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1143843#post1143843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Well, great...<br /> <br /> Now I'm imagining some kind of giant disco ball shooting laser beams in all directions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nightmare: You cannot kill it? (It being Disco)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T11:10:25-07:00","id":1143847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1143846#post1143846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nightmare: You cannot kill it? (It being Disco)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In all seriousness, what would that do? Inflict Beaten Down even on supernatural targets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T12:01:39-07:00","id":1143857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1143847#post1143847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In all seriousness, what would that do? Inflict Beaten Down even on supernatural targets?</div> </div> </div> </div>You Cannot Kill It is a Kinship Nightmare (Tammuz Prometheans in the example given) that causes your attacks to be ineffective.<br /> Specifically:<br /> - All attacks the victim makes against the Beast inflict only bashing damage, regardless of the damage type they normally inflict. Attacks that make use of one of the Beast\u2019s Anathema (p. 208) are not affected. (Normal Effect)<br /> -The victim\u2019s attacks against the Beast reduce their weapon damage rating by two. (Negative damage ratings subtract damage from the number of successes rolled.) If a negative damage modifier reduces damage on a successful attack to zero or less, the Beast takes one bashing damage instead. (High Satiety)<br /> - The Beast may spend multiple Satiety on this effect. For every Satiety spent, the Beast reduces damage from one attack by the victim to one bashing damage. (SatExpenditure)<br /> - Any time the victim fails an attack roll against the Beast, the victim loses a point of Willpower (Exceptional Success)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T13:03:59-07:00","id":1143875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1143857#post1143857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You Cannot Kill It is a Kinship Nightmare (Tammuz Prometheans in the example given) that causes your attacks to be ineffective.<br /> Specifically:<br /> - All attacks the victim makes against the Beast inflict only bashing damage, regardless of the damage type they normally inflict. Attacks that make use of one of the Beast\u2019s Anathema (p. 208) are not affected. (Normal Effect)<br /> -The victim\u2019s attacks against the Beast reduce their weapon damage rating by two. (Negative damage ratings subtract damage from the number of successes rolled.) If a negative damage modifier reduces damage on a successful attack to zero or less, the Beast takes one bashing damage instead. (High Satiety)<br /> - The Beast may spend multiple Satiety on this effect. For every Satiety spent, the Beast reduces damage from one attack by the victim to one bashing damage. (SatExpenditure)<br /> - Any time the victim fails an attack roll against the Beast, the victim loses a point of Willpower (Exceptional Success)</div> </div> </div> </div>A damage reduction effect sounds more like an atavism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T13:47:39-07:00","id":1143887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1143875#post1143875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A damage reduction effect sounds more like an atavism</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is not actually reducing damage that you deal, it is making you <i>ineffective </i>at causing it because you are afraid your efforts are in vain (mechanically the same, but fluff-wise very different). Playing on the Fear of being unable to make a difference, of harming that which seeks to harm you. Very common in monster movies. I think it is very appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T14:22:46-07:00","id":1143897,"title":"","content":"<b>The Corporate Dolphin:</b> An easy going, high spirited office worker who's playful antics gradually prod away at the success of many corporate sharks. Leaving their careers dead in the water.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://dolphins.org/uploads/miscellaneous/kids_area/sight.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-25-2017, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T02:35:39-07:00","id":1148255,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://9gag.com/gag/ajNXwnw\" target=\"_blank\">Diving into the deepest depths. Might make you want to make a Makara.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T09:40:28-07:00","id":1149451,"title":"","content":"This is probably going to be a very odd idea, given that it was actually inspired by the Kantai Collection of all things, but would a Horror in the shape of a naval vessel or, maybe better, a submarine work for a Makara? I have this image of an old - <i>really</i> old, by this point - seaman who served onboard the U-Boats during WWII who, when he left the sea after the war, kept his 'wolf of the seas' inside his soul. On the other hand, they could be one of the allied seamen who feared the U-Boats.<br /> <br /> Given that this Beast would be quite old and powerful, I'm thinking that it should have the Heart of the Ocean, From the Shadows, Needs Must (representing sonar and such), Titanic Blow (his soul is a massive chunk of steel that fires torpedoes) and Unbreakable (for the plating).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T21:14:42-07:00","id":1149597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1149451#post1149451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably going to be a very odd idea, given that it was actually inspired by the Kantai Collection of all things, but would a Horror in the shape of a naval vessel or, maybe better, a submarine work for a Makara? I have this image of an old - <i>really</i> old, by this point - seaman who served onboard the U-Boats during WWII who, when he left the sea after the war, kept his 'wolf of the seas' inside his soul. On the other hand, they could be one of the allied seamen who feared the U-Boats.<br /> <br /> Given that this Beast would be quite old and powerful, I'm thinking that it should have the Heart of the Ocean, From the Shadows, Needs Must (representing sonar and such), Titanic Blow (his soul is a massive chunk of steel that fires torpedoes) and Unbreakable (for the plating).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Arr, ye be seeking the Flying Dutchman!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T23:47:34-07:00","id":1149610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1149597#post1149597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Arr, ye be seeking the Flying Dutchman!</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is that I hadn't even thought of the Flying Dutchman. I do agree, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T15:37:00-07:00","id":1150220,"title":"","content":"<b>Ruby</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Who would have dreamed that one day I would learn to weaponize my depression? Life's funny like that. Anyway, over the next, let's say, month or so, I'm going to stalk, harass, and demoralize you until your mind snaps and you lose the will to live completely. I'd say that I hope that's okay with you, but really, I don't care either way.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> If any Beast embodies the archetype of the disinterested predator, it's Ruby. Devoured as a young adult, she's had plenty of years to come to terms with the nightmares she inflicts to survive. She hardly seems to care about teaching lessons at all; if asked about her choice of prey, she merely shrugs and claims to go after who ever &quot;seems interesting&quot; in the moment.<br /> <br /> For as long as she can remember, Ruby has suffered from melancholic episodes, that would leave her feeling listless and unworthy of love. On more than one occasion she would spend an entire day lying in bed, unable to muster the will to get up, imagining a misty, hag-like creature looming above her, sometimes whispering terrible things into her ears, other times staring silently in mute accusation.<br /> <br /> One night, Ruby went to sleep, and the fog-witch approached her with a proposition: If Ruby spread this misery she felt unto others, she would be freed from its grip. Ruby accepted.<br /> <br /> Now, Ruby is a woman in her mid-thirties, a Namtaru Predator whose Horror takes the form of a tall, mist-enshrouded humanoid with dark hair that falls all the way to the floor and bejeweled eyes that shine ruby-red through the darkness. Her Lair is a foggy swamp full of entangling thorns and poisonous plants.<br /> <br /> These days, Ruby feeds almost exclusively from using Nightmares. She's developed a taste for it, like how some chefs can't help but spice all their dishes with nutmeg or cayenne. She knows a broad variety of them; in addition, she developed all her Kinship Nightmares from an obscure group of vampires who use her association as a smokescreen for their illicit (&quot;unpopular&quot; in their words) feeding practices. Ruby is interested in learning even more Nightmares, particularly We Know All Your Secrets, You Can't Take It With You, and You Knew This Would Happen. A Beast who knows one of them possesses a potential bargaining chip.<br /> <br /> Ruby's powerful enough that, if she really wanted to, she could become the Apex of whatever area she inhabits. She's certainly thinking about it, and a little bit of persuasion would suffice to push her into taking decisive action.<br /> <br /> Barring that, she'd like to take a vacation, not just physically, but spiritually as well. To that end, once her schedule seems clear (and if she decides not to go after the Apex, it will be clear very soon), she's going to go on a feeding frenzy, provoking a wave of despair across the region, gorging on sadness, sorrow, and saudade until her oversatiated Horror falls asleep. Then, while the region is still reeling, she's going to hop on a plane to someplace else. Maybe somewhere sunny.<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Eye of Heaven, Infestation, Mimir's Wisdom, Shadowed Soul, Swamp Hag Cunning<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, Bugs Everywhere!, Everything You Do Is Worthless, Flying and Falling, You Are Alone, You Can't Wake Up, Everyone Hates You, You Are Lost, You Are an Impostor, Death Is a Prison<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Undergrowth, Fog, Toxic, Jagged, Viscous, Stinging<br /> <br /> <b>Pertinent Merits:</b> Allies (Children of Judas) 3, Fast-Talking 1, Guilty Pleasure (Suicides), Indomitable, Resources 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T13:28:38-07:00","id":1150436,"title":"","content":"I like to imagine while she's spending all day in bed, she's exploring the Primordial Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T07:50:58-07:00","id":1154118,"title":"","content":"<b>Family: </b>Makara<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Punishment<br /> <b>Horror: </b>The Haunter of the Marshes - The Haunter is a subtle, almost immaterial thing. With a shifting outline that always seems to hide the face of a loved one, it flits above the dark pools of its Lair like mist on the breeze.<br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> From the Shadows, Alien Allure, Untouchable, Ten Thousand Faces, Draining Kiss<br /> <b>Lair: </b>The Dead Marshes - Flooded, Undergrowth, Mirages, Fog, Viscous<br /> <b>Nightmares: </b>Follow The Lights, The Dead Are All Around You, You Can't Trust Your Senses, You Are Lost, Tainted Water<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><u>Follow The Lights</u></b><br /> <i>They're all around you, consuming your vision. They're beautiful. Surely, nothing bad would happen if you just... followed them?</i><br /> <br /> <b><u>The Dead Are All Around You</u></b><br /> <i>The world is built on the dead. The builders who died constructing your house, the drivers whose blood seeps into the road. </i><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T07:41:01-08:00","id":1158938,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1D4mtj6g-us\" target=\"_blank\">10 Two Sentence Horror Stories</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Feel free to take inspiration from these. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T05:49:43-08:00","id":1182884,"title":"","content":"A chef, wealthy, a local celebrity due to his likeablity, skilled in his trade and a rising star in the international cooking scene. What no one knows: he is always looking for special ingrediants to still his Hunger - having the meat of his victims consumed is all he needs, and although he is partial to eating it himself, he doesn't mind sharing with Family, family, friends and, occasionally, unsuspecting visitors. Most of the time, the attack leaves the victim alive albeit harmed or even crippled: missing whole groups of muscles can have severe consequences. Sometimes, all that is left are bones, picked clean.<br /> He doesn't seem to have a proper &quot;type&quot;, or the police might have found him out already. In fact, however, he has a type: he choses them based on how they treat food. E.g. giving back plates half-eaten or being careless with good food earns you a place on his list. Food needs to be treated with respect, after all.<br /> And turning something useless into something useful and delicious- isn't that the highest gift you can make?<br /> <br /> <br /> Eshmaki Nemesis, with a jaguar-sized toad-creature for a Horror. Has the From the Shadows, Alien Allure, Shadowed Soul and Limb from Limb Atavisms.<br /> Lair traits are Undergrowth, Viscous, Darkness and Cramped. Nightmares are You Deserve This and Run Away!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T07:54:23-08:00","id":1182924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1182884#post1182884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Has someone been watching Hannibal recently?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T13:26:18-08:00","id":1183032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1182924#post1182924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has someone been watching Hannibal recently?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, no, not in a long while. But was this inspired by Mads Mikkelsens awesome performance? Absolutely! =) Good performances stay with you for a long time =D<br /> But if you'd want an image of this Beast, you'd have to think Gordon Ramsay. At least, that's who I see as a fitting template.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T14:01:21-08:00","id":1183036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1183032#post1183032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I can see that. <br /> <br /> And now for my contribution:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ugallu Collector:</b></u> He runs an orphanage, and runs it well. The kids grow up clever and well-socialized, most go on to careers of wealth and success, or success regardless of wealth, seeming to breeze through life with a combination of wisdom, daring and fortune rarely seen. The successes of the children that have passed his doors over the long years are nearly a miracle, especially considering that many of his children come from what the euphemistically-inclined would term 'unstable backgrounds'. Feral children, abused sons and daughters, victims of human trafficking and more have come to the orphanage and been welcomed with open arms. Not all recover entirely, but none leave worse than they arrived. And if he's a vicious, uncompromising bastard whose will belies his years to those who seek to interfere with his good works, well, how's that a bad thing?<br /> <br /> Of course, all of this assumes that you haven't looked at other statistics in his city - how many child abusers are found out, compared to other places. How many trafficking rings are busted. And how many of the perpetrators don't make it to prison, or if they do make it, are found dead from 'retribution' by other criminals. Because the man whose Horror is the Simurgh is a Collector whose Hunger drives him to collect children - a terrible Hunger in any other situation, he has made it the mission of his long life to turn it to better ends, and he's seen enough of the darker side of the world that, for all the love, wisdom and affection he showers his big family with, and for all the wonders of the sunlit pinnacles of his Lair where he teaches them his most secret lessons, those of Primordial Sorcery and of the mastery of the supernatural, the monster in him is as terrible as any other.<br /> <br /> <b>Horror</b>: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://img00.deviantart.net/9f01/i/2016/220/3/e/encounters_with_the_imaginary___simurgh_by_kgoggles-dad4y75.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Wings of the Raptor, Eye of the Heavens, Limb from Limb, Alien Allure, Mimir's Wisdom, Needs Must <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> You Deserve This, Run Away, You Will Never Rest, Flying and Falling, They Are All Around You, You Cannot Wake Up<br /> <b>Lair Traits: </b>Maze, Blazing Light, Thin Air, Undergrowth, Exposed, Mirages<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T05:51:17-08:00","id":1183557,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Anakim Tyrant:</u></b> The Nemean doesn't know how old they are. They don't really care. To them, the time between fights is immaterial, a drop in an ocean. Only the moments edged by the sharp ecstasy of battle are really worth it, pleasurable as good company, good drink or good sex can be. The Nemean is pretty sure that they were male to begin with, but they learned the trick of shapeshifting at some point and have taken both male and female shapes over the years. They don't really care about the difference, save where it pertains to the fight. Muscle mass versus flexibility and dexterity. They've been a part of various Broods through out the years, but always on the periphery. They just don't care enough about their human side to really connect. They've had companions, friends and lovers who've stuck with them, revelling in the joy of conflict right next to them, and they've been of all kinds - vampire, Beast, werewolf, geist, even a human or two - but they only ever lasted so long. They achieved Incarnation a long time ago, but takes pleasure in not managing his Myth and even deliberately abandoning it on occasion so that they can prove their power by doing it all over again in another place and time. <br /> <br /> Most often, the first signs of the Nemean's arrival in a city is an uptick in streetfighting and fighting rings, particularly the no-holds-barred kind. Soon, stories about a blond-haired fighter will begin to circulate, a newcomer who beat all comers into the ground and walks away from every fight bruised at worst. Finally, there'll be a name attached to the fighter, and it's always - <i>always</i> - the Nemean. They make little effort to conceal their presence, but neither do they really try to announce it either. They've always got time for family - except before a fight - but they don't take any shit either. If someone comes to try and recruit them for a battle, they'll decide based on how good the fight looks to be, and on how much they like the asker. Appeals to morality, kindness or humanity will be met with a chuckle and a 'try again' at best. <br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> The Nemean's Horror is a lion the size of a pickup truck, its fur shimmering golden in the burning light of its Lair. Its teeth glint like steel in its maw and its limbs are corded with bunched muscle. Its eyes burn like the sun, their gaze heavy and piercing. When it roars, the air itself seems to shiver.<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Relentless Hunter, Unbreakable, Limb from Limb, Long of Limb, Ten Thousand Faces, Looming Presence, What Walks Between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T02:20:36-08:00","id":1184303,"title":"","content":"Long, long ago, when the best a human could hope for was a hut made with skins and wood to keep them safe from the elements, when survival largely depended on a successful hunt or finding a spot rich with berries, nuts or fish, when staying too long in one place was impossible, when spirits and stranger things still roamed the earth, people knew how to fear monsters.<br /> In the midst of fighting to survive this chaos, humans still found time for tribe wars - depleting their numbers was like culling themselves and ensured the survival of the tribes in times of lacking resources. And should a tribe actually win, the spoils were all the greater.<br /> It was in the aftermath of one such loss that a man became monster: Takar was hunter, and warrior. And more than anything else, he could not forgive what happened to his people.<br /> Thus he felt more than blessed when his soul became the <b>Lord of the Woods</b>, filled with a lush and dangerous forest and gave him strength to punish his enemies.<br /> Takar is an <b>Eshmaki Nemesis</b>- by subjugating those that nearly wiped out his people, he raised in status, and is worshipped as semi-divine by his followers, but what really matters is that in his woods, his rules are absolute - don't you dare break them, for you will never see him coming.<br /> Thanks to his skills as a life-long hunter and warrior, this Beast has survived for a very long time, and managed to gain a lot of power, so much so that it's territory is respected even by the People and the Wise. Nothing less to be expected of a Beast that is about to reach Incarnation through sheer power.<br /> Horror: The Lord of the Woods <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/80/17/9a/80179a36a200ce9d7d7ca18f88137df5.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Lair: 10<br /> Atavisms: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1136750#post1136750\">Manyskin</a>, From the Shadows, Limb From Limb, Monster from the Deep, Relentless Hunter, Looming Presence, Needs Must<br /> Nightmares: Run Away, Fear is Contagious, Behold my True Form, All your Teeth are Falling Out, Bugs Everywhere, You are not alone, You deserve this, You cannot Run, You will never rest.<br /> Lair Traits: Undergrowth, Jagged, Swarm, Stinging, Darkness, Toxic, Slick","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-10-2018, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T02:32:09-08:00","id":1184306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1184303#post1184303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Is he meant to have survived to the modern day or is he meant to have stayed in <i>Sundered World</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T03:56:37-08:00","id":1184321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1184306#post1184306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. Is he meant to have survived to the modern day or is he meant to have stayed in <i>Sundered World</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> Both work, and I really like the idea of that Incarnate still being around in some large Eastern European forest, e.g. the Virgin Komi Forests. Definitly an absolute end-tier kind of guy back then, would be more plot device than anything by now.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, such a being getting swept up and locked away with the Border Marches despite all its might sounds somehow saddingly appropriate. So I'd go with stayed in Sundered World.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:44:59-08:00","id":1189182,"title":"","content":"sorry for doublepost, but due to the difference in time, I felt justified in bumping this thread up a bit again.<br /> <br /> Being a Hunter is tough even in the best of times. To keep up with this lifestyle, one needs determination, devotion, and support. Damian Veidt had it all: the day a Vampire killed his mom before his eyes changed everything, and he swore to find that ugly beast and have it pay. All leads turned up nothing, however. So he went to serve in the army, and although he failed becoming a Seal (close call, though), he acquired the skills he was looking for. Once he was back, he started working with a private detective, and started looking out for signs of the supernatural. He learned that, once you really started looking, you could find hints everywhere. The hunt was on, and soon, he wasn't alone: his cell was top-notch, made up from good friends from the Days Before he convinced with evidence, people he's saved, and other Hunters that figured there was safety in numbers. All of them specialists with connections: a former Seal and currently Bodyguard, a cop, a journalist, a hunter, a lawyer and a pharmacist with an eye for the occult. They did good work. Sure, people left, and there were victims, but they all knew what they were doing it for: kill monsters, keep people save.<br /> <br /> Thus it was a nightmare on several levels when Damian was devoured. He'd become that which he hated most. His world came crushing down. What was he supposed to do, now that his soul was some sort of birds?<br /> He tried to hide it for a while. Ignored it, hoping that like a bad cold, it'd go away.<br /> It didn't.<br /> A Hero soon came after him, and was killed by his team in the subsequent firefight. Once he realized how much his Cell suffered under the Nightmares he inflicted upon them, and what dangers he invited upon them, he broke down, and told them the truth.<br /> He asked them to do what they always do: &quot;put the monster down&quot;. Surprisingly, they couldn't just do that.<br /> So they looked for another way. A remedy, an alternative, anything.<br /> And they found something. Becoming a monster was a blessing in duisguise, for it turns out, if you feed on fear, the fear of a Vampire is just as good as that of a human being. And being able to spot the creatures hiding in our midst is quite handy when you try to flush them out.<br /> Instead of going after them one by one, Damian identified several vampires, they set up surveillance, then he infiltrated their society in the lower ranks, and after gaining some more intel, they attacked once, hard, killing large groups of them at once. In another town, they went exclusively after high-profile targets.<br /> Their masterpiece: even a prince has trouble surviving a collapsing building while under attack by both prepared hunters and a Beast during the day, while a police taskforce handled the ghouls and blood dolls.<br /> Now, the Cell has proven a substantial danger to the supernatural society in their area, and while looking to exterminate all that is supernatural in their home town, decided they needed to move locations for a while. And once they are done here? Move on to the next area!<br /> The only trouble? Damian feels the pull of Family towards these creatures, and infiltrating them and getting to know them better doesn't make things easier, especially when he gets to know their plights and the parallels to his situation and theirs. His team constantly needs to make sure he doesn't &quot;fall off the deep end&quot;. On the other hand, the Cell has problems cooperating with other Cells due to having to keep Damian's abilities or his existence a secret, or be considered a Cancer Cell. This is mostly due to their willingness to be inflicted with a Nightmare like Flying and Falling or You are not Alone to increase their performance at crucial moments (e.g. research, a quick hit'n'run, preparing a site, eradicating clues etc.) despite the costs.<br /> How long will this last before it goes up in flames, because it will go up in flames for sure?<br /> <br /> <b>Name</b>: Damian Veidt <br /> <b>Family</b>: Ugallu<br /> <b>Hunger</b>: Prey<br /> <b>Horror</b>: Flock of nightmarish Shadow-Crows<br /> <b>Lair</b>: A dense, surreal seeming forest with gigantically tall trees, whose tops are filled with yellow-greenish eyes with blackish shapes for bodies watching from above, occassionally swooping down to attack.<br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Storm-Lashed, Infestation, Needs Must, Eye of Heaven, From the Shadows, Limb from Limb, Terror's Friend<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: You Cannot Run, Fear is Contagious, Bugs Everyhwere (refluffed to Bird Attack!), Flying and Falling, You are not Alone<br /> <b>Lair Traits</b>: Exposed, Mirages, Razored, Poor Light (Next up would be Undergrowth, Stench and Thunderous)<br /> <b>Merits</b>: Anonymity 4, Danger Sense (Advanced), Good Time Management, Patient, Hunger Management 3, Killer Instinct 3, Trained Observer 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  BPG came out, additional atavism 03-27-2018, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:32:58-08:00","id":1190282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1074807#post1074807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Castratos:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>snip</i></div> </div> </div> </div>What the fuck was I thinking!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T11:00:00-08:00","id":1190341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1190282#post1190282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What the fuck was I thinking!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno.<br /> I assume Freudian Theory for a typical male nightmare, a dislike for Big Game Hunters, a need for a horrible antagonist and some amounts of alcohol may have played a role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:02:53-08:00","id":1191116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1190341#post1190341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...a dislike for Big Game Hunters...</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be off-topic slightly, and I'm sure someone else has come up with it before, but does anyone else think a &quot;Great White Hunter&quot; would make a <i>fantastic</i> character concept for a Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T16:02:32-08:00","id":1191155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1191116#post1191116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This might be off-topic slightly, and I'm sure someone else has come up with it before, but does anyone else think a &quot;Great White Hunter&quot; would make a <i>fantastic</i> character concept for a Hero?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Check out Cinder's Belgian Congo Dark Era. She's a bit more sympathetic, but one of the Heroes is kinda like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T02:08:03-07:00","id":1199965,"title":"","content":"He's a Biker - one of those who just Drive place to place. He is genuinly nice, and helpful. People often say he is a Kind soul.<br /> However, what many dont realize is that he also maims people - criminals, Child abductors, drug dealers. Only those who break the rules of society for their own gain and pleasure - he would never touch a murderer who was out for vengeance, or a bankrobber who was ruined by said bank.<br /> Only the Guilty blood pleases the hellhound.<br /> Eshmaki Predator, with limb from limb, relentless hunter, shadowed soul, and death of light.<br /> Lair is a freezing hell, with extreme cold, poor light, jagged and unstable - a perfect hunting ground.<br /> Nightmares are you deserve this, all your teeth are falling out and there is not enough water (or something like that).<br /> (Will come back to flesh this out some.more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T06:11:13-07:00","id":1200001,"title":"","content":"A cold \u2018ice queen\u2019\u2019 survivalist from a cold place with Amarok as there horror and storm lord kin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 03-27-2018, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T08:53:21-07:00","id":1203027,"title":"","content":"Does anyone think that various mutants from the <i>X-Men</i> franchise would make for good Inguma Horrors? I mean, Mystique is the obvious one, but Magneto's 'rise up against you' schtick could work, as could an interpretation of Wolverine. Limb From Limb and Relentless Hunter, anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T09:17:51-07:00","id":1203041,"title":"","content":"Wrote something for a character I'm making. Whaddya think?<br /> <br /> Typhos has lived many lives. Literally. The Eshmaki claims to be a reincarnated Beast from bygone eras. Always of Greco-Roman descent. Always an orphan. And always, he awakens from his Devouring atop a stone altar, surrounded by butchered cultists. Some say he\u2019s lying. Others think he\u2019s mad. Of the two, the latter is beyond certain. A sado-masochist, he makes a game of hunting others, especially Vampires. Even when they bash his skull in, he laughs with giddy delight and exaggerated panache, eyes wild as he screams maniacally and with raw abandon. He never cries. He never snarls. He smiles, grins, cackles, or on rare occasions falls silent, his face like a cipher. But he never gets angry, no, he only gets excited.<br /> <br /> Of kinship, it is said he has called at least one Strix \u2018uncle\u2019, and if so, he is no friend of the Ventrue. Among fellow Begotten, some call him a heretic, the name \u2018Typhos\u2019 a reference to the Father of Monsters from Greek mythology. That anyone should claim to be the Dark Mother\u2019s mate\u2014reincarnated or otherwise\u2014is in poor taste at best. Other Beasts, meanwhile, see him as an eccentric black sheep (re: lunatic), and await the inevitable news of his being slain by Heroes.<br /> <br /> Wherever he goes, whenever he goes, chaos is sure to follow behind the scenes. Yet little does he know of the Hunter watching him from afar, an agent of the Lucifuge named Rebecca Adams. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <i>&quot;Behold, the rhapsody of OBLIVION!!<br /> &quot;The innocent are boring. Why hunt <b>them</b> when the nightmares of the damned are so much more rewarding?&quot;<br /> &quot;Hopes... dreams... where do they come from... where do they go?&quot;</i></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/0807/th/pre/i/2014/164/a/0/typhos__ancient_of_malaise_by_mrparaduo-d7m6ti1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 04-04-2018, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T13:43:34-07:00","id":1203121,"title":"","content":"I love him, great character!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T16:50:05-07:00","id":1203183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1203121#post1203121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love him, great character!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! He's based off a short story I wrote for a friend a long time ago. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T06:27:50-07:00","id":1203390,"title":"","content":"<br /> I was doing some spring cleaning of my PC and found a write-up of a NPC I mentioned here. It's been a while since I wrote her and I'm not so sure if she's good after all this time, but I might as well share it by now.<br /> <br /> She plays with the &quot;genetic horror&quot; tropes, half Parasite Eve, half AC's genetic memory, via Beast setting. Her Nightmare is a riff on Lovecraftian paranoia, hopefully removed enough from unfortunate implications and more focused on &quot;there's something wrong with your family heritage and its suddenly showing&quot;. But yes, it's pretty much meant to cause the target to go all &quot;Rats in the Walls&quot; on those around them and the Nightmare's description is styled along those lines (with a bit of purple prose for that very reason). She's not a nice character, but can be used as NPC of dubious allegiance with ease.<br /> <br /> <b>- Anita Rizzo</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Anita Rizzo, a Makara Collector, works as biologist in a renowned laboratory. She prefers to work alone and it's not the sort of person that socializes with the colleagues, but no one can deny that the few results she decides to share are often ground-breaking. What they don\u2019t know is that Anita hoards vials of blood of people she find interesting or peculiar, no regards of their consent. Sometimes she obtains it by inviting people to her lab and even paying for a donation, but she has assaulted people before, taking them by surprise and running away after obtaining a vial of blood. She is especially fond of the blood of other monster and people exposed to the supernatural, but Anita's reasons go beyond her Hunger. By analyzing their blood, the one of those touched by the Primordial Dream more than the others, the brilliant Begotten scientist is trying to discover a trace of the Dark Mother hidden inside it, hoping to find some sort of revelation that will lead her to the Mitochondrial Eve of Fear. While nobody has succeeded in a similar feat before, that does not stop Anita from trying.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Anita is a young woman in her thirties, tall and slim to the point of being gaunt. While working, Anita is attentive and precise, methodically following her own strict rules and writing down everything. Her dedication to order and efficiency is reflected by her appearance, which is always sterilely impeccable.</span></span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Other scientist are somewhat intimidated by Anita, which on her part avoids to talk with them unless necessary. When that happens, Anita actually is calm and well-mannered, but one can tell she\u2019d rather be elsewhere. Even with the several vampires she has a Kinship with, Anita is cold and detached, fearing that any distraction or not professional involvement might become a setback for her research.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Anita's Lair is an ocean made of blood, eerily clear enough to see perfectly through the \u201cwater\u201d. There's no surface in sight and whatever hidden sun shines its light in the ocean, it cannot be seen. The blood distorts everything, covering all in a reddish ting. Once deep enough, the skeletons of titanical beasts begin to appear. Floating inside the gore the deeper ones, the more numerous and bigger they become. Those attentive enough might even manage hear a distant beat, like a heart calling from the abyss. By following it, it eventually leads to a seafloor made of bone. Inside its chasms, the Heart of the Lair, both literally and figuratively, is waiting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Her Horror is to classical sirens what fish living close to the surface are to the creatures from the lightless abyss. Slender, vicious, the hairless monstrosity is covered in cartilage protrusions and its visage has nothing in common with a human face. No mouth, no nose, no humanity: just a pair of wide, soulless milky eyes. It usually feed with the lamprey mouths located on her four clawed hands or by piercing the body of her victims with the retractable bone proboscis she can grow from her arm, draining the blood avidly.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Legend: </span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ravenous. Anita hides it well, but when she wants something she\u2019ll do everything to obtain it no matter what. At first she might try to find a peaceful and reasonable compromise but, if that does not work, Anita will lie, deceive and even harm those who won\u2019t let her have her way </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Life:</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Meticulous. All aspects of Anita\u2019s wife are perfectly organized and she prepares every move accurately. She can\u2019t stand elements of disturbance and she quickly sets straight all that does not fit her plans.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Family: </span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Makara</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Hunger:</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hoard</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Horror:</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Vampiric Siren</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mental Attributes: </span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Intelligence 6, Wits 3, Resolve 4</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Physical Attributes:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Social Attributes:</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 4</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mental Skills:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Academics 4 (Genealogy), Computer 3, Craft 2, Investigation 4 (Lab Work), Medicine 5, Occult 3 (Supernatural Lineages), Science 5 (Hematology)</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Physical Skills:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Athletics 1, Brawl 2, Larceny 3 (Breaking In), Stealth 3 (Assault), Weaponry 2</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Social Skills:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Animal Ken 1, Expression 1, Intimidation 2, Persuasion 1, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 3 </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Merits:</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Area of Expertise (Hematology), Common Sense, Contacts (Local Vampires), Double Jointed, Double Jointed (Advanced), Eidetic Memory, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Science), Epic Potential (Intelligence), Fast Reflexes 1, Good Time Management, Killer Instinct 2, Library 3 (Science), Resources 3, Status 3 (Scientific Community), Trained Observer</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Atavisms:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">From The Shadows, Heart Of The Ocean, Limb From Limb, Relentless Hunter, Siren\u2019s Treacherous Song</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nightmares:</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, Fear Is Contagious, You Are Alone, You Cannot Run, You Are Infected, It\u2019s In Your Blood (see below)</span></span></span> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Willpower:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">7</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lair:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> 4 (Currents, Poor Light, Suffocating, Rotting)</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Size:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">5</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Initiative:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">8</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Defense:</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">4</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Speed: </span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">10</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Health</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>:</b> 9</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">New Nightmare: It's In Your Blood </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u201c<i>There's nothing you can do to fight it. The abominable seeds planted generations ago are about to bloom. All the weaknesses and deviances of your ancestors are hiding in your own blood and calling for you. You're doomed to suffer their same fate as your own body and mind betray you. Soon everyone will be able see it\u201d</i></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Dice Pool: </b>Intelligence + Satiety vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Normal:</b> </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">the victim gain the Paranoid Condition. She becomes convinced that there's some horrible secret or perversion that plagues her family which has tainted her very own genes. All those who can expose it or that are in the process of learning more about the past of her family and its members are seen as a threat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>High Satiety: </b>the victim gains the Broken Condition.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Satiety Expenditure: </span></span></b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">the victims enter a state of fugue. She attempts to flee the area and will violently attack anybody that tries to stop her even in the slightest. If that happens, she won't stop until her target is dead, at which point she regains her sense of self and won't remember much of the events, aside from a nightmarish recollection that has nothing to do with what really happened</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Exceptional Success: </b>For the duration of the Nightmare, the victim suffers a -2 penalty on breaking point rolls</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-05-2018, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T13:49:30-07:00","id":1203511,"title":"","content":"I see Lovecraftian Beasts, I upvote!<br /> Very nicely done, plus I like the Nightmare a lot - be sure to share it in the Homebrew Nightmares thread!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user