"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T14:26:43-07:00","id":1203525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1203524#post1203524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember seeing it there before sometime, but that might have just been the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're right, I did post the Nightmare there some time ago. Reposted it here since it was thanks to her that I made it in the first place and the two are pretty much pieces that come in the same package, at least in my mind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T12:43:50-07:00","id":1210127,"title":"","content":"Tell me that this video doesn't sound like a perfect concept for a Makara Enabler? Siren's Treacherous Song, Heart of the Ocean and Ravenous Maw for Atavisms, definitely.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u9RM4HwwoKs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u9RM4HwwoKs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u9RM4HwwoKs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u9RM4HwwoKs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:43:20-07:00","id":1212303,"title":"","content":"<b>The Great Warrior,</b> <b>Anakim Predator</b><br /> <i>&quot;Being at the top of the food chain does not make you safe.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Sparta is a warrior state, and this Beast is nothing if not an exemplary warrior - being Devoured only increased his already considerable ability and originally, his personal Agenda and his Horror's Hunger for Power entirely aligned. Once an admired leader, tragedy has befallen him and cost him everything. Now, all he seeks to do is overthrow those in power - the mightier, the better, to the degree even his Horror's appetites have changed.<br /> The fact that he keeps the company of weaponsmiths of great skill mightily increases his abilities, be they mages, dwarves or something else: as long as they can craft him a better shield, a mightier axe, a more powerful bow or stronger arrowheads, they are on comparatively good terms, and he will help them out in exchange for a boon.<br /> <b>Horror</b>: A violent storm of metal clashing upon metal, a composite being of weapons, and shields, and armours.<br /> His <b>Lair </b>a battlefield, broken weaponry strewn about, and bodies laying around. An eternal battle is being fought, and any travelers should take care not to get pulled into it, lest they get seperated and get lost on the battlefield.<br /> <b>Lair Traits</b>: Jagged, Undergrowth, Razoured, Crushing, Currents, Minions, Maze<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: All your Teeth are Falling Out, You Cannot Hurt It, Fear is Contagious, You Cannot Run Away<br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Cyclopean Strength, Relentless Hunter, Looming Presence, Fear's Friend<br /> <b>Merits:</b> A slew of battle-oriented stuff like Iron Skin (epic), Fighting Styles (Heavy Weapons and Relentless Assault come to mind) and Danger Sense (advanced) as well as Fast Reflexes (advanced), but also Demolisher (ooo), Epic Potential (Strength), Giant, Fleet of Foot (ooo) and Indomitable, Inspiring and Hunger Management. Most importantly, powerful weapons (e.g. blades crafted from perfected metals).<br /> <br /> Unlike other Horrors, especially of his time, the Great Warrior is not just scary for his own ability, but for his cunning use of tools and powerful weaponry. The great treasure that is his armory is envied him by some of his collection-oriented brethren, and he has been the target of more than one attack due to someone coveting one of his famous tools.<br /> <br /> <b>Thomas Slauenwitte, Namtaru Nemesis</b><br /> <i>&quot;Envy is most unbecoming.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This Doc was once set up for everything - recognition, prestige, riches, the best opportunities to further his career and studies (as befitting one of the best in the entire world). But all was undone when a friend stabbed him in the back, put out false claims, faked documents, and set him up for a heavy fall. And why all of that? Because he wanted what his best friend had, and couldn't stand watching him enjoy the fruits of his labour.<br /> Thomas never recovered from that, but his intense hatred and need for revenge apparantly were enough to attract nightmares.<br /> Upon being Devoured and developing a hunger for punishment, Thomas knew what he'd have to do: punish envy. The most fitting punishment was death, although he does not usually feed that deeply. Most of the time, he sees to it that the victim falls uterrly ill or in terrible disrepair, and is in need of the help of the very person they tried to destroy. Your fate in their hands - a karmic punishment, indeed. If that is not possible, he is, however, satisfied with making the person suffer.<br /> He's had to change identities a few times, but he doesn't mind giving them up anymore. Currently, he is entirely off the grid after returning home to the USA after a long time in South Africa, considering what to do next.<br /> Doc Slauenwitte does, however, still keep a diary under his real name, writing down all his deeds. Keeping a record, to be released at some point. Maybe this is his route to Inheritance?<br /> <br /> <b>Horror</b>: A Huge Cloud of Flies<br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Plague Bearer, Infestation, Shadowed Soul, Mimir's Wisdom, From the Shadows, Needs Must, Weakness Exposed<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: Everything you know is a Lie, You Were Never Right, This is Due Tomorrow, Bugs Everywhere!<br /> <b>Lair</b>: An African Jungle<br /> <b>Traits</b>: Extreme Heat, Undergrowth, Toxic, Engulfing, Diseased(, Maze, Slick)<br /> <b>Merits</b>: Among others - Killer Instinct (Epic), Alternate Identity (3), Anonymity (3), Direction Sense (Advanced), Eidetic Memory (advanced), Encycopedic Knowledge (Africa), Multilingual (Xhosa, Afrikaans), Epic Potential (Intelligence), Patient, Good Time Management, Resources (3), Trained Observer (3)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T04:21:41-07:00","id":1215442,"title":"","content":"Doublepost, sorry, but I feel the time difference justifies adding a new post.<br /> <br /> <br /> Margareth Baker, Eshmaki Nemesis<br /> <br /> Maggie is a very unassuming person, apparently average in every regard. She's the girl teachers are barely aware of that she's part of that class, the one the parents always forget to talk about because they feel there is nothing to talk about. Not isolated enough to draw attention, not outstanding in any way - perfectly average. And so, almost invisible.<br /> In truth, this is her cover, and weapon. Bad boys are always the first people consider to be responsible, and sometimes those in the spotlight are accused of being to perfect (or hiding some secret), but no one would even remember her enough to accuse her.<br /> Which is good, because otherwise people would notice the pattern behind the strange cases of what the school likes to term 'cases of food poisonings and drug abuse'.<br /> The truth is simple: you take part in any sort of mobbing (and not opposing it IS letting it happen and thus deemed punishable by Maggie's Horror), and you get the Hodag's poison-dripped talons. And you'll never be the wiser.<br /> Maggie feels pretty good about herself. She is, after all, making the world a better place.<br /> <br /> Horror: Hodag<br /> Atavisms: Basilisk's Touch, From the Shadows<br /> Nightmares: You Deserve This, You Are Worthless, This Is Due Tomorrow<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T08:39:15-07:00","id":1219975,"title":"","content":"I'm having trouble figuring out starting atavisms for an Anakim I want to create who's Horror is a swarm of super-adaptive nanobots. The fear he's supposed to represent is that even if he can't beat you the first time, he'll always be back, adapted to beat any strategy you've tried before, making him unbeatable in the long run. Stuff like Infestation and Weakness Exposed is good, but I can't think of Anakim Atavisms that fit. Mimir's Wisdom might work, but I'm not sure if knowing lies automatically works with the concept. Any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T09:24:13-07:00","id":1219988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1219975#post1219975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having trouble figuring out starting atavisms for an Anakim I want to create who's Horror is a swarm of super-adaptive nanobots. The fear he's supposed to represent is that even if he can't beat you the first time, he'll always be back, adapted to beat any strategy you've tried before, making him unbeatable in the long run. Stuff like Infestation and Weakness Exposed is good, but I can't think of Anakim Atavisms that fit. Mimir's Wisdom might work, but I'm not sure if knowing lies automatically works with the concept. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see Mimir's Wisdom working well, honestly. The benefits it provide resonate with the idea of an adaptive swarm of nanobots and lies often do come with a number of microscopic tells and changes in the liar's attitude that the supernatural nightmare of a cloud of hyper-technological sentient grey goo able to adapt to each situation has good reasons to spot. The conceptual space is there.<br /> <br /> In alternative, I suggest Vengeful Earth. Make some giant limbs/structures with those nanobots and smash stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T09:54:07-07:00","id":1220000,"title":"","content":"I guess I could replace the earthquake tilt with some sort of unstable footing from carpet of moving, sharp nanobots tilt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:03:35-07:00","id":1220004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1220000#post1220000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I could replace the earthquake tilt with some sort of unstable footing from carpet of moving, sharp nanobots tilt</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it's a good call. Keeping with Major Lair Traits, and depending on the kind of nanobots you have in mind, Corrosive, Engulfing, Razored and Viscous are those that come to my mind. Electrified too, but it's weirder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:09:20-07:00","id":1220008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1220004#post1220004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, it's a good call. Keeping with Major Lair Traits, and depending on the kind of nanobots you have in mind, Corrosive, Engulfing, Razored and Viscous are those that come to my mind. Electrified too, but it's weirder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially Mirages too, if you want to go the colour-changing, deceptive route. Which could potentially justify Enemy Within or From The Shadows for Atavisms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:19:44-07:00","id":1220011,"title":"","content":"I meant more the part where Vengeful Earth lets you create earthquakes at low Satiety. Haven't even thought about the Lair","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:27:58-07:00","id":1220014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1220011#post1220011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant more the part where Vengeful Earth lets you create earthquakes at low Satiety. Haven't even thought about the Lair</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was referring to that too. Reflavoring Earthquake and keeping the mechanics as they are is perfectly fine (perhaps while ignoring the part about falling debris or replacing it with sharp nanobots as you said). But in case you want to tinker with it a bit and apply other Tilts that might work better with your concept, those are the ones I think would not be hard to motivate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 05-18-2018, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T17:18:35-07:00","id":1221312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1078263#post1078263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Countess Amber:</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I might revisit this character idea when I get my hands on the player's guide.<br /> <br /> I understand it goes into detail about Beasts using magic? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T17:28:03-07:00","id":1221319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1221312#post1221312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I might revisit this character idea when I get my hands on the player's guide.<br /> <br /> I understand it goes into detail about Beasts using magic? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Obcasus Rites! They\u2019re delightful additions to a Beast\u2019s repertoire of supernatural tricks. <br /> <br /> And looking at her, she looks like she could be a Talassii instead of Makara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T19:59:23-07:00","id":1221358,"title":"","content":"The new Mean Girls musical's soundtrack has me wanting to stat up Regina George as a Beast...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Amv8T27SqCw\" data-code=\"Amv8T27SqCw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Amv8T27SqCw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I'm thinking feline Ereshmaki Tyrant...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T22:17:52-07:00","id":1221386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1221319#post1221319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obcasus Rites! They\u2019re delightful additions to a Beast\u2019s repertoire of supernatural tricks.<br /> <br /> And looking at her, she looks like she could be a Talassii instead of Makara.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Either that or make her an Inguma. Being an outsider would explain her kinship with those touched by the Fey.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> Huh... they sound a lot like Hex Girls from that one Scooby Do movie.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I now think Ghoul School would make for an excellent shard setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-23-2018, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T22:55:16-07:00","id":1221391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1221386#post1221386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Either that or make her an Inguma. Being an outsider would explain her kinship with those touched by the Fey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Countess\u2019 Horror resembles a huldra then? Nothing says \u201cthought she looked normal, but not!\u201d like revealing her back to be a hollowed out tree trunk. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\