the Web for more hair usage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:27:17-07:00","id":1223193,"title":"","content":"Anybody seen Kakegurui? The student council president looks like a Mental/Social focused Anakim Tyrant. Against her, the protagonist herself looks like an Inguma Ravager. The student council may be its president\u2019s Kin or brood. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> And all the Hundred Devouring Familes\u2019 members would be Beasts, including the protagonist. <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T17:41:58-07:00","id":1223779,"title":"","content":"I love that anime <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T08:17:38-07:00","id":1236415,"title":"","content":"Just to once again show how much damage even a Begotten fresh out of Character creation can cause:<br /> <br /> Rockie<br /> Family: Namtaru<br /> Hunger: Ruin<br /> Concept: Vandalizing Anarchistic Punk<br /> Lair Traits: Tornado, Unstable<br /> Atavisms: Storm-Lashed, Plague Bearer<br /> Nightmares: Your Rage Consumes You, Fear is Contagious<br /> Lesson: Society is just a flimsy cover - you are no better than your neolithic ancestors<br /> Life: Rebellious<br /> Legend: Vicious<br /> <br /> Rockie is a prick, and becoming a Begotten didn't make it any better. High on a power trip, disregarding of any semblance of order, he just does whatever he feels like.<br /> He loves showing people how they are no more than (arguably) smart animals by causing riots or making them worse, drinking up the fear of people realizing not the cops nor the law keeps them safe.<br /> However, his latest idea is more of a threat than any before: He plans on gorging himself, then expending all that fear into violent Tornadoes he sends into various directions, followed by massive plagues. The meals from that he plans to invest into violent riots to kick-off a &quot;us vs. them&quot; mentality.<br /> In essence, his goal is to tear down a city - all that fear should do the trick of Incarnating, right?<br /> Imagine his surprise when he will be beset from all sides by Siblings, Cousins, Hunters and Heroes for his activities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fun thing: with this setup, he has a reasonable chance of causing immense damage. Expending Satiety on creating a Tornado with Storm-Lashed, using that to also invoke Unstable to better crumble down buildings, then follow up with riots and plagues is a nightmare come true for all residents of the area, mortals and supernaturals alike.<br /> If he had 3 Broodmates (not too unusual a size for a player brood) with Titanic Blow, Heart of the Ocean and something like Dragonfire, and maybe Lair traits like Exposed, Burning, Decayed, Slick, Thin Air, and Thunderous, they could really tear down whole blocks of areas like New York - with no warning at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T07:21:58-07:00","id":1236761,"title":"","content":"arguably) smart animals That\u2019s exactly right humans are animals, that have a certain type,of intelligence that had them take over the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T09:28:47-07:00","id":1237174,"title":"","content":"Can anyone make Gamzee MAKARA as a beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T10:45:11-07:00","id":1237194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1237174#post1237174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone make Gamzee MAKARA as a beast?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you could make him","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T05:09:30-07:00","id":1237730,"title":"","content":"<b><u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Garret Blyushtein</span></span></span></u></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Legend: </b>Relentless. If Garret wants something, he is going to come for it, and nothing's gonna stop him.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Life:</b> Improvisational. Garret doesn't plan so much as act and react. He feels most at ease when he can just go with the flow, rather than follow a plan.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Family: </span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Eshmaki</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Hunger:</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hoard</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Horror:</b> </span></span></span>Scaly fox made from Shadows<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Lair</b>: Overstuffed Attic<br /> <b>Lair Traits</b>: Hoard, Fog, Maze, Murmurs, Cramped<br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Death of Light, Illusion of Safety, Shadowed Soul, From the Shadows, Ravenous Maw<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: Tabula Rasa, You Cannot Wake up, You cannot Rest, You Cannot move, You are not alone,<br /> <b>Merits</b>: Walk Lightly, Sleight of Hand, Fast Reflexes, Fleet of Food 3, Ressources 4, Parkour 5, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1234269-the-merits-of-speed-a-handful-of-new-advanced-merits#post1234269\">Confounding Sleight, Insuppressible Parkour, Light Footed, Lightning Reflexes, Scurry, Without Trace</a>, Fighting Finesse (knives), Killing Instinct, Advanced Killing Instinct, Language (Russian)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Garret is a master thief - not just out of passion, but a professional one. You want something stolen from (or placed at) a place? He's the guy. Unlike his contractors, he doesn't care about the financial value, but the emotional one: an old clock that belonged to someone's great grand-father, the young girl's first place diploma in some sports competition, a winning lottery ticket, the wedding ring of their late spouse. Even their supernatural cousins are not safe from him, though: a Created's Azothic Object, another Created's self-made pottery, a Defiant's lab log, a werewolf's last memento of his time before the Change (a basketball tricot), he even went so far as to steal from a Mummy, and managed to keep it.<br /> Having made friends with a Krewe as well as several Ghosts (getting people the heirloom back they need to pass on makes him a great help), he has a someone to make up for whatever he lacks in and a Family to rely on.<br /> Garret is very anti-confrontational and prefers to not be caught if he cannot manage to not be seen at all. He deals with Heroes in a comparatively unique way, therefore - he simply runs away, lures them into a Chamber, and leaves through the Underworld. All he has to do is lose them there or wait for his friends to get them.<br /> This does not mean he isn't dangerous in a fight at all, though: when it comes down to it, he relies on his nimble build and preciseness to cripple his enemy and leave them for dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T18:13:57-07:00","id":1238735,"title":"","content":"I just had an epiphany:<br /> <br /> The dog from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ugjWK82oWTo\" target=\"_blank\">Sandlot</a> is a Talassi Collector!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T02:50:22-07:00","id":1239232,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Why are you screaming? It's just like before isn't it? Then again...you're not in control this time around.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Name: Unknown, but a very lucky few know them by the name of Pan'sWrath.<br /> <br /> Family: Talassii<br /> <br /> Hunger: Punishment<br /> <br /> Concept: Satyr flavored <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_Candy_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Hard Candy</a><br /> <br /> Lair Traits: Darkness, Undergrowth<br /> <br /> Atavisms: Caught in the Webs, Enemy Within<br /> <br /> Nightmares: You Deserve This, They are All Around You<br /> <br /> Life: Methodical<br /> <br /> Legend: Vengeance<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Among forums for victims of sexual assault, there's a rumor. If you mention anywhere on the site that your attacker won't be going to jail, you may find yourself getting a PM from someone with a blank username with a ram's skull for their avatar.<br /> <br /> If you can offer a picture of yourself, details about the attack and 20 dollars, they promise to make your attacker suffer.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Perhaps they were victimized in the past, or perhaps they could do nothing but watch as a loved one was blamed for the vile act as the attacker walked away with their hands clean. While the beginning is shrouded in mystery, the Talassi known as Panswrath is a Nemesis with a desire for a certain kind of victim.<br /> <br /> Pan targets rapists and other sexual offenders, focusing on those who get away with their crimes. Their punishments are elaborate and methodical. Using the details supplied by the victim, Pan recreates the scenery where the attack happened within their Lair and drags the offender into the Lair.<br /> <br /> There, Pan brutally picks apart the offender's mind by talking about the attack and its aftermath, all from the victim's point of view. Through the use of their Atavisms and Nightmares, Pan forces the offender to face the victim and their crimes once more.<br /> <br /> The screaming is oh so satisfying, but even more satisfying is the relief from the victims after the offender has been punished. Pan will admit though, that their favorite cases ended with the offender killing themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23824-adorablechou","name":"AdorableChou","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T06:58:12-07:00","id":1239289,"title":"","content":"<b><u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Summer's Son</span></span></span></u></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Legend: </b>Relentless</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Life:</b> Caring</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Family: </span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ugallu</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Hunger:</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ravager</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Horror:</b> Phoenix </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Lair</b>: Stone Plateau similar to Uluru within a white desert<br /> <b>Lair Traits</b>: Extreme Heat, Exposed, Blazing Light, Engulfing, Disruption, Blizzard (Sandstorm)<br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Storm-Lashed, Dragonfire, Eye of Heaven, Wings of the Raptor, Relentless Hunter, Weakness Exposed<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: All your Teeth are Falling out, Your Tools betray you, You are lost, You are better than them<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Sometimes, we are too weak to let go of those things that harm us. But when you have to start over from scratch, it is easy to focus on the things that are truly important. Let me help you see what's truly important.&quot;</i><br /> The Summer's Son is a Begotten that wants to teach those with too many things going on to refocus. He does so by taking everything away, from their car, to their house, to their friends and job. When they are left with nothing but their body, mind and soul, they are free to reinvent themselves, and grow stronger for it - if they have what it takes.<br /> He got his name from the fact that he goes on a rampage during the summer, and often slumbers through winter.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T13:05:31-07:00","id":1252581,"title":"","content":"<b>All Mighty Skalgarox:</b> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You know, it's probably not a good idea to pick a fight with a being who has aspirations of killing God.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> A combination of nihilism, self loathing, and religious indoctrination lead to the creation of the being who now calls itself 'All Mighty Skalgarox.' Like most children in the recent decades, Skalgarox was the subject of too much love and support from those in charge of raising him. He took it to heart when people told him that his life had infinite possibilities ahead of him, or that good things come to those who wait, or that evil always gets its just rewards. In fact, he was so assured that life would turn out well for him, that he started to procrastinate growing up and assuming responsibility for his life. He started living at home with his parents, avoided getting a job because the world was going to end in 2012.<br /> <br /> And then reality kicked down his walls of his childhood fantasies, and he was made cruelly aware of how dark and terrible the world truly was. The people who took care of him all these years were reaching the age where the roles started to reverse, his friends had moved on to places unknown and he couldn't remember any of their contact information to keep in touch with them. He never made up his mind about what he wanted to be with his life, and finding a job in today's economy was one of the most degrading experiences of his life. Everything that made him happy was crumbling away, leaving him with nothing but regretful memories and bitter resentment towards life.<br /> <br /> Skalgarox did not take this revelation very well, and his mind shattered to a state that could only maintain clarity for fleeting moments at a time before slipping back into blissful denial in an attempt to keep from going completely off the edge. But in those moments, he realized just how deeply he hated everything. Not just bad moments in his life, but literally everything. The entire state of reality itself was revolting to him, and he longed for a way in which to change it to better suit his own perception of how it should be.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify, All Mighty Skalgarox is a Talassi Tyrant who seeks to subvert God itself, by obtaining total omnipotence over the universe. But since the very definition of omnipotence is a contradiction of itself, that means his goal is impossible to achieve, thereby leaving Skalgarox with an insatiable appetite for power.<br /> <br /> <b>Moment:</b> Void<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Power<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A roiling mass of amorphous flesh that produces and dissolves body parts at completely random intervals. It's outer skin has the same blackness of concentrated dark matter, while it's inner flesh sparkles with the light of an miniature galaxy. It has no discernible gender and seems to flow between male and female appendages with no rhyme or reason for any of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Honest<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Vicious<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> All Mighty Skalgarox is obsessed with obtaining additional power, no matter what form it happens to take. Those wishing to garner his support may be able to bribe him with rewards that appeal to this obsession.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T22:55:18-07:00","id":1252675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1252581#post1252581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>All Mighty Skalgarox:</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;You know, it's probably not a good idea to pick a fight with a being who has aspirations of killing God.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> A combination of nihilism, self loathing, and religious indoctrination lead to the creation of the being who now calls itself 'All Mighty Skalgarox.' Like most children in the recent decades, Skalgarox was the subject of too much love and support from those in charge of raising him. He took it to heart when people told him that his life had infinite possibilities ahead of him, or that good things come to those who wait, or that evil always gets its just rewards. In fact, he was so assured that life would turn out well for him, that he started to procrastinate growing up and assuming responsibility for his life. He started living at home with his parents, avoided getting a job because the world was going to end in 2012.<br /> <br /> And then reality kicked down his walls of his childhood fantasies, and he was made cruelly aware of how dark and terrible the world truly was. The people who took care of him all these years were reaching the age where the roles started to reverse, his friends had moved on to places unknown and he couldn't remember any of their contact information to keep in touch with them. He never made up his mind about what he wanted to be with his life, and finding a job in today's economy was one of the most degrading experiences of his life. Everything that made him happy was crumbling away, leaving him with nothing but regretful memories and bitter resentment towards life.<br /> <br /> Skalgarox did not take this revelation very well, and his mind shattered to a state that could only maintain clarity for fleeting moments at a time before slipping back into blissful denial in an attempt to keep from going completely off the edge. But in those moments, he realized just how deeply he hated everything. Not just bad moments in his life, but literally everything. The entire state of reality itself was revolting to him, and he longed for a way in which to change it to better suit his own perception of how it should be.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify, All Mighty Skalgarox is a Talassi Tyrant who seeks to subvert God itself, by obtaining total omnipotence over the universe. But since the very definition of omnipotence is a contradiction of itself, that means his goal is impossible to achieve, thereby leaving Skalgarox with an insatiable appetite for power.<br /> <br /> <b>Moment:</b> Void<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Power<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> A roiling mass of amorphous flesh that produces and dissolves body parts at completely random intervals. It's outer skin has the same blackness of concentrated dark matter, while it's inner flesh sparkles with the light of an miniature galaxy. It has no discernible gender and seems to flow between male and female appendages with no rhyme or reason for any of it.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Honest<br /> <br /> <b>Legend:</b> Vicious<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> All Mighty Skalgarox is obsessed with obtaining additional power, no matter what form it happens to take. Those wishing to garner his support may be able to bribe him with rewards that appeal to this obsession.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, he sounds like he'd be a good Insatiable. Void, I'd guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T04:23:23-07:00","id":1252716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1252675#post1252675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, he sounds like he'd be a good Insatiable. Void, I'd guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's kind of what I made him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T05:58:07-07:00","id":1252731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1252716#post1252716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That's kind of what I made him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Darn, my eyes or mind failed me there, I read 'ANAKIM' &gt;.&lt;<br /> Well, hey, at least now you know the write-up and classification totally add up ^^&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T10:05:37-07:00","id":1252789,"title":"","content":"Why did you call him a Talasii Tyrant then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T22:30:50-07:00","id":1252962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1252789#post1252789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you call him a Talasii Tyrant then?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I lack the player's guide, I grabbed information about the Insatiable from the wiki.<br /> <br /> <br /> In addition to listing what &quot;moment&quot; they represent, it also describes them based on Family and Hunger, so I thought that was normal.<br /> <br /> <br /> But if you're asking about why he's a Talassi specifically, I envisioned his prison as being the universe itself. His horror could even be described as a sentient universe, consisting of a black, shapeless void, with a galaxy contained inside of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T16:34:53-07:00","id":1253739,"title":"","content":"<b>The Windego:</b><br /> <br /> An air of mystery surrounds the monster known simply as The Windego. It is so ancient, that even the Begotten aren't sure whether the creature is somehow immortal, or if there have been multiple individuals who don the mantle of The Windego throughout the generations. Whatever the case may be, the origin of this particular monster is a fairly well known story. It was once a human who indulged in the taboo of cannibalism, inviting a cursed spirit to possess their body forever more.<br /> <br /> For the sin of eating its own kind, The Windego is cursed with an insatiable appetite for human flesh. No matter how many people they consume, they always feel ravenous, which has driven The Windego quite mad with hunger. They will attack humans on sight, often devouring them alive if they don't succumb to their injuries first. Thankfully, cannibalism is extremely rare, and those who do participate in it usually have little choice in the matter. The most traditional explanation is that they were starving and desperate while traveling through harsh, arctic environments.<br /> <br /> Schisms produced by The Windego cause those affected to develop a fear of starving to death. They may begin to stock pile as much food as they can get their hands on, and will defend it to the death if anybody tries to take it away from them. As food supplies begin to diminish, their hunger takes a darker aspect, turning their attention towards other people. First starting with their enemies, and gradually advancing towards their friends and family. By the time the Schism has fully taken hold, their victims are slaughtering each other in a desperate attempt to feed themselves for another day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Moment:</b> Frozen Hell<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Horror:</b> An enormous, anthropomorphic stag that towers at a height of nearly 12 feet tall. It's body is hideously emaciated and appears as though it has not eaten anything in months. Yet, despite its malnourished condition, it appears to have little trouble remaining physically active. Unlike most deer, it has no fur, instead displaying skin that is as pale and white as the snow itself. It's hand-like appendages end in wicked, black claws that can cleave through flesh like a butcher's tools. It's voice carries the horrific tone of a deer's cry, which is sure to deeply unnerve anyone close enough to hear it.<br /> <br /> <b>Life:</b> Shy<br /> <br /> <b>Legend</b>: Vicious<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vmlN5W6CWs8\" target=\"_blank\">Scream of the Windego</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-21-2018, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T10:14:09-07:00","id":1253943,"title":"","content":"Is that a valid spelling? For some reason I'm thinking they are from Minnesota.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T11:26:53-07:00","id":1253965,"title":"","content":"It's an Algonquian word so spelling can vary. Most common are wendigo and windigo. Minnesota is just a small part of the region where the original folklore was spread. (I say original because, to my knowledge, the whole stag imagery in Nyrufa's example stems from portrayals in modern media.) Basically the entire eastern half of Canada had some variations of the legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T22:11:49-07:00","id":1256011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1221391#post1221391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Heh, thought nobody else knew that movie <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Once they started making movies <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GkNask_pMKo\" target=\"_blank\">with real monsters in them</a>, I developed a renewed interest in the series. Having them unmask criminals every episode was getting kind of stale. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T20:20:13-07:00","id":1257067,"title":"","content":"Know who I just realized is a beast in the CofD? Michael Avennatti, specifically he is an ugallu nemesis punishing the powerful and corrupt by exposing their sins and ripping them to shreds on behalf of his clients","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T19:07:10-08:00","id":1267766,"title":"","content":"Well, I finally ordered the player's guide for my birthday. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And like every year, it will probably arrive either just in the nick of time, or nearly a week late. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.newgrounds.com/portal/view/406010\" target=\"_blank\">Old Willie Winkie:</a><br /> <br /> Old Willie Winkie, he's outside your door.<br /> <br /> He climbed up the stairs and cracked along the floor.<br /> <br /> In he comes quickly, knives shining bright.<br /> <br /> He's a collector of tongues, and it's your lucky night!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T22:05:38-08:00","id":1270004,"title":"","content":"&quot;SphinXxX&quot;, Ugallu Tyrant<br /> <br /> &quot;Amazing. Every word of what you just said was wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> Samuel - outside work, he usually goes by his screen name &quot;SphinXxX&quot; these days - was always a gifted child. Shy, bookish, and imaginative, he excelled in school from an early age. He didn't spend much time with the other children, preferring to lose himself in fiction, but as far as his parents were concerned that was to be expected. Though they did wish he'd stop reading before bed and giving himself nightmares.<br /> <br /> It was actually always the same nightmare, though it faded quickly upon waking each time: a great sphinx, stalking him, taunting him with questions and riddles. And when he inevitably failed to answer correctly she would lunge for him, claws outstretched, and he would wake screaming. Between his parents' high hopes for his future, his teachers' expectations of greatness, and the terrifying half-remembered dreams, he became very studious, fearful of letting others down or &quot;looking stupid&quot;.<br /> <br /> Adolescence soured his temperament, sadly. Having never really made friends in his peer group, he felt like an outsider, and his resentment of that fact turned to open contempt. He couched this contempt in the idea that they were intellectually beneath him, and made no secret of that opinion. They, in turn, shunned him further for being so arrogant and unpleasant. This pattern persisted and deepened during college; his professors came to appreciate his dedication to the coursework, but his sneering, argumentative demeanor did not endear him to any of them. When an academic advisor &quot;gently suggested&quot; he'd be a better fit for academia (preferably at some other institution) than a traditional career, he just took that as a final affirmation of his greatness. And that night was when the Horror struck for the final time and taught him what he really was.<br /> <br /> These days, he's a grad student. When he's not in the lab or teaching students (whom he hates), he spends most of his time arguing online and offline about his hobbies (tabletop RPGs being a big one), science, politics, and anything else he considers himself well-informed about (which is everything.) It doesn't really have anything to do with the subject in question, or about actually being right (though he's always able to convince himself he is): deep down he just needs to feel like the smartest person in the room, and making someone else look stupid for an audience is the most direct way he knows. If he can really break someone down in-person...that's when his Horror feasts.<br /> <br /> His brood mates, unsurprisingly, spend little time with him when they don't need to.<br /> <br /> Legend: Prideful. Samuel has a high opinion of himself and expects others to comport themselves accordingly. He has a hard time letting any disagreement or perceived slight go, and often doesn't know when to keep his mouth shut - because who wouldn't want his expertise?<br /> <br /> Life: Self-reliant. While it's been twisted a bit by his Horror, Samuel was independent and most comfortable left to his own devices from early on, and that has stuck with him.<br /> <br /> Horror: Sphinx<br /> <br /> Lair: A twisting maze of desert crags, lined with broken columns and collapsed tombs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 11-23-2018, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T14:56:05-08:00","id":1270203,"title":"","content":"Uhh. I was Reading the Mage Tarot Book and I Thought if someone could make a Beast Character from some Tarot cards. Here\u2019s what I drew.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/reblog/180424890371/sTVFCqkj?redirect_to=%2Fdashboard\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.tumblr.com/reblog/180424...o=%2Fdashboard</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://konradleijon.tumblr.com/post/180424890371\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/c29ee5eaf78d33ac9629dfbbbc933ed0/tumblr_pio4z15nEJ1vdq7ux_640.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://konradleijon.tumblr.com/post/180424890371\" target=\"_blank\"> Post by @konradleijon &middot; 2 images </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://konradleijon.tumblr.com/post/180424890371\" target=\"_blank\"> https://konradleijon.tumblr.com/post/180424890371 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \ud83d\udcac 0&nbsp;&nbsp;\ud83d\udd01 0&nbsp;&nbsp;\u2764\ufe0f 0 </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The first card represents there Mortal Life.<br /> The Three of Swords means Selfishness,heartbreak aand feeling like someone put A SHARP Daggered Sword in your Heart. <br /> <br /> Means she lived in a small town with a not so stable father <br /> <br /> before suffering a A cut to the Heart .after the Betrayal of Her father once he had enough off Her \u2018Odd\u2019 habits speading all her time by the lake. \u2018Playing\u2019 with the School bullies by holding themselves underwater for three minutes at a time.<br /> <br /> Blaming it on her mother and then ending her in the bathtub. After that her Psyche broke Blaming Herself for her fathers Misdeed she Broke and Got Minor hydrophobia feeling horrid Guilt from just when a Schoolmate drank from a Water fountain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 11-23-2018, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T16:24:17-08:00","id":1270218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1267766#post1267766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I finally ordered the player's guide for my birthday. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And like every year, it will probably arrive either just in the nick of time, or nearly a week late. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.newgrounds.com/portal/view/406010&amp;quot;]Old</a> Willie Winkie:[/URL]<br /> <br /> Old Willie Winkie, he's outside your door.<br /> <br /> He climbed up the stairs and cracked along the floor.<br /> <br /> In he comes quickly, knives shining bright.<br /> <br /> He's a collector of tongues, and it's your lucky night!</div> </div> </div> </div>you won't regret it either way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T08:41:53-08:00","id":1272974,"title":"","content":"My Player's Guide just now arrived! <br /> <br /> Probably gonna have more character ideas, once I've had time to read through it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T22:06:11-08:00","id":1274140,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Keiko, Talassii Predator</u></b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Don't say it. I swear, I'll end you if you say it.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Keiko was fascinated with the supernatural long before her Devouring. As a child, she spent many happy hours with her grandmother, absorbing the myths and childrens' tales the family matriarch had brought over from the old country after the bombs fell. Every night after hearing these stories, her dreams swept her away to an imagined version of that land, where she would roam alongside the yokai of legend. She loved those dreams, those hours spent in her personal storybook world.<br /> <br /> And yet somehow, despite all that noble and ancient mythology, the beast within her turned out to be a fucking tentacle monster.<br /> <br /> Given her Family's curse and her background, it really wasn't what she had hoped for. And she <i>absolutely</i> does not want to hear another joke about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T13:59:27-08:00","id":1275885,"title":"","content":"&quot;Cynn&quot;, Makara Enabler<br /> <br /> It's hard not to like Cynn. No, really, it's one of her Atavisms, and it serves her well. Cynn is a gentle Beast, and her hunts aren't painful or bloody - unless you're into that.<br /> <br /> Cynn's particular targets are the repressed or moralistic, and she thrills in tempting them into fulfilling their suppressed sexual desires (which may or may not involve her). She never violates consent, never does anything to her target they don't ask for: she has moral standards, after all. Still, she's not subtle about spelling out her Lesson that desire is nothing to be ashamed of, and as far as she's concerned any guilt you feel afterward is just part of that learning process.<br /> <br /> Her manner of feeding seems to attract more than her share of Heroes and their followers, a fact her less-benign broodmates find darkly ironic. There's no shortage of people out there who react with outrage to &quot;sexual immorality&quot; (the scare quotes are audible when she says this). But as she mockingly said to the last Hero who hunted her, just before the kill: 'love' conquers all.<br /> <br /> Horror: Mermaid.<br /> Lair: A sunny tropical lagoon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T06:11:29-08:00","id":1276038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1275885#post1275885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Cynn&quot;, Makara Enabler<br /> <br /> It's hard not to like Cynn. No, really, it's one of her Atavisms, and it serves her well. Cynn is a gentle Beast, and her hunts aren't painful or bloody - unless you're into that.<br /> <br /> Cynn's particular targets are the repressed or moralistic, and she thrills in tempting them into fulfilling their suppressed sexual desires (which may or may not involve her). She never violates consent, never does anything to her target they don't ask for: she has moral standards, after all. Still, she's not subtle about spelling out her Lesson that desire is nothing to be ashamed of, and as far as she's concerned any guilt you feel afterward is just part of that learning process.<br /> <br /> Her manner of feeding seems to attract more than her share of Heroes and their followers, a fact her less-benign broodmates find darkly ironic. There's no shortage of people out there who react with outrage to &quot;sexual immorality&quot; (the scare quotes are audible when she says this). But as she mockingly said to the last Hero who hunted her, just before the kill: 'love' conquers all.<br /> <br /> Horror: Mermaid.<br /> Lair: A sunny tropical lagoon.</div> </div> </div> </div>From that description, I'm imagining something like this: <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://images.fineartamerica.com/images-medium-large-5/mermaid-rescue-rob-carlos.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, does she and her Brood use her Lair as a getaway spot sometimes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T06:32:34-08:00","id":1276040,"title":"","content":"Now I want to see a Beast (or Brood) that uses their Lair as a &quot;Haunted&quot; House or carnival of fear. Not, that's-what-their-Lairs-are, but rather <i>monetizing</i> their Lairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T07:13:52-08:00","id":1276042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=1276038#post1276038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From that description, I'm imagining something like this: <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://images.fineartamerica.com/images-medium-large-5/mermaid-rescue-rob-carlos.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, does she and her Brood use her Lair as a getaway spot sometimes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine so, yeah! A Lair that can be enjoyed on its own terms meshes nicely with Cynn's overall outlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T22:15:07-08:00","id":1277770,"title":"","content":"<b>Dawson - Talassi Predator: </b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;A life for a life, this is how the balance is maintained.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> If you hear the word 'druid' and immediately think 'nature loving hippy' then you clearly don't know a thing about Celtic mythology. Dawson wasn't very knowledgeable about it either, not until the day of his devouring. When he came face to face with the Horned God who hunted him through the forests every night, like he was some kind of wild stag. When he turned to face his huntsman and felt the barbed arrows pierce his flesh, tearing him to pieces with each shot. He thought that was the end of it, his body too heavily wounded that he would not survive his injuries. But when the hunter tore out his heart and consumed it in two bites, his perceptions snapped over to his would be killer. Dawson had now become the hunter, and in that moment, he finally understood what it meant to consume another creature. To steal another's essence and make it your own, to extinguish another's life force to sustain yours for one more day!<br /> <br /> Dawson became obsessed with the Obcasus Rites after that, throwing himself head first into their study. The rituals he learned were merciless, barbaric practices involving the use of living sacrifices. But it was never about wanton murder for Dawson, it was about the cycle of life and death. Maintaining the delicate balance of creation and destruction. Many people do not comprehend the fundamental truth that he seeks to impart upon them. Those people often find themselves lost in the forest, having been targeted for Dawson's next hunt!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T15:05:38-07:00","id":1296520,"title":"","content":"So, something a bit different.<br /> <br /> <br /> People assume that a Begotten's Devouring is akin to their first brush with the supernatural elements of the world. But that is not the truth \u2013 not every Beast comes into their own in a supernatural vacuum, many have had brushes with the things that go bump in the night as humans, and quite a few get more than a passing glance. These experiences inform their outlook as Beasts, often influencing their choice of kinship, their allies and contacts... and occasionally, their prey.<br /> Meet the <b>Nightstalkers </b>Brood: a group of former ghouls who take their revenge against all things Kindred by Feeding on them.<br /> <br /> Christian Zimmermann has come all the way from Berlin to New York City in pursuit of his former tormentor's sire. When he was just a young man, Christian was enslaved by a particularly cruel Mekhet called Friedrich during the rebuilding that was the 50's who took an interest in him when he proved a capable paramedic. After decades of abuse, including a forceful state of Vitae deprivation to age him up for new jobs, Christian was just a bipolar conglomerate of complexes \u2013 until his Devouring. He was stripped to his core in a dark cave, running from a chiropterean Horror in the skies, until he couldn't run anymore; a new Christian awoke that morning. Guided by the Dark Mother's hand, the clarity of his new situation helped him realize what needed to be done, and he tore apart the organization he'd been forced to support: he freed herds, he took out important middlemen, he passed on dangerous information to enemies, he blackmailed and sabotaged. Friedrich and his ilk watched on in terror as the cozy little system they'd built for themselves was crumbling, leaving them open to enemies they'd long considered defanged, and finally, Christian cut of the head, and the Big Bad Bat feasted on their frantic panic. The 30-ish looking old-timer thought it'd be wisest to leave Berlin, after all he'd just unbalanced the careful equilibrium of the dans\u00e9. Armed with a lifetime's worth of experiences in dealing with Kindred, insight into their nature and behaviour, strengths and weaknesses, new supernatural powers outside their experience and an intense hatred for them, he decided to make them his primary food source. The Big Bad Bat was happy enough, since such powerful groups provided a more than decent meal, and Christian was able to feed on them as they did on mortals to extend his life and keep his acquired abilities. He struck terror into Germany's Kindred, teaching them that all their fancy abilities and societies and powers left them no more save than a mortal when the Bat came calling.<br /> Finally, Christian found informations on a Kindred in New York that had supposedly sired Friedrich in the 1910's. There, he met Ivan, and they started the Brood that would grow into the Nighstalkers.<br /> <b>Ugallu Ravager</b><br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Eye of Heaven, Needs Must, Mimir's Wisdom, Weakness Exposed, Storm-Lashed, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, Wings of the Raptor, Alien Mindset, Siren's Treacherous Song.<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: You Don't Have A Face, You Cannot Run, You Cannot Wake Up, You Can Never Rest, This Is Due Tomorrow, Behold My True Form!<br /> <b>Lair</b>: 8 (A dark cave that echoes terribly loud, the floor covered with crunchy smelly bones)<br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Poor Light, Unstable, Stench, Isolated, Crosswinds, Thunderous<br /> <b>Disciplines</b>: Obfuscate 3, Celerity 2<br /> <b>Notable Merits</b>: Sanguivore, Taste of Shadow, Weakened Bond, Advanced Danger Sense, Indomitable, Advanced Killer Instinct 3, Trained Observer 3, Bowmanship 3, Combat Archery 3, Marksmanship 4<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Originally, I considered going full-on Sunlight Phoenix to keep the anti-Kindred theme going and create a 'stronger' vampire hunter with Lair Traits like blazing light, but decided that a vampiric vampire hunter seemed like a more interesting idea for an actual character concept and way more topical. He's more the social actor, but when it comes to fighting, he is more of a long-range supporter and makes a rather fine marksman. He also loves using the bow and arrow, and for the extra shock against kindred, uses burning arrows. Nothing to destroy teamwork like Frenzy. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The man who now calls himself Ivan Gazmanov was the Ghoul equivalent of a fighting dog. A prize-winning fighting dog. Ivan knew nothing other than grueling fights, brutal training, and the rare moments of bliss when he was 'gifted' with Vitae. He hated what he'd become, a helpless addict, less than an animal, a tool to be used for entertainment, and thus avoided thinking about it whenever possible. Ivan had long since stopped counting days, nights, fights \u2013 he hadn't the slightest of how long this had been going on, and he didn't particularly care to know. When he wasn't training or fighting, he sought escape in drunken delirium. Some time in the late 90's, the Troll found him. And the Troll wouldn't let him have even that escape, haunting his dreams for weeks to the point he refused to sleep, taking the beatings in the fight due to poor performance, and even the punishments of his master Dorian, rather than facing the Troll again.<br /> Eventually, sleep won, and Ivan was Devoured. When he woke, he felt better than ever: not only had he power he couldn't have ever imagined, he had a purpose, now: to Hunt and Feed. To teach others Fear. To let them know there was always a bigger fish. He was a far more fearsome fighter than ever before, and the next fight a greater spectactle than ever when he longed to devour a piece of his opponent. His invigoration let to new thoughts, though, and he developed an interest in a new kind of enemy: the ones that shackled him, kept him from the pleasures of life, dared to raise themselves above him. He grew unruly and aggressive, attacked his 'handlers' given half a chance, but the blood bond proved stronger than his will, and he found himself unable to harm his master. Dorian realized he had a great tool, but a volatile one, and considered getting rid of Ivan once and for all. Luckily, his plans were put on hold when he had to deal with someone dismantling his little fighting rings bit by bit, and even his connections couldn't help against the cop raids, incarcerations of fighters and even the ghouls of associates' deaths during a firefight with a rivaling coterie. Dorian wasn't an idiot, he knew he was being targeted, so he laid a trap, intending to kill two birds with one stone. Things went differently, because when Christian knowingly went for the trap, Ivan didn't attack him like a rabid animal as Dorian expected. Rather, the two immediately shared a sense of comraderie, of belonging, and with just one understanding nod, Christian managed to push Ivan that little bit further: he tore into Dorian's men like a tornado of claws, and the Ugallu brought Dorian a burning end. Christian didn't even have to attempt to convince Ivan of his mission \u2013 the Anakim was on-board whole-heartedly. That way, their hunt for Kindred down the East Coast began.<br /> To Ivan, Christian was salvation, because he gave him something he lacked to free himself: a real Family.<br /> <b>Anakim Predator</b><br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Cyclopean Strenght, Relentless Hunter, Looming Presence, Unbreakable, Titanic Blow, Crushing Coils, Terror's Friend, Limb from Limb.<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: You cannot Kill It, Your Rage Consumes You, They don't love you, They walk among us<br /> <b>Lair</b>: 5 (Frozen breaking Wasteland)<br /> <b>Lair Traits</b>: Extreme Cold, Maze, Decayed, Unstable<br /> <br /> <b>Discplines</b>: Protean 4 (Quadripedal, Claws, Wall Crawling/Crow, Rat, Dog, Shark/Horrid Talons), Resilience 3, Vigor 3<br /> <b>Notable Merits</b>: Giant, Demolisher 3, Relentless Assault 5, Brute Force 2, Epic Iron Skin, Fast Reflexes, Fleet of Foot 3, Fist of Nightmares, Epic Potential (Stamina), Advanced Direction Sense<br /> <br /> Whereas Ivan and Christian are the powerhouses of the group, they have two rather new members, who lack their experience if not their dedication:<br /> Maria Minelli, <b>Makara Tempter</b> (coming soon)<br /> Jack O'Donell, <b>Eshmaki Whisper</b> (coming soon)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T14:38:30-07:00","id":1297088,"title":"","content":"Inspirational Tumblr Zodiac post I mean there Literally Called Apex,<br /> <a href=\"https://konradleijon.tumblr.com/post/183480071186/the-apex-signs\" target=\"_blank\">https://konradleijon.tumblr.com/post...the-apex-signs</a><br /> <br /> Aries: Something old. Something without teeth or eyes, dragging its great tendrils along the ocean floor, trawling for the corpses of leviathans. <br /> <br /> <br /> Taurus: Something fast. Something hidden by the dust storms. Something with wings and paws and talons and a beak. A golden blur from a rising savannah sun. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Gemini: Something drawn to the sites of naval battles. Hardened, twisted shells adorned with the eyes of dead sailors. Casualties of war pressed into grim pearls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Cancer: Something that looks like a hen. Something that disguises itself among the others in the coop. Rotten eggs. A second, gaping maw.<br /> <br /> <br /> Leo: Something with a sting worse than death. A mane of quills. Pellets of bone and hair. The king of the arid mountains. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Virgo: Something that sits just below the water. Long flexible antennae flashing to mimic the dancing of fireflies. Whiplike, threshing tentacles covered in stinging barbs. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Libra: Something pure white. Great wings and soft fur host to intoxicating spores. A great proboscis for feeding on sleeping giants. Thousands of lidless, orange eyes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Scorpio: Something slow and heavy. Powerful arms terminate in claws meant for digging. Something that hates the corpse-eaters. Something that plants seeds atop the unburied. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ophiuchus: Something like a tree stump, dragging itself along the ground on strong, gnarled roots. Following large prey until it dies of exhaustion, and replanting itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sagittarius: Something fragile and light. Something that drifts with the wind on gaseous bladders, protected by its own noxious cloud. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Capricorn: Something pale and hungry. Something that feeds off trash and the insects attracted to it. Something far worse than garbage and flies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aquarius: Something with scales and a mane of colorful feathers. Something that hunts in packs, sharing moisture from kills. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Pisces: Something colossal. Wings like a thunderstorm and talons like massive fishhooks. Migrating from pole to pole, catching whales for their young.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 03-16-2019, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T07:03:23-07:00","id":1297237,"title":"","content":"Actually, nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 03-16-2019, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T07:40:32-07:00","id":1297249,"title":"","content":"What do you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T09:36:26-07:00","id":1297269,"title":"","content":"Neat stuff!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:02:13-07:00","id":1297362,"title":"","content":"Thanks which ones your Favorite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T13:27:22-07:00","id":1297571,"title":"","content":"Takahashi Hiroto - the Flying Swordsman<br /> Ugallu Nemesis<br /> Hiroto grew up on old Samurai movies and had always dreamed of being a Samurai. He practised on his own (his parents called it playing; he was just 7 at the time, after all) and joined the Kendo and Iaido Clubs the second he could. As he got older, his classmates considered his fixation on his sword-hobbies a bit eccentric, but since he was likeable and wasn't too much on the nose (&quot;He's a chill guy. Just don't ask him about swords, or he won't shut up, though&quot;) he got along fine with others. Mr and Mrs Takahashi grew a bit worried over their son's fixation, as he was relentless in his training and would've practically spent every minute he didn't have to do something else training. His grades were okay, though, and his friends made him come along to social events all the time, so other than his hobby, his life was pretty normal. By the time he went to college, he taught the Iaido classes and even won national competitions. Then, suddenly, he stopped returning calls, holed himself up in his bunk bed, and seemed to fall into a deep depression. His Devouring had thrown him off the rails pretty hard, but eventually, he came to terms with it, even found joy in it. The power was great, and flying was simply indescribable.<br /> The Hunger was bad, but he managed to tell himself he was doing what is right by punishing murderers. He drew inspiration from his early childhood movies in what appropriate punishments would be, and the Black Crane found them to be acceptable, apparently.<br /> His love for the sword survived even the Onmoraki, and now, he patrolled the streets as a masked vigilante calling himself Tengu. He was closer to a ninja or Wuxia swordsman, sure, but he'd take what he could get. In a way, this was a dream come true. Sure, his grades were dropping, he had less of a social life, and the local mob (let's go with Bratva to break the thematic up a bit)<br /> If only that pesky detective wasn't hellbent on finding him...<br /> <br /> Life: Honorable<br /> Legend: Judgemental<br /> Atavisms:Wings of the Raptor, Lightning Strike, Shadowed Soul, Siren's Treacherous Song, Dragonfire, Eye of Heaven<br /> Nightmares: You Cannot Kill It, You Will Never Rest<br /> Lair Traits: Disruption (late Medieval technology), Crosswinds<br /> Notable Merits: Armed Defense 4, Two Weapon Fighting 4<br /> <br /> I started with an idea of Zatoichi, Bleach's Kurosaki Ichigo and League of Legend's Master Yi for the fighting style, mixed that with what I found about Onmoraki for the Horror and threw in some Ascended Fanboy + Blessed with Suck + With Great Power.... tropes to blurr out the initial Ichigo overdose for the character. The Atavisms are in order of acquisition, Wings of the Raptor and Lightning strike are essential, Siren's and Dragonfire are due to mythological connections with Onmoraki and one of those could be dropped. Eye of Heaven is meant to emulate the 'piercing insight' that is occasionally associated with (especially anime) swordmen who can tell someone's abilities with just a glance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T13:58:13-08:00","id":1370145,"title":"","content":"The Seven Deadly Sins (Brood) (no relation to the anime)<br /> <br /> A rather large Brood whose members involve the seven deadly sins in some way, shape or form when feeding.<br /> <br /> <b>David Nguyen </b>(Inguma Tempter) - <u>Wrath</u><br /> Due to being of mixed heritage, David had trouble fitting in - he was always the 'Vietnamese Friend' with his African-American friends and family, and faced a similar exclusion on the other side. When meeting Caucasians, they usually all asked the same question: &quot;You're mixed, right?&quot; The message he received was always the same: you're odd, you're not like us, you're not really one of us.<br /> They didn't mean anything by it other than maybe assigning a simple descriptor to him, but in effect, he was always the odd one out. Still, David felt blessed most of the time, because he got to take part in three different cultures and pick the things he liked from them (which may have added to his standing out). He couldn't change it, so he owned it, and the downsides were practically not worth mentioning. In fact, he started to take pride in it.<br /> At first.<br /> Then it got worse when they moved due to his dad's work, and ended up in a neighboorhood with tons of racial tension. The reasons were the same you'd find in almost any other place: lack of jobs due to influx of new immigrants with a single culture, friendships gone awry, gang friction etc. etc.<br /> And for David, it was the worst, because he couldn't fit in. He was always and outsider, and that meant, he was easy pickings for any group that needed to vent their frustrations on someone. He was always 'the other' to someone. Soon, he came to believe that everyone was racist, up to a certain degree.<br /> Those three years were hell, but his nightmares got even worse, to the point that at the end he'd rather be awake and suffer through the days than go to bed.<br /> Later, he said he didn't remember all that much, but a focus was the loss of himself - he started to look differently, to feel differently, then starting losing all his traits altogether, until nothing but a human of vague descent was left.<br /> Then, he was Devoured.<br /> As a Begotten, David quickly found his niche: enticing people to act violently against someone else (might even be himself), and have them face the fallout. <br /> He never uses his Nightmares directly on his Victim, but rather uses it on people around them to give them hell, bring them slowly to a boil, then give them the final incentive to explode.<br /> He might just take on a specific group of people's appearances instead and repeatedly use them to cause the Victim trouble (e.g. the Polish workers in the appartments one floor above the target's appartment; repeatedly scratch his car, bump into him, curse him out, outright threaten him etc. to get him to behave racist against his likely surprised neighbours who're certainly going to be shocked at this rampant racism and not going to take what look like unprovoked attacks for long.<br /> The racist spin is just for his personal satisfaction and has nothing to do with a lesson (he deliberately doesn't teach one).<br /> <br /> <br /> Life: Cautious<br /> Legend: Judgemental<br /> Atavisms: Enemy Within, Shadow Stalker, Basilisk's Touch.<br /> Nightmares: Your Rage Consumes You, Everyone Hates You, Fear is Contagious, They Don't Love You<br /> Horror: The Other - a humanoid that appears just slightly off but is hard to qualify: is that skin reddish, bronze, green, dark or pale? Are those Asian/Caucasian/African features? Is that hair straight or curled? Red, blond, brunette, black? Depends on the light and angle. The only thing that never changes is his lack of a shadow.<br /> Lair: A bus stop late at night, with a single light and a sitting bench. <br /> Lair Traits: Exposed, Poor Light, Slick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T07:56:44-07:00","id":1415537,"title":"","content":"The Seven Deadly Sins (Brood)<br /> <b>Jean Fehrwright </b>([Ugallu] Collector) - <u>Greed</u><br /> <br /> The man known to his friends as Jean Fehrwright is a compulsive liar, thief and impostor, and he is very, very good at it, quite possibly the best grifter around, in fact.<br /> Good enough to have robbed smart, rich people blind to enable a modest (read: utterly ridiculously luxurious) life long before his Devouring.<br /> Having been an extremely talented and actually already accomplished thief at an age where other people struggled with tying shoe laces or getting away with not doing their homework, it was only to be expected that he would lead a less than honest life.<br /> The Devouring introduced new dangers to his life - a Hunger for capers in absolutely unreasonable timespans, the danger of Heroes, a whole new world of dangerous beings capable of squashing him as easily as a fly- yet none of those came even close to his greatest shortcoming: he was brilliant, and he knew it. Instead of doing the smart and prudent thing and pulling of reliable heists and cons, he needs to show off: letting his target know about him robbing them without actually putting them off, going for the richest and most powerful, targeting the most secured treasures or any combination thereof - the only reason he didn't make the seat of Pride is the fact that Sarah's pride exceeds even his.<br /> <br /> Jean is pretty vague about his past, more due to nonchalance than any concept of guarding secrets.<br /> Despite a rather extensive education which allows him to slip into a large number roles of any sort at the drop of a hat (Professional Training 5 + Barfly), even he cannot do everything on his lonesome, which is part of the reason he joined the Seven Deadly Sins. The other, much more pressing reason is the fact that a rather powerful Cabal has it out for him after a humiliating battle which cost most of Jean's friends their lives.<br /> <br /> Jean prefers to do things in a 'cultivated manner', which leaves him about as good a fighter as the next best street rat with a nimble body and a knife (Borderline useless in a fight with professionals, can hold his own against the average untrained human criminal). He can stealth, charm locks, perform card tricks and make things dis- or reappear with the best of them (Sleight of Hand). However, he <i>really </i>shines when he can make use of his silver tongue to talk people into actions that are quite against their best interest (Fast Talking 3 and Etiquette 4).<br /> <br /> Having said all that, it might come as a surprise that Jean is his Brood's Obcasus Initiate, and a surprisingly devout follower of the Dark Mother's will.<br /> Never judge a book by it's many covers.<br /> <br /> RP: Jean Feeds often and heavily enough to try to stay in High Satiety. At some level, only really powerful opponents and valuable goods qualify - ideally, he punches way above his actual weight class and comes out (mostly) unscathed. Tricking a coterie of Lancea Kindred into handing him the valuable relic for 'safeguarding' from the 'devious Ordo' (which he riled up into actually looking for it), making Changelings swear an Oath for getting them out of trouble (which he actually got them into in the first place), or just plain try and rob a Cabal of Mammon Seers or a Mummy's cult blind.<br /> He is stubborn and believes himself to be quite capable of taking on almost anything, definitly being the smartest guy in the room - he isn't always, though, and often, others pay the price.<br /> <br /> Life: Arrogance<br /> Legend: Relentless<br /> Core Atavisms: Alien Allure, Relentless Hunter, Weakness Exposed<br /> Other possible Atavisms (less is more here - the majority of his Awesome and Success is pure skill, not reliance on supernatural powers):<ul><li>Needs Must (helps with finding insane Caper targets), Mimir's Wisdom (gives more wriggle room to focus on social skills, helps feigning knowledge when taking on fake identities), Illusion of Safety (makes scouting out a place and getting in - and out!- a lot easier), Alien Mindset (constantly shifting mind and identity? such a nice fit!) or Wings of the Raptor (increases mobility options, helps getting into and out of places)</li> </ul>Core Nightmares: The Walls have Eyes, This is due tomorrow, You were never right, Family is forever, You should fade away .<br /> Other possible Nightmares (some as above):<ul><li>They put something in your food, They walk among us, You will be first against the wall, or Everything you do is worthless &amp; Fear is Contagious (highly effective in reducing combat efficiency of a whole group of enemies at High Satiety)</li> </ul>Horror: [The Hoarding Wyvern]<br /> Lair: an underground cave filled with gold - and traps<br /> Lair Traits: Hoard, Bottomless, Slick<br /> Attributes: High Wits, High Dext, Good Charisma and Int, High Manipulation and Composure. <br /> Skills: Persuasion, Subterfuge, Empathy, Socialize and Streetwise are well developed. Crafts and Expression, too. Stealth, Athletics and Larceny.<br /> <br /> Did I take a lot of inspiration from The Lies of Locke Lamorra? Yes, yes I did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 05-25-2025, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T18:33:16-07:00","id":1415639,"title":"","content":"<b>The Beast of a Billion Songs</b><br /> It is one of the oldest Incarnate Anakim alive, of similar age to the Congo's Mokole-mbembe. It is at least 200 years old, and during that immense stretch of time it has become a thing of transcendent terror.<br /> <br /> It's Horror is a towering, beautiful androgynous winged figure, with feathers that are patterned as swirling colors and eyes that shine with bewitching light. When it takes to the skies the Hive of [Fill-in-the-Blank] shakes, and Horrorspawn are sent scuttling for cover.<br /> <br /> It's strength is vast, and it teaches its lesson well: <i>Prepare for the storm, or be swept away</i>. It finds communities that have suffered little, and it's brings its enormous power to bear. Natural disasters, earthquakes, tornados---it all comes out of nowhere, and wreckage and lost lives litter it's wake.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim.<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Ruin.<br /> <b>Inheritance:</b> Incarnate.<br /> <b>Horror:</b> A gigantic bird that caries storms on its back.<br /> <b>Lair:</b> 10.<br /> <b>Laor Descriptoon:</b> A hellish ruined cities, on fire with ashes falling from the sky and the ground perpetually ready to give way to a calamitous fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T10:55:52-08:00","id":1430097,"title":"","content":"The Toxic Avenger<br /> <br /> Jody had always been fascinated by poisons, pollution and contamination, even before she found her Horror. Humans and the things that feed off them are part of the same ecosystem as the birds and the bees, after all, and she enjoys teaching that Lesson with object demonstrations: her Lair is full of noxious fumes and caustic sludge that demonstrate the consequences of unchecked environmental degradation. Her day job with the state DNR provides her with ample opportunities to feed, as she uncovers one corporate polluter after another who need the fear of Mother Nature put into them. She's also forged good relations with several Uratha, who have taught her about the spiritual consequences of ecological damage and vice-versa.<br /> <br /> Recently, however, she's started exploring a very different kind of Kinship. While doing a survey of a landfill tainted with radioactive barium, she stumbled upon a miserable young Zeka who was rapidly festering a Wasteland. They had been abandoned by their genitor and had no idea how to manage their nuclear Azoth; while Jody knew nothing of the Created, she was fascinated by the way the Zeka's presence twisted the landscape. She helped this toxic stranger get to safety, and her curiosity and lack of Disquiet immediately endeared her to them.<br /> <br /> These days, the Zeka - now going by the name Westlake - has their own Chamber in Jody's Lair, a safe place to retreat from a hostile and fragile world. Jody has added a new Lair Trait, Irradiated, and is working on a special nuclear Nightmare. It's not exactly a match made in heaven, though; Westlake's volatile humor and shifting Roles are hard for Jody to handle, and she's openly and increasingly skeptical of this whole &quot;Pilgrimage&quot; idea. It seems like only a matter of time before the two of them come to an impasse - either Jody will finally tire of her friend's incomprehensible quest, or Westlake's explosive Torment will finally go off at the worst possible time.<br /> <br /> But for now, they're faced with a more immediate problem: the Irradiated Trait has started spreading through the local Hive, and the Apex is very interested in hunting down the source before it attracts too much mortal attention - or starts to sicken unprotected Begotten in their own Lairs.<br /> <br /> <i>Jody, the Toxic Avenger</i><br /> <b>Family: </b>Namtaru<br /> <b>Hunger: </b>Punishment<br /> <b>Legend: </b>Righteous<br /> <b>Life: </b>Curious<br /> <b>Horror: </b>A walking corpse covered in lesions, tumors, and burns.<br /> <b>Lair: </b>6<br /> <b>Lair Traits: </b>Slick, Stinging, Noxious Gases, Toxic, Irradiated<br /> <b>Atavisms: </b>Basilisk's Touch, Vengeful Earth, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, Skin Deep<br /> <b>Nightmares: </b>All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, You Deserve This, Your Rage Consumes You (Werewolf kinship), You Are Tainted (Zeka kinship)<br /> <br /> <b>Irradiated (Major Lair Trait): </b>The Lair is a radiological hazard with Intensity 2, and has a chance to apply the Contaminated Tilt (Night Horrors: The Tormented, p. 137-138). The sky may be hazy with fallout, or vivid blue flashes of Cherenkov radiation may flicker in the distance. Dead or dying animals, strangely stunted plants, or mutated insects may also be visible. Characters with no special resistance to radiation will start taking 1B per day after [Stamina] days, which they cannot heal without leaving the Irradiated area or resolving the Contaminated Tilt. <br /> <br /> Imposing the Irradiated Lair Trait, or opening a Primordial Pathway to an Irradiated Lair, leaves behind radiological residue at Intensity 1 for [Lair] weeks, due to induced radioactivity. This residue causes 1B every week after [Stamina] weeks, which cannot heal until the victim leaves the area or the residue finally decays.<br /> <br /> <b>You Are Tainted: </b>The victim is seized by the unshakable conviction that they are somehow tainted, toxic or corrupted, and everything they do only spreads the taint further. Everything they touch will be marred, and everyone around them is in danger due to their presence. For the duration of the Nightmare, the victim suffers the Agoraphobic Condition.<br /> <br /> <i>High Satiety: </i>The victim also gains a -2 penalty to Social rolls due to their feelings of self-loathing.<br /> <br /> <i>Satiety Expenditure: </i>the victim feels compelled to purge themselves of the imagined taint. They drop everything to bathe, clean their immediate surroundings or rid themselves of &quot;contaminated&quot; objects (food, clothing, furniture, etc). They must spend a Willpower to do anything <i>other </i>than clean for the duration of the Nightmare. On an exceptional success, Jody can suggest the taint originates from a particular place or object, which will make it the focus of the victim's cleaning efforts - or possibly motivate them to destroy it.<br /> <br /> <i>Westlake, codependent Created</i><br /> <b>Lineage: </b>Zeka<br /> <b>Refinement: </b>Mercurius<br /> <b>Elpis: </b>Love<br /> <b>Torment: </b>Paranoia<br /> <b>Azoth: </b>3<br /> <b>Pilgrimage: </b>4<br /> <b>Bestowment: </b>Victim Shadow<br /> <b>Transmutations: </b>The Tsar's Gift, Sanctus Aspiratus (Vulcanus), Stone, Elixer (Alchemicus), Externalize (Disquietism - Fixed), Anonymity (Deception - Fixed)<br /> <br /> Westlake knows they've gotten farther on the Pilgrimage than most of their kind thanks for Jody's help, and it's not that they're ungrateful. They were happy to help her feed while they mastered roles like Vigilante, Follower, and Daredevil. But Jody just doesn't understand why Westlake keeps changing Refinements, much less why they want to become human, and her criticism and impatience is getting hard to bear. Westlake knows it's time to go, for both their sakes, but they're worried about how long they'll be able to stay on the Pilgrimage without the safety of Jody's Lair to fall back on - and that Jody might turn her Lesson on them when they inevitably spawn another Wasteland.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T20:07:13-08:00","id":1430408,"title":"","content":"Not sure how to go about it, outside of two powers. However, Kirby has terrifying potential as one of the Beghotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T03:41:20-07:00","id":1450941,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Carrie O'Neil</b></u><br /> <b>Family</b>: Makara<br /> <b>Hunger</b>: Nemesis<br /> <b>Life</b>: Curious<br /> <b>Legend</b>: Relentless<br /> <b>Horror</b>: A shoggoth-looking blob monster. Like this:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img src=\"https://kawaraban.de/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/carrion_teaser-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> or this <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/bd/03/3e/bd033e51ec6c9035285a534b3c8b5bae.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Atavisms</b>:<br /> At Lair 1: Heart of the Ocean, Limb from Limb, Ravenous Maw<br /> At Lair 2: Wings of the Raptor, Illusion of Safety, Terror's Friend<br /> At Lair 3: Caught in the Webs, From the Shadows<br /> At Lair 4: Cyclopean Strength, Infestation<br /> At Lair 5: Titanic Blow, Lightning Strike<br /> At Lair 6: Shadow Stalker<br /> At Lair 7: Monster from the Deep, Looming Presence<br /> At Lair 8: Skin Deep<br /> At Lair 9: Unbreakable<br /> At Lair 10: Enemy Within<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares</b>:<br /> At Lair 1: The Walls have Eyes, Tentacles Everyhwere!<br /> At Lair 3: Fear Is Contagious, Run Away<br /> At Lair 5: You Are Not Alone<br /> At Lair 7: Tabula Rasa, They Walk Among Us<br /> At Lair 10: Your Rage Consumes You, You Are A Meat Machine<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: Legendary Horror (ooooo)<br /> <br /> <b>Lair</b>: A meatmoss covered cave, half the floor covered by a pink, viscious fluid pooling into a small lake of indeterminite depth at the room's center. Tendrils extend from the ground and walls and move about, ready to grasp and hold on to hapless victims, or even draw them towards one of the many maws, waiting to chomp on tasty biomass.<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits</b>:<br /> Lair 1: Slick, Flooded<br /> Lair 2: Maze<br /> Lair 4: Stench<br /> Lair 6: Undergrowth<br /> Lair 8: Engulfing<br /> Lair 10: Razored<br /> <br /> Carrie and her Shoggothy Horror have an unusual relationship. The former Unfettered Legendary Horror possessed her, and was fractured during that timeframe, ending up in the two becoming a Begotten. For most intents and purposes, she is a normal starting Beast, but this changes a few things: the Legendary Horror Merit applies with 1 dot, and as she gains Lair Dots, they will rise up to 5 at Lair 5. Her Horror is a little more indepent, as a result, with the appropriate consequences. Furthermore, when she rises in Lair and accumulates the appropriate XP, they are automatically spent on certain Atavisms, as they represent the Horror re-acquiring lost abilities (basically, preset Atavisms, gatekeeping additional dots in Lair).<br /> However, the Fragments of the Horror still exist - where she to find any, she would likely regain some of it's power (up to storyteller discretion if this takes the form of extra XP or handing out an Atavism or dot in Lair).<br /> Tbh, Carrie is mostly meant to be used as an NPC and storyhook, although it could be fun to have her as a PC, too.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Mental/Physical/Social -<br /> Carrie is both book-smart and hard-headed. Her job requires her to perform delicate analysis with her hands. She doesn't stand out socially in any way.<br /> <br /> <b>Skills</b>: Mental/Social/Physical -<br /> Carrie is well-versed in Academics and Science, due to her work, and has some knowledge of Medicine. She has a knack for Crafts, which comes in handy on the field when she needs to create special equipment, and knows enough about computers to program simple databanks to better organize her findings. She has learned to fit in with certain more affluent groups during her fundraisers, but left the actual contract talks to other people (low persuasion). Furthermore, even though recently she has had to lie very often, she is far from an expert yet. She is good at scientific journalism, however, and can write captivating reports, which are often a much-needed source of income.<br /> She has recently picked up the odd stealth skill to keep her more questionable acitivites hidden, but is still a novice. She's been running and climbing for a few years, however, to compensate for the deskwork.<br /> <br /> <b>Backstory</b>:<br /> Carrie always was fascinated with ruins and old places, stories and animals. No one was really surprised when she ended up studying Archeology and Biology. People were surprised and more than a little impressed, however, when she achieved double doctorates in Anthropology and Paleontology. Other than her family, of course, who kept complaining about Carrie's chosen profession: poor pay (especially compared to the amount of work), time-consuming, you could have become a real doctor etc.<br /> She didn't care, though, because she loved what she was doing.<br /> <br /> One fateful day, she was offered a unique opportunity: Tom, once her lover and now one of her professional connections, unearthed something &quot;really old and strange&quot; at their Antarctica base, which he believed to be extraterrestrial in origin. During a test-drive with a new drill meant to extract samples from otherwise unreachable sedimantary strata, something gave way, and the whole expensive equipment crashed into a cave some 20 metres below the ground. What had started as a horrible accident turned out to be a blessing in disguise: the cave was old, untouched - and filled with symbols, paintings, and mucous liquid. Tom was already composing a possible speech for their Nobel prize, but Carrie remained sceptical. Once there, Carrie could easily see why Tom believed to have found proof of aliens: the cave was old and had been closed off for at least half a million years, judging by the sediment strata they had broken through, yet it was filled with signs of civilisation, predating the first modern humans by more than 200.000 years. Carrie quickly bashed the dreams of extraterrestrial origins, but pushed the dreams of Nobel prizes: this seemed to be proof of intelligent, sapient hominids with a highly advanced society.<br /> Working relentlessly during the day, her nights were plagued with nightmares of the ever-present pink mucus, a giant mass resembling a mix of tubifex worms and lichen, growing tentacles, teeth and eyes to hunt her. The amorphous, ever-shifting blob moved quickly, cornered her, and when it touched her, she woke up, often screaming, sweating, still feeling the warmth radiating off of the monstrosity. She got strange looks, but she wasn't the only one having bad dreams. They concluded something about the air or liquid must be nightmare-inducing, but they pressed on. The lure of prestige and acknowledgement (and money!) was too strong.<br /> After one week of this, a large group of people entered the site. Masked men, black uniforms, military grade equipment. No questions, no demands, only the sound of gunfire at the first sign of resistance. After the first people were shot, Tom among them, no one dared resist. They were still beaten up, as if to make sure no one had the strength to fight back.<br /> That night, Carrie didn't run from the monster, because the horrors of the day had proven worse than anything her overstimulated mind could concoct. Instead, she found herself wishing she could be this creature, to exact vengeance.<br /> To her suprpise, the monster complied. Filled with horrific might, she attacked - but she was not in charge of her shifting, changing body. People died left and right in the resulting fight, as the creature tore through friends and enemies alike. However, something happened during the fight - her memory is blurry, partly due to the Horror's possession, partly due to the violence, and partly due to some colours she can only half recall- and the monstrosity was ripped apart. The pain it-she-THEY experienced was beyond expression. Desperate to survive, it burrowed deep inside her body, and made it's nest where her soul used to be. Carrie carried herself into a box, wounded, sure she was losing her mind, and ready to die, to have it all end.<br /> She was found by a rescue party later on, catatonic and starving, and committed for treatment, first for her body, then because her story and the physical evidence didn't align. As far as the official report went, the people struggled when they were enclosed in the cave after an avalanche and ran out of supplies, and a mutiny resulted in most people dying. She'd have believed it, too, if there wasn't a protoplasmic, oozing blob in her mind, Hungering, demanding to take revenge, to punish, to be made whole again.<br /> Carrie was smart enough to keep her mouth shut. Someone had tampered with the place, destroyed any sign of their findings, killed her colleagues and her friend, and turned her into a monster.<br /> She will find out who.<br /> And they will get what they deserve.<br /> <br /> In the mean-time, Carrie tries to adjust to a new world of secrets, violence and darkness that opens up to her like a twisted, horrifying adventure.<br /> <br /> <b>Feeding</b>: Mostly trying to get people way, way outside their comfort zone in response to misdeeds: blackmailing a professor? You might find yourself waking up naked in a bad part of the city.<br /> <br /> <b>RP</b>:<br /> Carrie is very conflicted: she hates the violence her new life entails - but she cannot deny she revels in the catharsis of vengeance dealt out, enjoys the thrill of the hunt and the feeling of power. She loves the mystery and intrigue of the things that go bump in the night, the anthropologist in her is delighted at all these new societies, the implications for human history - yet she is horrified at the atrocities and scared for herself and the people around her.<br /> She was and to a degree still is extremely passionate about her job/hobby, but now more than ever restrained in normal conversation. If you want to have small talk about the weather or the last movie to come out, she is the absolute worst person to talk to, giving monosyllabic, non-commital responses like a rebellious teenager, but if you want to talk about big concepts, scientific theories, or anything work related, she will be bubbly and can get carried away on tangents quite easily.<br /> The attack on the camp site left deep scars, both physical and psychologically. She is more than just slightly paranoid (having your life turned upside down by a brutal attack out of the blue will do that to you), and tends to lash out defensively when she feels threatened. Not knowing who was behind the attack or why makes her extremely cautious and reluctant to join with others - finding her in a Brood or similarly commited group is unlikely, though not impossible.<br /> <br /> <b>Story Hooks</b>:<br /> The main hook is obviously finding out who the mysterious attackers are, and what happened during the Fragmentation of the Shoggoth-lookalike.<br /> Less obviously, what do they do with the Fragments? Do they need them, are they just trying to prevent the Horror from becoming whole again? Do they have a relationship with the Horror, or was it purely accidental? And how did the thing end up there in the first place? Was that truly a pre-Homo Homo Sapiens civilisation, or is there some other explanation? Where the drawings markings of a holy site, warnings, something else entirely and unrelated to the Shoggoth?<br /> <br /> - The Cheiron Group is always a fun enemy. Maybe they found out about the cave, and came sniffing. The Fragmentation could have been an accident, and Cheiron being who they are weren't going to let a chance to study monster parts fall by the wayside. What did they do in the meantime with the stuff? Are there 'shoggoth-spawn' running around?<br /> <br /> - Maybe the people were a cult and the site holy to them. Breaching might have activated a Mummy, who was involved in Fragmenting the Horror. Where are they now? Why have they not taken revenge on Carrie afterwards? Is the Mummy still out for her?<br /> <br /> - Was it the Seers who attacked, because they wanted the Horror for something? Maybe they mistook it for an Abyssal creature. Maybe it WAS an abyssal creature and the Fracturing changed its nature tremendously? If that is true, what will happen when it regains it's Fragments and therefore power?<br /> <br /> - Maybe this Horror IS as old as they thought, the remnant of a hominid Begotten from a time long age, following slightly different rules. It was slumbering for a long time. The cave used to be a Chamber, and the excavation somehow disturbed or even collapsed it, resulting in it waking up and feeding on the tasty fears it got for breakfast, slowly adapting to the new hominids' fearscape. The Fragmentation might have been the result of this adaptation, or an intervention from the Dark Mother, wanting to see one of her oldest children play again. Maybe it was another Beast, the local Apex, annoyed at the competition, who showed up with a paramilitary group to show who's boss, and, surprised at the power of his Sibling, managed to Fracture them with an Obcasus Rite at the cost of his own power. Now they're hiding, trying to fend of their enemies who smell weakness, trying to rebuild, trying to stay away from whatever this horrible thing was that almost cost them everything. Or maybe they have a different plan altogether.<br /> <br /> -This story is true: Father Wolf banished a Spirit of Change and Violence so foul and gluttonous, it threatened them all. Now, it has been set free. Maybe the military men were a particularly devoted Pack, noticing a terrible wound in the Gauntlet. Was the Horror originally a Magath, maybe even an Idigam, Fractured rather than cleansed by a powerful Ritual? Or did they simple misunderstand it's nature and apply a pre-existing narrative upon it? And what will happen when the Uratha meet Carrie once more?<br /> <br /> - Was this perhaps the handywork of Kindred? The Horror being the result of a particular Dragon's experiments, he might see Carrie's existence as an unusual result to be studied, carefully observing her, prodding, probing, testing. Or he might want to have his rightful property returned to him - but why hasn't he made a move yet?<br /> <br /> - Maybe someone tried to keep the Horrors sealed, having been given a vision that they are machines of violence and death. Maybe everyone they shot was already possessed by a similar monstrosity? What will Carrie do with the information that her friends had to die to save the world?<br /> <br /> - Maybe, however, the answer is simpler: Tom had been possessed by a monster not entirely unlike Carrie, who planned to excavate the rest to gorge itself on her peers and grow more powerful before going back to sleep. The armed men were mercenaries, and his being 'shot' was just part of the act, the bullying and murder just tenderizing its dinner, so to speak. Carrie also becoming a host was an unexpected wrench in it's plans, and it Fractured her at the cost of a lot of itself. Now also lessened, it tries to navigate the modern world to find the Fragments. There is no conspiracy outside the mercenaries' clean-up to avoid being persecuted, and all her rage has no outlet other than the friend she thinks dead. How will she react to the truth, finding Tom's shell, and will she be satisfied with the mercenaries being pawns, or will she demand their lives?<br /> <br /> - Then again, maybe it was Demons? The Dark Mother and her Spawn seem Anathema to the G-M, and some Demons believe that to be suited to their needs. The Horror could very well be just the thing a group of Unchained need to dismantle a part of the G-M and finally find their Hell - but do they need Carrie attached to it to that end? Can they bargain it off of her? Were they involved in the attacks, or was that the G-M at work, as they claim? Maybe it was neither, and they just try to gain an advantage, by taking advantage of her lack of knowledge...<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Inspiration</i>:<br /> I like the Lovecraftian Mythos and I like the Thing, so it was only natural I'd play Carrion, which I also liked. Hence this Character concept came up. I apologize for the uncreative name, I just had to put something resembling the game's title in there somehow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Missing information, typos 06-04-2021, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T05:07:23-07:00","id":1451431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823870#post823870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Anakim Ravager:</b> They say too much of a good thing is bad for you. So it is that this Beast satiates itself by indulging the vice of others. They are more than a drug pusher, more than a chef, they are addiction incarnate. That voice in your heard encouraging you to try one more serving. Drugs, food, sex, anything that his victims may derive pleasure from, he is happy to provide. And then, when they finally go too far and their body retaliates against them, he feasts!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Beast's soul is a horrifying figure that appears to be made out of living candy with syringes strapped to its fingers and bottles of narcotic drugs embedded into its backside. Its skin is like ginger bread, white frosting dripping from its mouth filled with candy corn teeth and specks of red cinnamon pepper his body, completely nude for all to see. A mane of black licorice wreathes its head and it speaks with a pleasant voice and trustworthy tone. The vials in his backside pump through his arms and into his fingers, ready to empty their contents into his victim's veins if he catches them!</div> </div> </div> </div>This greatly reminds me of the Candy Mare from the fanfic \u2018<a href=\"http://&amp;quot;http://https://www.fimfiction.net/story/51716/something-sweet-to-bite\" target=\"_blank\">Something Sweet To Bite</a>\u2019 on <a href=\"https://www.fimfiction.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Fimfiction</a>. Well done! I might use this as my character, should I ever find myself a viable group (though I\u2019ll probably modify it a bit). Though, from what I'm inferring, the Beast could just as likely be an Enabler, Hungering for the Transgressions of those who got too far to satiate their desires, as a Ravager, Hungering for the Ruin of those who let their addictions consume them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823876#post823876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Slaanesh would be proud. Don't forget the painfully exaggerated sexual characteristics both primary and secondary. What if someone is addicted to adrenaline? Does he invite them to a fist fight or petty crime? He sounds like a perfect candidate for the Alien Allure Atavism and the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous Lair Trait.</b></a></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with ya\u2019, mate! May-haps said Lair trait could take the form of the Lair being filled to the brim with entire ecosystems/landscapes formed from sweets, junk food, drugs (both prepared in various ways, and \u2018raw\u2019), sexual equipment and a kaleidoscopic menagerie of other things?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=823904#post823904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I'm thinking about possibly altering their appearance a bit. A creature with needles strapped to their fingers doesn't exactly say &quot;Let's be friends!&quot; as well as he's supposed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could easily smooth that over with the Alien Allure Atavism; the poor buggers who find themselves in the lair typically wind up focusing way too much on the Horror\u2019s beauty, its chest (bouncy-bouncy boing-boings, if ya\u2019 know what I mean), abdomen (\u201cWhat a six-pack!\u201d), ass (damn that\u2019s fine!) and/or loins (for obvious reasons *waggles eyebrows with a lecherous smirk-leer-grin*) and/or the fact that it\u2019s made of food to notice anything until it\u2019s too late.<br /> <br /> Heck, particularly arrogant, lustful, gluttonous and/or otherwise vice-ridden Heroes could end up falling into the trap of trying to claim this \u2018mis-lead beauty\u2019 for themselves, or the weaker(-willed) ones just outright pledging themselves into the Beast\u2019s service in exchange for just <i>one more taste</i> of what their new master/mistress has to offer.<br /> <br /> Basically, Horrors are creatures born from the very essence of nightmares. Thus, they\u2019re as beholden to dream logic as their Lairs are when it comes to exact limits on their forms and morphologies.<br /> <br /> Edit: Apologies for the mess, I\u2019m on my phone at \u2018work\u2019. I\u2019ll fix it when I get home.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Okay, it <i>should</i> be sorted out now\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 06-09-2021, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T13:14:17-07:00","id":1451567,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Sarah Morales (Seven Deadly Sins Brood - Pride) (WIP)</b></u><br /> <b>Concept</b>: egomaniac thrill/attention-seeking Alpha Bitch<br /> <b>Family</b>: Anakim<br /> <b>Hunger</b>: Ravager<br /> <b>Life</b>: Arrogant<br /> <b>Legend</b>: Judgemental<br /> <b>Horror</b>: A winged and horned lion<br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Alien Allure, Illusion of Safety, Mimir's Wisdom, Weakness Exposed<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: Fear is Contagious, Family is Forever, Behold my True Form,<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Social / Physical / Mental<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Social/ Physical/ Mental<br /> <b>Lair</b>: A painted pyramid amidst a desert<br /> <b>Lair Traits</b>:<br /> Blazing<br /> Extreme Heat<br /> <br /> <br /> She was the Cheerleader to end all cheerleaders, the queen alpha of all girls believing the world to orbit around them - and then she had a rude awakening when, in college, all her partying took its toll on her plans of becoming rich and leading an easy life by crushing them to dust when she was expelled.<br /> Except Sarah wouldn't take the Seat of Pride if that was were it all came to an end. No, as far as she was concerned, this was just the beginning of her gracing the world with her unparalleled beauty, brilliant mind and peerless social skills.<br /> Egomaniac extraordinaire, Sarah gets away with things not only because of her charm and good looks, but because of the sheer refuge in audacity.<br /> No one would come in during a lesson to take the projector away for 'repairs', right? What about just showing up at a travel agency and starting to order around people like she owned the place, leaving with a number of sensitive data? Well, all those things would have been just child's play.<br /> Sarah didn't waste her time on that.<br /> She got a realistic looking uniform and a good road flare and stole a policeman's motorcycle, stopped a money transporter with claims of a bomb threat, and made a scene of the bomb &quot;about to blow&quot;. All that was left was to jump into the now-empty driver's seat and take off.<br /> Sure, she didn't get to keep most of the money, and was sent to prison - but she did leave. Well, break-out, but &quot;Is it really a prison break if you simply walk out?&quot; The helicopter probably was a bit much, but she wanted to leave an impression, after all.<br /> If only her 'pranks' had stayed that harmless.<br /> Changing identities turned out to be easier if you had her particular set of skills and no inhibitions to go all-out to get what you want. But her Horror found a taste in shaking up the people's sense of security, and Sarah was vindictive to a fault. Usually, she would lounge and enjoy life as a party queen, but occasionally, she would pick someone or something catching her eye at the wrong moment, and set out to destroy them as thouroughly as she can.<br /> She is a looks first, force second person, with things like &quot;Thinking things through&quot; never even crossing her mind. <br /> If she can't charm her way out, she'll slug it out, and she's a mean hit.<br /> The main problem with this is that she is constantly drawing Hero heat, to the point even her Broodmates have considered cutting her loose more than once. And now, she has a particularly nasty individual back on her trail... someone she'd sworn is dead. How will the Brood react to the news Sarah's arch-nemsis is out and about, survived the last confrontation, and she'd known about it for months but kept quiet because she, for some reason, thought it wasn't gonna be 'that bad'?<br /> <br /> Inspiration: The Real Life TV Tropes page on Bavarian Fire Drills. What the hell, people, what the hell.<br /> <br /> This is still a work in progress, as the themes are a little bit over the place, I am aware. Still, should serve well as a starting point / inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 05-25-2025, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T11:55:26-07:00","id":1495130,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve got a character idea inspired by Cinder\u2019s \u2018<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1170442-christmas-bonus-klaus-krampus\">Christmas Bonus</a>\u2019, and DR. Seuss\u2019s \u2018How the Grinch stole Christmas\u2019;<br /> <br /> <b>Ugallu</b> <b>Collector/<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1170442-christmas-bonus-klaus-krampus\">Festive</a>;</b> A holiday is an almost sacred thing, a time where people get together to celebrate such things as Community, Love, the Coming of Spring, the Autumnal Harvest, the Lives of those who\u2019ve since passed from this world, the New Year, and so much more. Sometimes, however, there are those who begin to lose sight of what one or more of such events actually <i>mean</i>, and begin to get caught up in the dross, the paraphernalia, the lights and fancy decorations, the dressing of the holidays as they slowly start to ring more and more hollow with each passing year. Such is what this Begotten Child of the Dark Mother seeks to avert.<br /> <br /> Each year, they find a person, or group, or community, or some other such target who\u2019s starting to lose sight of what a holiday <i>means</i>, and seeks to remind them by stripping away all of that fancy-schmancy \u2018stuff\u2019 that they\u2019ve been slowly accumulating. All in the hopes of their target realising the error of their ways and begin appreciating the holiday once again (or at least earnestly beginning, and sticking to, the journey towards such).<br /> <br /> Those who, for whatever reason, refuse to change their ways eventually meet their fate within the clutches of the beast\u2019s Horror. A green-furred creature somewhere between a human and a full-grown grizzly in size, with long spindly limbs, a sizeable belly, jaws full of crooked, yellow, termite-infested teeth and a coat of mangy fur filled with every manner of fur-based parasite one can imagine, \u200bthe last two being stained with various substances of\u2026 let\u2019s just say \u2018dubious origins\u2019, and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> Said Lair takes the form of a vast mountain, frigid, treacherous and topographically weird even by the warped standards of such un-places. Upon its slopes lies many of the dangers you would typically expect of any mountain, only twisted into far more nightmarish forms, along with a dump filled with all the manifold waste of human civilisation, from the simplest scraps of trash all the way to biohazardous materials, cast-off chemical substances and radioactive waste. Should one somehow navigate the dangerous landscape until they were almost at the peak of the mountain, they would find a small green door set into the rock. This leads into a labyrinthian network of caves, caverns, tunnels, ravines and other such underground features, all laden with tricks and traps meant to confuse and entrap.<br /> <br /> Edit: And <i>there</i>. That... should be about it, I think. Sorry it took so long, got side-tracked by a particularly <i>persistent</i> ear infection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 12-05-2023, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T18:50:04-08:00","id":1496568,"title":"","content":"[What follows is a Junji Ito story. It is not my own idea. I\u2019ve turned it into a Beast character idea, but it\u2019s not mine. All credit goes to Junji Ito.]<br /> <br /> <b><i>The Ever-Pregnant Abomination</i></b><br /> It became a Rampant Beast long, long, <i>long</i> ago, and it is ancient. A Talassi of impossible age and power, it has forgotten its human life, even its original gender. A vast, eel-like fish, it\u2019s belly is translucent, allowing one to see inside. This horrid cavern is where it stores its victims.<br /> <br /> It swallows down all seafarers it can, and keeps them alive and fed in its gullet intravenously. They can\u2019t move, can\u2019t escape, but can see outside with no problems. These people\u2019s slow descent into madness keeps it nice and Satiated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T16:12:57-08:00","id":1500878,"title":"","content":"Been into Fnaf as well as Fmab recently, so have some Beasts based on characters:<br /> <br /> <b>William Afton, Namtaru Ravager</b> - William was never a good man, even before the devouring. His first murder, that of his friend and business partner\u2019s daughter, was the beginning of a long tradition for him, as he devised ways to kill children using the animatronics he created. It was only after his daughter Elizabeth\u2019s death, hover, that he discovered what he really was and embraced it wholeheartedly, feeding on the families destroyed by his killings. His horror is Springtrap, a decaying version of the golden bunny outfit he uses for his killings, mixing both the unnerving nature of animatronics with the disgust and horror at seeing a decaying corpse. His Lair is a pizzeria, one that gets more and more run down the longer you stay, until blood is seeping through the walls and the dismantled versions of your childhood buddies are coming to tear your face off. His worst nemesis isn\u2019t a Hero, but his son, Michael, who became a sin-eater after falling victim to his father, and is now determined to shut him down for good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roy Mustang, Ugallu Collector </b>- He was devoured on the battlefield, becoming a monster in more ways than one. It\u2019s only fitting, really. Still, he\u2019s determined to use whatever powers he has in order to make up for the very human horrors he committed. His horror is a dragon, the fire-breathing western classic, complete with a mountaintop lair. He collects people - his team, his subordinates, his friends, those two boys he\u2019s now found himself looking after - and protects them with a ferocity only a dragon can match. One day, he hopes to collect the entire country, and protect all of them, and woe is anyone who hurts, or god forbid kills, one of his precious hoard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27217-skyewards","name":"Skyewards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T21:25:49-07:00","id":1510855,"title":"","content":"An Ugallu Ruin detective who uses their job in two very important ways. Firstly, by uncovering cheaters, kidnappers, abusers, and murderers, ruining their lives by exposing them and therefore fearing their hunger. Secondly, using their position to help cover up fetch-murders and fake identities for the local freehold. They\u2019ve got some good friends in the Autumn court who they regularly have deep discussions on the nature of dreams and fear with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27217-skyewards","name":"Skyewards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T11:07:37-07:00","id":1551270,"title":"","content":"The Seven Deadly Sins (Brood) -adjacent<br /> <u><b>Konstantinios Dimakos ('Father Charity')</b></u><br /> <b>Concept</b>: devout priest of the Dark Mother seeking to reconnect estranged family members through very questionable means<br /> <b>Family</b>: Makara<br /> <b>Hunger</b>: Ravager<br /> <b>Life</b>: Parental<br /> <b>Legend</b>: Unexpected<br /> <b>Horror</b>: A Devil<br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Dragonfire, Fear's Friend, Alien Mindset, Looming Presence<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: You Cannot Run, You Cannot Wake Up, You Deserve This<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Mental/ Physical / Social<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Physical/ Mental/ Social<br /> <b>Lair</b>: a blazing hellscape<br /> <b>Lair Traits</b>:<br /> Burning<br /> Extreme Heat<br /> <br /> Konstantinios is a bit different from the rest of the Seven Deadly Sins. Despite being the oldest by age (62), he is the newest member. He wasn't found for a job like Sarah or picked for his skill like David, or joined them because e.g. a Cabal of mages had it out for him like Jean, but sought them out to join them on the behest of the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> His Devouring happened at a very bad time in his life, with him being orphaned just a few days prior, at the age of 15. The last things he said to his parents were words said in anger - words he since wished to take back. When he started having nightmares of hell, he thought it was his guilt manifesting. He soon learned that indeed, these were not just &quot;bad dreams&quot;.<br /> Unlike many, he took his change religiously, and bought into the &quot;Teach Lessons&quot; stuff with a fervor that outright scared other Begotten.<br /> Konstantinios likes to take away what is truly important to you to make you realize their worth- for a time. Kidnapping kids, demanding payment from their parents over two days of negotiation (&quot;no police!&quot; though he'll always expect police to be involved), money he'll never go pick up, but releasing the victims after a day or two. Taking a spouse hostage during a robbery, apparently coincidentally. Calling in the name of your old parent's hospice to apologize for the bad news of them passing away at night, despite them still being alive, to get you to go meet them more.<br /> Sometimes, these are more sinister, though, and in his mind, long-term physical, emotional or mental scars are well worth the pay-off of 'repairing' relationships no one asked him to repair (and he certainly isn't keeping tabs on all of them after a year of two...).<br /> After barely surviving a Hero due to sheer luck (random avalanche), he sought out communion with the Dark Mother and got the distinct impression of having to find and follow Jean due to something big being about to take place.<br /> <br /> He is NOT one of the seven core members, but rather hovers around them, and they occassionally rever to him as Father Charity, since the retired sports science professor spends almost all his free time in soup-kitchens and youth centers and similar places of, well, charity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Seven Deadly Sins (Brood)<br /> <u><b>Terry Wong('Gluttony')</b></u><br /> <b>Concept</b>: reluctant monster turned insatiable cannibalist<br /> <b>Family</b>: Eshmaki<br /> <b>Hunger</b>: Predator<br /> <b>Life</b>: Honest<br /> <b>Legend</b>: Brutal<br /> <b>Horror</b>: A belly mouth monster, similar to a Mapinguari, Xing Tian or a Blemmyae - headless, with no eyes, but a huge mouth on the belly with brutally sharp teeth<br /> <b>Atavisms</b>: Skin Deep, Ravenous Maw, Cyclopean Strength<br /> <b>Nightmares</b>: They are all around you, All Your Teeth are falling out<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Physical / Mental / Social <br /> <b>Skills</b>: Physical/ Social/ Mental<br /> <b>Lair</b>: a jungle<br /> <b>Lair Traits</b>:<br /> Engulfing<br /> Extreme Heat<br /> <br /> &quot;You are so talented in x, why don't you make something of yourself? Why do you always do y/z/... instead?&quot; Terry is very familiar with statement like this or their variations. He starts playing the violin, his teacher and parents are amazed at his quick progress - but after a few months, he drops it in favour of learning Spanish. He makes great headway, after a few months is able to hold very simple conversations - and drops it in favour of bushcraft. Rinse and repeat (although, to be fair, he revisits some of his 'hobbies' after some time, like a year of two, only to grow frustrated at the lack of growth, being where he is instead of where he could have been had he kept going).<br /> His parents despair at their son wasting his potential on trivial pursuits, he tells himself he isn't satisfied with just one thing. The truth, of course, is something else. Deep down, he is scared he is not as amazing as everyone thinks at the start, so when things start getting harder, when the initial passion wanes and the work sets in, when he starts making mistakes, he simply... finds something else to show great promise in. To relive the feeling of being talented, gifted, effortlessly doing what others need to work hard for... <br /> And then, everything got more complicated. His Devouring, as all, turned his world upside down, but he got saddled with a Hunger more gruesome than most Begotten: his Horror wants blood. Fresh, taken himself through biting. Preferably devouring their prey wholesale.<br /> For the first time, his life's rhythm was changed around; he had a terribly rough start, failed to Feed multiple times, until the drawbacks of it outweighed his disgust and worries. But by now, five years later? Oh, he's gotten <i>good </i>at it. And he's starting to enjoy it far too much, Feeding every chance he gets.<br /> Without the Brood, he'd likely have drawn way too much attention to himself. But with the Brood, their networks and help, and most of all, their various enemies? There is always more prey.<br /> <br /> RP: the mid-twenties student has changed majors three times by now. Terry likely has some sort of ADD and is an addiction-shifting maladaptive perfectionist with avoidance coping. Despite that, he has amassed quite a bit of knowledge, if in Breadth rather than Depth (many different low-level skills, Merits like Encyclopedic Knowledge, Interdisciplinary Specialty, Multi-Lingual, Hobbyist Clique), and he's really good at trivia nights in bar clubs.<br /> His obsession with his feeding has given him a creepy edge, and before long, his demeanor will make people think 'serial killer' (which isn't too far off).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 05-25-2025, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T01:53:51-07:00","id":1560880,"title":"","content":"An Eshmaki who waits on the side of the road at night, waiting to hurl itself in front of passing vehicles and pretending to be fatally injured in the resulting crash. It preys upon those who attempt to conceal the accident, inflicting punishment upon them for their callous disregard for life. It's Horror takes the form of a reanimated piece of roadkill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}